m/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/3a329f571637dc76f662851558cd6a28bd0be891/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:44:11Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":1,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:44:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: don''t crash decorating an error with a getter-only message (#34821)\n\n* fix: don''t crash decorating an error with a getter-only message\n\n`modifyErrMsg` assigned directly to `err.message`, which throws for any\nerror object that inherits `message` as a getter-only accessor — most\nnotably `DOMException`, the shape browsers use for cross-origin access\ndenials and CSP violations. The resulting `TypeError` replaced the error\nthat actually failed the test, so the real cause was never shown.\n\nFall back to defining an own `message` property when assignment is\nrefused, and leave the error untouched if that is refused too, so the\noriginal error always reaches the user.\n\nFixes #34818\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K18SejRs9DF3pC7pYjkXzs\n\n* chore: tighten comments on getter-only message handling\n\nKeep the comments to what the code cannot say for itself and follow the\nrepo convention of a bare issue link in specs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K18SejRs9DF3pC7pYjkXzs\n\n* chore: move the changelog entry to the pending 16.1.2 release\n\n16.0.1 shipped as part of 16.1.0 while this branch sat, so merging develop\nsilently carried the entry into a released section.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K18SejRs9DF3pC7pYjkXzs\n\n* chore: attach each comment to the code it explains\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K18SejRs9DF3pC7pYjkXzs\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"88151d231409e7bf33caf482626b9af3126ac138","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/88151d231409e7bf33caf482626b9af3126ac138"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/3a329f571637dc76f662851558cd6a28bd0be891","verification":{"payload":"tree 88151d231409e7bf33caf482626b9af3126ac138\nparent 6fd7cb94ec5d9ccd4bbef2520e17c22290f843d3\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1791319451 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791319451 -0400\n\nfix: don''t crash decorating an error with a getter-only message (#34821)\n\n* fix: don''t crash decorating an error with a getter-only message\n\n`modifyErrMsg` assigned directly to `err.message`, which throws for any\nerror object that inherits `message` as a getter-only accessor — most\nnotably `DOMException`, the shape browsers use for cross-origin access\ndenials and CSP violations. The resulting `TypeError` replaced the error\nthat actually failed the test, so the real cause was never shown.\n\nFall back to defining an own `message` property when assignment is\nrefused, and leave the error untouched if that is refused too, so the\noriginal error always reaches the user.\n\nFixes #34818\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K18SejRs9DF3pC7pYjkXzs\n\n* chore: tighten comments on getter-only message handling\n\nKeep the comments to what the code cannot say for itself and follow the\nrepo convention of a bare issue link in specs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K18SejRs9DF3pC7pYjkXzs\n\n* chore: move the changelog entry to the pending 16.1.2 release\n\n16.0.1 shipped as part of 16.1.0 while this branch sat, so merging develop\nsilently carried the entry into a released section.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K18SejRs9DF3pC7pYjkXzs\n\n* chore: attach each comment to the code it explains\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K18SejRs9DF3pC7pYjkXzs\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxV2bCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtigQAAv9IDjkwotDE7fbhbnjRu1/\nDvbrCF/i2Z7JeEXIZGiyrBhaE2547lwcq3JL3MneUoTS+tWnaQwhLiEEQ1Vzhpif\nqsgDWIgkrcM2eLwpfykfrpTDRrG28ntW+OY3CJqg6MPis6xn22R0bCXJNlgWfApn\n8uTpmb8S0K0Xg/8NH13bfUUc+e/eUMh0Gt8OuQwcKLx9iRKTOOp40/e5LidBMrYd\npYFQ3U9holjOXS2qKF7WGDOhc/6SAZk84L+dObVQRKGF8z5d5vgR+vjeRvj3QCLc\nylGn9N3JYjbnXJAXPOLSWeXpyk1aLE8IV0HLKgp2VFR5yjxEn2ggUqsu7hPKd6qj\ndVnifpWwlgqrH96hqHODfqfVT5+RePY/7Pm2FugEmdGTy+iRjYgHEkYHlryM+KuJ\nRorqsr0/Lc77qH4EicQ1Yx81zx8HMrv8BKGVzapt+bXc6ksXLejkqAfYA+PS8RU3\nBcdDyJnWHsqs2+ehsKWZdIPoPHnhJx0Uv5iOgWbUur4ISyS0A5bnP39JgeUSCwVF\nz4of1ylTJy01fnXgNw8HkCYJ9vrjnNFrxocjusqTYCDXdCA0mz8cxGVTpL95bF7L\nux/BqrRwK9A9vFj+sj2+5wV+KguebaGBEvR6wVNe4Ji1tyZN4vFmDkpIonVfxCXl\nq5S6XbKIxaEKWna/BGc9\n=nTzv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T20:44:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/3a329f571637dc76f662851558cd6a28bd0be891","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDNhMzI5ZjU3MTYzN2RjNzZmNjYyODUxNTU4Y2Q2YTI4YmQwYmU4OTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/6fd7cb94ec5d9ccd4bbef2520e17c22290f843d3","sha":"6fd7cb94ec5d9ccd4bbef2520e17c22290f843d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/6fd7cb94ec5d9ccd4bbef2520e17c22290f843d3"}],"sha":"3a329f571637dc76f662851558cd6a28bd0be891","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/3a329f571637dc76f662851558cd6a28bd0be891"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/6fd7cb94ec5d9ccd4bbef2520e17c22290f843d3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:43:26Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":1,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:43:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: convert the @packages/data-context build script to TypeScript (#34813)\n\n* refactor: convert @packages/data-context build script to TypeScript\n\n`scripts/build.js` reads the committed GraphQL SDL and writes the minified\nurql introspection into `src/gen/urql-introspection.gen.ts`. Renamed it to\n`.ts` and pointed `build:schema` at `ts-node`, matching the sibling\n`nexus-build` script in the same directory.\n\nThe package tsconfig only includes `src` and `graphql`, so neither script is\ncovered by `check-ts` — but ts-node type-checks by default, so a type error\nhere now fails `yarn build` rather than surfacing at runtime.\n\nThe generated output is byte-identical to what the JavaScript version\nproduced.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013LYKKqnoj69vYJriEcLHJM\n\n* chore: declare @urql/introspection in @packages/data-context\n\n`scripts/build.ts` imports `@urql/introspection`, but the package was only\ndeclared in the monorepo root, so the import resolved through hoisting.\nDeclared it as a devDependency where it is used — build-time only, and\n`scripts` is outside the package''s published `files`.\n\nKept the root declaration: `scripts/gulp/tasks/gulpGraphql.ts` imports it\ntoo. Reused root''s `^0.3.3` so the existing lockfile entry is shared rather\nthan forking a second resolution; `yarn.lock` is unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013LYKKqnoj69vYJriEcLHJM\n\n* test: cover the urql introspection minify step\n\n`scripts/build.ts` minifies the introspection before writing it, but nothing\nasserted that it did. Dropping `minifyIntrospectionQuery` grew the generated\nartifact from 183KB to 437KB with the whole data-context suite still green —\nand that artifact is bundled into the frontend and baked into the V8\nsnapshot, so the regression would have shipped silently.\n\nAsserts none of the keys `minifyIntrospectionQuery` strips reach the output,\nalongside a check that the schema is non-trivial and keeps its NON_NULL\nwrappers, so the first assertion cannot pass vacuously.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013LYKKqnoj69vYJriEcLHJM\n\n* refactor: share the urql introspection writer with the gulp task\n\n`scripts/gulp/tasks/gulpGraphql.ts` carried a character-identical copy of the\nlogic in `@packages/data-context`''s build script, both writing\n`src/gen/urql-introspection.gen.ts`. Whichever ran last won — gulp under\n`yarn dev`, `build:schema` in CI — so a change to one silently diverged from\nthe other. Extracted `writeUrqlIntrospection` into a module both call.\n\nKept it as a module the script calls rather than exporting from `build.ts`\nbehind a `require.main` guard, so the script stays a script.\n\nThat left `@urql/introspection` with no consumer at the root, so its root\ndeclaration is removed; `packages/data-context` declares it. Removing it\nsurfaced that knip''s globs for that workspace never covered `scripts`, which\nis why the declaration read as used before — it was resolving against the\nroot entry, not real usage. Added `scripts` to the workspace''s entry and\nproject patterns, matching `cli` and `packages/icons`, so knip checks the\nfile that actually imports it.\n\n`build:schema` and `gulp generateFrontendSchema` both still emit output\nbyte-identical to before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013LYKKqnoj69vYJriEcLHJM\n\n* docs: correct the urql introspection comments\n\nThe size claim was measured against the raw JSON payload, not the artifact as\nwritten; minifying more than halves it rather than cutting it to a third.\n\nThe spec''s comment restated the constant''s own name and repeated the\nGraphCache rationale from the writer, so it now records the part that is not\nobvious: the list mirrors the library''s behaviour and has to track it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013LYKKqnoj69vYJriEcLHJM\n\n* test: derive the minify expectation instead of hardcoding it\n\nThe spec listed the nine keys `minifyIntrospectionQuery` drops. That list\ndecays quietly rather than loudly: on a graphql 15 to 16 upgrade\n`specifiedByUrl` becomes `specifiedByURL`, and the entry stops matching\nanything while the assertion still passes, covering one key less than it\nreads as covering.\n\nCompares the artifact''s key set against one minified from the same schema in\nthe test, so the expectation tracks whatever the library strips. The failing\ndiff now lists the keys that leaked through, which is what the hardcoded list\nwas there to spell out.\n\nDrops the companion non-vacuous check — a derived expectation carries the\nwhole schema, so there is nothing left to pass vacuously against.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013LYKKqnoj69vYJriEcLHJM\n\n* docs: repair the truncated comments in the graphql gulp task\n\nTwo JSDoc blocks were cut off mid-sentence and carried no information:\n\"Watches & regenerates the\" and \"Generates the schema so the urql GraphCache\nis\".\n\nDropped the first rather than finishing it — `nexusCodegenWatch` passes its\nwatch paths and output path to `watchNexusTypegen` inline, so any completion\nwould restate the call it sits above, and the `nexusCodegen` sibling has no\ncomment either.\n\nCompleted the second, since the function writes generated files into two\ndifferent packages and the name only mentions one of them.\n\n`generateTestExtensions` kept an empty `@param`/`@returns` pair that said\nnothing; replaced with what the extension is for.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013LYKKqnoj69vYJriEcLHJM\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0f3d9d3292b0d6501fd71a8e77878c1f18f79641","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/0f3d9d3292b0d6501fd71a8e77878c1f18f79641"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/6fd7cb94ec5d9ccd4bbef2520e17c22290f843d3","verification":{"payload":"tree 0f3d9d3292b0d6501fd71a8e77878c1f18f79641\nparent 17a166a5f6849a090f8ad05efc2420b2f420ce38\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1791319406 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791319406 -0400\n\nrefactor: convert the @packages/data-context build script to TypeScript (#34813)\n\n* refactor: convert @packages/data-context build script to TypeScript\n\n`scripts/build.js` reads the committed GraphQL SDL and writes the minified\nurql introspection into `src/gen/urql-introspection.gen.ts`. Renamed it to\n`.ts` and pointed `build:schema` at `ts-node`, matching the sibling\n`nexus-build` script in the same directory.\n\nThe package tsconfig only includes `src` and `graphql`, so neither script is\ncovered by `check-ts` — but ts-node type-checks by default, so a type error\nhere now fails `yarn build` rather than surfacing at runtime.\n\nThe generated output is byte-identical to what the JavaScript version\nproduced.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013LYKKqnoj69vYJriEcLHJM\n\n* chore: declare @urql/introspection in @packages/data-context\n\n`scripts/build.ts` imports `@urql/introspection`, but the package was only\ndeclared in the monorepo root, so the import resolved through hoisting.\nDeclared it as a devDependency where it is used — build-time only, and\n`scripts` is outside the package''s published `files`.\n\nKept the root declaration: `scripts/gulp/tasks/gulpGraphql.ts` imports it\ntoo. Reused root''s `^0.3.3` so the existing lockfile entry is shared rather\nthan forking a second resolution; `yarn.lock` is unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013LYKKqnoj69vYJriEcLHJM\n\n* test: cover the urql introspection minify step\n\n`scripts/build.ts` minifies the introspection before writing it, but nothing\nasserted that it did. Dropping `minifyIntrospectionQuery` grew the generated\nartifact from 183KB to 437KB with the whole data-context suite still green —\nand that artifact is bundled into the frontend and baked into the V8\nsnapshot, so the regression would have shipped silently.\n\nAsserts none of the keys `minifyIntrospectionQuery` strips reach the output,\nalongside a check that the schema is non-trivial and keeps its NON_NULL\nwrappers, so the first assertion cannot pass vacuously.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013LYKKqnoj69vYJriEcLHJM\n\n* refactor: share the urql introspection writer with the gulp task\n\n`scripts/gulp/tasks/gulpGraphql.ts` carried a character-identical copy of the\nlogic in `@packages/data-context`''s build script, both writing\n`src/gen/urql-introspection.gen.ts`. Whichever ran last won — gulp under\n`yarn dev`, `build:schema` in CI — so a change to one silently diverged from\nthe other. Extracted `writeUrqlIntrospection` into a module both call.\n\nKept it as a module the script calls rather than exporting from `build.ts`\nbehind a `require.main` guard, so the script stays a script.\n\nThat left `@urql/introspection` with no consumer at the root, so its root\ndeclaration is removed; `packages/data-context` declares it. Removing it\nsurfaced that knip''s globs for that workspace never covered `scripts`, which\nis why the declaration read as used before — it was resolving against the\nroot entry, not real usage. Added `scripts` to the workspace''s entry and\nproject patterns, matching `cli` and `packages/icons`, so knip checks the\nfile that actually imports it.\n\n`build:schema` and `gulp generateFrontendSchema` both still emit output\nbyte-identical to before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013LYKKqnoj69vYJriEcLHJM\n\n* docs: correct the urql introspection comments\n\nThe size claim was measured against the raw JSON payload, not the artifact as\nwritten; minifying more than halves it rather than cutting it to a third.\n\nThe spec''s comment restated the constant''s own name and repeated the\nGraphCache rationale from the writer, so it now records the part that is not\nobvious: the list mirrors the library''s behaviour and has to track it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013LYKKqnoj69vYJriEcLHJM\n\n* test: derive the minify expectation instead of hardcoding it\n\nThe spec listed the nine keys `minifyIntrospectionQuery` drops. That list\ndecays quietly rather than loudly: on a graphql 15 to 16 upgrade\n`specifiedByUrl` becomes `specifiedByURL`, and the entry stops matching\nanything while the assertion still passes, covering one key less than it\nreads as covering.\n\nCompares the artifact''s key set against one minified from the same schema in\nthe test, so the expectation tracks whatever the library strips. The failing\ndiff now lists the keys that leaked through, which is what the hardcoded list\nwas there to spell out.\n\nDrops the companion non-vacuous check — a derived expectation carries the\nwhole schema, so there is nothing left to pass vacuously against.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013LYKKqnoj69vYJriEcLHJM\n\n* docs: repair the truncated comments in the graphql gulp task\n\nTwo JSDoc blocks were cut off mid-sentence and carried no information:\n\"Watches & regenerates the\" and \"Generates the schema so the urql GraphCache\nis\".\n\nDropped the first rather than finishing it — `nexusCodegenWatch` passes its\nwatch paths and output path to `watchNexusTypegen` inline, so any completion\nwould restate the call it sits above, and the `nexusCodegen` sibling has no\ncomment either.\n\nCompleted the second, since the function writes generated files into two\ndifferent packages and the name only mentions one of them.\n\n`generateTestExtensions` kept an empty `@param`/`@returns` pair that said\nnothing; replaced with what the extension is for.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013LYKKqnoj69vYJriEcLHJM\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxV1uCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAL7YQAIw3wf9J/NpXBOMyzHI6k8TE\nRwA7p+8LyfRZ4BUpkeMJGLsuCmcfb8x/ka/VvSWRXlQb8n8YGtstXraykpNccQHL\nMqG/f1XUg91KTcnWjLDRZitfDkjLZT+9VMsL5ASTcSY0C31Dhn7ajJZUyGWfCUHk\nqtf6Jn5ouU/F1vv0WGN2MqRUuvZRlFdBd+rw7kIum2mk8+qef9eB1WjM5Ji7z8cW\nRwJgtyWrWV+15VHWLp3ts7/S5IbF2aZFIukezmo/XBtdHA0AFRgUuXtxUoZKFCXa\nBWF1ZIzggr/FAACBo8XHZSGHpS88S/YomeeImQFUcn9itoGlsAKlmqEEljHjBu4i\n+56HJAR7PrR2tZIcpz/JMLMF30Hhrg6/hoZiZvSi+JHCBvRBgJFXkxFBivI0Vp79\nEjMmfA