,"events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/semantic-release-bot","id":32174276,"login":"semantic-release-bot","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMTc0Mjc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/17a166a5f6849a090f8ad05efc2420b2f420ce38/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:46:24Z","email":"semantic-release-bot@martynus.net","name":"semantic-release-bot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:46:24Z","email":"semantic-release-bot@martynus.net","name":"semantic-release-bot"},"message":"chore: release @cypress/webpack-dev-server-v6.1.0\n\n[skip ci]","tree":{"sha":"31a6c8deacc680f7d09b1c120a06e01cdd2df1d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/31a6c8deacc680f7d09b1c120a06e01cdd2df1d7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/17a166a5f6849a090f8ad05efc2420b2f420ce38","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32174276?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/semantic-release-bot","id":32174276,"login":"semantic-release-bot","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMTc0Mjc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/17a166a5f6849a090f8ad05efc2420b2f420ce38","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDE3YTE2NmE1ZjY4NDlhMDkwZjhhZDA1ZWZjMjQyMGIyZjQyMGNlMzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/514aff43d95eb04f1fc629572b5177ad03283284","sha":"514aff43d95eb04f1fc629572b5177ad03283284","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/514aff43d95eb04f1fc629572b5177ad03283284"}],"sha":"17a166a5f6849a090f8ad05efc2420b2f420ce38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/17a166a5f6849a090f8ad05efc2420b2f420ce38"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/514aff43d95eb04f1fc629572b5177ad03283284/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T16:11:24Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":2,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T16:11:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: wait for the page cy.go() navigates to before resolving (#34938)\n\n* fix: wait for the page cy.go() navigates to before resolving\n\nSince 15.0.0, cy.go() resolved a few milliseconds after it was called,\nbecause the chain that waits for the history navigation to unload and\nload the page was no longer returned. It yielded undefined instead of\nthe AUT window, never enforced its timeout or pageLoadTimeout, and let\nthe next command run against the page being navigated away from.\n\nReturn that chain again. When cy.go() lands on a cross-origin page, the\nwindow it yields is cross-origin, so assertions on it read its\nproperties safely instead of throwing a SecurityError.\n\nAdds deterministic regression tests for yielding the window, waiting for\nload, enforcing both timeouts, and not waiting on same-document\nnavigations, plus cross-origin coverage, and un-skips the cy.origin\n.go() consoleProps test, which now passes reliably.\n\nFixes #32460\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P9qT7De18KSz5cqaH8qd73\n\n* test: un-skip the cy.go() suite\n\nThe suite was skipped as flaky in #23308. With cy.go() waiting for the\npage it navigates to, 20 of its 21 tests pass as written. The other two\nneeded fixing:\n\n- \"logs before + after\" expected the log to hold both snapshots while\n  the page was unloading, but the \"after\" snapshot is only taken when\n  the command finishes. It now expects one, as the matching cy.reload()\n  test does, and drops the wait that covered for cy.go() resolving\n  early.\n- \"only logs once on error\" finished as soon as cy.go() timed out, with\n  the navigation still in flight, which could hang the next test. It\n  now waits for the page to load before finishing, as \"throws when go\n  times out\" does.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P9qT7De18KSz5cqaH8qd73\n\n* test: drop the cy.go() timeout test duplicated by the un-skipped suite\n\n\"fails when given a timeout shorter than the page load\" goes back with\n{ timeout: 1 } and asserts the same error as \"throws when go times out\"\nin the now un-skipped #go suite.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P9qT7De18KSz5cqaH8qd73\n\n* test: tidy comments on the cy.go() tests\n\nDrop a comment repeated within the navigation spec, say why the\nsame-document navigation tests pass a short timeout, and match the\ncomment style of the driver test server.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P9qT7De18KSz5cqaH8qd73\n\n* fix: start cy.go()''s unload check once the navigation is issued\n\ncy.go() started its 100ms check for whether the page unloaded without\nwaiting for the navigate:aut:history automation request. When that\nround trip took longer than 100ms, the page hadn''t started unloading\nyet, so cy.go() resolved on the page it was leaving.\n\nAdds a test that delays the automation request past the check.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P9qT7De18KSz5cqaH8qd73\n\n* test: give \"only logs once on error\" time to wait for the page load\n\nThe #go errors block sets defaultCommandTimeout to 50ms, which also\ncaps how long a done() test waits once its commands finish. The test\nwaits for the page cy.go() started loading before calling done(), and\nin CI that reload can take longer than 50ms, so it failed with \"The\ndone() callback was never invoked\". Extend the timeout to 1000ms, as\n\"throws when go times out\" in the same block already does.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P9qT7De18KSz5cqaH8qd73\n\n* fix: describe what getProperty does in its comment\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P9qT7De18KSz5cqaH8qd73\n\n* chore: move the cy.go() changelog entry to 16.1.2\n\n16.1.1 has shipped, so the entry belongs under the next release.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P9qT7De18KSz5cqaH8qd73\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9610ea14c5742b42c36daa95d86b3be04a177d35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/9610ea14c5742b42c36daa95d86b3be04a177d35"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/514aff43d95eb04f1fc629572b5177ad03283284","verification":{"payload":"tree 9610ea14c5742b42c36daa95d86b3be04a177d35\nparent 9f0e4a962eccde5c34faa09bf04576c769788303\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1791303084 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791303084 -0400\n\nfix: wait for the page cy.go() navigates to before resolving (#34938)\n\n* fix: wait for the page cy.go() navigates to before resolving\n\nSince 15.0.0, cy.go() resolved a few milliseconds after it was called,\nbecause the chain that waits for the history navigation to unload and\nload the page was no longer returned. It yielded undefined instead of\nthe AUT window, never enforced its timeout or pageLoadTimeout, and let\nthe next command run against the page being navigated away from.\n\nReturn that chain again. When cy.go() lands on a cross-origin page, the\nwindow it yields is cross-origin, so assertions on it read its\nproperties safely instead of throwing a SecurityError.\n\nAdds deterministic regression tests for yielding the window, waiting for\nload, enforcing both timeouts, and not waiting on same-document\nnavigations, plus cross-origin coverage, and un-skips the cy.origin\n.go() consoleProps test, which now passes reliably.\n\nFixes #32460\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P9qT7De18KSz5cqaH8qd73\n\n* test: un-skip the cy.go() suite\n\nThe suite was skipped as flaky in #23308. With cy.go() waiting for the\npage it navigates to, 20 of its 21 tests pass as written. The other two\nneeded fixing:\n\n- \"logs before + after\" expected the log to hold both snapshots while\n  the page was unloading, but the \"after\" snapshot is only taken when\n  the command finishes. It now expects one, as the matching cy.reload()\n  test does, and drops the wait that covered for cy.go() resolving\n  early.\n- \"only logs once on error\" finished as soon as cy.go() timed out, with\n  the navigation still in flight, which could hang the next test. It\n  now waits for the page to load before finishing, as \"throws when go\n  times out\" does.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P9qT7De18KSz5cqaH8qd73\n\n* test: drop the cy.go() timeout test duplicated by the un-skipped suite\n\n\"fails when given a timeout shorter than the page load\" goes back with\n{ timeout: 1 } and asserts the same error as \"throws when go times out\"\nin the now un-skipped #go suite.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P9qT7De18KSz5cqaH8qd73\n\n* test: tidy comments on the cy.go() tests\n\nDrop a comment repeated within the navigation spec, say why the\nsame-document navigation tests pass a short timeout, and match the\ncomment style of the driver test server.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P9qT7De18KSz5cqaH8qd73\n\n* fix: start cy.go()''s unload check once the navigation is issued\n\ncy.go() started its 100ms check for whether the page unloaded without\nwaiting for the navigate:aut:history automation request. When that\nround trip took longer than 100ms, the page hadn''t started unloading\nyet, so cy.go() resolved on the page it was leaving.\n\nAdds a test that delays the automation request past the check.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P9qT7De18KSz5cqaH8qd73\n\n* test: give \"only logs once on error\" time to wait for the page load\n\nThe #go errors block sets defaultCommandTimeout to 50ms, which also\ncaps how long a done() test waits once its commands finish. The test\nwaits for the page cy.go() started loading before calling done(), and\nin CI that reload can take longer than 50ms, so it failed with \"The\ndone() callback was never invoked\". Extend the timeout to 1000ms, as\n\"throws when go times out\" in the same block already does.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P9qT7De18KSz5cqaH8qd73\n\n* fix: describe what getProperty does in its comment\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P9qT7De18KSz5cqaH8qd73\n\n* chore: move the cy.go() changelog entry to 16.1.2\n\n16.1.1 has shipped, so the entry belongs under the next release.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P9qT7De18KSz5cqaH8qd73\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxR2sCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGb0QACw89bLXginc2J2cr/OVuTth\nQ5Ns0ZTWjFG0B920HsItm1wZAjRN5SKPabutdUru9aau97HrUHdY93PxsXyXH5CY\nQOsaB7AFYGNmODpdHP5iVF54z2jZwEf010KSC7Em/Au1KaZwPu4a2iVQo579KcxL\nUrS85rmWjP9b3AEYpdOMKd6P49B17lEp5feWMx51EsPXeSgEuYZPrJDqrnetAwtE\nEyegj/j0S6q2UchPzMNJKHFpkjWlpEXqoVLE3na6N8GRWA5ZVz5DxSHfCpMWbL9n\n0rVJ//206FQFeb5EEtGQyXVwRmEs7ych92jqZt3dvdlBfv1sNT6Y+IOYMIoNwor6\n5p+fcrMU/e2hVZ3U60KysIpw3IEgdIUayLfEF6vXA/3A8+1iO4XOb9n2rs18CZOU\nJUHd8oqUfeAZMBo6dIF02gIi52OUEk+wzmVmK/HHPTh0k75wC23JI9fYfQZcBizH\n59ljBGl52wSa/gL7ylG834UTyATIFkGE+xCNC9HmIu1qm5j9D5qU5CRMhxjT3QIi\nGanFVQYlftke+uaUXVwNz/N9x7DSXAnstTp4jYbzHFAMgJo50/BiX4bYmZhx3Izv\nX4MGimOLuFADSAIn/2NqqPlHzreai/XuW720CmvEoGDFcxGSmsQwQfkyBkKQ9Nbb\nI9lOmec9if05UFITBrQw\n=ESOC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T16:11:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/514aff43d95eb04f1fc629572b5177ad03283284","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDUxNGFmZjQzZDk1ZWIwNGYxZmM2Mjk1NzJiNTE3N2FkMDMyODMyODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/9f0e4a962eccde5c34faa09bf04576c769788303","sha":"9f0e4a962eccde5c34faa09bf04576c769788303","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/9f0e4a962eccde5c34faa09bf04576c769788303"}],"sha":"514aff43d95eb04f1fc629572b5177ad03283284","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/514aff43d95eb04f1fc629572b5177ad03283284"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/9f0e4a962eccde5c34faa09bf04576c769788303/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:47:34Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":1,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:47:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add cy.getByRole() query (#34937)\n\n* feat: add cy.getByRole() query\n\nAdds `cy.getByRole(role, { name, hidden, native, timeout, log,\nincludeShadowDom })`, which finds elements by ARIA role and, optionally,\naccessible name. It yields every match, retries, works as a parent or child\ncommand and inside `.within()`, and when nothing matches the error lists the\nroles and names that were found.\n\n`native: true` matches only elements whose tag gives them the role, such as\n`<button>`, so a test fails if the page fakes one with `<div role=\"button\">`.\nIt throws for widget roles such as `tab`, which HTML has no element for.\n\nIt is built on a shared foundation that later `cy.getBy*()` queries can\nreuse:\n\n- `dom/accessibility/`: text matchers, and role, hidden-element and\n  accessible-name helpers wrapping aria-query 5.3.0 and\n  dom-accessibility-api 0.5.16, with a cache that lives for one retry\n- `querying/get_by.ts`: `addGetByQuery()`, which registers a `getBy*` query\n  from a small definition and handles scope, shadow DOM, retries, logging\n  and errors\n- a `get_by` error namespace\n\nThe public types add `GetByRoleOptions`, and take the role union from\n`@types/aria-query`, which is synced into `cli/types` like the other\nbundled third-party types.\n\nThe app, launchpad, frontend-shared and webpack-dev-server tests now use\n`cy.getByRole()` in place of Testing Library''s `findByRole`, with\n`native: true` wherever the target is a native element, and the testing\nguide recommends it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* fix: address getByRole review findings and CI failures\n\n- Call `hasPreviouslyLinkedCommand()` so a parent `cy.getByRole()` logs as\n  `parent` instead of always `child`.\n- Sort matches into document order when more than one root is searched, so\n  shadow DOM matches sit at their host rather than after all light DOM ones.\n- Keep an element''s implicit role when its `role` attribute is blank.\n- Read `elementRoles.entries()` through `Array.from`.\n- Point the cy.origin `getByRole` specs at a button that exists in dom.html.\n- Ignore the synced aria-query typedefs in cli lint, add get_by_role.ts to\n  knip''s command exports, and stop exporting internal-only helpers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* test: generate getByRole name and validation specs from tables\n\nDrive the accessible-name sources and the argument validation errors from\ndata tables, check the docs URL on every validation error, and drop a\nduplicate child-log test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* fix: use the right article for a hidden native getByRole description\n\nWith `hidden: true` and `native: true`, the not-found error read \"an native\nelement\". Pick the article from the first word of the description.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* feat: make cy.getByRole() match native elements by default\n\nFor a role that HTML has an element for, `cy.getByRole()` now only matches\nthat element unless `native: false` is passed, so `cy.getByRole(''button'')`\nfinds a `<button>` but not a `<div role=\"button\">`. Roles that HTML has no\nelement for, such as `tab` or `menuitem`, still match their `role`\nattribute; passing `native: true` with one of them still throws.\n\nThe not-found hint now says how to opt out, and the types, changelog entry\nand testing styleguide describe the new default. The repo''s own call sites\ndrop `native: true` and pass `native: false` where they target a Headless UI\n`dialog`, `listbox`, `option` or `radio`, keeping their behavior unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* fix: only suggest native: false when it would find a match\n\nThe getByRole not-found hint suggested `{ native: false }` whenever an\nelement had the role through a `role` attribute, even when that element\ndid not match the requested name or was hidden, so following the advice\nstill failed. Check skipped elements against the same matching rules,\nwith `native: false`, before showing the hint.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* fix: give a <select> with size=\"1\" the combobox role\n\naria-query maps `<select>` to `listbox` only when `size` is greater than\n1, but the implicit-role selector reduced that constraint to `[size]`, so\na `<select size=\"1\">` was a `listbox` and not a `combobox`. Check the\nparsed `size` property for both rules instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* fix: treat <td role=\"gridcell\"> as a native gridcell\n\naria-query lists `<td>` as both a `cell` and, inside a grid, a `gridcell`,\nand the implicit-role lookup always picks `cell`. Because the native check\ncompared against that one implicit role, no element ever counted as a\nnative gridcell, so `cy.getByRole(''gridcell'')` matched nothing unless\n`native: false` was passed. Check every native element for the role\ninstead.\n\nAlso restore the blank line between the getByRole changelog entry and the\nBugfixes heading that the develop merge dropped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* fix: use the first valid token of a role attribute\n\nA `role` attribute lists fallbacks, and browsers use the first token that\nis a real, non-abstract role, so `role=\"foo button\"` is a button. getRoles\ntook the first token whatever it was. Skip unknown and abstract roles, and\nfall back to the implicit role when no token is valid.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* misc: clarify getByRole checked hint and native-default exceptions\n\nThe `checked` option hint suggested `.filter('':checked'')`, which only works\nfor native checkboxes and radios. Also suggest `[aria-checked=true]` for\nelements that get their role from a `role` attribute. Document in the\n`native` option that `<input role=\"combobox\">` and `<svg role=\"img\">` need\n`native: false`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* fix: reject getByRole roles that contain whitespace\n\nA role is a single token, so a role with whitespace, such as\n''switch checkbox'', could never match. A line break in the role also made\nthe attribute selector invalid, so querySelectorAll threw a SyntaxError\nDOMException mid-query. Validate the role up front with a clear error.\n\nAlso add a regression test that a subject chained inside .within() is\nsearched instead of the .within() scope, as reported against Testing\nLibrary in testing-library/cypress-testing-library#201.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* fix: name an element from the hidden content of a hidden aria-labelledby target\n\nWhen the node an `aria-labelledby` points at is hidden, accname step 2A\nsays its hidden descendants still count towards the name, so\n`<button aria-labelledby=\"l\">` with `<span id=\"l\" aria-hidden=\"true\">`\nwrapping `display: none` text is named by that text, as Chromium names it.\ndom-accessibility-api (every release through 0.7.1) dropped those\ndescendants, giving an empty name. Patch it so a traversal that starts at a\nhidden referenced node keeps its hidden descendants, while a visible\nreferenced node still leaves out hidden children.\n\nReported against Testing Library in\ntesting-library/cypress-testing-library#290.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* fix: let a project''s own getByRole command replace the built-in\n\nMany projects already define `getByRole`, through @testing-library/cypress\nor a custom command. Adding it as a built-in would make that registration\nthrow \"is an existing Cypress command\" and stop the suite from loading.\nMark getByRole as a replaceable built-in, so `Commands.add()` and\n`Commands.addQuery()` accept the name and the project''s definition wins.\nKeep the command and query registries exclusive so `cy.now()` and\n`Commands.overwrite()` act on whichever definition is current.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* fix: address getByRole review feedback\n\n- Scope the dom-accessibility-api hidden-traversal flag to each\n  aria-labelledby/aria-describedby traversal, so a nested reference to a\n  visible node leaves out its hidden descendants again.\n- Check an element''s tag before reading tag-specific properties in the\n  implicit role rules, and read aria-query''s attribute constraints through\n  an explicit type, with a unit test that fails if aria-query adds one.\n- Derive getBy option kinds from the option types, and getByRole''s options\n  from the public GetByRoleOptions, so the validation can''t drift from them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* refactor: split getBy query steps into named helpers\n\naddGetByQuery now reads as the query''s steps (validate the arguments,\nresolve the scope, collect the search roots, find the matches, log and\nyield), each a named helper it calls in order, so a reader no longer has\nto piece the flow together across files. It stays the single entry point\nthat future getBy* queries register through. Behaviour is unchanged.\n\nAlso link the upstream dom-accessibility-api issue from the accname patch,\nso it can be dropped once that''s fixed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* refactor: replace type assertions in getByRole with type guards\n\nTurn isShadowRoot into a type guard and the getBy* argument validators\ninto assertion functions, so options and matchers narrow without `as`.\nRemaining assertions carry a \"Safe because\" comment. Document the\nconvention in the TypeScript guide, and add driver notes on cross-realm\n`instanceof` and linking upstream issues from patches.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* refactor: have getByRole list its own query steps\n\ngetByRole now registers its own query and reads top to bottom: validate,\nlog, search the scope, match, yield. get_by.ts becomes a set of shared\nhelpers that future getBy* queries can call, rather than a driver that\ncalls back into each query.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* fix: name hidden elements and give grid cells the gridcell role in getByRole\n\nWith `hidden: true`, an element that is itself hidden had an empty name, so\nthe `name` option could never match it. It''s now named as if it were shown.\n\nA `<td>` was always a `cell`. It''s now a `gridcell` inside a grid or treegrid,\nand has no role inside a presentational table, as in browsers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* chore: tighten getByRole code comments\n\nCorrect the whitespace comment in matchesRole, drop comments that repeated\nothers in roles.ts, and share one \"Safe because\" comment for the role-key\ncast.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* refactor: drop the replaceable built-in for getByRole\n\nRemove the exception that let a project''s own getByRole command replace\nthe built-in query, along with its spec, type test and changelog note.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* chore: trim the getByRole changelog entry\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* fix: search a bare element or shadow root yielded by cy.wrap() in getByRole\n\ncy.wrap() yields a DOM element or shadow root as is, not as a jQuery\ncollection, so cy.wrap(element).getByRole() threw. The subject is now\nwrapped before it''s searched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b0bd64a1cc63a0b8ade842528869c31458238423","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/b0bd64a1cc63a0b8ade842528869c31458238423"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/9f0e4a962eccde5c34faa09bf04576c769788303","verification":{"payload":"tree b0bd64a1cc63a0b8ade842528869c31458238423\nparent 773bc81be0c46bdf6fd30f5a4789930f92094a9a\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1791301654 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791301654 -0400\n\nfeat: add cy.getByRole() query (#34937)\n\n* feat: add cy.getByRole() query\n\nAdds `cy.getByRole(role, { name, hidden, native, timeout, log,\nincludeShadowDom })`, which finds elements by ARIA role and, optionally,\naccessible name. It yields every match, retries, works as a parent or child\ncommand and inside `.within()`, and when nothing matches the error lists the\nroles and names that were found.\n\n`native: true` matches only elements whose tag gives them the role, such as\n`<button>`, so a test fails if the page fakes one with `<div role=\"button\">`.\nIt throws for widget roles such as `tab`, which HTML has no element for.\n\nIt is built on a shared foundation that later `cy.getBy*()` queries can\nreuse:\n\n- `dom/accessibility/`: text matchers, and role, hidden-element and\n  accessible-name helpers wrapping aria-query 5.3.0 and\n  dom-accessibility-api 0.5.16, with a cache that lives for one retry\n- `querying/get_by.ts`: `addGetByQuery()`, which registers a `getBy*` query\n  from a small definition and handles scope, shadow DOM, retries, logging\n  and errors\n- a `get_by` error namespace\n\nThe public types add `GetByRoleOptions`, and take the role union from\n`@types/aria-query`, which is synced into `cli/types` like the other\nbundled third-party types.\n\nThe app, launchpad, frontend-shared and webpack-dev-server tests now use\n`cy.getByRole()` in place of Testing Library''s `findByRole`, with\n`native: true` wherever the target is a native element, and the testing\nguide recommends it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* fix: address getByRole review findings and CI failures\n\n- Call `hasPreviouslyLinkedCommand()` so a parent `cy.getByRole()` logs as\n  `parent` instead of always `child`.\n- Sort matches into document order when more than one root is searched, so\n  shadow DOM matches sit at their host rather than after all light DOM ones.\n- Keep an element''s implicit role when its `role` attribute is blank.\n- Read `elementRoles.entries()` through `Array.from`.\n- Point the cy.origin `getByRole` specs at a button that exists in dom.html.\n- Ignore the synced aria-query typedefs in cli lint, add get_by_role.ts to\n  knip''s command exports, and stop exporting internal-only helpers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* test: generate getByRole name and validation specs from tables\n\nDrive the accessible-name sources and the argument validation errors from\ndata tables, check the docs URL on every validation error, and drop a\nduplicate child-log test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* fix: use the right article for a hidden native getByRole description\n\nWith `hidden: true` and `native: true`, the not-found error read \"an native\nelement\". Pick the article from the first word of the description.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* feat: make cy.getByRole() match native elements by default\n\nFor a role that HTML has an element for, `cy.getByRole()` now only matches\nthat element unless `native: false` is passed, so `cy.getByRole(''button'')`\nfinds a `<button>` but not a `<div role=\"button\">`. Roles that HTML has no\nelement for, such as `tab` or `menuitem`, still match their `role`\nattribute; passing `native: true` with one of them still throws.\n\nThe not-found hint now says how to opt out, and the types, changelog entry\nand testing styleguide describe the new default. The repo''s own call sites\ndrop `native: true` and pass `native: false` where they target a Headless UI\n`dialog`, `listbox`, `option` or `radio`, keeping their behavior unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* fix: only suggest native: false when it would find a match\n\nThe getByRole not-found hint suggested `{ native: false }` whenever an\nelement had the role through a `role` attribute, even when that element\ndid not match the requested name or was hidden, so following the advice\nstill failed. Check skipped elements against the same matching rules,\nwith `native: false`, before showing the hint.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* fix: give a <select> with size=\"1\" the combobox role\n\naria-query maps `<select>` to `listbox` only when `size` is greater than\n1, but the implicit-role selector reduced that constraint to `[size]`, so\na `<select size=\"1\">` was a `listbox` and not a `combobox`. Check the\nparsed `size` property for both rules instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* fix: treat <td role=\"gridcell\"> as a native gridcell\n\naria-query lists `<td>` as both a `cell` and, inside a grid, a `gridcell`,\nand the implicit-role lookup always picks `cell`. Because the native check\ncompared against that one implicit role, no element ever counted as a\nnative gridcell, so `cy.getByRole(''gridcell'')` matched nothing unless\n`native: false` was passed. Check every native element for the role\ninstead.\n\nAlso restore the blank line between the getByRole changelog entry and the\nBugfixes heading that the develop merge dropped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* fix: use the first valid token of a role attribute\n\nA `role` attribute lists fallbacks, and browsers use the first token that\nis a real, non-abstract role, so `role=\"foo button\"` is a button. getRoles\ntook the first token whatever it was. Skip unknown and abstract roles, and\nfall back to the implicit role when no token is valid.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* misc: clarify getByRole checked hint and native-default exceptions\n\nThe `checked` option hint suggested `.filter('':checked'')`, which only works\nfor native checkboxes and radios. Also suggest `[aria-checked=true]` for\nelements that get their role from a `role` attribute. Document in the\n`native` option that `<input role=\"combobox\">` and `<svg role=\"img\">` need\n`native: false`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* fix: reject getByRole roles that contain whitespace\n\nA role is a single token, so a role with whitespace, such as\n''switch checkbox'', could never match. A line break in the role also made\nthe attribute selector invalid, so querySelectorAll threw a SyntaxError\nDOMException mid-query. Validate the role up front with a clear error.\n\nAlso add a regression test that a subject chained inside .within() is\nsearched instead of the .within() scope, as reported against Testing\nLibrary in testing-library/cypress-testing-library#201.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* fix: name an element from the hidden content of a hidden aria-labelledby target\n\nWhen the node an `aria-labelledby` points at is hidden, accname step 2A\nsays its hidden descendants still count towards the name, so\n`<button aria-labelledby=\"l\">` with `<span id=\"l\" aria-hidden=\"true\">`\nwrapping `display: none` text is named by that text, as Chromium names it.\ndom-accessibility-api (every release through 0.7.1) dropped those\ndescendants, giving an empty name. Patch it so a traversal that starts at a\nhidden referenced node keeps its hidden descendants, while a visible\nreferenced node still leaves out hidden children.\n\nReported against Testing Library in\ntesting-library/cypress-testing-library#290.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* fix: let a project''s own getByRole command replace the built-in\n\nMany projects already define `getByRole`, through @testing-library/cypress\nor a custom command. Adding it as a built-in would make that registration\nthrow \"is an existing Cypress command\" and stop the suite from loading.\nMark getByRole as a replaceable built-in, so `Commands.add()` and\n`Commands.addQuery()` accept the name and the project''s definition wins.\nKeep the command and query registries exclusive so `cy.now()` and\n`Commands.overwrite()` act on whichever definition is current.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* fix: address getByRole review feedback\n\n- Scope the dom-accessibility-api hidden-traversal flag to each\n  aria-labelledby/aria-describedby traversal, so a nested reference to a\n  visible node leaves out its hidden descendants again.\n- Check an element''s tag before reading tag-specific properties in the\n  implicit role rules, and read aria-query''s attribute constraints through\n  an explicit type, with a unit test that fails if aria-query adds one.\n- Derive getBy option kinds from the option types, and getByRole''s options\n  from the public GetByRoleOptions, so the validation can''t drift from them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* refactor: split getBy query steps into named helpers\n\naddGetByQuery now reads as the query''s steps (validate the arguments,\nresolve the scope, collect the search roots, find the matches, log and\nyield), each a named helper it calls in order, so a reader no longer has\nto piece the flow together across files. It stays the single entry point\nthat future getBy* queries register through. Behaviour is unchanged.\n\nAlso link the upstream dom-accessibility-api issue from the accname patch,\nso it can be dropped once that''s fixed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* refactor: replace type assertions in getByRole with type guards\n\nTurn isShadowRoot into a type guard and the getBy* argument validators\ninto assertion functions, so options and matchers narrow without `as`.\nRemaining assertions carry a \"Safe because\" comment. Document the\nconvention in the TypeScript guide, and add driver notes on cross-realm\n`instanceof` and linking upstream issues from patches.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* refactor: have getByRole list its own query steps\n\ngetByRole now registers its own query and reads top to bottom: validate,\nlog, search the scope, match, yield. get_by.ts becomes a set of shared\nhelpers that future getBy* queries can call, rather than a driver that\ncalls back into each query.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* fix: name hidden elements and give grid cells the gridcell role in getByRole\n\nWith `hidden: true`, an element that is itself hidden had an empty name, so\nthe `name` option could never match it. It''s now named as if it were shown.\n\nA `<td>` was always a `cell`. It''s now a `gridcell` inside a grid or treegrid,\nand has no role inside a presentational table, as in browsers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* chore: tighten getByRole code comments\n\nCorrect the whitespace comment in matchesRole, drop comments that repeated\nothers in roles.ts, and share one \"Safe because\" comment for the role-key\ncast.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* refactor: drop the replaceable built-in for getByRole\n\nRemove the exception that let a project''s own getByRole command replace\nthe built-in query, along with its spec, type test and changelog note.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* chore: trim the getByRole changelog entry\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n* fix: search a bare element or shadow root yielded by cy.wrap() in getByRole\n\ncy.wrap() yields a DOM element or shadow root as is, not as a jQuery\ncollection, so cy.wrap(element).getByRole() threw. The subject is now\nwrapped before it''s searched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GKAByFvvtR4zfoQV2xW316\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxRgWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvxIQAKbctgNUQrjC4zsY2MCbPXiU\n61YRuMTe/yR7gReJzXrp9BQBSw+D+Ul3QhTonCko+QBZ7qq2nnDZ5bAIzrFO8U+x\nL9p219e+6CTgE4com9iAaFGRWcdi3ZtKLrhFsaGW14TAB7TB4nN0UR9Ggbh0i/St\n9CUiZPG3Rmkxvx0W4CvxlPpq8Z9gJCD8NmgwT2flOOk/YYM1PhB2Nfq5xKR37l0U\nx47OM7SfMMFxhJsAlb+iajAw4W5bHPNYy5ivkd9b2lTUqRzOmcmzkOMJXUCe6M9n\nmyEcy4JEjgdTr+SP5ltcMVo7vzNdmBXZVjPXg73r6fKCuFee38Aw8P4ECV8nUnTm\nGTVGj4Qsy2+f8U0vtzJLwSUZqyw2XFcOORTOJmDR9vviTKNVJBuow70tRF7VGgSd\nhkTcR9ZVGltrjO+rtwhCiFRNfJzKDX/2yhYKbHZvwvylLf4QUPIcithtXldAUd6e\nA1Rulg3MZcZs/105vSNGobGCn7OpPKX5jSq5hDB0mTTd6zhiSqiSoOKn+qNDNTjt\nwNQGjjVCKq7rt8PhmwvvDEan47Nfigf0HwYDoldUBxlUvP651tC3YXvK/6B1tqcK\n2aie2t6JiR91cLa3XZpDYkErI3cldbtPUTLifc77pVmPOHmg56fxHvkeLsmUKyJQ\neRxQEOvT8ESWBrFPM10S\n=ToIp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T15:47:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/9f0e4a962eccde5c34faa09bf04576c769788303","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDlmMGU0YTk2MmVjY2RlNWMzNGZhYTA5YmYwNDU3NmM3Njk3ODgzMDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/773bc81be0c46bdf6fd30f5a4789930f92094a9a","sha":"773bc81be0c46bdf6fd30f5a4789930f92094a9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/773bc81be0c46bdf6fd30f5a4789930f92094a9a"}],"sha":"9f0e4a962eccde5c34faa09bf04576c769788303","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/9f0e4a962eccde5c34faa09bf04576c769788303"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/773bc81be0c46bdf6fd30f5a4789930f92094a9a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:12:35Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":1,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:12:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: use client-id for Cypress Bot app token generation (#34850)\n\nactions/create-github-app-token deprecated the `app-id` input in favor of\n`client-id`, which warns on every run that generates the bot token.\n\nThe client ID is a distinct value from the numeric app ID, so this points\nat a new `CYPRESS_BOT_APP_CLIENT_ID` secret. Bumps update-browser-versions\nto the v3 pin the other workflows already use, since the v2 pin has no\n`client-id` input, and drops the job-level `CYPRESS_BOT_APP_ID` env vars\nthat nothing reads.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UYfoPv7jxKHWYcpsCg9ati\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5b53db43ca0e10a637ec029d8647d64e9d9b93be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/5b53db43ca0e10a637ec029d8647d64e9d9b93be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/773bc81be0c46bdf6fd30f5a4789930f92094a9a","verification":{"payload":"tree 5b53db43ca0e10a637ec029d8647d64e9d9b93be\nparent 842967450e6c51d454ddb306715ab2ea39a62036\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1791299555 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791299555 -0400\n\nchore: use client-id for Cypress Bot app token generation (#34850)\n\nactions/create-github-app-token deprecated the `app-id` input in favor of\n`client-id`, which warns on every run that generates the bot token.\n\nThe client ID is a distinct value from the numeric app ID, so this points\nat a new `CYPRESS_BOT_APP_CLIENT_ID` secret. Bumps update-browser-versions\nto the v3 pin the other workflows already use, since the v2 pin has no\n`client-id` input, and drops the job-level `CYPRESS_BOT_APP_ID` env vars\nthat nothing reads.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UYfoPv7jxKHWYcpsCg9ati\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxQ/jCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAD4IQABQSaJWad8EMd7mPOW8EOBPy\n7bCT/OUClBfs/SEeu8sLgnHdvyfIj0ZbnHv29/t0GVgBv2zEIG/s9M4x8P3Tw8Xe\nUMV4zQvZzGp4rv6Pf+MHwQ4UAkHT6CFOkWYCk4i2KTM7FvJxP6cWG+nNidFNwdf2\nOTDAsWKp6H71memsbFMRoI6agsVZnIJ6BDnMcmwE5k46WSTYl14944utWeERzeY4\n2zqThw7mqfanrq+cUZBjvFpMtrgJjTWEIj+sTG/WrpOFm7JSelIa1Wus+L3LfP4T\no/sVKRZJoF+/NY3XefMKMUUWWym+iYvtxe+tXUHysr+Jeczw6GsW5a5FysQr/vTO\n73lXabs5cnqCzCvkn/z7eOECqurQgZxyibpaH681cn24wBVtbBXhA0ewsU2ic5k7\nKtvMZzJFsoeDsySCiRr8+xjd/4XcWcuB7KEEzQVO3t2W8PAzK4o++zr/7ud1ibT/\nitzOrtIhbPfvDXeSUONUGMqMsTPudlTz1gfguqJaGTrwwEqoQCxsl4dHBvU/f2tg\npnGWj7qcJNIfEy08z1Y8rT4bWVCF2ttebR1SuTGPZzyClcAfdnJP3LBlytG34On9\nxvPF5V57w5anvSIxUCLCMdZPhLBPt0vfNQ5mpKqp6ogwZcroGtJRtGye18inLEzo\nTZA2al6T8pyg8lUmQaww\n=A24l\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T15:12:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravat