hub.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/a91e5188431fcab1c4fd9688978e1b4fba70c036/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T20:31:47Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":6,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T20:31:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: keep the cookie jar in sync when cookies are set outside the proxy (#34894)\n\n* fix: keep the cookie jar in sync when cookies are set outside the proxy\n\ncy.request() and cy.setCookie() set cookies in the browser through the\nset:cookie automation, which never passes through the proxy. The server-side\ntough-cookie jar therefore kept whatever value a navigation response had put\nthere, and since jar cookies take precedence over the request''s own when both\ncarry the same name, the stale value overwrote the browser''s on the next AUT\nframe navigation. A test that logged in through cy.request() arrived at the\nnext page anonymous, while cy.getCookie() reported the rotated value.\n\n15.20.0 made this reachable: before #34287 the first visit''s Set-Cookie never\nlanded in the jar, so there was nothing stale to overwrite with.\n\nset:cookie now mirrors the accepted cookie into the jar, the counterpart to\nwhat clear:cookie and clear:cookies already do. set:cookies and add:cookies\nare deliberately left alone: add:cookies applies cookies that came from the\njar, and cy.session() restore clears the jar before calling set:cookies, so\nneither can leave a stale entry behind.\n\nFixes #34891\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019fdEXJv8TGM2XjxtAn6U7q\n\n* fix: sync a cookie whose domain carries a leading dot\n\ntough-cookie''s store keys on the dot-stripped domain and `getCookies` only\nsearches those keys. `cy.setCookie(''sid'', ''x'', { domain: ''.example.com'' })`\nforwards the domain verbatim, so the jar write landed under a `.example.com`\nkey that nothing reads and the stale value kept winning. The tracked-cookie\ncheck still passed, because `getCookieUrl` strips the dot when it builds the\nurl, which made the write look successful.\n\nStrip the leading dot for the write too, matching what `getCookieUrl` already\ndoes. Also moves the changelog entry to 16.1.2, since 16.1.1 has taken its\nown entries on develop.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019fdEXJv8TGM2XjxtAn6U7q\n\n* fix: treat an explicit ''unspecified'' SameSite as lax when syncing the jar\n\n`cy.setCookie()` accepts the extension vocabulary''s literal ''unspecified''\nalongside an omitted sameSite, and both mean the browser''s default of Lax.\nThe string is truthy, so the `?? ''lax''` fallback skipped it and the jar stored\n''unspecified'' verbatim. tough-cookie does not recognise that level and treats\nit as None, so the jar copy was attached to cross-site requests the browser\nwould withhold it from.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019fdEXJv8TGM2XjxtAn6U7q\n\n* chore: trim repeated consequences from the cookie sync comments\n\nThe function header already establishes that a stale jar copy wins over the\nbrowser''s. The guard and dot-strip comments each re-derived that as the code\nflowed through, which the repo''s comment guidelines call out. Each comment now\ncarries only the why the line it sits above needs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019fdEXJv8TGM2XjxtAn6U7q\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f947c28ed43041ae4d3afd40a5d506d668b792bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/f947c28ed43041ae4d3afd40a5d506d668b792bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/a91e5188431fcab1c4fd9688978e1b4fba70c036","verification":{"payload":"tree f947c28ed43041ae4d3afd40a5d506d668b792bc\nparent 9641177a5e56813d35a0ec94d3aed08b5ae2b0b7\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1790800307 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790800307 -0400\n\nfix: keep the cookie jar in sync when cookies are set outside the proxy (#34894)\n\n* fix: keep the cookie jar in sync when cookies are set outside the proxy\n\ncy.request() and cy.setCookie() set cookies in the browser through the\nset:cookie automation, which never passes through the proxy. The server-side\ntough-cookie jar therefore kept whatever value a navigation response had put\nthere, and since jar cookies take precedence over the request''s own when both\ncarry the same name, the stale value overwrote the browser''s on the next AUT\nframe navigation. A test that logged in through cy.request() arrived at the\nnext page anonymous, while cy.getCookie() reported the rotated value.\n\n15.20.0 made this reachable: before #34287 the first visit''s Set-Cookie never\nlanded in the jar, so there was nothing stale to overwrite with.\n\nset:cookie now mirrors the accepted cookie into the jar, the counterpart to\nwhat clear:cookie and clear:cookies already do. set:cookies and add:cookies\nare deliberately left alone: add:cookies applies cookies that came from the\njar, and cy.session() restore clears the jar before calling set:cookies, so\nneither can leave a stale entry behind.\n\nFixes #34891\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019fdEXJv8TGM2XjxtAn6U7q\n\n* fix: sync a cookie whose domain carries a leading dot\n\ntough-cookie''s store keys on the dot-stripped domain and `getCookies` only\nsearches those keys. `cy.setCookie(''sid'', ''x'', { domain: ''.example.com'' })`\nforwards the domain verbatim, so the jar write landed under a `.example.com`\nkey that nothing reads and the stale value kept winning. The tracked-cookie\ncheck still passed, because `getCookieUrl` strips the dot when it builds the\nurl, which made the write look successful.\n\nStrip the leading dot for the write too, matching what `getCookieUrl` already\ndoes. Also moves the changelog entry to 16.1.2, since 16.1.1 has taken its\nown entries on develop.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019fdEXJv8TGM2XjxtAn6U7q\n\n* fix: treat an explicit ''unspecified'' SameSite as lax when syncing the jar\n\n`cy.setCookie()` accepts the extension vocabulary''s literal ''unspecified''\nalongside an omitted sameSite, and both mean the browser''s default of Lax.\nThe string is truthy, so the `?? ''lax''` fallback skipped it and the jar stored\n''unspecified'' verbatim. tough-cookie does not recognise that level and treats\nit as None, so the jar copy was attached to cross-site requests the browser\nwould withhold it from.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019fdEXJv8TGM2XjxtAn6U7q\n\n* chore: trim repeated consequences from the cookie sync comments\n\nThe function header already establishes that a stale jar copy wins over the\nbrowser''s. The guard and dot-strip comments each re-derived that as the code\nflowed through, which the repo''s comment guidelines call out. Each comment now\ncarries only the why the line it sits above needs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019fdEXJv8TGM2XjxtAn6U7q\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvXGzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHioQAFvhKYwNl6FKm3PwUftyGGIA\n9cNPVMMT2Syp+LmVR5+/uLEi7YHSEhgJLLwcaic3WJ7jRTpzakGhnJzW0Zq9RK0w\nIeJw5LofSMEJMrcxRCma0YvXVKPw2KVBAqpRmqYQQAXEB+upt2ri9TkcrUNYaTxZ\nWHZbs3jcltspuMwz01ZJZUCKPBlwhha7IsDifeucl4bT7fdmaG04/O7ipL/fS5Nk\nG6EcgMh5g/qcNjJyW2/wxGHcJlN5ptXrw+p7z3eexM+MHxYBfwTYJSUCio00aqvW\njEEye3O5+15XvLhkwMq7VcX33V4fz+Dl2488z5vNcC5TtD6tw2q5XYg1HAHL/mkx\naRGN2USxh3uTR6QILrK/Oj6sPBCSgny1KNdi4eLii4LvPvptGdM831xwU10eexWD\nSk3gnWPjCnWKE9mdmzwJNywLa1E6yB8Nbogol3Q6Ze4X0YkqPTSc0ml2XZNdzWAv\noU2D+c8qQuWGW2XdXn4alRoVxtCnS9Lv7DPmf/A5CbEABTqYyG+rtuoek3ifYnSj\nIJRFWgcxDYGtLnG94zJTCKUbuyPlAWG6+1x2x3Ll/nOaUOJJaRyec/qfEGUsOGCi\n48ZVkUPyL2egPYoKYZk7BlrRLdaB9kXYo+6dBfWoEkoEtyt2M0WmxkzX30vKHqAJ\nyXrpuUJqabH3M8eHhasc\n=snQ6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T20:31:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/a91e5188431fcab1c4fd9688978e1b4fba70c036","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKGE5MWU1MTg4NDMxZmNhYjFjNGZkOTY4ODk3OGUxYjRmYmE3MGMwMzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/9641177a5e56813d35a0ec94d3aed08b5ae2b0b7","sha":"9641177a5e56813d35a0ec94d3aed08b5ae2b0b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/9641177a5e56813d35a0ec94d3aed08b5ae2b0b7"}],"sha":"a91e5188431fcab1c4fd9688978e1b4fba70c036","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/a91e5188431fcab1c4fd9688978e1b4fba70c036"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/9641177a5e56813d35a0ec94d3aed08b5ae2b0b7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T20:26:17Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":2,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T20:26:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"dependency: upgrade shell-quote and simple-git to address critical Snyk advisories (#34960)\n\n* dependency: upgrade shell-quote to 1.11.0 to address SNYK-JS-SHELLQUOTE-20250993\n\nshell-quote is pulled in transitively by launch-editor (via\n@packages/data-context, @packages/server, and webpack-dev-server).\nAll requesting ranges already allow 1.11.0, so this is a lockfile-only\nbump with no resolutions override.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KJAmR6EbRQag1YzbppPXBJ\n\n* chore: move shell-quote changelog entry to a new 16.1.2 section\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KJAmR6EbRQag1YzbppPXBJ\n\n* chore: link PR in shell-quote changelog entry\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KJAmR6EbRQag1YzbppPXBJ\n\n* dependency: upgrade simple-git to 4.0.2 to address command injection advisories\n\nAddresses SNYK-JS-SIMPLEGIT-20335524, SNYK-JS-SIMPLEGIT-20335531,\nSNYK-JS-SIMPLEGIT-20335540 and SNYK-JS-SIMPLEGITARGVPARSER-20335528.\nNo 3.x release carries the fix.\n\nsimple-git 4 removes the default export, so imports switch to the named\nsimpleGit export. The patch that stripped a class static block for the\nV8 snapshot is removed: 4.0.2 no longer contains one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KJAmR6EbRQag1YzbppPXBJ\n\n* test: pass real debuggers through the ProjectConfigIpc debug mock\n\nsimple-git 4 calls debug''s `extend` while it is imported, which the\nmock''s bare wrapper functions lacked. Only the ProjectConfigIpc\nlifecycle namespace needs capturing, so every other namespace now\ngets the real debugger.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KJAmR6EbRQag1YzbppPXBJ\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ebe9ee0dc19f45ad5d29fd4d6f8171d62ce96bd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/ebe9ee0dc19f45ad5d29fd4d6f8171d62ce96bd0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/9641177a5e56813d35a0ec94d3aed08b5ae2b0b7","verification":{"payload":"tree ebe9ee0dc19f45ad5d29fd4d6f8171d62ce96bd0\nparent e0185393e189f7cf0d4924a4e74eb7174209814a\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1790799977 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790799977 -0400\n\ndependency: upgrade shell-quote and simple-git to address critical Snyk advisories (#34960)\n\n* dependency: upgrade shell-quote to 1.11.0 to address SNYK-JS-SHELLQUOTE-20250993\n\nshell-quote is pulled in transitively by launch-editor (via\n@packages/data-context, @packages/server, and webpack-dev-server).\nAll requesting ranges already allow 1.11.0, so this is a lockfile-only\nbump with no resolutions override.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KJAmR6EbRQag1YzbppPXBJ\n\n* chore: move shell-quote changelog entry to a new 16.1.2 section\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KJAmR6EbRQag1YzbppPXBJ\n\n* chore: link PR in shell-quote changelog entry\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KJAmR6EbRQag1YzbppPXBJ\n\n* dependency: upgrade simple-git to 4.0.2 to address command injection advisories\n\nAddresses SNYK-JS-SIMPLEGIT-20335524, SNYK-JS-SIMPLEGIT-20335531,\nSNYK-JS-SIMPLEGIT-20335540 and SNYK-JS-SIMPLEGITARGVPARSER-20335528.\nNo 3.x release carries the fix.\n\nsimple-git 4 removes the default export, so imports switch to the named\nsimpleGit export. The patch that stripped a class static block for the\nV8 snapshot is removed: 4.0.2 no longer contains one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KJAmR6EbRQag1YzbppPXBJ\n\n* test: pass real debuggers through the ProjectConfigIpc debug mock\n\nsimple-git 4 calls debug''s `extend` while it is imported, which the\nmock''s bare wrapper functions lacked. Only the ProjectConfigIpc\nlifecycle namespace needs capturing, so every other namespace now\ngets the real debugger.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KJAmR6EbRQag1YzbppPXBJ\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvXBpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACa8QADN+UmJ90VHfcgxUTGxMfgFh\nQfvxQaKQJxHtA7xQmGWbDPU+pxzj8jWU49mH9Zby7Ls8ostocshdEMKc6sW2wCQl\nOhTKkanb7iktMRrSIg0JeAqF7hWJgi6jAKsgrpHzoLKGZ1+C7m6iyeHJbLhXj4l8\nKM30o6vTcVgv1Eo6hetbPnwX7Phib6cXatiO/zp/HV/NJk9D+4W3u2wrhzLBaevv\nM5/EDhyjMT/yqmQUoCFF7JOzvHPNtnTTZCqNRJoktLjExKqPPejTqwDP/lqJ+4Mb\nRL8nT4buC65gxhSoGQbjzncx8XwQ576F/VXcWpLwkXFq30HkokPkYgk7/hhmOANG\nBIcEU5I763PH4epKcil5eAQYIBxTjNs7OHB5I/WhUe62O5JdqA5em6APH0Tce7Oi\nDS5ekvTYqHws+8Bs4EDCETX+rijjznVNFM/Q3/Lz/2+8LngdP7Z5vAa1O1j7TmDE\nORFXkt3K4Ctm6TLHgDUwoMh4xD8BhsIr7e60iXrDfX7z9OiL67NnYcHz+3sHXC2z\nqTECvd6InBwjO5nJE5AkMl51ltlI0ukAtZdaQyEBK6R92NZJhD7a6xdyUzK21qL6\n0TPdJh6wgbRDCG3PYR0hSK4SL3PAgRcALuF7FxF8+XzPo8wmaqoj+J4VqS6i8yK5\nQsXiINxWisqwVQl5GabH\n=jv5Z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T20:26:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","follow