chore: drop unused typescript-cached-transpile from the ts-node require hook (#34753)\n\n* chore: drop typescript-cached-transpile from the ts-node require hook\n\nts-node 10.9.2 routes transpileOnly through its own createTsTranspileModule\nfor any TypeScript >= 4.7, so it never calls ts.transpileModule. That is the\nonly thing typescript-cached-transpile patches, which makes the wrapper\nunreachable: instrumenting it shows zero calls and no cache directory written\non both TypeScript 5.4.5 and 5.9.3. All it still contributes is an eager\nspread of the TypeScript namespace at require time.\n\nRemoving the compiler option, its cache env var, the TS_NODE_COMPILER override\nand the dependency together, since dropping the dependency alone would leave\nTS_NODE_COMPILER pointing at a missing module and ts-node would throw into\nregisterDir''s catch, silently disabling TypeScript transpilation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R92rtovZzJQn9qc4PUdDNz\n\n* chore: prune typescript-cached-transpile from the lockfile\n\nRegenerated after dropping the dependency from @packages/ts. Also removes the\n@types/node and tslib selectors it was the sole consumer of.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R92rtovZzJQn9qc4PUdDNz\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bea0a71173612ca92183c059f7596564b60b3796","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/bea0a71173612ca92183c059f7596564b60b3796"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/88472712e81d6183a37c23478dd6526a6692062e","verification":{"payload":"tree bea0a71173612ca92183c059f7596564b60b3796\nparent 6351af6dc9ed2185b01d8ab08a7ec2611491cee7\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1790707323 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790707323 -0400\n\nchore: drop unused typescript-cached-transpile from the ts-node require hook (#34753)\n\n* chore: drop typescript-cached-transpile from the ts-node require hook\n\nts-node 10.9.2 routes transpileOnly through its own createTsTranspileModule\nfor any TypeScript >= 4.7, so it never calls ts.transpileModule. That is the\nonly thing typescript-cached-transpile patches, which makes the wrapper\nunreachable: instrumenting it shows zero calls and no cache directory written\non both TypeScript 5.4.5 and 5.9.3. All it still contributes is an eager\nspread of the TypeScript namespace at require time.\n\nRemoving the compiler option, its cache env var, the TS_NODE_COMPILER override\nand the dependency together, since dropping the dependency alone would leave\nTS_NODE_COMPILER pointing at a missing module and ts-node would throw into\nregisterDir''s catch, silently disabling TypeScript transpilation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R92rtovZzJQn9qc4PUdDNz\n\n* chore: prune typescript-cached-transpile from the lockfile\n\nRegenerated after dropping the dependency from @packages/ts. Also removes the\n@types/node and tslib selectors it was the sole consumer of.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R92rtovZzJQn9qc4PUdDNz\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvAZ7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjnUQAE95/Tz5OvH1PdmZNFoyCz5k\ngiyQKp+vfSSt0utPU1e/waXl3i80jfPDh520cPZ9xzmohvlJiRJgWiTN7oSoRHpJ\ndX/c+6C+YYw42CvTuBpnoDNY67XJA2OLaz/c5B58sDKdUmYacvHDWygmPh+wI+cH\n0/UCNXhsemWoXyrEE+OP7kOLldBMdUKSCuElUFI+Hm4L1Wrbpx1ArwjHNKgz4E7k\nWxVOkZN86bEClt7Gjr8OTSdenNCn/q1kWFpg2xjzZ99bx57mfh/R/HFXzY6l2zWR\nLS59g8VaUhtS0uPNAeRYLGPU/sKnEoDQQQpAIO3q9CgTRc//schKfx1ZbstOhqyw\nymmOCrplSvb3hsQervBkyh4V1QM453bCiDQCGP8rHhjCZJQUl9Hkqz/fOjLvnCJk\nrWdlcFb06yTaEE9msYGKT0PysBR4POS8exnT6xpB+64YQ9KJaTdMH78rP1B4RqW0\nKdcPfjJyPkiemf5YvSrwXpYXNz