scriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/0a34f86be63ce198661cc2142062240ccdeb6a40","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDBhMzRmODZiZTYzY2UxOTg2NjFjYzIxNDIwNjIyNDBjY2RlYjZhNDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/08ec143f851da73c533204141ac4ba33315cdd32","sha":"08ec143f851da73c533204141ac4ba33315cdd32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/08ec143f851da73c533204141ac4ba33315cdd32"}],"sha":"0a34f86be63ce198661cc2142062240ccdeb6a40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/0a34f86be63ce198661cc2142062240ccdeb6a40"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/08ec143f851da73c533204141ac4ba33315cdd32/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T02:40:10Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":2,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T02:40:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf: make shadow-aware .closest() linear instead of quadratic (#34925)\n\n* perf: make shadow-aware .closest() linear instead of quadratic\n\nThe shadow DOM branch of .closest() built its result with\nnodes.concat(closestNode) inside _.reduce, copying the whole accumulator\nfor every subject element. Push into the accumulator instead. The result\nis unchanged: same nodes, same order, deduplicated by sortedUnique().\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0191UNxihzKxSL4a1LcbLe4F\n\n* docs: drop \"For example\" from the .closest() changelog entry\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0191UNxihzKxSL4a1LcbLe4F\n\n* docs: drop benchmark figures from the .closest() changelog entry\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0191UNxihzKxSL4a1LcbLe4F\n\n* docs: link the .closest() changelog entry to #34925\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0191UNxihzKxSL4a1LcbLe4F\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"32f0180c6597723ef8ff6cb52ff63260e0754e64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/32f0180c6597723ef8ff6cb52ff63260e0754e64"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/08ec143f851da73c533204141ac4ba33315cdd32","verification":{"payload":"tree 32f0180c6597723ef8ff6cb52ff63260e0754e64\nparent 764fa3dad1e5d8b449a70601a558758cf54d4839\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1790563210 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790563210 -0400\n\nperf: make shadow-aware .closest() linear instead of quadratic (#34925)\n\n* perf: make shadow-aware .closest() linear instead of quadratic\n\nThe shadow DOM branch of .closest() built its result with\nnodes.concat(closestNode) inside _.reduce, copying the whole accumulator\nfor every subject element. Push into the accumulator instead. The result\nis unchanged: same nodes, same order, deduplicated by sortedUnique().\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0191UNxihzKxSL4a1LcbLe4F\n\n* docs: drop \"For example\" from the .closest() changelog entry\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0191UNxihzKxSL4a1LcbLe4F\n\n* docs: drop benchmark figures from the .closest() changelog entry\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0191UNxihzKxSL4a1LcbLe4F\n\n* docs: link the .closest() changelog entry to #34925\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0191UNxihzKxSL4a1LcbLe4F\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqudOKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgisQAIVijswA6i2cFEwiNDdeuY7p\nbzxjULK/P+KIqpn7yB4wLfcKlE1U17fuYZ1yEuSdCoYVdubbftO7MlpCjkQsCy5z\nnyWNznF7fm0UIMN3q/SEC3XG57cc6eYcoJ4lQbrveBTJwQes/5iDtyubwUgvyLVk\nRrEg97/nauEocMVq6UePeDKydbYjZiRdG2xWwZ7R2KnF6EpP5bHQaMJo3GZ6TOl9\nvrBDI/6eFVTfSj/syyWfsSbDg6TukpLVLa4rNDZ3cZGvt8cCJxeYy1dFxVnI3f7R\nqlQHG2osx7SC/+rg2s+bhGx5aXF1FI0lO7fOxINWXrzp3rJ72bB00L9zNjsNos0s\nq3dMDP8fwRYPdV8Gxc7IVxWpkZhkPHi2abbsidQVZ//f6blyGgpA5RhyWhyWrD/O\npoX4njD+ng1rrP+4Lwa9FORgObCIosm2MQBnGk6Bv945oFIKpk0y9GAhayY6cejp\nn2G5plIKAK68rr6xmtu4bLwzy7kfr9NmFNlOgsl965I97Af8TMbNt4UuCQZ0XceH\n87Fvg+rhV0AGQ4bmaQjUeTcvSAO3vYDQJCnS3zSBElbNi03Eoh/eTSmTBnrSi4UQ\n7gC+PsL8P/10iglpDRexnHmaYABTp+GS2a5FpPH7xCYVocWzkPK4k9rSIWoU4ZSg\nO6jU+d5UuJ7dCESyFbrH\n=zYAs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T02:40:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/08ec143f851da73c533204141ac4ba33315cdd32","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDA4ZWMxNDNmODUxZGE3M2M1MzMyMDQxNDFhYzRiYTMzMzE1Y2RkMzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/764fa3dad1e5d8b449a70601a558758cf54d4839","sha":"764fa3dad1e5d8b449a70601a558758cf54d4839","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/764fa3dad1e5d8b449a70601a558758cf54d4839"}],"sha":"08ec143f851da73c533204141ac4ba33315cdd32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/08ec143f851da73c533204141ac4ba33315cdd32"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/764fa3dad1e5d8b449a70601a558758cf54d4839/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T14:29:59Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":7,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T14:29:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"misc: name the running command in the .each() and .spread() mixed async/sync error and type .each()''s third argument as the jQuery collection (#34933)\n\n* misc: name the running command in the .each() and .spread() mixed async/sync error and type .each()''s third argument as the jQuery collection\n\nThe callback_mixes_sync_and_async error raised from thenFn always named\ncy.then(), even when .each() or .spread() ran the callback. It now takes\nthe current command''s name, following invoke_its.timed_out, and links to\nthat command''s docs.\n\nThe DOM overloads of .each() typed the callback''s third argument as E[],\nbut the driver passes the original subject, which for DOM subjects is the\njQuery collection. They now type it as JQuery<E>. The non-DOM overloads''\n$list widens from any[] to any: TypeScript fixes an unannotated callback\nparameter to the first overload''s type, so with any[] a partly annotated\ncallback like (num: number, i, array) => {} no longer matched either\noverload.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012aPnumJCuSNjueeLCrT48L\n\n* docs: file type corrections and error wording changes under Misc in the changelog\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012aPnumJCuSNjueeLCrT48L\n\n* docs: tighten the .each() changelog entry and the Misc section description\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012aPnumJCuSNjueeLCrT48L\n\n* misc: link the .each() changelog entries to #34933\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012aPnumJCuSNjueeLCrT48L\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3404cae8b29057dcaadb23ec0a996dfa5414988b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/3404cae8b29057dcaadb23ec0a996dfa5414988b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/764fa3dad1e5d8b449a70601a558758cf54d4839","verification":{"payload":"tree 3404cae8b29057dcaadb23ec0a996dfa5414988b\nparent 9fd0ea18f112f9908d7d70f363c9d19383740b01\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1790519399 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790519399 -0400\n\nmisc: name the running command in the .each() and .spread() mixed async/sync error and type .each()''s third argument as the jQuery collection (#34933)\n\n* misc: name the running command in the .each() and .spread() mixed async/sync error and type .each()''s third argument as the jQuery collection\n\nThe callback_mixes_sync_and_async error raised from thenFn always named\ncy.then(), even when .each() or .spread() ran the callback. It now takes\nthe current command''s name, following invoke_its.timed_out, and links to\nthat command''s docs.\n\nThe DOM overloads of .each() typed the callback''s third argument as E[],\nbut the driver passes the original subject, which for DOM subjects is the\njQuery collection. They now type it as JQuery<E>. The non-DOM overloads''\n$list widens from any[] to any: TypeScript fixes an unannotated callback\nparameter to the first overload''s type, so with any[] a partly annotated\ncallback like (num: number, i, array) => {} no longer matched either\noverload.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012aPnumJCuSNjueeLCrT48L\n\n* docs: file type corrections and error wording changes under Misc in the changelog\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012aPnumJCuSNjueeLCrT48L\n\n* docs: tighten the .each() changelog entry and the Misc section description\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012aPnumJCuSNjueeLCrT48L\n\n* misc: link the .each() changelog entries to #34933\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012aPnumJCuSNjueeLCrT48L\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquShnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXBwQAEv/50s4ERcMImp8M47dQWTM\nGZ6HX9SV25+GN2p3TLppsF4Ogr92/+RP7meziIKsDNdkxIkW7UnsDd5pw4xvwKSM\n+jaPtarbb6kf+/jgfxZ6aGgN+qSMoCXEUUAvDjWBVWE/GEdVIffg4I7AKevpJAps\n2VvfTk76FS/IjkElpMtvH1F2joPBHo2vdNf5IZl09AtuwtxIv8IdthBu+vIjIAUK\nDOyMpME/yY3VUyPs6IdhkxdszD9NX41jaTrxY+7TJTfJsxRo81vOCshWXSlW+4Ok\nqpjh0EUvxA0wDTceCfzzF25RCgUj5zQfrAel9AOJsHyd3watoqQ233zIvOhDSMzo\nTwukObx4CreUh2tXmNlNqegbXZFQKTBYCaogBHadS46qHmQNotX04oRvqFAUcz5E\nODgynq9z+ia8FM1ZYc+Rk/mD90en/p7DpRDkFFeE+Reo7VEBK8Clkhx4S8XWykQM\npR2vOjJQ5om0AysfQH5KHPC+HDRLVUm7L0fvXT9g83m7bw1rTHI4d/x9tZ6DGEzc\nc1+Duo9H/0ddJDfqqOivjzJgTeq8e84HoRs2H/POErlWDFFE2gOisS7wKVcq1jU8\nRBKcM0o+5rxHNe5C7mHz5roIRHg/3/3Yfd0pXRTpwbFj40qT2czguc3odHoHs6G1\nKr2Iq8aZyGL/7TWqK/6w\n=cwlM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T14:30:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/764fa3dad1e5d8b449a70601a558758cf54d4839","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDc2NGZhM2RhZDFlNWQ4YjQ0OWE3MDYwMWE1NTg3NThjZjU0ZDQ4Mzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/9fd0ea18f112f9908d7d70f363c9d19383740b01","sha":"9fd0ea18f112f9908d7d70f363c9d19383740b01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/9fd0ea18f112f9908d7d70f363c9d19383740b01"}],"sha":"764fa3dad1e5d8b449a70601a558758cf54d4839","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/764fa3dad1e5d8b449a70601a558758cf54d4839"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/9fd0ea18f112f9908d7d70f363c9d19383740b01/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T10:54:13Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":1,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T10:54:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"misc: show the injectDocumentDomain hint in the cross-origin command error (#34930)\n\n* fix: show injectDocumentDomain hint in cross-origin command error\n\nThe cross_origin_command template read `isSkipDomainInjectionEnabled`,\na leftover from experimentalSkipDomainInjection, while its only caller\npasses `isInjectDocumentDomainEnabled`, so the hint never rendered.\n\nRead the name the caller passes and invert the condition to match the\nflag''s meaning: with injectDocumentDomain disabled (the default), every\norigin change, including a subdomain of the same domain, requires\ncy.origin(). With it enabled, this error only fires for a different\nsuperdomain, where the existing cy.origin() guidance already applies.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PRfrgLqjwx49v7JiyGGZ6q\n\n* misc: move cross-origin hint changelog entry to Misc\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PRfrgLqjwx49v7JiyGGZ6q\n\n* misc: stop cross-origin hint from repeating the cy.origin() advice\n\nThe injectDocumentDomain hint now explains why a subdomain counts as a\ndifferent origin, and leaves the fix to the cy.origin() line after it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PRfrgLqjwx49v7JiyGGZ6q\n\n* misc: shorten cy.origin() advice in cross-origin command error\n\n\"Using cy.origin() to wrap the commands run on X will likely fix this\nissue.\" becomes \"Use cy.origin() to wrap the commands run on X.\"\n\nUpdate the web_security system-test snapshot for this line and for the\ninjectDocumentDomain hint, which now renders when the flag is disabled.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PRfrgLqjwx49v7JiyGGZ6q\n\n* misc: show injectDocumentDomain hint only for same-superdomain origins\n\nThe hint explains that a subdomain counts as a different origin, which\nonly helps when the spec and the application share a superdomain. For a\nmove to an unrelated domain it was true but beside the point, so it now\nrenders only when both origins share a superdomain origin, the boundary\ninjectDocumentDomain uses. An opaque ''null'' origin never shows it.\n\nCover the new condition in the ensure unit spec, along with the branch\nthat appends the message to an existing error. The web_security snapshot\ncrosses superdomains, so it no longer includes the hint.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PRfrgLqjwx49v7JiyGGZ6q\n\n* misc: keep commandCanCommunicateWithAUT doc comment above its function\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PRfrgLqjwx49v7JiyGGZ6q\n\n* misc: link the changelog entry to #34930\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PRfrgLqjwx49v7JiyGGZ6q\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"303b3b0146bc8deed1a7ca0b634b95ee25b4f131","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/303b3b0146bc8deed1a7ca0b634b95ee25b4f131"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/9fd0ea18f112f9908d7d70f363c9d19383740b01","verification":{"payload":"tree 303b3b0146bc8deed1a7ca0b634b95ee25b4f131\nparent 21122f50f1377b3e7a7dce8de59018da82aaa807\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1790506453 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790506453 -0400\n\nmisc: show the injectDocumentDomain hint in the cross-origin command error (#34930)\n\n* fix: show injectDocumentDomain hint in cross-origin command error\n\nThe cross_origin_command template read `isSkipDomainInjectionEnabled`,\na leftover from experimentalSkipDomainInjection, while its only caller\npasses `isInjectDocumentDomainEnabled`, so the hint never rendered.\n\nRead the name the caller passes and invert the condition to match the\nflag''s meaning: with injectDocumentDomain disabled (the default), every\norigin change, including a subdomain of the same domain, requires\ncy.origin(). With it enabled, this error only fires for a different\nsuperdomain, where the existing cy.origin() guidance already applies.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PRfrgLqjwx49v7JiyGGZ6q\n\n* misc: move cross-origin hint changelog entry to Misc\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PRfrgLqjwx49v7JiyGGZ6q\n\n* misc: stop cross-origin hint from repeating the cy.origin() advice\n\nThe injectDocumentDomain hint now explains why a subdomain counts as a\ndifferent origin, and leaves the fix to the cy.origin() line after it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PRfrgLqjwx49v7JiyGGZ6q\n\n* misc: shorten cy.origin() advice in cross-origin command error\n\n\"Using cy.origin() to wrap the commands run on X will likely fix this\nissue.\" becomes \"Use cy.origin() to wrap the commands run on X.\"\n\nUpdate the web_security system-test snapshot for this line and for the\ninjectDocumentDomain hint, which now renders when the flag is disabled.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PRfrgLqjwx49v7JiyGGZ6q\n\n* misc: show injectDocumentDomain hint only for same-superdomain origins\n\nThe hint explains that a subdomain counts as a different origin, which\nonly helps when the spec and the application share a superdomain. For a\nmove to an unrelated domain it was true but beside the point, so it now\nrenders only when both origins share a superdomain origin, the boundary\ninjectDocumentDomain uses. An opaque ''null'' origin never shows it.\n\nCover the new condition in the ensure unit spec, along with the branch\nthat appends the message to an existing error. The web_security snapshot\ncrosses superdomains, so it no longer includes the hint.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PRfrgLqjwx49v7JiyGGZ6q\n\n* misc: keep commandCanCommunicateWithAUT doc comment above its function\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PRfrgLqjwx49v7JiyGGZ6q\n\n* misc: link the changelog entry to #34930\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PRfrgLqjwx49v7JiyGGZ6q\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquPXVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAt5AQAB6uaAAfb7M1WWLJ8+ailiGd\nosum5x0aly/Y4/261DUYJeuvSaqeHndd7qIDsBB6uyuvrXQLVWgM5YekqHwJrvQT\nySVTqBL/LMea/LP1afW3ew8OuJbFx5t3g8fqsW/6dvIoTExZyatHUMy382L8qOQe\nGgkB36XzIKOO4fwBbZ+Wo+hSjArnwNPJXrZ+TC+SQVIS3F//US36ZdJi2zLObF+T\naOAAyqeX/6PgW4