","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/acdc34668084434e4178ccfac3e347f3b6ca09fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T16:51:10Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":1,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T16:51:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: convert the driver''s service worker spec to TypeScript (#34916)\n\n* test: convert the driver''s service worker spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `service-worker.cy.js` to `.ts` and resolve the type errors the rename\nsurfaces:\n\n- Type `self` as the service worker''s global scope inside the scripts the\n  spec stringifies and serves as the worker. The webworker lib conflicts with\n  the dom lib program-wide, so the members the scripts use are declared\n  structurally, as `@packages/proxy`''s service worker injector does. Listeners\n  also accept `undefined`, which the tests register and remove on purpose.\n- Assert the empty listener object in the delayed `handleEvent` test gains\n  its `handleEvent` after registration.\n- Type `validateFetchHandlers`'' options, making `onFetchHandlerType` optional.\n- State what `cy.wrap` yields for `getRegistrations()`, since it cannot infer\n  a promise''s resolved type.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BZRZVGYx58nQJSksojWa1X\n\n* test: tighten the service worker spec''s type comments\n\nDrop the pointer to the proxy''s injector, which explains nothing and can go\nstale, and move the note on accepting `undefined` next to the listener type it\ndescribes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BZRZVGYx58nQJSksojWa1X\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1dd20cc09227a335596a6757e62d1fa1e9507bbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/1dd20cc09227a335596a6757e62d1fa1e9507bbd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/acdc34668084434e4178ccfac3e347f3b6ca09fc","verification":{"payload":"tree 1dd20cc09227a335596a6757e62d1fa1e9507bbd\nparent d421e5ec6a3e6f73f7af3e7205e813bea33434ef\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1790268670 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790268670 -0400\n\ntest: convert the driver''s service worker spec to TypeScript (#34916)\n\n* test: convert the driver''s service worker spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `service-worker.cy.js` to `.ts` and resolve the type errors the rename\nsurfaces:\n\n- Type `self` as the service worker''s global scope inside the scripts the\n  spec stringifies and serves as the worker. The webworker lib conflicts with\n  the dom lib program-wide, so the members the scripts use are declared\n  structurally, as `@packages/proxy`''s service worker injector does. Listeners\n  also accept `undefined`, which the tests register and remove on purpose.\n- Assert the empty listener object in the delayed `handleEvent` test gains\n  its `handleEvent` after registration.\n- Type `validateFetchHandlers`'' options, making `onFetchHandlerType` optional.\n- State what `cy.wrap` yields for `getRegistrations()`, since it cannot infer\n  a promise''s resolved type.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BZRZVGYx58nQJSksojWa1X\n\n* test: tighten the service worker spec''s type comments\n\nDrop the pointer to the proxy''s injector, which explains nothing and can go\nstale, and move the note on accepting `undefined` next to the listener type it\ndescribes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BZRZVGYx58nQJSksojWa1X\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtVT+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+DYQAKx0L2C/Px/XOnJGx6T+4Eqs\n3/mAs2PGvAnRf/EIsIxOu2rMjWbu4o0bf1hVkHktoF4EBajhlsUvQF0yd2UmQYmG\nniAOg26ggehCrC3fNHA/JOeLUDZXzDhrvaJCfwZocPNc1I8GeTzZl/yWIAavXqEF\nF6LRmtOP5AW6pUHagz4dK1EQM9MXWoiTGyMMA9zplYPFqDiYjtwxqpNYbvvkCs0o\nT+EHQG+hw5uQ232ceKATUuoM3ZOlmMt1nuN6mamjxnr8xSMMi+jQHJ2X+OTyBnXC\nNqNYNAnc1cgAL2EOHnoCDUJEs6L5I3WhvX6D8ZuO0WbbYZ8Gy8rNAViAMYYK8McG\n86Dvlw5f7re7lUBccfTVV3yRMRqzcbuAb5qhGXz/XPHu4CQR829EoEdkPULKrJEd\nHa7nEcSppDdNcVoSv6hco/ysBa0rSKTzbNeC/m+GJ74tUB6fgdDT2r5Rp6ZOI0bG\nPeSppCAExMuH7CaziyvK86J+sACPaJ+edSvDUiANTZbaDTPvT8P0k8C8UFnBd89q\nn5jXMD9bQnrssmC/4zZBbny/9VqV0y7D1UWjEZelKxzhNBSf7djPQwyV+uVyxOCx\nxpAuhUIEpgGEhrXMXUnLB1JFNlzWvadBCKZDa7/zJRaU9svWGjsGEjs8mZKZ+vjk\ngekyNs0vxY0hXS55tRBK\n=ZBfO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T16:51:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/acdc34668084434e4178ccfac3e347f3b6ca09fc","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKGFjZGMzNDY2ODA4NDQzNGU0MTc4Y2NmYWMzZTM0N2YzYjZjYTA5ZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/d421e5ec6a3e6f73f7af3e7205e813bea33434ef","sha":"d421e5ec6a3e6f73f7af3e7205e813bea33434ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/d421e5ec6a3e6f73f7af3e7205e813bea33434ef"}],"sha":"acdc34668084434e4178ccfac3e347f3b6ca09fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/acdc34668084434e4178ccfac3e347f3b6ca09fc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/d421e5ec6a3e6f73f7af3e7205e813bea33434ef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T16:49:36Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":1,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T16:49:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: convert the driver''s screenshot, stack_utils and utils specs to TypeScript (#34913)\n\n* test: convert the driver''s screenshot spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `screenshot.cy.js` to `.ts` and resolve the type errors the rename\nsurfaces:\n\n- Add `InternalScreenshot` alongside `InternalKeyboard` and cast the singleton to\n  it. The published `Cypress.Screenshot` type carries only the documented\n  `defaults()`, so `reset()`, `getConfig()` and the two callbacks have no\n  declared surface. `commands/screenshot.cy.js` stubs three of those, so it has\n  this waiting when it converts. `export {}` keeps the spec''s `DEFAULTS` out of\n  the global scope `keyboard.cy.ts` declares one in.\n- Hand the callbacks the element they forward rather than calling them bare. No\n  assertion reads it, but the driver passes one and the signature says so.\n- Mark the call that omits a required argument on purpose, as `keyboard.cy.ts`\n  does for the same test.\n\nThe `clip` and `padding` tests turn up a type the module had wrong. `_reset()`\nreturns a `Pick` of the eight options it restores, while `defaults()` extends\nthat same object with `clip` and `padding`, so `getConfig()` has been handing\nback two options its type denies. Name the shape and make those two optional\nmembers of it, rather than widening the config at the reads in the spec.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NBFkuw6KWcTCY6ELt12YyB\n\n* test: convert the driver''s stack_utils spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `stack_utils.cy.js` to `.ts` and resolve the type errors the rename\nsurfaces:\n\n- `require` the spec''s two dependencies as `import`s, and hold the stubbed\n  `getSourcePosition` in a typed binding, since `onCall` is on the stub rather\n  than on the function it replaces.\n- Route the `platform` and `repoRoot` writes through a helper. `Cypress.config()`''s\n  setter overload takes only the keys in `TestConfigOverrides`, and these are\n  runtime values the source reads.\n- Name the shape `getSourceStack` returns for a real stack. It answers a bare `{}`\n  when handed none, and the inferred union hides the results from every other call.\n- Assert the details `getSourceDetailsForFirstLine` yields where the test then\n  reads a property off them.\n\n`getCodeFrame` and `getSourceStack` both handle a missing second and first\nargument respectively, so mark those parameters optional rather than have the\ncallers that rely on it pass `undefined` explicitly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NBFkuw6KWcTCY6ELt12YyB\n\n* test: convert the driver''s utils spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `utils.cy.js` to `.ts` and resolve the type errors the rename surfaces:\n\n- `require` `LimitedMap` as an `import`, and type `Cypress.utils` off the driver''s\n  own `utils` module. The `CypressUtils` declaration lists only the handful of\n  helpers other packages reach for, while this spec covers the whole module.\n- Annotate the fixtures the stringify tests then point back at themselves. An\n  inferred `{}` or `never[]` has nowhere to hang the circular reference the test\n  is about.\n- Give `reduceProps` its own binding rather than reassigning the object it\n  reduces, which the narrower input type no longer accepts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NBFkuw6KWcTCY6ELt12YyB\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c7e6bbcfafb68d03cec852ee1357338a914dc1fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/c7e6bbcfafb68d03cec852ee1357338a914dc1fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/d421e5ec6a3e6f73f7af3e7205e813bea33434ef","verification":{"payload":"tree c7e6bbcfafb68d03cec852ee1357338a914dc1fe\nparent 6b991996b73e9e8b09e05e97bc319c331c34ad38\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1790268576 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790268576 -0400\n\ntest: convert the driver''s screenshot, stack_utils and utils specs to TypeScript (#34913)\n\n* test: convert the driver''s screenshot spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `screenshot.cy.js` to `.ts` and resolve the type errors the rename\nsurfaces:\n\n- Add `InternalScreenshot` alongside `InternalKeyboard` and cast the singleton to\n  it. The published `Cypress.Screenshot` type carries only the documented\n  `defaults()`, so `reset()`, `getConfig()` and the two callbacks have no\n  declared surface. `commands/screenshot.cy.js` stubs three of those, so it has\n  this waiting when it converts. `export {}` keeps the spec''s `DEFAULTS` out of\n  the global scope `keyboard.cy.ts` declares one in.\n- Hand the callbacks the element they forward rather than calling them bare. No\n  assertion reads it, but the driver passes one and the signature says so.\n- Mark the call that omits a required argument on purpose, as `keyboard.cy.ts`\n  does for the same test.\n\nThe `clip` and `padding` tests turn up a type the module had wrong. `_reset()`\nreturns a `Pick` of the eight options it restores, while `defaults()` extends\nthat same object with `clip` and `padding`, so `getConfig()` has been handing\nback two options its type denies. Name the shape and make those two optional\nmembers of it, rather than widening the config at the reads in the spec.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NBFkuw6KWcTCY6ELt12YyB\n\n* test: convert the driver''s stack_utils spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `stack_utils.cy.js` to `.ts` and resolve the type errors the rename\nsurfaces:\n\n- `require` the spec''s two dependencies as `import`s, and hold the stubbed\n  `getSourcePosition` in a typed binding, since `onCall` is on the stub rather\n  than on the function it replaces.\n- Route the `platform` and `repoRoot` writes through a helper. `Cypress.config()`''s\n  setter overload takes only the keys in `TestConfigOverrides`, and these are\n  runtime values the source reads.\n- Name the shape `getSourceStack` returns for a real stack. It answers a bare `{}`\n  when handed none, and the inferred union hides the results from every other call.\n- Assert the details `getSourceDetailsForFirstLine` yields where the test then\n  reads a property off them.\n\n`getCodeFrame` and `getSourceStack` both handle a missing second and first\nargument respectively, so mark those parameters optional rather than have the\ncallers that rely on it pass `undefined` explicitly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NBFkuw6KWcTCY6ELt12YyB\n\n* test: convert the driver''s utils spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `utils.cy.js` to `.ts` and resolve the type errors the rename surfaces:\n\n- `require` `LimitedMap` as an `import`, and type `Cypress.utils` off the driver''s\n  own `utils` module. The `CypressUtils` declaration lists only the handful of\n  helpers other packages reach for, while this spec covers the whole module.\n- Annotate the fixtures the stringify tests then point back at themselves. An\n  inferred `{}` or `never[]` has nowhere to hang the circular reference the test\n  is about.\n- Give `reduceProps` its own binding rather than reassigning the object it\n  reduces, which the narrower input type no longer accepts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NBFkuw6KWcTCY6ELt12YyB\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtVSgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHJoQABUbJxB+9ZT9utDe3+i+qGW2\n5NXzqvRJEatPBS9kNRxcus8hcCsMou9woEt3TwaoM2Q7vid0NYlUynBeVsyEfm8Z\nbXfDz1PPJa3KDTUNbggQae191Y5Ox4sL6pSqmDSLEiqEsuH8p11lnTElpe7NYgsm\nGCYpcNU+EdhTbQPTbk3b+r7yy8Wp3GOUtNHKFiSLaUsxLe4OJEx6FhF5qXYojvsA\nWTcnPDn6jTS54QfouQlb4tqPS8D4yw0XnanyJtU5lff+Zej86YXysL4yAPVqhEN7\n99frU3QHMZL1B3KWiDzUI8A1LwmdAtldA8w9Rp7V1Gw4aIHR0bY8p/MfI4wqGwkh\nAzuiVOBI3XTecE+vDKjpDmumKsFxXCZkWdpeONmurSkKDFFOIm0SKH99TkouYwHP\nITZwT0MdhISWzI73IdCRU+iBXhnfjphOhvpZIA4ASamYUaLh3yEUm65zsKFghs94\n5IC9LTuvQgGCBT1ZWzSPCzwVVzls0NjvZM/63/gDBTj1pKWUx3BOamjWHaiEbg5Z\n4rITTYfNLdAIr5IoAoUfFcSn17fL8XR4G5UhCox0X3/brKGJidnNx4c8IzjbyHVy\niKeCwLy7jtrmALTmJmKca1Tzr8tjP1TmTvpMU4oF+CQ15Ii237GJrn831LU3tHPJ\nXeU96l3fsSFzzkV1OVp4\n=2u1t\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T16:49:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/d421e5ec6a3e6f73f7af3e7205e813bea33434ef","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKGQ0MjFlNWVjNmEzZTZmNzNmN2FmM2U3MjA1ZTgxM2JlYTMzNDM0ZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/6b991996b73e9e8b09e05e97bc319c331c34ad38","sha":"6b991996b73e9e8b09e05e97bc319c331c34ad38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/6b991996b73e9e8b09e05e97bc319c331c34ad38"}],"sha":"d421e5ec6a3e6f73f7af3e7205e813bea33434ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/d421e5ec6a3e6f73f7af3e7205e813bea33434ef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/6b991996b73e9e8b09e05e97bc319c331c34ad38/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T16:48:01Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":1,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T16:48:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: split the driver''s assertions spec into smaller files (#34909)\n\n* test: split the driver''s assertions spec into a directory\n\n`assertions.cy.js` had grown to 3,289 lines and 204 tests in a single file.\nSplit it into `commands/assertions/`, matching the existing `commands/actions/`\nand `commands/querying/` layout.\n\nThe three `chai plugins` files follow the grouping the implementation already\nuses: `packages/driver/src/cypress/assertions/assert.ts` splits these\nassertions into `selectors` (generated by one `_.each` loop in\n`chai_jquery.ts`), `accessors` (generated by a second loop), and the\nindividually defined methods. Each spec file now mirrors one code path.\n\nTest bodies are moved verbatim and the `describe`/`context` titles are\nunchanged, so every test keeps its full title. The per-context `log:added`\nhooks stay duplicated rather than shared — the four variants differ in\nwhether and when they set `lastLog`, and unifying them would change behavior.\n\n`captureCommands` is only read by `#should` and `implicit assertions`, which\nland in the same file, so it stays local there; the other files need only the\nfixture visit.\n\nVerified: 204 passing before and after, with the same per-file counts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E53GVgCzTefzZZb22GQS4S\n\n* test: collapse the non-DOM assertion tests into a fixture table\n\nSeventeen `throws when obj is not DOM` tests, one per chai-jQuery assertion,\nrepeated the same body with only the assertion, the subject and the expected\nerror fragments varying.\n\nThey all exercise a single code path: the guard in `assertDom`\n(packages/driver/src/cypress/assertions/assert.ts) that fails an assertion\nhanded a non-DOM subject and reports the method and subject it saw. Move them\ninto `chai_jquery_non_dom.cy.js` as one row per assertion, so the file mirrors\nthat guard the way the other plugin specs mirror theirs.\n\nEach row keeps what its original asserted, including the two that differ: the\n`data` message is checked only for presence, and `focused` matches a substring.\nTest count is unchanged at 204; the titles now name the assertion, so a failure\nreads `throws when obj is not DOM: prop` rather than one of seventeen\nidentically named tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E53GVgCzTefzZZb22GQS4S\n\n* test: tighten the comments in the non-DOM assertion table\n\nDrop the sentence restating what the table itself shows, and reword the note on\nthe one row that leaves its message unasserted so it explains the choice rather\nthan the mechanism.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E53GVgCzTefzZZb22GQS4S\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f416f38749a10c5053d8630a647fa6d1cfed4dd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/f416f38749a10c5053d8630a647fa6d1cfed4dd1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/6b991996b73e9e8b09e05e97bc319c331c34ad38","verification":{"payload":"tree f416f38749a10c5053d8630a647fa6d1cfed4dd1\nparent b84ed71d639ca3abb643c5128f38125a1deb57d1\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1790268481 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790268481 -0400\n\ntest: split the driver''s assertions spec into smaller files (#34909)\n\n* test: split the driver''s assertions spec into a directory\n\n`assertions.cy.js` had grown to 3,289 lines and 204 tests in a single file.\nSplit it into `commands/assertions/`, matching the existing `commands/actions/`\nand `commands/querying/` layout.\n\nThe three `chai plugins` files follow the grouping the implementation already\nuses: `packages/driver/src/cypress/assertions/assert.ts` splits these\nassertions into `selectors` (generated by one `_.each` loop in\n`chai_jquery.ts`), `accessors` (generated by a second loop), and the\nindividually defined methods. Each spec file now mirrors one code path.\n\nTest bodies are moved verbatim and the `describe`/`context` titles are\nunchanged, so every test keeps its full title. The per-context `log:added`\nhooks stay duplicated rather than shared — the four variants differ in\nwhether and when they set `lastLog`, and unifying them would change behavior.\n\n`captureCommands` is only read by `#should` and `implicit assertions`, which\nland in the same file, so it stays local there; the other files need only the\nfixture visit.\n\nVerified: 204 passing before and after, with the same per-file counts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E53GVgCzTefzZZb22GQS4S\n\n* test: collapse the non-DOM assertion tests into a fixture table\n\nSeventeen `throws when obj is not DOM` tests, one per chai-jQuery assertion,\nrepeated the same body with only the assertion, the subject and the expected\nerror fragments varying.\n\nThey all exercise a single code path: the guard in `assertDom`\n(packages/driver/src/cypress/assertions/assert.ts) that fails an assertion\nhanded a non-DOM subject and reports the method and subject it saw. Move them\ninto `chai_jquery_non_dom.cy.js` as one row per assertion, so the file mirrors\nthat guard the way the other plugin specs mirror theirs.\n\nEach row keeps what its original asserted, including the two that differ: the\n`data` message is checked only for presence, and `focused` matches a substring.\nTest count is unchanged at 204; the titles now name the assertion, so a failure\nreads `throws when obj is not DOM: prop` rather than one of seventeen\nidentically named tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E53GVgCzTefzZZb22GQS4S\n\n* test: tighten the comments in the non-DOM assertion table\n\nDrop the sentence restating what the table itself shows, and reword the note on\nthe one row that leaves its message unasserted so it explains the choice rather\nthan the mechanism.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E53GVgCzTefzZZb22GQS4S\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtVRBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAW8QQAI7yPJYZA1w3kL+3YRkZPu5N\ne8xU1VPSSMiAqw2zQKqDOPcn/EK+fZT0qX6dryRaLKM/TwkU5Z9RAAWCWBPa/7cH\ny5j9/DeLPs7jTEXKT+LgnDeZSPrifbQYqN6C/cfjY5wB2V/2vN1VTRhjH4BYJQsS\ng195CDgp5MLpimjF+OB5hKIadLw9XZMSmxrJR/Tc7Vm3Sr2DBY3SS2pBrjmvYRkQ\nzl+DeJS2gGOZEwH4G+JZZsk63cx/4ivrLNDzg55JRvrDHMZNoWmW2maB/xXa/vRJ\nycQmPScks5CQNquH6TrUTq6hIz2tJWvZSEx7+JXt5bldP5tYKKMjQCpO8HXCvyzt\nSy602HJhHdM6VhIgnmzj9fNfPs8wmDemZaFZAus0MzZb0XEDvv2hswOK6Vgo1fnu\nC7cWLoHstOGghsPgm7sl0JYm8Jf//CL/qEVaP9AWxW6/3xmgr0oDTbTbHSeGpQoK\ntzT/eXv27w1NxDV3qgeQqAm//fLOGxzjz9xrJdU6me7D2i5jREMZDQxewwgMtp53\n6ZzKmHciFPSOZjyy7GSPJnbhSbdRQVPFk6VITVNXtcHV8TYPP5fmRlrhhMTut9fq\nUIEI6R7zdh8VWaKzbvxuNLOmxCflc5hqHzLVI4YER05jnxIOy/QSbSiDNO4O9cgv\npVd85QAtFui/kd4Vu5Zv\n=HXFS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T16:48:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/6b991996b73e9e8b09e05e97bc319c331c34ad38","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDZiOTkxOTk2YjczZTllOGIwOWUwNWU5N2JjMzE5YzMzMWMzNGFkMzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/b84ed71d639ca3abb643c5128f38125a1deb57d1","sha":"b84ed71d639ca3abb643c5128f38125a1deb57d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/b84ed71d639ca3abb643c5128f38125a1deb57d1"}],"sha":"6b991996b73e9e8b09e05e97bc319c331c34ad38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/6b991996b73e9e8b09e05e97bc319c331c34ad38"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/b84ed71d639ca3abb643c5128f38125a1deb57d1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T16:46:35Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":1,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T16:46:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"misc: accept every cy.clock() function name and a null now in types (#34912)\n\n* misc: accept every cy.clock() function name and a null now in types\n\ncy.clock() forwards its function list to @sinonjs/fake-timers as `toFake`,\nso any function the clock fakes in the browser is valid at runtime, but the\ntypes allowed only five names. The documented `cy.clock(null, [...])` form\nalso failed under strictNullChecks even though null starts the clock at 0.\n\n- Add a named Cypress.ClockFunction union covering every function cy.clock()\n  can override in the browser, and use it for the `functions` argument\n- Allow `null` for `now` in the overload that takes `functions`\n- Type Clock.tick() as returning the new `now` (fake-timers returns it)\n- List every default-faked function in the cy.clock() JSDoc\n- Add dtslint cases for the new names, null, tick''s return type, and\n  negative cases for Node-only and unknown names\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LSepHm8AesCf9Q6wqdxgAx\n\n* misc: accept queueMicrotask in cy.clock() function types\n\nfake-timers fakes queueMicrotask when it is named explicitly; Cypress only\nleaves it out of the default list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LSepHm8AesCf9Q6wqdxgAx\n\n* misc: link cy.clock() changelog entry to #34912\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LSepHm8AesCf9Q6wqdxgAx\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fb3677555e1bd856fe4e29bd3de84b13d70babe8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/fb3677555e1bd856fe4e29bd3de84b13d70babe8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/b84ed71d639ca3abb643c5128f38125a1deb57d1","verification":{"payload":"tree fb3677555e1bd856fe4e29bd3de84b13d70babe8\nparent 27dbdcaff924d11a57675cdc752f3b17fc0d5b45\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1790268395 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790268395 -0400\n\nmisc: accept every cy.clock() function name and a null now in types (#34912)\n\n* misc: accept every cy.clock() function name and a null now in types\n\ncy.clock() forwards its function list to @sinonjs/fake-timers as `toFake`,\nso any function the clock fakes in the browser is valid at runtime, but the\ntypes allowed only five names. The documented `cy.clock(null, [...])` form\nalso failed under strictNullChecks even though null starts the clock at 0.\n\n- Add a named Cypress.ClockFunction union covering every function cy.clock()\n  can override in the browser, and use it for the `functions` argument\n- Allow `null` for `now` in the overload that takes `functions`\n- Type Clock.tick() as returning the new `now` (fake-timers returns it)\n- List every default-faked function in the cy.clock() JSDoc\n- Add dtslint cases for the new names, null, tick''s return type, and\n  negative cases for Node-only and unknown names\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LSepHm8AesCf9Q6wqdxgAx\n\n* misc: accept queueMicrotask in cy.clock() function types\n\nfake-timers fakes queueMicrotask when it is named explicitly; Cypress only\nleaves it out of the default list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LSepHm8AesCf9Q6wqdxgAx\n\n* misc: link cy.clock() changelog entry to #34912\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LSepHm8AesCf9Q6wqdxgAx\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtVPrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOtEQAHW+R+GdQ9LpNT09Pkcq3E8j\nJLqVGO5DLSlBLVluqjy+2Hcb5jNa5j1X/8ByO24P1jSss7eKhpbk