":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/a6a04edd9621c6c66807ae9740e0c1dccd2ac494/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T14:41:44Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":2,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T14:41:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: convert three driver specs to TypeScript (#34900)\n\n* test: convert the driver''s mocha custom methods spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `mocha_custom_methods.cy.js` to `.ts` and resolve the type errors the\nrename surfaces:\n\n- Drop the `.ts` extension from the `mocha` import. TypeScript rejects it\n  without `allowImportingTsExtensions`, and the spec''s sibling specs already\n  import driver source extensionless.\n- Type the mock test factory. `calculateTestStatus` takes a Mocha test carrying\n  Cypress'' retry bookkeeping, a type internal to `mocha.ts`, so read it back off\n  the function signature rather than widening the source''s exports. The mock\n  stubs only the members the function reads, so it needs asserting.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0111VkTEPJifr5E8nRczSBtm\n\n* test: convert the driver''s config util spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `config.cy.js` to `.ts` and resolve the type errors the rename surfaces:\n\n`validateConfig` takes a `StateFunc`, but `$SetterGetter.create` is untyped, so\nthe setter/getter it returns does not structurally satisfy that interface''s\noverloads. Wrap the factory once so the assertion is stated in a single place\nrather than at each of the twenty call sites.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0111VkTEPJifr5E8nRczSBtm\n\n* test: convert the driver''s test config overrides spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `testConfigOverrides.cy.js` to `.ts` and resolve the type errors the\nrename surfaces:\n\n- Read user-defined config values through an untyped view of `Cypress.config()`.\n  Cypress resolves those values alongside its own, but `Cypress.Config` and\n  `SuiteConfigOverrides` enumerate only the options Cypress owns, so the suites\n  setting `foo`/`bar`/`baz` need their overrides asserting too.\n- Mark the three `Cypress.config()` calls the suite expects to fail as\n  `@ts-expect-error`. `chromeWebSecurity` is read-only, `env` was removed in\n  Cypress 16, and `foo` is user-defined, so none appears in\n  `TestConfigOverrides` — the types reject exactly what the tests assert throws.\n- Reach Mocha''s `_onlySuites`/`_onlyTests` by element access, since its types\n  declare them private, and accept that `currentTest` is optional.\n- Assert `window.top` is present, matching `cypress/support/defaults.ts`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0111VkTEPJifr5E8nRczSBtm\n\n* test: describe the config override type errors in the present tense\n\nState once, above the suite, why the calls it expects to reject do not type-check,\nrather than repeating a variation of it at each of the three `@ts-expect-error`\ndirectives.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0111VkTEPJifr5E8nRczSBtm\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"661ab5f48a42c89f5abfb3afad7bbb05fcf1194d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/661ab5f48a42c89f5abfb3afad7bbb05fcf1194d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/a6a04edd9621c6c66807ae9740e0c1dccd2ac494","verification":{"payload":"tree 661ab5f48a42c89f5abfb3afad7bbb05fcf1194d\nparent 0e3f5a2cbd3ea0bcdaaa28d31b8b1ca5c11f3daa\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1790174504 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790174504 -0400\n\ntest: convert three driver specs to TypeScript (#34900)\n\n* test: convert the driver''s mocha custom methods spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `mocha_custom_methods.cy.js` to `.ts` and resolve the type errors the\nrename surfaces:\n\n- Drop the `.ts` extension from the `mocha` import. TypeScript rejects it\n  without `allowImportingTsExtensions`, and the spec''s sibling specs already\n  import driver source extensionless.\n- Type the mock test factory. `calculateTestStatus` takes a Mocha test carrying\n  Cypress'' retry bookkeeping, a type internal to `mocha.ts`, so read it back off\n  the function signature rather than widening the source''s exports. The mock\n  stubs only the members the function reads, so it needs asserting.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0111VkTEPJifr5E8nRczSBtm\n\n* test: convert the driver''s config util spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `config.cy.js` to `.ts` and resolve the type errors the rename surfaces:\n\n`validateConfig` takes a `StateFunc`, but `$SetterGetter.create` is untyped, so\nthe setter/getter it returns does not structurally satisfy that interface''s\noverloads. Wrap the factory once so the assertion is stated in a single place\nrather than at each of the twenty call sites.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0111VkTEPJifr5E8nRczSBtm\n\n* test: convert the driver''s test config overrides spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `testConfigOverrides.cy.js` to `.ts` and resolve the type errors the\nrename surfaces:\n\n- Read user-defined config values through an untyped view of `Cypress.config()`.\n  Cypress resolves those values alongside its own, but `Cypress.Config` and\n  `SuiteConfigOverrides` enumerate only the options Cypress owns, so the suites\n  setting `foo`/`bar`/`baz` need their overrides asserting too.\n- Mark the three `Cypress.config()` calls the suite expects to fail as\n  `@ts-expect-error`. `chromeWebSecurity` is read-only, `env` was removed in\n  Cypress 16, and `foo` is user-defined, so none appears in\n  `TestConfigOverrides` — the types reject exactly what the tests assert throws.\n- Reach Mocha''s `_onlySuites`/`_onlyTests` by element access, since its types\n  declare them private, and accept that `currentTest` is optional.\n- Assert `window.top` is present, matching `cypress/support/defaults.ts`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0111VkTEPJifr5E8nRczSBtm\n\n* test: describe the config override type errors in the present tense\n\nState once, above the suite, why the calls it expects to reject do not type-check,\nrather than repeating a variation of it at each of the three `@ts-expect-error`\ndirectives.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0111VkTEPJifr5E8nRczSBtm\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs+UoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5l0QAKNg8kG7dInCZ4Le7e92Z4wp\nkv8Ma58L/lrlZu+5qEXAZNIYg3Bzo4M/OBXZ65f4ZDPvbG+hlTMO6EyihTM0wgt1\nqc+cahOlFH5S5GOvS26lZu2qc7ufpehDhk08zjxaHO09MlmGt7UVdiUEnsVy5DND\nAFpho0