271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/f80f791c26a14fcf57fa9fd2314ceda3569d02b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T02:45:51Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":1,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T02:45:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: remove dead code from @packages/web-config (#34723)\n\nThe package accumulated unreferenced files, a webpack rule that never\nmatched, and devDependencies with no consumer. Its only consumers are\npackages/reporter and packages/runner, both of which use only\ngetCommonConfig, getSimpleConfig, HtmlWebpackPlugin,\ngetCopyWebpackPlugin and getCleanWebpackPlugin.\n\n- Delete node-register.js (unreferenced; knip.json declared it an entry\n  point, which is why it was never flagged) and index.d.ts (two\n  triple-slash references to jquery/mocha types that the sole source file\n  in the program does not use).\n- Drop the CSS-modules sass loader. The repo contains no\n  *.module.scss / *.modules.scss files, so the /\\.modules?\\.s[ac]ss$/i\n  branch never matched. makeSassLoaders collapses to a no-argument\n  function and css-loader''s `modules` option becomes a constant false.\n  css-modules-typescript-loader stays: it generates the checked-in\n  main.scss.d.ts / main-runner.scss.d.ts files.\n- Narrow stats.excludeModules to `main`; no test-entry.scss exists.\n- Remove 6 devDependencies with no consumer: chai, @babel/register,\n  @babel/helper-define-map, @babel/plugin-transform-object-rest-spread,\n  @types/webpack (a stub over webpack 5''s bundled types) and webpack-cli\n  (spawned by gulpWebpack with cwd set to reporter/runner, both of which\n  declare their own copy).\n- Clean up knip.json, the README bullet describing a nodejs unit testing\n  utility that does not exist, and a filename typo in testStaticAssets.js.\n\nRemoving chai here left the root ignoreDependencies entry for it dead, so\nit is dropped as well.\n\nVerified: reporter/runner bundle output (cypress_runner.css and\ncypress_runner.js) is byte-for-byte identical to before, the checked-in\n*.scss.d.ts files are unchanged under the loader''s CI verify mode, and\ntype_check and knip report no new findings.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"39b9ffb8e865ada7bea53bc931f2dc398dc3e19b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/39b9ffb8e865ada7bea53bc931f2dc398dc3e19b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/f80f791c26a14fcf57fa9fd2314ceda3569d02b2","verification":{"payload":"tree 39b9ffb8e865ada7bea53bc931f2dc398dc3e19b\nparent 1ecb3a09106511955b34effb4aae7987c06a5026\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1790131551 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790131551 -0400\n\nchore: remove dead code from @packages/web-config (#34723)\n\nThe package accumulated unreferenced files, a webpack rule that never\nmatched, and devDependencies with no consumer. Its only consumers are\npackages/reporter and packages/runner, both of which use only\ngetCommonConfig, getSimpleConfig, HtmlWebpackPlugin,\ngetCopyWebpackPlugin and getCleanWebpackPlugin.\n\n- Delete node-register.js (unreferenced; knip.json declared it an entry\n  point, which is why it was never flagged) and index.d.ts (two\n  triple-slash references to jquery/mocha types that the sole source file\n  in the program does not use).\n- Drop the CSS-modules sass loader. The repo contains no\n  *.module.scss / *.modules.scss files, so the /\\.modules?\\.s[ac]ss$/i\n  branch never matched. makeSassLoaders collapses to a no-argument\n  function and css-loader''s `modules` option becomes a constant false.\n  css-modules-typescript-loader stays: it generates the checked-in\n  main.scss.d.ts / main-runner.scss.d.ts files.\n- Narrow stats.excludeModules to `main`; no test-entry.scss exists.\n- Remove 6 devDependencies with no consumer: chai, @babel/register,\n  @babel/helper-define-map, @babel/plugin-transform-object-rest-spread,\n  @types/webpack (a stub over webpack 5''s bundled types) and webpack-cli\n  (spawned by gulpWebpack with cwd set to reporter/runner, both of which\n  declare their own copy).\n- Clean up knip.json, the README bullet describing a nodejs unit testing\n  utility that does not exist, and a filename typo in testStaticAssets.js.\n\nRemoving chai here left the root ignoreDependencies entry for it dead, so\nit is dropped as well.\n\nVerified: reporter/runner bundle output (cypress_runner.css and\ncypress_runner.js) is byte-for-byte identical to before, the checked-in\n*.scss.d.ts files are unchanged under the loader''s CI verify mode, and\ntype_check and knip report no new findings.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsz1fCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAn5YQAH3Mf7f9pV8R8dtkM/GTcZEK\n2cUBsGjmq1qC9C6u7O751x97cEUQZjRxecJL4weVYsM7R5AZqF0a778/UOD7LG19\nefmfC7UHS76wqkNf9hVAYxukp06tDm1Fnbl5DhRw1lovIdNml1GZZN48AHE60RD0\nMGcgDhJRRkWyp5CNU/0hk6Y6ghIgU7pLUphx6fyawNQ7W7umIDgHFgXO+np/lIUW\n1XBiNqHMtMW6t68TboeoWCXswwzzP/XesE9vDE4V9VN9Jp6slgtW2tGuKGw4QHqF\nG8IlGIH+rUbZs7MgUoE3VteubaxdjpZtUJx+maglVdSiYsav0iXKtDh7oED6m0PX\nuLM2fgxaYFLotV3rrcZmg7scMgrR8nrrpWu8XYUUA8TuhUHjFfXETgDiO1h0oIfW\nY++5jWucXKjPbPBQMb4e1sUjiaPle3AJUhtriwsag+2DPM4DTphMhNXzQpvDaAM2\nKzd2o6fLK6y9v633bgsyeS/QYn1rl12lNG6jLd60Eah1hCiAShcSn9ay0gDe0sUZ\nasOov3wHY6osB4ehO0iKe/njhI55ZDj9uYaU8FM7z1fCTQ4iK3lURPjjY6+0teSz\naOB4oYC+eq+inVRrVLowUN6vH2LMeNw0JKkd+RiW5+krFR0VuVPm0bin/vhBQIIY\n2ssg5y+R1Giq1CcFRUNU\n=BzHw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T02:45:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/f80f791c26a14fcf57fa9fd2314ceda3569d02b2","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKGY4MGY3OTFjMjZhMTRmY2Y1N2ZhOWZkMjMxNGNlZGEzNTY5ZDAyYjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/1ecb3a09106511955b34effb4aae7987c06a5026","sha":"1ecb3a09106511955b34effb4aae7987c06a5026","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/1ecb3a09106511955b34effb4aae7987c06a5026"}],"sha":"f80f791c26a14fcf57fa9fd2314ceda3569d02b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/f80f791c26a14fcf57fa9fd2314ceda3569d02b2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/142877?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cacieprins","id":142877,"login":"cacieprins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Mjg3Nw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/1ecb3a09106511955b34effb4aae7987c06a5026/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T17:27:23Z","email":"cacieprins@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Cacie Prins"},"comment_count":8,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T17:27:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: path-filter CI jobs on develop merges (#34817)\n\n* chore: path-filter CI jobs on develop merges\n\nPath-based job selection already ran on PR branches, but a branch override\nin generate-pipeline-parameters.sh emitted all-true on develop before any\npath inspection, so every merge ran the full graph. The run-* guards are\nalready threaded through the shared job definitions in @pipeline.yml, which\nboth pull-request.yml and @main.yml reference, so removing the override is\nenough to filter develop.\n\nFiltering applies only to genuine webhook pushes. The nightly platform cron\nruns on the develop branch, so a branch check cannot tell it apart from a\nmerge; scoping filtering to trigger_source == webhook keeps the scheduled\nsweep unfiltered and covers manual and API triggers at the same time.\n\nA develop push needs its own diff base: its merge base against upstream\ndevelop is HEAD itself, which would yield an empty diff and fail the merge\npipeline. Use pipeline.git.base_revision, falling back to HEAD~1, and run\neverything if neither resolves.\n\nTwo defects found while testing this:\n\n- verify-release-readiness was guarded by run-unit-tests. It exists only in\n  @main.yml and is npm-release''s only pre-flight check, so a merge touching\n  just packages/driver would have published @cypress/* with the\n  semantic-release dry run skipped. It is a release gate, not a test group,\n  so the guard is removed.\n\n- git diff --name-only reports only a rename''s destination, so moving a\n  file out of a globally triggering package escaped that trigger. All three\n  diff call sites now pass --no-renames.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: sync .circleci/AGENTS.md with the repointed platform schedule\n\nThe develop platform schedule was repointed on 2026-09-18 (confirmed live via\nthe CircleCI API): it''s now named \"Platform Develop Branch Schedule\", fires\nonce per weekday at 02:00 UTC instead of twice, and sets\nrun-platform-workflows=true instead of the retired run-windows-workflow.\n\nFolds the now-done \"repoint the develop schedule\" task into \"what exists\",\nleaving only the release-branch schedule as still needed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f87b8f93337d62696f5ad86936ec57533cad8fba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/f87b8f93337d62696f5ad86936ec57533cad8fba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/1ecb3a09106511955b34effb4aae7987c06a5026","verification":{"payload":"tree f87b8f93337d62696f5ad86936ec57533cad8fba\nparent 0cc3b364ea4758cffbc3ce5ead18b918fa41ee00\nauthor Cacie Prins <cacieprins@users.noreply.github.com> 1790098043 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790098043 -0400\n\nchore: path-filter CI jobs on develop merges (#34817)\n\n* chore: path-filter CI jobs on develop merges\n\nPath-based job selection already ran on PR branches, but a branch override\nin generate-pipeline-parameters.sh emitted all-true on develop before any\npath inspection, so every merge ran the full graph. The run-* guards are\nalready threaded through the shared job definitions in @pipeline.yml, which\nboth pull-request.yml and @main.yml reference, so removing the override is\nenough to filter develop.\n\nFiltering applies only to genuine webhook pushes. The nightly platform cron\nruns on the develop branch, so a branch check cannot tell it apart from a\nmerge; scoping filtering to trigger_source == webhook keeps the scheduled\nsweep unfiltered and covers manual and API triggers at the same time.\n\nA develop push needs its own diff base: its merge base against upstream\ndevelop is HEAD itself, which would yield an empty diff and fail the merge\npipeline. Use pipeline.git.base_revision, falling back to HEAD~1, and run\neverything if neither resolves.\n\nTwo defects found while testing this:\n\n- verify-release-readiness was guarded by run-unit-tests. It exists only in\n  @main.yml and is npm-release''s only pre-flight check, so a merge touching\n  just packages/driver would have published @cypress/* with the\n  semantic-release dry run skipped. It is a release gate, not a test group,\n  so the guard is removed.\n\n- git diff --name-only reports only a rename''s destination, so moving a\n  file out of a globally triggering package escaped that trigger. All three\n  diff call sites now pass --no-renames.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: sync .circleci/AGENTS.md with the repointed platform schedule\n\nThe develop platform schedule was repointed on 2026-09-18 (confirmed live via\nthe CircleCI API): it''s now named \"Platform Develop Branch Schedule\", fires\nonce per weekday at 02:00 UTC instead of twice, and sets\nrun-platform-workflows=true instead of the retired run-windows-workflow.\n\nFolds the now-done \"repoint the develop schedule\" task into \"what exists\",\nleaving only the release-branch schedule as still needed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsrp7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArMAQAFCjjV8mGB12j/Ti32w8nGZw\nK2/p0Gv6hkdjgSjd63Gldo/V67YnzanmoEKZDG1kq7XYcoUG2iO/hcixztKQHPrr\npqqjHk95ydLQmS0zaCXmXlDGJr8zH33oDHTqzelStAP92KaqUklTcZ5Ksbqlsr8S\nDe9IsmVLLpquL+d7Y8aPx8JhoyEibxlxM+SQ1jqyZXfOM3OXTrvunFp9vSwJgXy6\nv2cBwXSJboFVBbR5wwIRjtS21wLURzHg84O4yzQw1XJ2ssTRFduh+qMLOiL6tWeW\nMcpoWhcU5H9CxG56/7dbbx62+YIagxLERDyZEkz4sIOsWta30bUpaFqrPUa6F7+J\nN42DS0woJfZ6GSawtZYCCoCgR2nj0alUhJNreXc7+IUSx8E4RbKw977tn03DwHmt\nv72hNKb42URXYWCpSlxXCJSZsn9UfEfpMGlZp01tO1Eb6D/9tBQvdbyi4WoKUS8Q\nHyRR65fI8ZN6MOLHMAvtcUWpWc0n/QIWsryCffobj/66hpBuZ2Wng6Ppbx3IH/MI\nYE0AimL2/6EM1oUV/rzjdj6ZI9C8s5ZUCE3pJyvIbv7CWpcfo6EQhtrpKztk8wOe\nN11d/tNuGUu/BozDlP7BWwDtkclhXcn7znAqLFWCLhntDSVx93aGuCYLMqvLIpyd\nGmh3oY2k4UnPdUoAEDeB\n=x9RI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T17:27:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/1ecb3a09106511955b34effb4aae7987c06a5026","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDFlY2IzYTA5MTA2NTExOTU1YjM0ZWZmYjRhYWU3OTg3YzA2YTUwMjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/0cc3b364ea4758cffbc3ce5ead18b918fa41ee00","sha":"0cc3b364ea4758cffbc3ce5ead18b918fa41ee00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/0cc3b364ea4758cffbc3ce5ead18b918fa41ee00"}],"sha":"1ecb3a09106511955b34effb4aae7987c06a5026","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/1ecb3a09106511955b34effb4aae7987c06a5026"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/142877?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cacieprins","id":142877,"login":"cacieprins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Mjg3Nw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/0cc3b364ea4758cffbc3ce5ead18b918fa41ee00/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T15:18:38Z","email":"cacieprins@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Cacie Prins"},"comment_count":1,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T15:18:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: move binary jobs off pull requests (#34865)\n\n* chore: move binary jobs off pull requests\n\nBinary build and verification is the most expensive part of the pipeline and\nran on every PR push regardless of what changed. Remove it from the\npull-request workflow entirely and rely on the develop build instead.\n\nAdd notify-binary-failure to linux-x64 to close the gap that creates. It\nrequires every binary job at `terminal` so it runs once they have all settled,\nreads their real statuses from the CircleCI API, and comments on the commit\ntagging its author when one of them is `failed`. Reading statuses rather than\nconditioning on `not_run` keeps a cancelled job from being reported as a\nbreakage, and lets the comment name the jobs that broke.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: close three gaps in notify-binary-failure\n\nAll three came out of review on this PR.\n\nFollow pagination on GET /workflow/{id}/job. linux-x64 is already ~80 jobs and\nthat endpoint paginates, so a dropped page would have silently reported no\nfailures. Not live today - a real workflow returns all 81 jobs with a null\nnext_page_token - but the failure mode is a silent miss, so it is worth the loop.\n\nTreat timedout, infrastructure_fail and terminated-unknown as breakage. Matching\nonly `failed` missed them; all four are in CircleCI''s documented job status enum.\n\nWatch the packaging jobs, not just the leaves. When\ncreate-and-trigger-packaging-artifacts or get-published-artifacts fails, every\nleaf below it is not_run rather than failed, so watching only the leaves saw\nnothing wrong in exactly the case the alert exists for.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: link the workflow, not the notifier job, in the failure comment\n\nCIRCLE_BUILD_URL is the URL of the job doing the interpolating, so the comment\nsaid \"view the workflow\" and sent the author to a green notify-binary-failure\njob. Build the workflow URL from CIRCLE_WORKFLOW_ID instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3e8e6cc45871237a9ee3a24d7d0cfc3e01e2d6c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/3e8e6cc45871237a9ee3a24d7d0cfc3e01e2d6c1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/0cc3b364ea4758cffbc3ce5ead18b918fa41ee00","verification":{"payload":"tree 3e8e6cc45871237a9ee3a24d7d0cfc3e01e2d6c1\nparent 190f97e24e95d1705b4e3cb7e02b5f6ac4cd2591\nauthor Cacie Prins <cacieprins@users.noreply.github.com> 1790090318 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790090318 -0400\n\nchore: move binary jobs off pull requests (#34865)\n\n* chore: move binary jobs off pull requests\n\nBinary build and verification is the most expensive part of the pipeline and\nran on every PR push regardless of what changed. Remove it from the\npull-request workflow entirely and rely on the develop build instead.\n\nAdd notify-binary-failure to linux-x64 to close the gap that creates. It\nrequires every binary job at `terminal` so it runs once they have all settled,\nreads their real statuses from the CircleCI API, and comments on the commit\ntagging its author when one of them is `failed`. Reading statuses rather than\nconditioning on `not_run` keeps a cancelled job from being reported as a\nbreakage, and lets the comment name the jobs that broke.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: close three gaps in notify-binary-failure\n\nAll three came out of review on this PR.\n\nFollow pagination on GET /workflow/{id}/job. linux-x64 is already ~80 jobs and\nthat endpoint paginates, so a dropped page would have silently reported no\nfailures. Not live today - a real workflow returns all 81 jobs with a null\nnext_page_token - but the failure mode is a silent miss, so it is worth the loop.\n\nTreat timedout, infrastructure_fail and terminated-unknown as breakage. Matching\nonly `failed` missed them; all four are in CircleCI''s documented job status enum.\n\nWatch the packaging jobs, not just the leaves. When\ncreate-and-trigger-packaging-artifacts or get-published-artifacts fails, every\nleaf below it is not_run rather than failed, so watching only the leaves saw\nnothing wrong in exactly the case the alert exists for.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: link the workflow, not the notifier job, in the failure comment\n\nCIRCLE_BUILD_URL is the URL of the job doing the interpolating, so the comment\nsaid \"view the workflow\" and sent the author to a green notify-binary-failure\njob. Build the workflow URL from CIRCLE_WORKFLOW_ID instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqspxOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+yUQAFDQN7WDRmPafxEDXKrQ+7CS\nD8+K9YqEYgi9VfYE9nUipgfo2RhosKGGZzN7gVzuKsh5EhQ8mSq9YHJJJShf5CDs\nP9hyG3b4eoKKHsSsKgHqB4JyJuZ++jc/lfje1d/Cusuiai5j12ftqbp4zAX5VBSY\nlHaA2HsSwo+IVBmO9LZDdVjg94T3kI0wmmg0+GhKfSeHK8zfPX2oP96Ldzape+aD\n8r/9dMls6+/j8e13kme6Op6gE9UrFRd3RpXloShUzggOGA7/z2HcwwiAVSbASE53\nvU1tbETZFTrnDFPDoVO1DR2buOMpVNklFmRQiiPHOfz7JgCnulnCD8rFRIwqPThf\nFuyRLPB7H2l+LdslEj75NsnxPnZBvj0iR1pJZLbZz6moO8v5QD0ql4DAt1cbUQ/c\nGRe2GcpfQC15YxpXtnhOj0Ih8iGQhKjeeEZUS8NoCxQXH0sK7y6I/nAU3/vSYP5R\nyGnWsTTXVFsh0LDQOZ8VPuczFUzM6U7yJZtpJ3sVW8MLxN9iMQp/YT0447EeOLXH\nqNj3aTAGP+DuJ2g92sAM9lu3Ev1b4GhAo03ePWtXu34xbid+2oH/LlXTWFpFPw+A\nKVRQTYYvwQaZe0XApqsRI6DbYD9yMpiPnD6wUH3ArUord/DS9X0YdZIsad26kWkT\nWHUGuXuEEj/IuhZmet2m\n=8l/V\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T15:18:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/0cc3b364ea4758cffbc3ce5ead18b918fa41ee00","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDBjYzNiMzY0ZWE0NzU4Y2ZmYmMzY2U1ZWFkMThiOTE4ZmE0MWVlMDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/190f97e24e95d1705b4e3cb7e02b5f6ac4cd2591","sha":"190f97e24e95d1705b4e3cb7e02b5f6ac4cd2591","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/190f97e24e95d1705b4e3cb7e02b5f6ac4cd2591"}],"sha":"0cc3b364ea4758cffbc3ce5ead18b918fa41ee00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/0cc3b364ea4758cffbc3ce5ead18b918fa41ee00"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/142877?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cacieprins","id":142877,"login":"cacieprins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Mjg3Nw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/190f97e24e95d1705b4e3cb7e02b5f6ac4cd2591/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T20:44:08Z","email":"cacieprins@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Cacie Prins"},"comment_count":5,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T20:44:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: use expression-based job filters so path-filtered PR jobs are never scheduled (#34866)\n\n* chore: filter path-filtered PR jobs instead of halting them\n\nPath-filtered jobs were disabled, not skipped: every one was scheduled, a\ncontainer spun up, and halt-if-skipped ended it as the first step. An\nexpression filter on the workflow entry means the job is never scheduled.\n\nEach of the 48 conditional entries in pull-request.yml gains a filter\ntesting the same pipeline parameters its guard already consults, via one\nanchor per parameter.\n\nThree entries are not a straight one-to-one mapping:\n\n- system-tests-node-modules-install is guarded by a four-way or, and is\n  the only dependency of eleven entries. CircleCI does not execute a job\n  whose dependencies are all filtered out, so a narrower filter here\n  would drop those eleven silently while all-jobs-passed still reported\n  green. The filter reproduces the full or.\n- percy-finalize halts on percy-enabled as well as on a seven-way or.\n  percy-enabled is never set by emit_all_true, so filtering on the or\n  alone would keep scheduling it on every develop run.\n- The four force-http1 entries already carried a filter for a different\n  parameter than their guard. The guard is now anded onto it, so\n  behavior is unchanged once the halts come out.\n\nhalt-if-skipped stays in place for now. It is a rollback lever, not a\nsafety net: it only catches a filter that is too permissive, and only a\nfilter that is too restrictive loses coverage.\n\nscripts/audit-ci-job-filters.js checks both invariants — every guarded\nentry carries a matching filter, and no guarded entry can lose every\ndependency while still being wanted. It runs in the lint job and in\npack-ci.sh --validate, which the pre-commit hook already calls. That\ncheck has to exist before the halts are deleted, because at that point\nthe guard lives only at the workflow entry.\n\nRefs #34782\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: document why the filter audit gates in lint, not pack-workflows\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: also audit unguarded jobs whose dependencies are all conditional\n\nAn unguarded entry runs on every pipeline, so if every one of its\ndependencies can be filtered out it can be dropped instead. Three binary\nsystem-test entries depend on system-tests-node-modules-install, which is\nnow conditional; they are safe only because they also require\nget-published-artifacts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: skip audit entries whose requires name no entry in the workflow\n\nWithout this an entry with an unresolvable dependency name reports as\nhaving no unconditional dependency, which is a false positive rather\nthan a finding.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6ad02c71158b61cfcf276da50fbce6a32879475d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/6ad02c71158b61cfcf276da50fbce6a32879475d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/190f97e24e95d1705b4e3cb7e02b5f6ac4cd2591","verification":{"payload":"tree 6ad02c71158b61cfcf276da50fbce6a32879475d\nparent daeb8d0b5a1892a0c48c0bf9638f139d873c12ae\nauthor Cacie Prins <cacieprins@users.noreply.github.com> 1790023448 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790023448 -0400\n\nchore: use expression-based job filters so path-filtered PR jobs are never scheduled (#34866)\n\n* chore: filter path-filtered PR jobs instead of halting them\n\nPath-filtered jobs were disabled, not skipped: every one was scheduled, a\ncontainer spun up, and halt-if-skipped ended it as the first step. An\nexpression filter on the workflow entry means the job is never scheduled.\n\nEach of the 48 conditional entries in pull-request.yml gains a filter\ntesting the same pipeline parameters its guard already consults, via one\nanchor per parameter.\n\nThree entries are not a straight one-to-one mapping:\n\n- system-tests-node-modules-install is guarded by a four-way or, and is\n  the only dependency of eleven entries. CircleCI does not execute a job\n  whose dependencies are all filtered out, so a narrower filter here\n  would drop those eleven silently while all-jobs-passed still reported\n  green. The filter reproduces the full or.\n- percy-finalize halts on percy-enabled as well as on a seven-way or.\n  percy-enabled is never set by emit_all_true, so filtering on the or\n  alone would keep scheduling it on every develop run.\n- The four force-http1 entries already carried a filter for a different\n  parameter than their guard. The guard is now anded onto it, so\n  behavior is unchanged once the halts come out.\n\nhalt-if-skipped stays in place for now. It is a rollback lever, not a\nsafety net: it only catches a filter that is too permissive, and only a\nfilter that is too restrictive loses coverage.\n\nscripts/audit-ci-job-filters.js checks both invariants — every guarded\nentry carries a matching filter, and no guarded entry can lose every\ndependency while still being wanted. It runs in the lint job and in\npack-ci.sh --validate, which the pre-commit hook already calls. That\ncheck has to exist before the halts are deleted, because at that point\nthe guard lives only at the workflow entry.\n\nRefs #34782\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: document why the filter audit gates in lint, not pack-workflows\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: also audit unguarded jobs whose dependencies are all conditional\n\nAn unguarded entry runs on every pipeline, so if every one of its\ndependencies can be filtered out it can be dropped instead. Three binary\nsystem-test entries depend on system-tests-node-modules-install, which is\nnow conditional; they are safe only because they also require\nget-published-artifacts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: skip audit entries whose requires name no entry in the workflow\n\nWithout this an entry with an unresolvable dependency name reports as\nhaving no unconditional dependency, which is a false positive rather\nthan a finding.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsZcYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnkEQAD2cKxxObjZQHcrn/9An/5cc\nQFIEjxlwbFG85yhLqCkpFH6Qc3uiA384X80MJae1Dnjp3lAHVVXe6Z1Fn5SRZr8q\nl5jk8MCw5n/8MRLAGquSwuMWrwN4kZkCx90JhEfS9pP0q86m0NJ2a2bBwddhzvHY\nFOZOBvZ0d49jkYWKh1U8Pc25V62OSBe1VviqGe8b0m3kwjKCTUtHE05O60FX+vjz\nyLDINOEIYaQxQX7F/huxjsvSU1f0BqtFmsDYQPVkO5HEN8m2BHVhsk8BIp1LuAz0\nu6sC8oTOsxp1y876WlQk4QB4KzKvMOH/sI0xDZ6nfnoJR8egKi4SzOnHFaAsuMCy\n3BOaQMAgyo4x4iIpDc2JxZVOrsDTARZZircz61QEL374iIy10Eo3DZn6edLKOW7e\n/JjcMLwW8y4MsMuj6kQ0ChkORz5kZX80kB4uyF4AiLCeq1N/+F3tibSb0hmUPS8Z\nagTb2FNciVdZBUHxSTzaiivhma/wyN8x1aNMhlEHyB169joe2AMATsy7vXp8etRK\n2rMLTeaJwtIzE4I8p9hf6E2nEV01WnM1gEJHdknVUOdxWaIq1JNkvYN9s6tfU3QU\neq/JECE7rNvtQzD9SrNVlkO9unzM2MqADD7tKtkxPHqRzzV03aa5xaDAfc7YJFqn\nDCXbzqOkERqXfvfjzotU\n=16cv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T20:44:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/190f97e24e95d1705b4e3cb7e02b5f6ac4cd2591","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDE5MGY5N2UyNGU5NWQxNzA1YjRlM2NiN2UwMmI1ZjZhYzRjZDI1OTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/daeb8d0b5a1892a0c48c0bf9638f139d873c12ae","sha":"daeb8d0b5a1892a0c48c0bf9638f139d873c12ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/daeb8d0b5a1892a0c48c0bf9638f139d873c12ae"}],"sha":"190f97e24e95d1705b4e3cb7e02b5f6ac4cd2591","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/190f97e24e95d1705b4e3cb7e02b5f6ac4cd2591"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/daeb8d0b5a1892a0c48c0bf9638f139d873c12ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T13:20:27Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":2,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T13:20:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: add system test coverage for Chrome remote debugging (#34890)\n\nCDP / remote-debugging-port handling had effectively no coverage: the\nonly other test in cdp_spec.ts is skipped. The fixture drives the port\nfrom setupNodeEvents, and each assertion is anchored to Cypress code\nrather than to CDP semantics:\n\n- `--remote-debugging-port` is in the args `before:browser:launch`\n  receives, and the port is the one `CYPRESS_REMOTE_DEBUGGING_PORT`\n  asked for (`chrome.ts` `_getArgs`, `protocol.ts`)\n- the port belongs to the browser Cypress automates, cross-checked\n  against `Cypress.automation(''remote:debugger:protocol'')`\n- a second CDP client can drive the page while Cypress is attached, and\n  Cypress''s own automation still works after that client disconnects\n\nThe connection is made with the `fetch` and `WebSocket` globals, so the\nproject needs no `node_modules`.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GHfv3LBb35bJaZgBRjBCPJ\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2108658b4441bcbb92230efbf5270385a50fa14a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/2108658b4441bcbb92230efbf5270385a50fa14a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/daeb8d0b5a1892a0c48c0bf9638f139d873c12ae","verification":{"payload":"tree 2108658b4441bcbb92230efbf5270385a50fa14a\nparent bbcd1ea26b9f1eb95a1a70ee13a6eaeb00466b54\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1789996827 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789996827 -0400\n\ntest: add system test coverage for Chrome remote debugging (#34890)\n\nCDP / remote-debugging-port handling had effectively no coverage: the\nonly other test in cdp_spec.ts is skipped. The fixture drives the port\nfrom setupNodeEvents, and each assertion is anchored to Cypress code\nrather than to CDP semantics:\n\n- `--remote-debugging-port` is in the args `before:browser:launch`\n  receives, and the port is the one `CYPRESS_REMOTE_DEBUGGING_PORT`\n  asked for (`chrome.ts` `_getArgs`, `protocol.ts`)\n- the port belongs to the browser Cypress automates, cross-checked\n  against `Cypress.automation(''remote:debugger:protocol'')`\n- a second CDP client can drive the page while Cypress is attached, and\n  Cypress''s own automation still works after that client disconnects\n\nThe connection is made with the `fetch` and `WebSocket` globals, so the\nproject needs no `node_modules`.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GHfv3LBb35bJaZgBRjBCPJ\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsS8bCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA