/bbcd1ea26b9f1eb95a1a70ee13a6eaeb00466b54","sha":"bbcd1ea26b9f1eb95a1a70ee13a6eaeb00466b54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/bbcd1ea26b9f1eb95a1a70ee13a6eaeb00466b54"}],"sha":"daeb8d0b5a1892a0c48c0bf9638f139d873c12ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/daeb8d0b5a1892a0c48c0bf9638f139d873c12ae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/bbcd1ea26b9f1eb95a1a70ee13a6eaeb00466b54/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T02:56:40Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":6,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T02:56:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: convert the driver''s fixtures and location specs to TypeScript (#34888)\n\n* test: convert the driver''s fixtures spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `fixtures.cy.js` to `.ts` and resolve the type errors the rename\nsurfaces:\n\n- `require` the spec''s two dependencies as `import`s.\n- Hold the stubbed backend in a typed binding. The public `Backend` type is\n  a single call signature with no sinon surface, so `Cypress.backend.withArgs`\n  does not type-check; `cy.stub` already hands back the typed stub.\n- Assert the `fixturesFolder` test override, which is absent from the\n  hand-curated `Pick` behind `TestConfigOverrides`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014PC3AGx1yhiev4M4sj8Js2\n\n* test: convert the driver''s location spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `location.cy.js` to `.ts` and resolve the type errors the rename\nsurfaces:\n\n- Import `$Location` from the driver source rather than destructuring it off\n  `Cypress`, matching `e2e/cy/navigation.cy.ts`. The spec had no imports, so\n  it compiled as a script, where its top-level `_` and `Location` bindings\n  collided with the lodash and DOM globals; the import also gives the class\n  its real static surface, which the `Cypress.Location` declaration only\n  stubs out.\n- Drop the second argument to `Location.create`, which takes one parameter\n  and has been discarding it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014PC3AGx1yhiev4M4sj8Js2\n\n* test: check the location spec''s url names against the url map\n\nGive the url map a `keyof typeof` parameter type so a name that is not in\nit fails to compile. The factory that reads the map moves out of\n`beforeEach` and off the mocha context, which is what makes the annotation\nreach the call sites: on `this` it was erased to `any`.\n\nThat turns up a test asking for a `hash` url the map never defined, so it\nhad been passing `undefined` to the constructor. Give it a url with an\nempty fragment and assert the `#` that `cy.hash()` documents, rather than\nthe '''' that `window.location` would report — the location object is a plain\nliteral, not `window.location`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014PC3AGx1yhiev4M4sj8Js2\n\n* test: record the documented hash behavior the location object misses\n\n`cy.location()` yields `window.location`''s values, and the browser reports\nan empty fragment as ''''. `getHash()` returns the `#` that `url-parse` keeps,\nso the assertion this spec has always carried is the correct one and the\nbehavior is what diverges. Skip it against that divergence rather than\nasserting the current output as intended.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014PC3AGx1yhiev4M4sj8Js2\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"403c1a98ea049a5792172369efafd970e773fb9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/403c1a98ea049a5792172369efafd970e773fb9e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/bbcd1ea26b9f1eb95a1a70ee13a6eaeb00466b54","verification":{"payload":"tree 403c1a98ea049a5792172369efafd970e773fb9e\nparent 60db5b495c203fb08d12ef819b607050518350c7\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1789873000 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789873000 -0400\n\ntest: convert the driver''s fixtures and location specs to TypeScript (#34888)\n\n* test: convert the driver''s fixtures spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `fixtures.cy.js` to `.ts` and resolve the type errors the rename\nsurfaces:\n\n- `require` the spec''s two dependencies as `import`s.\n- Hold the stubbed backend in a typed binding. The public `Backend` type is\n  a single call signature with no sinon surface, so `Cypress.backend.withArgs`\n  does not type-check; `cy.stub` already hands back the typed stub.\n- Assert the `fixturesFolder` test override, which is absent from the\n  hand-curated `Pick` behind `TestConfigOverrides`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014PC3AGx1yhiev4M4sj8Js2\n\n* test: convert the driver''s location spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `location.cy.js` to `.ts` and resolve the type errors the rename\nsurfaces:\n\n- Import `$Location` from the driver source rather than destructuring it off\n  `Cypress`, matching `e2e/cy/navigation.cy.ts`. The spec had no imports, so\n  it compiled as a script, where its top-level `_` and `Location` bindings\n  collided with the lodash and DOM globals; the import also gives the class\n  its real static surface, which the `Cypress.Location` declaration only\n  stubs out.\n- Drop the second argument to `Location.create`, which takes one parameter\n  and has been discarding it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014PC3AGx1yhiev4M4sj8Js2\n\n* test: check the location spec''s url names against the url map\n\nGive the url map a `keyof typeof` parameter type so a name that is not in\nit fails to compile. The factory that reads the map moves out of\n`beforeEach` and off the mocha context, which is what makes the annotation\nreach the call sites: on `this` it was erased to `any`.\n\nThat turns up a test asking for a `hash` url the map never defined, so it\nhad been passing `undefined` to the constructor. Give it a url with an\nempty fragment and assert the `#` that `cy.hash()` documents, rather than\nthe '''' that `window.location` would report — the location object is a plain\nliteral, not `window.location`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014PC3AGx1yhiev4M4sj8Js2\n\n* test: record the documented hash behavior the location object misses\n\n`cy.location()` yields `window.location`''s values, and the browser reports\nan empty fragment as ''''. `getHash()` returns the `#` that `url-parse` keeps,\nso the assertion this spec has always carried is the correct one and the\nbehavior is what diverges. Skip it against that divergence rather than\nasserting the current output as intended.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014PC3AGx1yhiev4M4sj8Js2\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqr0toCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1aEQAFEvjzEKu1sdGBRhtB/lUeuo\nAEsAByElW+K21dzLC9IYrNTSzepeO8RZ7SmFNDJxbIa/33mqgt/xK2Gz0b9HCJKP\nTAHFy+yynJm4M77TYa8NM0+P8dZRV6EpbunJPj1khfJyev7q79Fqt9wOLoToy7qr\nss8FRraOAx9XvE3mrhkpct7yiL0OnmnmYvohbdVX8wiHbUz+83mbTTTy6IlVVrYc\n5EQ6PP9ZRk8UTLgtgO8BC9bGY7ztfo+n0/Tw7N2EUM6+PK9sSnbiGFeZg3naaihi\nS7HqxxKB+LRpRwfEg3NWgRdN2F1okuSOBSvaTbJqfOESMlDSdfA88g2ptyKlCe/P\nQeJTtdrzABiusY7y97zusRsYeAwplHK9I0zlgWw6lqtXMfu8LCoKOlwY1Jke/CVE\nVqBK/wC0t7/3f3KI79x8Q4mlBIb8cZwnFJ+zaMt3ztVgF7zJz2r0I3qA4i6cp2TG\nFtXY//h8unXqq9yQveR/bL+ES0ChjF9ZiC6i6eLSJsIMGwL9lV+nj+3YxSVA/UyM\nxt78MhU66oNIhUUylpdrLKVtQYZ7RGkVeu+M2p16XlS7EMkNQUOYaBBU7wT+hOZA\n+w/FFlyeemxaw1r0exooXALtFDbQg3crsNDYXxa9VlhC+rDaxK6kyVuvVeDmh3wz\nIrmWKPDzG1Ex7zf8gJWM\n=9O3b\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T02:56:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/bbcd1ea26b9f1eb95a1a70ee13a6eaeb00466b54","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKGJiY2QxZWEyNmI5ZjFlYjk1YTFhNzBlZTEzYTZlYWViMDA0NjZiNTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/60db5b495c203fb08d12ef819b607050518350c7","sha":"60db5b495c203fb08d12ef819b607050518350c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/60db5b495c203fb08d12ef819b607050518350c7"}],"sha":"bbcd1ea26b9f1eb95a1a70ee13a6eaeb00466b54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/bbcd1ea26b9f1eb95a1a70ee13a6eaeb00466b54"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/60db5b495c203fb08d12ef819b607050518350c7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T02:33:14Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":1,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T02:33:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: convert four more driver e2e specs to TypeScript (#34887)\n\n* misc: convert the driver''s misc command spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `misc.cy.js` to `misc.cy.ts` and annotate the objects the circular\nreference tests mutate after construction, so their shapes admit the extra\nkeys.\n\n`can extend the default timeout` passed its 200ms delay as a second argument\nto the `Promise` constructor rather than to `setTimeout`, so the promise\nresolved on the next tick and the test never exercised the extended timeout.\nMove the delay onto `setTimeout`, matching the sibling timeout tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ni8bFkFaiTMaWZKzapfa4G\n\n* misc: convert the driver''s task command spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `task.cy.js` to `task.cy.ts`. `Cypress.backend` is typed as the plain\nfunction it is at runtime, so hold the stub `beforeEach` installs in a variable\nand drive the sinon API through that, as the sessions and prompt specs do.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ni8bFkFaiTMaWZKzapfa4G\n\n* misc: convert the driver''s traversals command spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `traversals.cy.js` to `traversals.cy.ts`. The suite drives jQuery\ntraversal methods by name, and jQuery''s numeric index signature resolves\n`$el[name]` to an element rather than a method, so route those three call\nsites through a helper that names the reason once.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ni8bFkFaiTMaWZKzapfa4G\n\n* misc: convert the driver''s timers spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `timers.cy.js` to `timers.cy.ts`. The tests park their callbacks and\nresults on the AUT window, which `AUTWindow` does not declare, so describe\nthose scratch properties once and annotate the `cy.window()` callbacks that\nuse them.\n\nKeeping the window typed rather than reaching for `any` leaves the timer APIs\nthe spec exercises under type control, which is what flags the deliberately\nextra `requestAnimationFrame` arguments and the non-function `setTimeout`\nhandlers as the intentional violations they are.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ni8bFkFaiTMaWZKzapfa4G\n\n* misc: tighten the comments added by the driver spec conversions\n\nDrop the clauses that restated the code and bring the `@ts-expect-error`\nreasons in line with the one-line form used elsewhere in the driver specs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ni8bFkFaiTMaWZKzapfa4G\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"014b4663004a7b37fbf79dd1e513122b4d1109a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/014b4663004a7b37fbf79dd1e513122b4d1109a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/60db5b495c203fb08d12ef819b607050518350c7","verification":{"payload":"tree 014b4663004a7b37fbf79dd1e513122b4d1109a8\nparent 028c0808d85dfd962d6017c23d0a2b04ac4a8689\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1789871594 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789871594 -0400\n\nchore: convert four more driver e2e specs to TypeScript (#34887)\n\n* misc: convert the driver''s misc command spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `misc.cy.js` to `misc.cy.ts` and annotate the objects the circular\nreference tests mutate after construction, so their shapes admit the extra\nkeys.\n\n`can extend the default timeout` passed its 200ms delay as a second argument\nto the `Promise` constructor rather than to `setTimeout`, so the promise\nresolved on the next tick and the test never exercised the extended timeout.\nMove the delay onto `setTimeout`, matching the sibling timeout tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ni8bFkFaiTMaWZKzapfa4G\n\n* misc: convert the driver''s task command spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `task.cy.js` to `task.cy.ts`. `Cypress.backend` is typed as the plain\nfunction it is at runtime, so hold the stub `beforeEach` installs in a variable\nand drive the sinon API through that, as the sessions and prompt specs do.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ni8bFkFaiTMaWZKzapfa4G\n\n* misc: convert the driver''s traversals command spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `traversals.cy.js` to `traversals.cy.ts`. The suite drives jQuery\ntraversal methods by name, and jQuery''s numeric index signature resolves\n`$el[name]` to an element rather than a method, so route those three call\nsites through a helper that names the reason once.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ni8bFkFaiTMaWZKzapfa4G\n\n* misc: convert the driver''s timers spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `timers.cy.js` to `timers.cy.ts`. The tests park their callbacks and\nresults on the AUT window, which `AUTWindow` does not declare, so describe\nthose scratch properties once and annotate the `cy.window()` callbacks that\nuse them.\n\nKeeping the window typed rather than reaching for `any` leaves the timer APIs\nthe spec exercises under type control, which is what flags the deliberately\nextra `requestAnimationFrame` arguments and the non-function `setTimeout`\nhandlers as the intentional violations they are.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ni8bFkFaiTMaWZKzapfa4G\n\n* misc: tighten the comments added by the driver spec conversions\n\nDrop the clauses that restated the code and bring the `@ts-expect-error`\nreasons in line with the one-line form used elsewhere in the driver specs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ni8bFkFaiTMaWZKzapfa4G\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqr0XqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHZQQADN9Lsjx4lbCQdiS1ZuSxTRP\nF+OeGqLuNr+cKSnP8VG9OIU+CB1poNmpYUnhCOun2sBmlcZnjQeaJGv53kKmt8Wy\niiN/TdLpOfoqCPMHENo9OWZSvZme3ml9eiwxIwyY+d0IEP7L7txzK5r8ugiDW0LE\napk1V8Vei/QRbaFZzkZT0dKDzFIafRsuqSl4lfYZhi3W+UG5YfbLKoyvi11JH1iO\nxgtoMMXpIBaMY5CAyN/wZgleRH940FD1fs9dk7K68nBu6LXuyCYzh8Vo0KK6XUKG\n9sNXmy4K0oiw+YSHQ9mV3gj8i73wS6GLLYI3Ml+kpsGEpKXeQGFo8Xu6JhwGLq64\nN9F7F0nMPudr5QLmt7LzNbR49YzTJexYU0RRWOa6URu2UNXPc7f8MknajspmZOJv\nRbMsHwOAqzYKSMXqpl7m1RPawoB3KHqY/8/gNAwC4EZYNaHO9h9WLUVNCEBmiZ79\n39VfVo8dCbYMRxj1hkhkdojHa/4sOkwhGtdIjS5uFHomBrFFtci1iwsLNqAVY7x5\n8U5YoTkTmql5k5nW4+exfWMaBJashRDFsxuEdOgms35aEEkE09RA/g285T/hkZsk\nNCKvXMRXJV7NxXHfa++BCCZIHg39UFKl0czWzSXjQ2heoaYh7kFZBa94cj8JJ4+e\nNDvOVisb0KVlg1+sNbKH\n=1aFr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T02:33:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/60db5b495c203fb08d12ef819b607050518350c7","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDYwZGI1YjQ5NWMyMDNmYjA4ZDEyZWY4MTliNjA3MDUwNTE4MzUwYzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/028c0808d85dfd962d6017c23d0a2b04ac4a8689","sha":"028c0808d85dfd962d6017c23d0a2b04ac4a8689","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/028c0808d85dfd962d6017c23d0a2b04ac4a8689"}],"sha":"60db5b495c203fb08d12ef819b607050518350c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/60db5b495c203fb08d12ef819b607050518350c7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/028c0808d85dfd962d6017c23d0a2b04ac4a8689/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T02:32:30Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":1,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T02:32:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"misc: type the option arguments these commands already accept (#34886)\n\n* chore: convert after_hooks_page_load_timeout spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/after_hooks_page_load_timeout.cy.js to\n.ts. The spec type-checks as-is; no source changes were needed. No other spec\nimports it, so the conversion lands on its own.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BgApYKrneGCzzurPBfFKcj\n\n* chore: convert 510 spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/510.cy.js to .ts. The spec type-checks\nas-is; no source changes were needed. No other spec imports it, so the\nconversion lands on its own.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BgApYKrneGCzzurPBfFKcj\n\n* chore: convert the space-in-spec-name privileged commands spec to TypeScript\n\nRename \"packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/privileged_commands with space.cy.js\"\nto .ts. The spec type-checks as-is; no source changes were needed. No other\nspec imports it, so the conversion lands on its own.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BgApYKrneGCzzurPBfFKcj\n\n* chore: convert the em-dash-in-spec-name privileged commands spec to TypeScript\n\nRename \"packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/privileged_commands—em dash.cy.js\" to\n.ts. The spec type-checks as-is; no source changes were needed. No other spec\nimports it, so the conversion lands on its own.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BgApYKrneGCzzurPBfFKcj\n\n* chore: convert command_option_immutability spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/commands/command_option_immutability.cy.js\nto .ts. No other spec imports it, so the conversion lands on its own.\n\n`testOptions` takes each command''s options object and hands the clone to a\ncallback that invokes that command, so the helper is generic over the options\ntype. The type parameter is `const` so an options literal keeps its narrow\ntype: `cy.screenshot`''s `capture` is a union of string literals, which a widened\n`string` would not satisfy.\n\nSix call sites pass options in a position the public types do not model, so\nthey carry a `@ts-expect-error` naming the gap rather than changing what the\nspec exercises:\n\n- next/parents/prevUntil read options from the filter argument (traversals.ts\n  assigns `userOptions` from either arg).\n- each and spread take `(options, fn)`; the published overloads declare only\n  `(fn)`.\n- scrollIntoView merges a partial offset over `{ left: 0, top: 0 }`, while the\n  public `Offset` requires both keys.\n- cy.wait''s numeric overload takes no `requestTimeout`.\n\nNo option values, argument order, or assertions changed, so each test still\ncovers the command it did before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BgApYKrneGCzzurPBfFKcj\n\n* misc: type the option arguments these commands already accept\n\nFive commands accept an options object in a position the published types do\nnot model, so TypeScript rejects code the driver runs correctly:\n\n- next/parents/prevUntil take options in place of the filter argument.\n  `traversalFn` assigns `userOptions` from either argument, so\n  `cy.get(el).nextUntil(''#b'', { timeout: 1000 })` works at runtime while the\n  overloads only allow a string there. Each gains a two-argument form\n  alongside the existing three-argument one.\n- each and spread take `(options, fn)`. Both implementations shift their\n  arguments when the callback is the only one passed, and each reaches the\n  same `thenFn` that `then` does, whose published type already carries the\n  `Partial<Timeoutable>` overload these lacked.\n- scrollIntoView takes an offset for one axis. The value is handed to the\n  scroll plugin, which reads it as `offset[pos] || 0`, so a missing axis is\n  already 0. `offset` is now `Partial<Offset>` rather than requiring both keys.\n\nEach addition is a new overload or a widened property, so calls that type-check\ntoday are unaffected.\n\nThe driver''s command_option_immutability spec exercises all five and carried a\n`@ts-expect-error` per call naming the gap; those are removed. The one on\n`cy.wait` stays, since `requestTimeout` genuinely is not an option of the\nnumeric overload.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BgApYKrneGCzzurPBfFKcj\n\n* misc: link the changelog entry to its pull request\n\nReplace the TBD placeholder now that #34886 is open.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BgApYKrneGCzzurPBfFKcj\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6f32b4a7facdf689ed822c916e9eb0bf6c023ca5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/6f32b4a7facdf689ed822c916e9eb0bf6c023ca5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/028c0808d85dfd962d6017c23d0a2b04ac4a8689","verification":{"payload":"tree 6f32b4a7facdf689ed822c916e9eb0bf6c023ca5\nparent 61aeb9dbbe94ac9ab31a785be9ea4518bde65f10\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1789871550 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789871550 -0400\n\nmisc: type the option arguments these commands already accept (#34886)\n\n* chore: convert after_hooks_page_load_timeout spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/after_hooks_page_load_timeout.cy.js to\n.ts. The spec type-checks as-is; no source changes were needed. No other spec\nimports it, so the conversion lands on its own.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BgApYKrneGCzzurPBfFKcj\n\n* chore: convert 510 spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/510.cy.js to .ts. The spec type-checks\nas-is; no source changes were needed. No other spec imports it, so the\nconversion lands on its own.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BgApYKrneGCzzurPBfFKcj\n\n* chore: convert the space-in-spec-name privileged commands spec to TypeScript\n\nRename \"packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/privileged_commands with space.cy.js\"\nto .ts. The spec type-checks as-is; no source changes were needed. No other\nspec imports it, so the conversion lands on its own.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BgApYKrneGCzzurPBfFKcj\n\n* chore: convert the em-dash-in-spec-name privileged commands spec to TypeScript\n\nRename \"packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/privileged_commands—em dash.cy.js\" to\n.ts. The spec type-checks as-is; no source changes were needed. No other spec\nimports it, so the conversion lands on its own.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BgApYKrneGCzzurPBfFKcj\n\n* chore: convert command_option_immutability spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/commands/command_option_immutability.cy.js\nto .ts. No other spec imports it, so the conversion lands on its own.\n\n`testOptions` takes each command''s options object and hands the clone to a\ncallback that invokes that command, so the helper is generic over the options\ntype. The type parameter is `const` so an options literal keeps its narrow\ntype: `cy.screenshot`''s `capture` is a union of string literals, which a widened\n`string` would not satisfy.\n\nSix call sites pass options in a position the public types do not model, so\nthey carry a `@ts-expect-error` naming the gap rather than changing what the\nspec exercises:\n\n- next/parents/prevUntil read options from the filter argument (traversals.ts\n  assigns `userOptions` from either arg).\n- each and spread take `(options, fn)`; the published overloads declare only\n  `(fn)`.\n- scrollIntoView merges a partial offset over `{ left: 0, top: 0 }`, while the\n  public `Offset` requires both keys.\n- cy.wait''s numeric overload takes no `requestTimeout`.\n\nNo option values, argument order, or assertions changed, so each test still\ncovers the command it did before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BgApYKrneGCzzurPBfFKcj\n\n* misc: type the option arguments these commands already accept\n\nFive commands accept an options object in a position the published types do\nnot model, so TypeScript rejects code the driver runs correctly:\n\n- next/parents/prevUntil take options in place of the filter argument.\n  `traversalFn` assigns `userOptions` from either argument, so\n  `cy.get(el).nextUntil(''#b'', { timeout: 1000 })` works at runtime while the\n  overloads only allow a string there. Each gains a two-argument form\n  alongside the existing three-argument one.\n- each and spread take `(options, fn)`. Both implementations shift their\n  arguments when the callback is the only one passed, and each reaches the\n  same `thenFn` that `then` does, whose published type already carries the\n  `Partial<Timeoutable>` overload these lacked.\n- scrollIntoView takes an offset for one axis. The value is handed to the\n  scroll plugin, which reads it as `offset[pos] || 0`, so a missing axis is\n  already 0. `offset` is now `Partial<Offset>` rather than requiring both keys.\n\nEach addition is a new overload or a widened property, so calls that type-check\ntoday are unaffected.\n\nThe driver''s command_option_immutability spec exercises all five and carried a\n`@ts-expect-error` per call naming the gap; those are removed. The one on\n`cy.wait` stays, since `requestTimeout` genuinely is not an option of the\nnumeric overload.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BgApYKrneGCzzurPBfFKcj\n\n* misc: link the changelog entry to its pull request\n\nReplace the TBD placeholder now that #34886 is open.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BgApYKrneGCzzurPBfFKcj\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqr0W+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoC8QAAxRGA5wi8xXXaY1dgO+NoSo\n91OnPL4kND2SIUdRgyw4MubLIpawcOQGThTy/FzfvPIHadxdeAcdKuplrJENeVEE\nouPwr0hLerc5NsWzSOED3OzGJbOpJDj1pZ7nKEdVPSqwCTiqRewb0TNSk+TAinad\n1ZPLvjNQ0ExkyQr/xiJf7yUgUHfB92YUcZIoVRd3oqJdfBY7bumWQjPHgsDvvt16\nzDmUk3j8B/o0uzpaiuC+sFPx/VGxWoD8YZBSskaPGBnkFYCchVzhBFKGMyliBYBx\no5CZAGur2hoLR04Ue97sy0+GsrPrvxdNu5rpJZafTbZjLrm5asDCYAcnI8uYbcA1\n4jiPkiIqQeUcePYlnNCY+ETjee180FNm4gnP/gDGCfYlhwOqpLGA4S+ZcfLSRYMx\nuuHoq30/jg0uG+gRJPuZCrUILwo8j6dA7+TxPBDDHc7DZhFicm92VvqnuoivUzjP\n9ziAzNXGB+o25j+NfP5U30MAin7VUTEXSmaFUshIKny2mkQAv82DQ9iTcAtPR/rN\nbrHadfg/zqpVBLlfUC+TE7B97yQyVAFaRfY7QKzVpZb1VxZz7ackLVr04FlXVsAr\nqHopfg2DIVaVbMAmFrgpOAlX+HHzimFc6pAN2+hWM4jpaavhDWc2FC3ks3sr8q0P\nIla37amvlnrkRsS0WsXa\n=S4l5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T02:32:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/028c0808d85dfd962d6017c23d0a2b04ac4a8689","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDAyOGMwODA4ZDg1ZGZkOTYyZDYwMTdjMjNkMGEyYjA0YWM0YTg2ODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/61aeb9dbbe94ac9ab31a785be9ea4518bde65f10","sha":"61aeb9dbbe94ac9ab31a785be9ea4518bde65f10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/61aeb9dbbe94ac9ab31a785be9ea4518bde65f10"}],"sha":"028c0808d85dfd962d6017c23d0a2b04ac4a8689","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/028c0808d85dfd962d6017c23d0a2b04ac4a8689"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/61aeb9dbbe94ac9ab31a785be9ea4518bde65f10/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T12:26:32Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":1,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T12:26:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: dissolve the driver''s e2e/issues folder into behavior specs (#34882)\n\n* test(driver): move querying regressions out of issues/ into querying spec\n\nFold the cy.contains(0) log assertion into the existing 1119 test, and add\nthe invalid-selector (3847) and Node.prototype-patching custom element\n(4373) tests under #get.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KQvu372WPriwBUQ38Rovtc\n\n* test(driver): move invoke dot-path regression out of issues/ into connectors spec\n\nThe 3871 tests now sit under #invoke > function property.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KQvu372WPriwBUQ38Rovtc\n\n* test(driver): move intercept overwrite regression out of issues/ into net_stubbing spec\n\nThe 3890 tests now sit under ''overwrite cy.intercept''. The chrome force-http1\nsmoke job and the proxy-middleware transport script pinned the old spec path;\nthe CI job already runs net_stubbing.cy.ts, so only the stale entry is dropped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KQvu372WPriwBUQ38Rovtc\n\n* test(driver): move whole-file specs out of issues/ into e2e/ by behavior name\n\nThese specs depend on whole-file state (a single test with testIsolation off,\nroot-level after hooks, or a spec path containing a space or em dash that is\nitself under test), so they move as-is. 510.cy.js keeps its name: it holds\ntwo empty tests and is a candidate for removal.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KQvu372WPriwBUQ38Rovtc\n\n* test(driver): move clock-before-visit regression out of issues/ into clock spec\n\nThe 2850 tests now sit under #clock > window changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KQvu372WPriwBUQ38Rovtc\n\n* test(driver): move visibility regressions out of issues/ into e2e visibility spec\n\n5682 and 8998 keep visibilityStrategy: ''legacy''; 29605 runs under the\ndefault strategy as before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KQvu372WPriwBUQ38Rovtc\n\n* test(driver): move type regressions out of issues/ into type spec\n\n7170 sits under input[type=number] and keeps its webkit exclusion; 14864 gets\nits own describe for the async input handler case.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KQvu372WPriwBUQ38Rovtc\n\n* test(driver): move click scrolling regressions out of issues/ into click spec\n\n565 and 8279 now sit under #click > actionability.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KQvu372WPriwBUQ38Rovtc\n\n* test(driver): move uncaught error regressions out of issues/ into uncaught_errors spec\n\n27183 joins the unhandled rejection tests; 27415 gets a nested describe for\nthe deduped log case.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KQvu372WPriwBUQ38Rovtc\n\n* test(driver): move cy.origin undefined rejection regression out of issues/\n\n23927 now sits under cy.origin - uncaught errors > unhandled rejections.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KQvu372WPriwBUQ38Rovtc\n\n* test(driver): move navigation regressions out of issues/ into navigation spec\n\n1244, 17512, 26206 and base_target form one context about target=_top,\ntarget=_parent and <base target> neutralization. 652 and 3975 sit under\n#visit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KQvu372WPriwBUQ38Rovtc\n\n* test(driver): move element screenshot regression out of issues/ into screenshot spec\n\n2034 sits directly under #screenshot, where take:screenshot is not stubbed,\nso the real capture still runs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KQvu372WPriwBUQ38Rovtc\n\n* test(driver): group AUT window patch regressions into aut_window_patches spec\n\n1436, 6412, 1854, 5707, 2582, 4295, 599 and 2784 all check how Cypress\npatches the AUT window (parent, setTimeout, frameElement, document.referrer,\nXHR onreadystatechange, cross-origin iframes). navigation.cy.js has no\nobstructive-code context, so they get a spec of their own. The\nmodifyObstructiveCode: false test restores the config it mutates, since\nCypress.config() changes persist across tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KQvu372WPriwBUQ38Rovtc\n\n* test(driver): move XHR abort regressions out of issues/ into xhr_abort spec\n\nrequest.cy.js covers cy.request only, so the raw XHR abort tests get a spec of\ntheir own.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KQvu372WPriwBUQ38Rovtc\n\n* test(driver): move focus regressions out of issues/ into focus_blur spec\n\n1909 joins the top-level focus tests; 1939, 1940 and 2190 form a\ndocument.hasFocus() describe with retries: 0, matching the old beforeEach.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KQvu372WPriwBUQ38Rovtc\n\n* test(driver): move basic auth regression out of issues/ into basic_auth spec\n\n573 covers cy.visit with credentials rather than downloads, so it gets its\nown spec next to the other e2e behaviors and reuses the auth_creds fixture.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KQvu372WPriwBUQ38Rovtc\n\n* test(driver): move navigator.webdriver regression out of issues/\n\n27939 becomes e2e/navigator_webdriver.cy.ts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KQvu372WPriwBUQ38Rovtc\n\n* test(driver): move command log scroll regression out of issues/ into runner spec\n\n3253 sits before the root after-hook test that must stay last.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KQvu372WPriwBUQ38Rovtc\n\n* test(driver): move CYPRESS env var regression out of issues/ into env spec\n\n18805 becomes a second top-level describe in env.cy.ts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KQvu372WPriwBUQ38Rovtc\n\n* docs(driver): state where regression tests for GitHub issues live\n\nRegression tests go in the spec for the command or behavior they exercise,\ntitled by behavior, with the issue URL as a comment above the test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KQvu372WPriwBUQ38Rovtc\n\n* docs(driver): drop the standalone-spec sentence from the regression test convention\n\nThe convention is the placement rule and the issue URL comment; the note\nabout which specs stand on their own was extra.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KQvu372WPriwBUQ38Rovtc\n\n* test(driver): run the 3890 intercept baseline before any cy.intercept overwrite\n\nMocha runs a context''s own tests before its nested suites, so the moved pair\nin a nested describe ran after three overwrites and its sanity test no longer\nexercised the original command. They are now direct tests placed ahead of the\nfirst overwrite.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KQvu372WPriwBUQ38Rovtc\n\n---------\n