eived_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/7ee973bae88534296e5a06dda1fa625ff4072a4c","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDdlZTk3M2JhZTg4NTM0Mjk2ZTVhMDZkZGExZmE2MjVmZjQwNzJhNGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/e8c6e5fe8f2b649b436f606775c649fbe3cedd75","sha":"e8c6e5fe8f2b649b436f606775c649fbe3cedd75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/e8c6e5fe8f2b649b436f606775c649fbe3cedd75"}],"sha":"7ee973bae88534296e5a06dda1fa625ff4072a4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/7ee973bae88534296e5a06dda1fa625ff4072a4c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/e8c6e5fe8f2b649b436f606775c649fbe3cedd75/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T17:09:30Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":1,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T17:09:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"misc: type docsUrl as string | string[] on CypressError (#34879)\n\n* chore: convert driver return_value spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/return_value.cy.js to .ts, switch\nthe utils helper to an ESM import, and suppress the per-test `cy.foo()`\ncustom command with `@ts-expect-error`, matching promises.cy.ts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BG2HpEY72JXZmsK5Cp57gm\n\n* chore: convert driver video spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/video.cy.js to .ts and pass\nHTMLVideoElement to `cy.get` so the yielded element exposes `play()`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BG2HpEY72JXZmsK5Cp57gm\n\n* chore: convert driver webcam spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/webcam.cy.js to .ts and assert the\n`video` element is present, since `querySelector` widens to include null.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BG2HpEY72JXZmsK5Cp57gm\n\n* chore: convert driver zonejs spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/zonejs.cy.js to .ts, give the\nPromise an explicit void type so `resolve()` takes no argument, and\nsuppress `Cypress.Log`, which is typed as a log instance rather than the\ninternal namespace it holds at runtime.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BG2HpEY72JXZmsK5Cp57gm\n\n* chore: convert driver uncaught_errors spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/uncaught_errors.cy.js to .ts and\ncast to `Cypress.CypressError` to read `docsUrl`, which the\n`uncaught:exception` handler types as a plain `Error`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BG2HpEY72JXZmsK5Cp57gm\n\n* misc: type docsUrl as string | string[] on CypressError\n\nAn uncaught exception carries both the originating error''s docs url and\nCypress''s own, so `createUncaughtException` assigns an array\n(`packages/driver/src/cypress/error_utils.ts`) and `processErr` reads it\nback through `castArray`. The reporter''s error model already declares the\nunion; the published type still promised a lone string.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BG2HpEY72JXZmsK5Cp57gm\n\n* misc: add changelog entry for docsUrl type correction\n\nThe PR link is a placeholder until this branch has a pull request number;\nvalidation matches an entry by the issue or PR links it cites.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BG2HpEY72JXZmsK5Cp57gm\n\n* misc: tighten docsUrl changelog entry\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BG2HpEY72JXZmsK5Cp57gm\n\n* misc: link changelog entry to PR #34879\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BG2HpEY72JXZmsK5Cp57gm\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"148e97d84a01426ed13ff5c31330fb0dc13851ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/148e97d84a01426ed13ff5c31330fb0dc13851ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/e8c6e5fe8f2b649b436f606775c649fbe3cedd75","verification":{"payload":"tree 148e97d84a01426ed13ff5c31330fb0dc13851ea\nparent 3afb67dfd95ff33f3e39dfcfde5ef6ff7e7ed7ec\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1789751370 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789751370 -0400\n\nmisc: type docsUrl as string | string[] on CypressError (#34879)\n\n* chore: convert driver return_value spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/return_value.cy.js to .ts, switch\nthe utils helper to an ESM import, and suppress the per-test `cy.foo()`\ncustom command with `@ts-expect-error`, matching promises.cy.ts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BG2HpEY72JXZmsK5Cp57gm\n\n* chore: convert driver video spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/video.cy.js to .ts and pass\nHTMLVideoElement to `cy.get` so the yielded element exposes `play()`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BG2HpEY72JXZmsK5Cp57gm\n\n* chore: convert driver webcam spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/webcam.cy.js to .ts and assert the\n`video` element is present, since `querySelector` widens to include null.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BG2HpEY72JXZmsK5Cp57gm\n\n* chore: convert driver zonejs spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/zonejs.cy.js to .ts, give the\nPromise an explicit void type so `resolve()` takes no argument, and\nsuppress `Cypress.Log`, which is typed as a log instance rather than the\ninternal namespace it holds at runtime.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BG2HpEY72JXZmsK5Cp57gm\n\n* chore: convert driver uncaught_errors spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/uncaught_errors.cy.js to .ts and\ncast to `Cypress.CypressError` to read `docsUrl`, which the\n`uncaught:exception` handler types as a plain `Error`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BG2HpEY