Fjes0rhlhHt9PGrK\nqKD3Ct1Iir/jvKsNA23eq1bOX6fwSDxIXnukkk/2kIz6pnci5sDkKQRAZbjYkpQv\nPYnUnV+RUBj+yMumenzF\n=qQTg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T17:09:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/e8c6e5fe8f2b649b436f606775c649fbe3cedd75","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKGU4YzZlNWZlOGYyYjY0OWI0MzZmNjA2Nzc1YzY0OWZiZTNjZWRkNzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/3afb67dfd95ff33f3e39dfcfde5ef6ff7e7ed7ec","sha":"3afb67dfd95ff33f3e39dfcfde5ef6ff7e7ed7ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/3afb67dfd95ff33f3e39dfcfde5ef6ff7e7ed7ec"}],"sha":"e8c6e5fe8f2b649b436f606775c649fbe3cedd75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/e8c6e5fe8f2b649b436f606775c649fbe3cedd75"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/142877?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cacieprins","id":142877,"login":"cacieprins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Mjg3Nw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/3afb67dfd95ff33f3e39dfcfde5ef6ff7e7ed7ec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T14:44:13Z","email":"cacieprins@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Cacie Prins"},"comment_count":1,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T14:44:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: run macOS and ARM platform CI on a schedule instead of every develop merge (#34812)\n\n* chore: run macOS and ARM platform CI on a schedule instead of every develop merge\n\n`darwin-x64`, `darwin-arm64`, and `linux-arm64` ran on every develop push via\n`&full-workflow-filters`. A new `run-platform-workflows` pipeline parameter now\ngates them, mirroring how `run-windows-workflow` has gated `windows` since\n#34437, so a CircleCI scheduled pipeline drives them on develop instead.\n\nThe two darwin workflows compete for leased self-hosted macOS hardware, and\nper-merge platform signal on develop is not actionable — develop passed 47 of\n213 runs. `linux-arm64` is cheap but shares the gate so all platform coverage\nlands in one sweep. `linux-x64` stays per-push, and `release/*`, `electron/*`,\n`update-v8-snapshot-cache-on-develop`, and allowlisted branches keep per-push\nplatform coverage.\n\nThe parameter is declared in both the setup config and the packed pipeline so\nCircleCI inherits it into the continuation. It is deliberately absent from\ngenerate-pipeline-parameters.sh: re-passing an already-declared parameter\nthrough the continuation is rejected as a conflicting pipeline parameter.\n\n`.circleci/AGENTS.md` now records the scheduled pipeline''s id, owner, current\nstate, and target state. Those were invisible in-repo, and the three platform\nworkflows have no develop coverage until the schedule sets the new parameter.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: consolidate windows and platform CI onto one schedule parameter\n\n`run-windows-workflow` and `run-platform-workflows` set the same scheduled\npipeline and always fire together, so the two-parameter split served no\npurpose beyond letting each platform be triggered independently — a\ncapability nothing used. `windows`, `linux-arm64`, `darwin-x64`, and\n`darwin-arm64` now all read `run-platform-workflows`.\n\n`force-persist-artifacts` moves to the top level of each gate''s `or:`,\nalongside the schedule parameter, instead of living only inside\n`&full-workflow-filters`. Nested there, it only ever satisfies the \"some\nbranch is allowed to run this at all\" half of the gate; on develop the\nplatform gate''s `NOT develop` clause still zeroes it out, so a manual\nTrigger Pipeline run asking for one platform binary got five on a feature\nbranch but only linux-x64 on develop — backwards from what setting the flag\nmeans. Nothing in this repo sets `force-persist-artifacts` automatically\n(no script or workflow does), so hoisting it doesn''t touch per-push or\ncron spend; it only changes what a human gets from one manual flag.\n\n`guides/release-process.md` said CI builds Linux, Mac, and Windows binaries\non every develop commit. That has been false for Windows since #34437;\nthis change extends the same schedule-gating to macOS, so the doc is\ncorrected for all three rather than left half-true.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: schedule linux-arm64/darwin-* on release/* too, matching windows\n\nREVERTS a decision from the previous commit on this branch: linux-arm64,\ndarwin-x64, and darwin-arm64 kept running per-push on release/* branches;\nthis makes them skip it, same as windows already does.\n\nwindows, linux-arm64, darwin-x64, and darwin-arm64 now share one `when:`\ngate instead of windows carrying its own copy with an extra release/*\nexclusion the other three lacked. All four read run-platform-workflows and\nskip develop and release/* the same way; force-persist-artifacts still\nforces any of them regardless of branch.\n\nThis needs a second CircleCI Scheduled Pipeline, retargeted at whichever\nrelease/* branch is active. Confirmed for darwin-x64 and darwin-arm64:\ncreate-build-artifacts is the only thing that builds and signs their\nbinaries, with no external fallback, so gating it off release/* means zero\nnew signed Mac binaries for a release sha until the schedule covers it.\nlinux-arm64 is different and unconfirmed either way: like linux-x64, it\ntriggers the external cypress-publish-binary project behind a manual\napproval gate rather than building locally, and this repo can''t see whether\nthat project''s own build already covers arm64 as part of the same trigger.\n\nDocumented as a hard prerequisite in .circleci/AGENTS.md rather than an\naccompanying nice-to-have, and guides/release-process.md gets the matching\nwait-for-the-nightly-build step for release day. The existing develop\nschedule''s 23:00 UTC slot is left exactly as is; nothing here touches or\nproposes changing it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: apply review corrections to release/CI guides and param comments\n\nBill checked the external cypress-publish-binary config directly and\nconfirmed linux-arm64 has no fallback either: a normal develop push only\nproduces the linux-x64 binary. Corrects the continuous-integration.md\nBinary Creation row and release-process.md accordingly, and restores the\noriginal \"Build the Linux, Mac & Windows binaries\" wording there — the\nschedule change is about when they build, not whether they do, and the\nguide shouldn''t read like Mac/Windows binaries stopped existing.\n\nAlso widens the run-platform-workflows comment in both config.yml and\n@pipeline.yml to say \"develop or release/*\", matching the previous commit''s\ngate change.\n\nLeaves .circleci/AGENTS.md''s \"what exists today\" schedule paragraph alone\non purpose: the live schedule has already drifted further since that text\nwas written (the 17:00 slot stopped firing 09-10, and 23:00 was reverted\nto run-windows-workflow on 09-15), and the plan is to fix that paragraph\nin a later PR once the schedule is actually repointed, not now.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e3a87bfd33d31d4eee54de187c0325d4ec762349","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/e3a87bfd33d31d4eee54de187c0325d4ec762349"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/3afb67dfd95ff33f3e39dfcfde5ef6ff7e7ed7ec","verification":{"payload":"tree e3a87bfd33d31d4eee54de187c0325d4ec762349\nparent d43e0c485c902918059dd88551b367d3ec6c8cd6\nauthor Cacie Prins <cacieprins@users.noreply.github.com> 1789742653 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789742653 -0400\n\nchore: run macOS and ARM platform CI on a schedule instead of every develop merge (#34812)\n\n* chore: run macOS and ARM platform CI on a schedule instead of every develop merge\n\n`darwin-x64`, `darwin-arm64`, and `linux-arm64` ran on every develop push via\n`&full-workflow-filters`. A new `run-platform-workflows` pipeline parameter now\ngates them, mirroring how `run-windows-workflow` has gated `windows` since\n#34437, so a CircleCI scheduled pipeline drives them on develop instead.\n\nThe two darwin workflows compete for leased self-hosted macOS hardware, and\nper-merge platform signal on develop is not actionable — develop passed 47 of\n213 runs. `linux-arm64` is cheap but shares the gate so all platform coverage\nlands in one sweep. `linux-x64` stays per-push, and `release/*`, `electron/*`,\n`update-v8-snapshot-cache-on-develop`, and allowlisted branches keep per-push\nplatform coverage.\n\nThe parameter is declared in both the setup config and the packed pipeline so\nCircleCI inherits it into the continuation. It is deliberately absent from\ngenerate-pipeline-parameters.sh: re-passing an already-declared parameter\nthrough the continuation is rejected as a conflicting pipeline parameter.\n\n`.circleci/AGENTS.md` now records the scheduled pipeline''s id, owner, current\nstate, and target state. Those were invisible in-repo, and the three platform\nworkflows have no develop coverage until the schedule sets the new parameter.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: consolidate windows and platform CI onto one schedule parameter\n\n`run-windows-workflow` and `run-platform-workflows` set the same scheduled\npipeline and always fire together, so the two-parameter split served no\npurpose beyond letting each platform be triggered independently — a\ncapability nothing used. `windows`, `linux-arm64`, `darwin-x64`, and\n`darwin-arm64` now all read `run-platform-workflows`.\n\n`force-persist-artifacts` moves to the top level of each gate''s `or:`,\nalongside the schedule parameter, instead of living only inside\n`&full-workflow-filters`. Nested there, it only ever satisfies the \"some\nbranch is allowed to run this at all\" half of the gate; on develop the\nplatform gate''s `NOT develop` clause still zeroes it out, so a manual\nTrigger Pipeline run asking for one platform binary got five on a feature\nbranch but only linux-x64 on develop — backwards from what setting the flag\nmeans. Nothing in this repo sets `force-persist-artifacts` automatically\n(no script or workflow does), so hoisting it doesn''t touch per-push or\ncron spend; it only changes what a human gets from one manual flag.\n\n`guides/release-process.md` said CI builds Linux, Mac, and Windows binaries\non every develop commit. That has been false for Windows since #34437;\nthis change extends the same schedule-gating to macOS, so the doc is\ncorrected for all three rather than left half-true.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: schedule linux-arm64/darwin-* on release/* too, matching windows\n\nREVERTS a decision from the previous commit on this branch: linux-arm64,\ndarwin-x64, and darwin-arm64 kept running per-push on release/* branches;\nthis makes them skip it, same as windows already does.\n\nwindows, linux-arm64, darwin-x64, and darwin-arm64 now share one `when:`\ngate instead of windows carrying its own copy with an extra release/*\nexclusion the other three lacked. All four read run-platform-workflows and\nskip develop and release/* the same way; force-persist-artifacts still\nforces any of them regardless of branch.\n\nThis needs a second CircleCI Scheduled Pipeline, retargeted at whichever\nrelease/* branch is active. Confirmed for darwin-x64 and darwin-arm64:\ncreate-build-artifacts is the only thing that builds and signs their\nbinaries, with no external fallback, so gating it off release/* means zero\nnew signed Mac binaries for a release sha until the schedule covers it.\nlinux-arm64 is different and unconfirmed either way: like linux-x64, it\ntriggers the external cypress-publish-binary project behind a manual\napproval gate rather than building locally, and this repo can''t see whether\nthat project''s own build already covers arm64 as part of the same trigger.\n\nDocumented as a hard prerequisite in .circleci/AGENTS.md rather than an\naccompanying nice-to-have, and guides/release-process.md gets the matching\nwait-for-the-nightly-build step for release day. The existing develop\nschedule''s 23:00 UTC slot is left exactly as is; nothing here touches or\nproposes changing it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: apply review corrections to release/CI guides and param comments\n\nBill checked the external cypress-publish-binary config directly and\nconfirmed linux-arm64 has no fallback either: a normal develop push only\nproduces the linux-x64 binary. Corrects the continuous-integration.md\nBinary Creation row and release-process.md accordingly, and restores the\noriginal \"Build the Linux, Mac & Windows binaries\" wording there — the\nschedule change is about when they build, not whether they do, and the\nguide shouldn''t read like Mac/Windows binaries stopped existing.\n\nAlso widens the run-platform-workflows comment in both config.yml and\n@pipeline.yml to say \"develop or release/*\", matching the previous commit''s\ngate change.\n\nLeaves .circleci/AGENTS.md''s \"what exists today\" schedule paragraph alone\non purpose: the live schedule has already drifted further since that text\nwas written (the 17:00 slot stopped firing 09-10, and 23:00 was reverted\nto run-windows-workflow on 09-15), and the plan is to fix that paragraph\nin a later PR once the schedule is actually repointed, not now.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrU49CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKjsQAIbSnZA8fWeU7NlskyaZKrP/\nhAHkiQNmrQ3c76OowxpUKc8TQzYcbwLeXdDsF4u2B25FZ2mGTYwOB/W+L4tTD6Jy\nH0CCTrh4ILvxvBp6nAFDsAvY89OZiXXRP/rNLY1g0IWuES/J+d1mj/i5UwkWGFAb\nBgz5t7iZMnReQWXy608AUae/guMsiZTvJSRlI5EcQ2n82n9WsopdW8JhHoYgbVrd\na/nFLS+ZVUdGgflPqRTtbw1rTZ6Aj1KFSL6M6by+lSNBIwiy9Mj3OgvuqYzL/sEa\nIKApgCk9B7/JgQNFHbFMqFh57vPnJOlgD2jm6neCUEBkRcTE6+bwiZIxrbW4AC3x\nQAcHGPsFrJzla4OCUXuzuij50Wn7vR7GvtN+nN4iXWaneWs/0N0XPh3o3fhdOtTy\nHupOr4Vmk1KEXkYm5JUHE9tq0+qMwIXTeydDerqafmxvSlVLRdIwDzJB3/iq6wDB\nP28NcqpaTjdX+a4FnPwRmdok1CCCqPt4DfzfSH+VyO2jlIM2bpRDSQOQafbvzxXB\nFZCSi+GoCLOaaMKIeylR7Urse45K7zg3SPQXcMwvMxRffV7reUZSUHP6e9uEYDyY\nKGPGCPfj0TYUmraxMCzKwEsjgMqFrw+FzDZsTBgKtAD0MOb/xZ2QdPKjFch6dn7W\nBGgpZ9m+ujL5j4uCUlGQ\n=jPEU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T14:44:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/3afb67dfd95ff33f3e39dfcfde5ef6ff7e7ed7ec","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDNhZmI2N2RmZDk1ZmYzM2YzZTM5ZGZjZmRlNWVmNmZmN2U3ZWQ3ZWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/d43e0c485c902918059dd88551b367d3ec6c8cd6","sha":"d43e0c485c902918059dd88551b367d3ec6c8cd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/d43e0c485c902918059dd88551b367d3ec6c8cd6"}],"sha":"3afb67dfd95ff33f3e39dfcfde5ef6ff7e7ed7ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/3afb67dfd95ff33f3e39dfcfde5ef6ff7e7ed7ec"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/d43e0c485c902918059dd88551b367d3ec6c8cd6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T14:37:24Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":3,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T14:37:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: convert four driver e2e specs to TypeScript (#34875)\n\n* chore: convert testConfigOverrides-describe-only spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/testConfigOverrides-describe-only.cy.js\nto .ts. No other spec imports it, so the conversion lands on its own.\n\nThe spec asserts that the driver''s internal `testConfigList` and\n`unverifiedTestConfig` bookkeeping keys never reach the resolved config, and\nneither is part of the public `Cypress.Config` type, so the read goes through a\nlocal intersection type. The spec is also marked as a module so its\n`shouldNotExecute` helper no longer collides with the sibling it-only spec now\nthat both are in the same TypeScript program.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AsWTAC9VuZ1vnFAQ5FMEJT\n\n* chore: convert testConfigOverrides-it-only spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/testConfigOverrides-it-only.cy.js to\n.ts. No other spec imports it, so the conversion lands on its own.\n\nThe spec asserts that the driver''s internal `testConfigList` and\n`unverifiedTestConfig` bookkeeping keys never reach the resolved config, and\nneither is part of the public `Cypress.Config` type, so the read goes through a\nlocal intersection type. The spec is also marked as a module so its\n`shouldNotExecute` helper no longer collides with the sibling describe-only\nspec now that both are in the same TypeScript program.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AsWTAC9VuZ1vnFAQ5FMEJT\n\n* chore: convert text_mask spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/text_mask.cy.js to .ts. The spec\ntype-checks as-is; no source changes were needed. No other spec imports it, so\nthe conversion lands on its own.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AsWTAC9VuZ1vnFAQ5FMEJT\n\n* chore: correct the test override config comment in the converted specs\n\nThe comment claimed the driver strips `testConfigList` and\n`unverifiedTestConfig` off the resolved config. It does not — they live on the\nrunnable''s `_testConfig`, and only the individual override values are ever\npassed to `config()`. Replace it with a single line stating why the keys are\nabsent from the public config type, which is the part the cast needs explained.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AsWTAC9VuZ1vnFAQ5FMEJT\n\n* chore: convert visibility spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/visibility.cy.js to .ts. No other spec\nimports it, so the conversion lands on its own.\n\nThe mode array the suites iterate over inferred as `string[]`, which does not\nsatisfy the `visibilityStrategy` override''s literal union. Mark it `as const`\nso each mode keeps its literal type.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AsWTAC9VuZ1vnFAQ5FMEJT\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4198c5638b356cde89354d42fcb1a744d3ae2c69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/4198c5638b356cde89354d42fcb1a744d3ae2c69"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/d43e0c485c902918059dd88551b367d3ec6c8cd6","verification":{"payload":"tree 4198c5638b356cde89354d42fcb1a744d3ae2c69\nparent 8fa654f635e1daa0b59574710a7cbdc4239f4abc\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1789742244 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789742244 -0400\n\nchore: convert four driver e2e specs to TypeScript (#34875)\n\n* chore: convert testConfigOverrides-describe-only spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/testConfigOverrides-describe-only.cy.js\nto .ts. No other spec imports it, so the conversion lands on its own.\n\nThe spec asserts that the driver''s internal `testConfigList` and\n`unverifiedTestConfig` bookkeeping keys never reach the resolved config, and\nneither is part of the public `Cypress.Config` type, so the read goes through a\nlocal intersection type. The spec is also marked as a module so its\n`shouldNotExecute` helper no longer collides with the sibling it-only spec now\nthat both are in the same TypeScript program.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AsWTAC9VuZ1vnFAQ5FMEJT\n\n* chore: convert testConfigOverrides-it-only spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/testConfigOverrides-it-only.cy.js to\n.ts. No other spec imports it, so the conversion lands on its own.\n\nThe spec asserts that the driver''s internal `testConfigList` and\n`unverifiedTestConfig` bookkeeping keys never reach the resolved config, and\nneither is part of the public `Cypress.Config` type, so the read goes through a\nlocal intersection type. The spec is also marked as a module so its\n`shouldNotExecute` helper no longer collides with the sibling describe-only\nspec now that both are in the same TypeScript program.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AsWTAC9VuZ1vnFAQ5FMEJT\n\n* chore: convert text_mask spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/text_mask.cy.js to .ts. The spec\ntype-checks as-is; no source changes were needed. No other spec imports it, so\nthe conversion lands on its own.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AsWTAC9VuZ1vnFAQ5FMEJT\n\n* chore: correct the test override config comment in the converted specs\n\nThe comment claimed the driver strips `testConfigList` and\n`unverifiedTestConfig` off the resolved config. It does not — they live on the\nrunnable''s `_testConfig`, and only the individual override values are ever\npassed to `config()`. Replace it with a single line stating why the keys are\nabsent from the public config type, which is the part the cast needs explained.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AsWTAC9VuZ1vnFAQ5FMEJT\n\n* chore: convert visibility spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/visibility.cy.js to .ts. No other spec\nimports it, so the conversion lands on its own.\n\nThe mode array the suites iterate over inferred as `string[]`, which does not\nsatisfy the `visibilityStrategy` override''s literal union. Mark it `as const`\nso each mode keeps its literal type.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AsWTAC9VuZ1vnFAQ5FMEJT\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrUykCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATEMQAHRJA/eHilfmnV/AFRhSTzGh\nzl2L6Q8o3+CVnK1+/qlgpe2oTGPJtc+RzaRblIGnApN6hTMc2VwInCCmE/KnWkaF\nQqrFkmK85VVr1LQt6/kGl3OMjKY2N3oAYe/RkhE9jcstLOqwF3B5M2w+mBADI9/E\ndplQusnr00muP/ZwL25ha4S25sCccVWWxEIcwrftLqZ0yyPy+MtGJZ32S5B8p3X9\nxdAZgW2Ugcpw7htxXjABPE8Qi/DqFSdsDMCsbKKq+4+0wm/hZ3eJhGwhvOnBfPTN\n9pYUvZAmyRAW1sPEJe8qPGVAauuEHRA+O3gwuFRqdQjrywXS6fC3Ga84m1z1WgMg\nqS4DekRDeibxCg9kVu0iTAUNli69ZBOuQT4ZJ3DALk9XXwBfTwpE93g2SF/wwLX4\n4ALmDmFBOodXC2+N3QO1gUxoUC0+rHdk827FZVdczm3eTu78FYWwAIC9XkLRFKYV\nRoAgifxzfDNlHVpZEj7Dz+u02DAoLcYntyZ0ScgWb7uwMr/VFiTiBihXxVcHLrAk\nN6iDOt9oTet5Ho/ry8WoY9HXPyT0Ow2jBi1cWY0C0/9IRrPnj7b+dX6zoscisT4z\nU1uc/zKktpQ1KV7g8IlFghzN5rArL1BNB2ABReiWjNlgMaiZi4IPjOb/POS9GJYE\n0lnVAbpZHrflR/UNEyDF\n=A8Fe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T14:37:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/d43e0c485c902918059dd88551b367d3ec6c8cd6","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKGQ0M2UwYzQ4NWM5MDI5MTgwNTlkZDg4NTUxYjM2N2QzZWM2YzhjZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/8fa654f635e1daa0b59574710a7cbdc4239f4abc","sha":"8fa654f635e1daa0b59574710a7cbdc4239f4abc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/8fa654f635e1daa0b59574710a7cbdc4239f4abc"}],"sha":"d43e0c485c902918059dd88551b367d3ec6c8cd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/d43e0c485c902918059dd88551b367d3ec6c8cd6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/8fa654f635e1daa0b59574710a7cbdc4239f4abc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T20:52:36Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":13,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T20:52:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: convert driver source_map_utils, redirects, and rerun specs to TypeScript (#34864)\n\n* chore: convert driver source_map_utils spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/cypress/source_map_utils.cy.js to .ts and\nswap the source-map require for an import. No other spec imports it, so the\nconversion lands on its own.\n\nThree type errors needed fixing, none of which change what the tests assert:\n\n`SourceMapConsumer.initialize` exists at runtime but not in source-map''s\npublished typings, which source_map_utils already works around with a\n@ts-ignore. Aliasing the import and declaring `initialize` on it keeps every\ntest body byte-identical to the JS original.\n\n`Cypress.utils.encodeBase64Unicode` was missing from the CypressUtils\ninterface even though `$Cypress.utils` is the driver''s utils module, which\nexports it.\n\n`initializeSourceMapConsumer` declared `sourceMap` as required, so the test\ncovering the no-source-map path failed arity checking. The function returns\nearly when the argument is absent, so the parameter is now optional.\n\nVerified with yarn workspace @packages/driver cypress:run --spec\ncypress/e2e/cypress/source_map_utils.cy.ts (13 passing), plus check-ts, lint,\nand the source_map_utils vitest unit spec.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CBt3sGZxxPQeC6EifGS3AJ\n\n* chore: convert driver redirects spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/redirects.cy.js to .ts and swap the\nsupport/utils require for an import. No other spec imports it, so the\nconversion lands on its own.\n\nThe only type error was a third argument passed to assertLogLength, which\ntakes two. The extra message was silently dropped at runtime, and the local\nreduce that built it was only ever used for that argument, so both are gone.\nNothing is lost: assertLogLength already builds its own failure message\nlisting every received log by name and message. The javascript context\nfurther down this same file, and all other call sites in the repo, already\nuse the two-argument form.\n\nVerified with yarn workspace @packages/driver cypress:run --spec\ncypress/e2e/e2e/redirects.cy.ts (2 passing, 2 pending from the skipped\njavascript context, 0 failing), plus check-ts and lint.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CBt3sGZxxPQeC6EifGS3AJ\n\n* chore: convert driver rerun spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/rerun.cy.js to .ts. No other spec\nimports it, so the conversion lands on its own.\n\nTwo classes of type error, both from the spec reaching past the public API\non purpose:\n\nwindow.top is Window | null and carries no runCount, which accounted for 13\nof the 15 errors across 8 dereferences. A single typed alias covers both\nhalves and reads better than repeating a non-null assertion; the file stays\na script, so the counter is not leaked onto the global Window type. The\nassertion is honest because the initialization directly below it establishes\nthe invariant.\n\nCypress.config''s setter overload only accepts test config overrides, and\nisTextTerminal is runtime server config, so toggling it to suppress mocha\nend events is unsupported by design. Marked with @ts-expect-error, matching\nissues/28527.cy.ts, which does the same for isInteractive and exit.\n@ts-expect-error over @ts-ignore so the suppression fails loudly if the\ntypes are ever widened to cover these keys.\n\nVerified with yarn workspace @packages/driver cypress:run --spec\ncypress/e2e/e2e/rerun.cy.ts (2 passing, 0 failing), plus check-ts and lint.\nBecause this spec turns on its own rerun, the converted output was diffed\nagainst a run of the original .js: both print the suite header twice,\nconfirming the rerun fires, and both report the same 2 passing tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CBt3sGZxxPQeC6EifGS3AJ\n\n* chore: address review on the driver spec TypeScript conversions\n\nKeep initializeSourceMapConsumer''s sourceMap parameter required. Making it\noptional so the spec''s one-argument call type-checked also let any future\ncaller drop the argument, take the `if (!sourceMap) return null` early\nreturn, and silently register no consumer. The spec passes undefined\nexplicitly instead, which still exercises the no-source-map path and states\nthe intent at the call site. Typing the parameter rather than reverting it\nwas not an option: the vitest spec passes a partial { sources } object that\nRawSourceMap would reject. source_map_utils.ts is now unchanged from\ndevelop.\n\nUpdate the event-manager comment that still pointed at rerun.cy.js, which\nno longer exists after the rename.\n\nVerified with check-ts and lint on @packages/driver and @packages/app, the\nsource_map_utils vitest spec (18 passing), and all three converted specs:\nsource_map_utils 13 passing, rerun 2 passing, redirects 2 passing with 2\npending.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CBt3sGZxxPQeC6EifGS3AJ\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0ad3bb2381781f853d6a4c2fd4cca75fbaec6629","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/0ad3bb2381781f853d6a4c2fd4cca75fbaec6629"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/8fa654f635e1daa0b59574710a7cbdc4239f4abc","verification":{"payload":"tree 0ad3bb2381781f853d6a4c2fd4cca75fbaec6629\nparent bc30be53c7b36af129edfacbb9f934025fadab7a\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1789678356 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789678356 -0400\n\nchore: convert driver source_map_utils, redirects, and rerun specs to TypeScript (#34864)\n\n* chore: convert driver source_map_utils spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/cypress/source_map_utils.cy.js to .ts and\nswap the source-map require for an import. No other spec imports it, so the\nconversion lands on its own.\n\nThree type errors needed fixing, none of which change what the tests assert:\n\n`SourceMapConsumer.initialize` exists at runtime but not in source-map''s\npublished typings, which source_map_utils already works around with a\n@ts-ignore. Aliasing the import and declaring `initialize` on it keeps every\ntest body byte-identical to the JS original.\n\n`Cypress.utils.encodeBase64Unicode` was missing from the CypressUtils\ninterface even though `$Cypress.utils` is the driver''s utils module, which\nexports it.\n\n`initializeSourceMapConsumer` declared `sourceMap` as required, so the test\ncovering the no-source-map path failed arity checking. The function returns\nearly when the argument is absent, so the parameter is now optional.\n\nVerified with yarn workspace @packages/driver cypress:run --spec\ncypress/e2e/cypress/source_map_utils.cy.ts (13 passing), plus check-ts, lint,\nand the source_map_utils vitest unit spec.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CBt3sGZxxPQeC6EifGS3AJ\n\n* chore: convert driver redirects spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/redirects.cy.js to .ts and swap the\nsupport/utils require for an import. No other spec imports it, so the\nconversion lands on its own.\n\nThe only type error was a third argument passed to assertLogLength, which\ntakes two. The extra message was silently dropped at runtime, and the local\nreduce that built it was only ever used for that argument, so both are gone.\nNothing is lost: assertLogLength already builds its own failure message\nlisting every received log by name and message. The javascript context\nfurther down this same file, and all other call sites in the repo, already\nuse the two-argument form.\n\nVerified with yarn workspace @packages/driver cypress:run --spec\ncypress/e2e/e2e/redirects.cy.ts (2 passing, 2 pending from the skipped\njavascript context, 0 failing), plus check-ts and lint.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CBt3sGZxxPQeC6EifGS3AJ\n\n* chore: convert driver rerun spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/rerun.cy.js to .ts. No other spec\nimports it, so the conversion lands on its own.\n\nTwo classes of type error, both from the spec reaching past the public API\non purpose:\n\nwindow.top is Window | null and carries no runCount, which accounted for 13\nof the 15 errors across 8 dereferences. A single typed alias covers both\nhalves and reads better than repeating a non-null assertion; the file stays\na script, so the counter is not leaked onto the global Window type. The\nassertion is honest because the initialization directly below it establishes\nthe invariant.\n\nCypress.config''s setter overload only accepts test config overrides, and\nisTextTerminal is runtime server config, so toggling it to suppress mocha\nend events is unsupported by design. Marked with @ts-expect-error, matching\nissues/28527.cy.ts, which does the same for isInteractive and exit.\n@ts-expect-error over @ts-ignore so the suppression fails loudly if the\ntypes are ever widened to cover these keys.\n\nVerified with yarn workspace @packages/driver cypress:run --spec\ncypress/e2e/e2e/rerun.cy.ts (2 passing, 0 failing), plus check-ts and lint.\nBecause this spec turns on its own rerun, the converted output was diffed\nagainst a run of the original .js: both print the suite header twice,\nconfirming the rerun fires, and both report the same 2 passing tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CBt3sGZxxPQeC6EifGS3AJ\n\n* chore: address review on the driver spec TypeScript conversions\n\nKeep initializeSourceMapConsumer''s sourceMap parameter required. Making it\noptional so the spec''s one-argument call type-checked also let any future\ncaller drop the argument, take the `if (!sourceMap) return null` early\nreturn, and silently register no consumer. The spec passes undefined\nexplicitly instead, which still exercises the no-source-map path and states\nthe intent at the call site. Typing the parameter rather than reverting it\nwas not an option: the vitest spec passes a partial { sources } object that\nRawSourceMap would reject. source_map_utils.ts is now unchanged from\ndevelop.\n\nUpdate the event-manager comment that still pointed at rerun.cy.js, which\nno longer exists after the rename.\n\nVerified with check-ts and lint on @packages/driver and @packages/app, the\nsource_map_utils vitest spec (18 passing), and all three converted specs:\nsource_map_utils 13 passing, rerun 2 passing, redirects 2 passing with 2\npending.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CBt3sGZxxPQeC6EifGS3AJ\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrFMUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwc0QACPKPFcg28FI5bU1FLoZAcHg\n+mPfIJuBOvM7IqBbN4lzFVTnIbAVrz1fqtFYOFaPHhxL9W1d4sgU0CscoKJ5KeKJ\nQwX+7eSw8y2LZ7adcXws2gutFDUOxOLZbqvYCMwnurS0vpDtu2mZCNTw0EufJzrq\nFZFTl+SVI8sTjezLHM+TXHJbESEhBKf7cW84GPUsBDv/sbeeMwZx8RVC3HPfuR0l\nM/4WYCE2Rbba5nCKJzX+hfxiTfYTIH+kG7eNzos4juK9FEAg5I+M8KpzOjNUu5+e\n2UZJG8TCUpEpjpm1HindxlyUhJ2hLIVjQ0O2Ge7x/PiXKfAb1GNTzD1c9WWsbnLe\nP50WNdOIldfKZUhUfY+9YaBRsAO4bCN7YRiR1a3iAdcFXPKjm9BW/FjRnZg4KkTL\nvByjDo5BSVSSrMDCtG4hcsxDz6cl9xCBKGjbcqWeA1F7f8BJM0pgBCWuXDE4X/b2\na9HYGIasAc8IsR3soTNdDco7ns7BjMQRZw0swFzpL1qFKFl+HnTsKPoJcX7Ud30U\nIBELWBbccI5IO6/hgffuBFRnZtBESWLmhfX+XmbhhUluuGXguqwz5cL6vhXzKVEi\nUTqfbdjGusTh+izXYZ2mM4xQkteR1nmbImn3Nxa09IGlvLbgGr1GkTTJ3Dh74T/Z\nmrXXrrk06gxF03DxfHAR\n=kIwm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T20:52:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/8fa654f635e1daa0b59574710a7cbdc4239f4abc","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDhmYTY1NGY2MzVlMWRhYTBiNTk1NzQ3MTBhN2NiZGM0MjM5ZjRhYmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/bc30be53c7b36af129edfacbb9f934025fadab7a","sha":"bc30be53c7b36af129edfacbb9f934025fadab7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/bc30be53c7b36af129edfacbb9f934025fadab7a"}],"sha":"8fa654f635e1daa0b59574710a7cbdc4239f4abc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/8fa654f635e1daa0b59574710a7cbdc4239f4abc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3980464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AtofStryker","id":3980464,"login":"AtofStryker","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5ODA0NjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/bc30be53c7b36af129edfacbb9f934025fadab7a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T17:00:04Z","email":"bglesias@gmail.com","name":"Bill Glesias"},"comment_count":4,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T17:00:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: add a skill for migrating `@packages/server` unit tests to vitest (#34847)\n\n* chore: run @packages/server unit specs on mocha and vitest, split by filename\n\nvitest owns test/unit/**/*.spec.{js,ts}; mocha keeps *_spec.{js,ts}. test-unit\nruns both, so server-unit-tests now expects two junit files and the\ncloud-environment job targets the mocha runner directly. The branch is\nallowlisted for the platform workflows so the four-platform cloud-environment\njob is exercised; drop those two .circleci entries before merge.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: exclude vitest specs from the mocha unit runner with --ignore\n\nThe shell expands the include glob before mocha sees it, and /bin/sh treats\n** as a single *, so narrowing the include glob to *_spec.ts dropped every\ntop-level and deeper spec (78 of 149 files ran). Keep the original include\nglob, which expands to directories mocha recurses, and exclude *.spec.* with a\nquoted --ignore instead. This also covers the filename-filter form, which\npreviously still matched vitest specs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: add a skill for migrating @packages/server unit specs to vitest\n\nOne consolidated skill in place of the fifteen proposed in #33596. It keeps\nonly the conversions that pass while proving less than the mocha original:\nthe runner contract, spec_helper hooks that must be inlined, mocks that load\nthe real module, assertions that change meaning, and the GraphQL, nock, and\ntimer traps. The @cypress/* deps.inline claim from #33596 is replaced with\nwhat PR #34844 measured: vi.mock never intercepts a bare require(), so the\nCJS cache is the seam. .cursor/skills is allowlisted in .gitignore so the\nautomation can read the skill from the checkout.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e61aeb408f56d3ed0dfca37b84e7418f059f58bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/e61aeb408f56d3ed0dfca37b84e7418f059f58bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/bc30be53c7b36af129edfacbb9f934025fadab7a","verification":{"payload":"tree e61aeb408f56d3ed0dfca37b84e7418f059f58bc\nparent b1287eb839b37598d4ae5002535a15f337e0bb3d\nauthor Bill Glesias <bglesias@gmail.com> 1789664404 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789664404 -0400\n\nchore: add a skill for migrating `@packages/server` unit tests to vitest (#34847)\n\n* chore: run @packages/server unit specs on mocha and vitest, split by filename\n\nvitest owns test/unit/**/*.spec.{js,ts}; mocha keeps *_spec.{js,ts}. test-unit\nruns both, so server-unit-tests now expects two junit files and the\ncloud-environment job targets the mocha runner directly. The branch is\nallowlisted for the platform workflows so the four-platform cloud-environment\njob is exercised; drop those two .circleci entries before merge.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: exclude vitest specs from the mocha unit runner with --ignore\n\nThe shell expands the include glob before mocha sees it, and /bin/sh treats\n** as a single *, so narrowing the include glob to *_spec.ts dropped every\ntop-level and deeper spec (78 of 149 files ran). Keep the original include\nglob, which expands to directories mocha recurses, and exclude *.spec.* with a\nquoted --ignore instead. This also covers the filename-filter form, which\npreviously still matched vitest specs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: add a skill for migrating @packages/server unit specs to vitest\n\nOne consolidated skill in place of the fifteen proposed in #33596. It keeps\nonly the conversions that pass while proving less than the mocha original:\nthe runner contract, spec_helper hooks that must be inlined, mocks that load\nthe real module, assertions that change meaning, and the GraphQL, nock, and\ntimer traps. The @cypress/* deps.inline claim from #33596 is replaced with\nwhat PR #34844 measured: vi.mock never intercepts a bare require(), so the\nCJS cache is the seam. .cursor/skills is allowlisted in .gitignore so the\nautomation can read the skill from the checkout.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrByUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwukQAHz3eYiebidzi3FKv10T6+68\nz2Q4nGBOmAk+qtsg/zP7M2YqNtsUOmiyTviGhTY7l8p2tfA/15Fzq5YBzbQcz6+K\ncyWV5BvzHiYf5vX/uVgrWuVa9W5FqhqHSSElYfqWeS7Yjn3jvNmNDq+PRFGrvZb6\ncPnKeWlRouDNenBWxEeH91sE0aSFeIcb0ECAb3iGH+VPjhWSEtUPIX3EEUaFEwCh\n1T8CVbYLYspfwaz0p6gAIK8XOICLRFy0V2dFkMn4nrB8uzy7fXoS5ljyW1WCl9hN\nDUmT2abhvbt/SnK8iYxISFV9u4NP7pnKHYXzGi5cGOCmgGSS4B1udBSN34EyU6n3\nGls9QnzYfRC9HYxP7T4MCyfvu3qAYzJxZsuDFprQlWFPFvGwNULYXXqaETfA5ygo\nBhq6XzU8qL+TIr6P2Pvb4QMbujgPpznFPsTgBP7Ahti3wVBZodTzejgD2QEOcotQ\nbytbeVY8G4UxpU4MSP8URBoHLPWoNAVtyXsMAww25lLcWHfuNNSIfe67Bepbjzg+\nmt/B8nE5epF4d+XnImdl7OCzih9zS8k9G77EzvlsNfzl4E+HVwsfM5Ttcsfc7TZl\n6hoEOqfUYXnnNSeEx7Mn0u8JcHTBww/f+UJw7E6VQSmGu9d/1l7jAHB5eirst3Bv\nQd84DRmVi8qZHRftZJ6m\n=n7QA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T17:00:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_u