cloud-environment\njob is exercised; drop those two .circleci entries before merge.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: migrate test/unit/automation/commands/key_press.spec to vitest\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: migrate test/unit/cloud/api/put_protocol_artifact_spec to vitest\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: migrate test/unit/cloud/api/create_instance_spec to vitest\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: migrate test/unit/plugins/child/run_plugins_spec to vitest\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: migrate test/unit/routes_spec to vitest\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: migrate test/unit/browsers/cri-client_spec to vitest\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: migrate test/unit/server-base_spec to vitest\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: exclude vitest specs from the mocha unit runner with --ignore\n\nThe shell expands the include glob before mocha sees it, and /bin/sh treats\n** as a single *, so narrowing the include glob to *_spec.ts dropped every\ntop-level and deeper spec (78 of 149 files ran). Keep the original include\nglob, which expands to directories mocha recurses, and exclude *.spec.* with a\nquoted --ignore instead. This also covers the filename-filter form, which\npreviously still matched vitest specs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"45944f2eef18097d0a888cc2bbc4e49ce8e4c9ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/45944f2eef18097d0a888cc2bbc4e49ce8e4c9ad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/7e9f631a660456ebf520c435fe2ed3adbdff6c27","verification":{"payload":"tree 45944f2eef18097d0a888cc2bbc4e49ce8e4c9ad\nparent ea131f7f608689e746ba8a0be265ac929f02cdc5\nauthor Bill Glesias <bglesias@gmail.com> 1789573035 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789573035 -0400\n\nchore: add vitest to `@packages/server` unit tests (#34844)\n\n* chore: run @packages/server unit specs on mocha and vitest, split by filename\n\nvitest owns test/unit/**/*.spec.{js,ts}; mocha keeps *_spec.{js,ts}. test-unit\nruns both, so server-unit-tests now expects two junit files and the\ncloud-environment job targets the mocha runner directly. The branch is\nallowlisted for the platform workflows so the four-platform cloud-environment\njob is exercised; drop those two .circleci entries before merge.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: migrate test/unit/automation/commands/key_press.spec to vitest\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: migrate test/unit/cloud/api/put_protocol_artifact_spec to vitest\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: migrate test/unit/cloud/api/create_instance_spec to vitest\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: migrate test/unit/plugins/child/run_plugins_spec to vitest\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: migrate test/unit/routes_spec to vitest\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: migrate test/unit/browsers/cri-client_spec to vitest\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: migrate test/unit/server-base_spec to vitest\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: exclude vitest specs from the mocha unit runner with --ignore\n\nThe shell expands the include glob before mocha sees it, and /bin/sh treats\n** as a single *, so narrowing the include glob to *_spec.ts dropped every\ntop-level and deeper spec (78 of 149 files ran). Keep the original include\nglob, which expands to directories mocha recurses, and exclude *.spec.* with a\nquoted --ignore instead. This also covers the filename-filter form, which\npreviously still matched vitest specs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqrerCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcX8QAJ7CMByIyQtW1599NTPMmYpF\nvbPWYVhJp3e1Aw1gXP3natQ/kPGTlKxHSioVSOzQ+ZpN4O6fSz6IMOX7675w4C67\n1UAqmpp+ZNDS9cbFG1U9i1/MKRVEuGZ8gbxYrNmsFuZD+e8uMeUZ8LxUc59ibbc5\nZ32TzyEZjzS5zXf54TWALOnqttWrueBaQ0N4jgKn2FaTdIxd5V0fiJ/uIncbxM3F\nxLsxsUeN/VV+XxWjGr+v7UQECB+y43OzPpErcpx0LdeVoh/4DRkwAxRKxo/GEebj\nIpay63xWMm66R1OZ97kWUrf/3Arb90i+Ax1ji1euOQIwS4I2bHNhf2xOcV8DNR/G\niOYikHXkF32YBS9tKr5/fYSABu6ndinS+2pWb3MCzKehjfAlA8PeBN1ELNmcaCSj\nMVJI9FU1mN7ZCbOC3hYOFJgA1Qw67eIRp7XiGpl0cMg9DZybtTMb+kDQFTrJhkpu\nWRRPMdmSflVlAU4Hv7q9vopjpV5auoV5YqnnsQe98tskdrGzEOepA3rb9nlOUcHP\nUKy6dEufJJ48d9u/F1eAhKMUk+q7+hrhSCfyxxutE3+pspfieFl5hBSF7e2ZaYcp\npfpEGM7X9JSoz5pr4DPatO7ts+kGrbWPu5V/2M+XRvUoniCQxQ95Hk3uq0aCYv1J\nQw0dRn5zNvBAEWEENgjo\n=EvvH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T15:37:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/7e9f631a660456ebf520c435fe2ed3adbdff6c27","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDdlOWY2MzFhNjYwNDU2ZWJmNTIwYzQzNWZlMmVkM2FkYmRmZjZjMjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/ea131f7f608689e746ba8a0be265ac929f02cdc5","sha":"ea131f7f608689e746ba8a0be265ac929f02cdc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/ea131f7f608689e746ba8a0be265ac929f02cdc5"}],"sha":"7e9f631a660456ebf520c435fe2ed3adbdff6c27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/7e9f631a660456ebf520c435fe2ed3adbdff6c27"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3980464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AtofStryker","id":3980464,"login":"AtofStryker","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5ODA0NjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/ea131f7f608689e746ba8a0be265ac929f02cdc5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T14:13:57Z","email":"bglesias@gmail.com","name":"Bill Glesias"},"comment_count":4,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T14:13:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"dependency(security): upgrade proxy-addr to 2.0.8 (#34859)\n\nAddresses CVE-2026-90711 (https://security.snyk.io/vuln/SNYK-JS-PROXYADDR-19812342).\n\nproxy-addr is only reached through express, whose ~2.0.7 range already\nadmits 2.0.8, so this is a lockfile-only bump with no package.json change.\n\nAddresses #34858\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"43b4397ad587a42a2841c3eaca6fd414c1c7f25b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/43b4397ad587a42a2841c3eaca6fd414c1c7f25b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/ea131f7f608689e746ba8a0be265ac929f02cdc5","verification":{"payload":"tree 43b4397ad587a42a2841c3eaca6fd414c1c7f25b\nparent a1b69653f1fca97228bde651e304e7d7d01682a1\nauthor Bill Glesias <bglesias@gmail.com> 1789568037 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789568037 -0400\n\ndependency(security): upgrade proxy-addr to 2.0.8 (#34859)\n\nAddresses CVE-2026-90711 (https://security.snyk.io/vuln/SNYK-JS-PROXYADDR-19812342).\n\nproxy-addr is only reached through express, whose ~2.0.7 range already\nadmits 2.0.8, so this is a lockfile-only bump with no package.json change.\n\nAddresses #34858\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqqQlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGq4QAJuRJjGuIxb1J/BHUEZSQRNT\n0rGqgLd+B6cy9Iki0Nq8R0qpWY2LsR7Zd4zzCG7oIpFPQBvQ4IiC9yLjC7xdCmuK\ncYMFFM9Clc/iGFeFtxi2OGUg4vXIv7667JBVVjqBu/Mi/+l7B0BxyGC930vpk2Fg\naviKsO8+qR22tbRK7DAg/OLEvH4VbNKP36LdjiuXodVm0nO+gM4XCy+4nofV82iw\nySFE+KEOpNKHrF/VX4KXfVWU1OMQoMCFb1PxPNIX+TKbHq9sUIpxYCXMU4AtgCzm\nw0djz3JVopfEM/lxXBgTkiZk+WZw6BpCM1mj9qsDqA+KXcY1H79bdiO+ZusMZ6UG\nFmLmdiXfOsoEZcrefHeZx4FFKTzFfuGofYtQhdxs4IkzYkKR3NjJPwWehrgh7AFl\nfqduuEMEnp+sH6vsAoRMstXZmY9t6CQC6cwDzfdDLdANsa/Ut4zcBGb8NVI6D1Vq\n5A0Pmnk+eg3mkxss47ti6shStC424wjLI2wMOxJhPUsvhAk4klQifq86a3IejPrY\nAoEt4b5OHKTqDcA9R305sA2FjJAIxEUMw+oyXYtFap9rRbKIT/PMd7/Q+Zt6GQvN\nGrqM+7IDtaBlyGf79bA65jG5nrhvDvV4Mgjf1WhBVT05vMshFca8Dx5IXofWwmNa\n11EbHdb0k34+gVJeDH9e\n=q9jl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T14:13:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/ea131f7f608689e746ba8a0be265ac929f02cdc5","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKGVhMTMxZjdmNjA4Njg5ZTc0NmJhOGEwYmUyNjVhYzkyOWYwMmNkYzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/a1b69653f1fca97228bde651e304e7d7d01682a1","sha":"a1b69653f1fca97228bde651e304e7d7d01682a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/a1b69653f1fca97228bde651e304e7d7d01682a1"}],"sha":"ea131f7f608689e746ba8a0be265ac929f02cdc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/ea131f7f608689e746ba8a0be265ac929f02cdc5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/a1b69653f1fca97228bde651e304e7d7d01682a1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:22:38Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":12,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:22:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: add path-scoped Claude rules and correct drifted agent guidance (#34851)\n\n* chore: add path-scoped Claude rules and fix orphaned agent docs\n\nAdds `.claude/rules/`, a thin path-scoped layer for guidance that is only\ncorrect in one part of the tree: the two runtime floors, which test runner a\npackage uses, how each kind of snapshot is regenerated, and which generated\nfiles must be regenerated rather than hand-edited. Each rule links back to the\nguide or AGENTS.md section that owns the topic, so they stay pointers rather\nthan a second source of truth and other agents can skip them.\n\n`.claude/*` was ignored except for settings.json and skills, so the new\ndirectory needed an explicit negation to be tracked at all.\n\nFour AGENTS.md files had no CLAUDE.md sibling and so never loaded for Claude\nCode, including `.circleci/` (which the root AGENTS.md points at) and\n`cli/lib/tap/render/`. Adds the missing stubs.\n\nAlso corrects the test-scoping guidance in AGENTS.md. Lerna unions `--scope`\nflags, and the root `test` script already sets ~20 of them, so\n`yarn test --scope <pkg>` broadened the run to the whole default suite instead\nof narrowing it. `yarn lint --scope` and `yarn check-ts --scope` are unaffected,\nsince those root scripts carry no pre-set scope.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GYbc8aoorHsVeNQLsofiQU\n\n* chore: use lists instead of tables in the Claude rules\n\nConverts the three tables in `.claude/rules/` to unordered lists. Content is\nunchanged; long cells no longer have to fit a column, so the runner, snapshot\nand regeneration entries read at any width.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GYbc8aoorHsVeNQLsofiQU\n\n* chore: correct the Claude rules'' path globs and runner claims\n\nReview of the previous commit found the rules layer largely inert and, in one\ncase, actively misleading.\n\nThe `paths:` globs were written against `*.spec.ts`, but this repo names specs\n`*_spec.ts` and `*.cy.js` — 164 of 165 server test files and 143 of 147\nsystem-tests files are `_spec`. The corrected globs reach 381 `_spec` and 879\n`.cy` files where the old ones reached almost none. The snapshot rule likewise\nmissed `packages/app/cypress/e2e/runner/snapshots/`, whose files are neither\n`__snapshots__/` nor `.snap`, so the one bullet describing them never loaded.\n\nCorrects three runner claims:\n\n- `@packages/driver` was listed as vitest. Its `test` script is vitest, but that\n  covers a handful of unit specs; the driver''s real coverage is 100+ `.cy.js`\n  specs run via `cypress:run`. A green `test` there says nothing about them.\n- `npm/webpack-preprocessor`''s `test` is the webpack-5 matrix script, which\n  swallows `-u`, rewrites `package.json` and reinstalls deps. Snapshot updates\n  go through `test-e2e -u`.\n- `@tooling/packherd` runs mocha and was missing from the mocha list.\n\n`yarn codegen` is a gulp watcher series that never exits, so it cannot be given\nas a one-shot regeneration command for autobarrel files. Adds\n`packages/errors/src/errors.ts` to the generated-files globs, since editing it\nis what triggers that rule''s schema.graphql warning.\n\nDocuments rules in CONTRIBUTING.md alongside skills, including the constraint\nthat a rule is a pointer rather than a source of truth, and the instruction to\ncheck globs against real filenames — an inert rule is worse than no rule.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GYbc8aoorHsVeNQLsofiQU\n\n* chore: stop caching derivable answers in the agent docs\n\nHand-maintained inventories of things a script could compute are the main way\nthis layer goes stale, and every example of it here was already wrong.\n\nThe test-runner rule enumerated which packages use vitest, mocha, jest and\nCypress — a snapshot of 60 package.json files that is wrong the first time\nanyone migrates a package. It now teaches the lookup instead, and keeps only the\npart a lookup cannot give you: the three packages whose `test` script exits 0\nwithout running the suite you care about.\n\nRoot AGENTS.md claimed \"32 packages total\" (35), \"15 packages\", \"3 packages\",\nand \"Version: 15.x\" while the develop line is 16 and `cli/package.json` is\n`0.0.0-development` under semantic-release. The counts are removed rather than\ncorrected, since the next one rots the same way, and the version now describes\nwhere the real number comes from.\n\nThe architecture inventory was missing six packages outright: agent-info,\ncypress-sessions, network-interception, example, root, and a distinct entry for\nnet-stubbing vs network-interception — the last mattering because net-stubbing''s\nown AGENTS.md delegates its core logic to a package the root file never named.\nAll are added, and the section now says plainly that it is orientation rather\nthan a registry, so a future gap reads as expected rather than as a claim.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GYbc8aoorHsVeNQLsofiQU\n\n* chore: dedupe repeated facts in AGENTS.md to one canonical home\n\nFacts stated in N places rot in N places, and three copies here were already\nwrong. Each cluster below now has one canonical description; the other files\ncarry a pointer, which cannot go stale because it states no facts.\n\nCorrections found while consolidating:\n\n- The adapter re-export does not copy `dist/`. `sync-exported-npm-with-cli.js`\n  resolves the file list with `npm-packlist` — the files npm would publish, per\n  the `files` key — wipes `cli/<name>/`, copies them, then rewrites the `exports`\n  map in `cli/package.json`. Five of the seven copies said `dist/`, and\n  mount-utils claimed a second destination that the script never writes.\n- `npm/webpack-dev-server` said cypress-in-cypress needs \"special env vars\"\n  without naming any; `npm/vite-dev-server` named one without its value. There\n  are two vars, not one: outer `CYPRESS_INTERNAL_E2E_TESTING_SELF_PARENT_PROJECT=1`\n  and inner `INTERNAL_E2E_TESTING_SELF_PARENT_PROJECT=true` via `--expose`.\n- `packages/AGENTS.md` said nohoist was set in `driver` and `frontend-shared`.\n  It is also set in `proxy`, `server`, `socket`, and `types`.\n- The v8-snapshot build command was quoted two different ways, neither complete.\n  The missing `rimraf` is precisely what makes the stale-blueprint failure mode\n  possible, and `ensure-typedefs` was absent from both.\n\nLeft deliberately duplicated: the per-package command blocks, which are\nparameterized by package name rather than copies of one statement, and the\n\"generated by tsc, do not edit\" lines, where the generator legitimately differs\nper package. Short invariants stated identically in two or three files are also\nleft in place — a pointer would be no shorter and less useful at the point of\nreading; where those disagreed, the wording is now aligned instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GYbc8aoorHsVeNQLsofiQU\n\n* chore: derive the user-Node floor instead of hardcoding it\n\nThe rule restated the `engines.node` range, the major derived from it, and the\n`.node-version` value, three lines below a link to the file that owns all three.\nA stale floor here is worse than no floor: it answers \"is this API safe\" with a\nnumber nobody rechecked.\n\nThe durable part is the derivation — the floor is the lowest major in\n`engines.node`, and it sits deliberately below the dev Node — so that is what\nthe rule now says, with the one-liner to read the current value. This matches\nhow the Runtime targets section of AGENTS.md already stated the same fact.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GYbc8aoorHsVeNQLsofiQU\n\n* chore: drop the driver spec extension from the test-runner rule\n\ndevelop is converting driver specs from `.cy.js` to `.cy.ts`, and the count has\nalready crossed over. Naming an extension and a count in the prose was the same\ncaching mistake the rule itself warns about, so it now just says \"its Cypress\nspecs under cypress/e2e\". The `paths:` glob already matched both extensions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GYbc8aoorHsVeNQLsofiQU\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1947fbb2987833af28997996220c88d40ffce7fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/1947fbb2987833af28997996220c88d40ffce7fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/a1b69653f1fca97228bde651e304e7d7d01682a1","verification":{"payload":"tree 1947fbb2987833af28997996220c88d40ffce7fa\nparent ce6f8fbf58b98b25527e99069029a15f022cb155\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1789482158 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789482158 -0400\n\nchore: add path-scoped Claude rules and correct drifted agent guidance (#34851)\n\n* chore: add path-scoped Claude rules and fix orphaned agent docs\n\nAdds `.claude/rules/`, a thin path-scoped layer for guidance that is only\ncorrect in one part of the tree: the two runtime floors, which test runner a\npackage uses, how each kind of snapshot is regenerated, and which generated\nfiles must be regenerated rather than hand-edited. Each rule links back to the\nguide or AGENTS.md section that owns the topic, so they stay pointers rather\nthan a second source of truth and other agents can skip them.\n\n`.claude/*` was ignored except for settings.json and skills, so the new\ndirectory needed an explicit negation to be tracked at all.\n\nFour AGENTS.md files had no CLAUDE.md sibling and so never loaded for Claude\nCode, including `.circleci/` (which the root AGENTS.md points at) and\n`cli/lib/tap/render/`. Adds the missing stubs.\n\nAlso corrects the test-scoping guidance in AGENTS.md. Lerna unions `--scope`\nflags, and the root `test` script already sets ~20 of them, so\n`yarn test --scope <pkg>` broadened the run to the whole default suite instead\nof narrowing it. `yarn lint --scope` and `yarn check-ts --scope` are unaffected,\nsince those root scripts carry no pre-set scope.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GYbc8aoorHsVeNQLsofiQU\n\n* chore: use lists instead of tables in the Claude rules\n\nConverts the three tables in `.claude/rules/` to unordered lists. Content is\nunchanged; long cells no longer have to fit a column, so the runner, snapshot\nand regeneration entries read at any width.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GYbc8aoorHsVeNQLsofiQU\n\n* chore: correct the Claude rules'' path globs and runner claims\n\nReview of the previous commit found the rules layer largely inert and, in one\ncase, actively misleading.\n\nThe `paths:` globs were written against `*.spec.ts`, but this repo names specs\n`*_spec.ts` and `*.cy.js` — 164 of 165 server test files and 143 of 147\nsystem-tests files are `_spec`. The corrected globs reach 381 `_spec` and 879\n`.cy` files where the old ones reached almost none. The snapshot rule likewise\nmissed `packages/app/cypress/e2e/runner/snapshots/`, whose files are neither\n`__snapshots__/` nor `.snap`, so the one bullet describing them never loaded.\n\nCorrects three runner claims:\n\n- `@packages/driver` was listed as vitest. Its `test` script is vitest, but that\n  covers a handful of unit specs; the driver''s real coverage is 100+ `.cy.js`\n  specs run via `cypress:run`. A green `test` there says nothing about them.\n- `npm/webpack-preprocessor`''s `test` is the webpack-5 matrix script, which\n  swallows `-u`, rewrites `package.json` and reinstalls deps. Snapshot updates\n  go through `test-e2e -u`.\n- `@tooling/packherd` runs mocha and was missing from the mocha list.\n\n`yarn codegen` is a gulp watcher series that never exits, so it cannot be given\nas a one-shot regeneration command for autobarrel files. Adds\n`packages/errors/src/errors.ts` to the generated-files globs, since editing it\nis what triggers that rule''s schema.graphql warning.\n\nDocuments rules in CONTRIBUTING.md alongside skills, including the constraint\nthat a rule is a pointer rather than a source of truth, and the instruction to\ncheck globs against real filenames — an inert rule is worse than no rule.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GYbc8aoorHsVeNQLsofiQU\n\n* chore: stop caching derivable answers in the agent docs\n\nHand-maintained inventories of things a script could compute are the main way\nthis layer goes stale, and every example of it here was already wrong.\n\nThe test-runner rule enumerated which packages use vitest, mocha, jest and\nCypress — a snapshot of 60 package.json files that is wrong the first time\nanyone migrates a package. It now teaches the lookup instead, and keeps only the\npart a lookup cannot give you: the three packages whose `test` script exits 0\nwithout running the suite you care about.\n\nRoot AGENTS.md claimed \"32 packages total\" (35), \"15 packages\", \"3 packages\",\nand \"Version: 15.x\" while the develop line is 16 and `cli/package.json` is\n`0.0.0-development` under semantic-release. The counts are removed rather than\ncorrected, since the next one rots the same way, and the version now describes\nwhere the real number comes from.\n\nThe architecture inventory was missing six packages outright: agent-info,\ncypress-sessions, network-interception, example, root, and a distinct entry for\nnet-stubbing vs network-interception — the last mattering because net-stubbing''s\nown AGENTS.md delegates its core logic to a package the root file never named.\nAll are added, and the section now says plainly that it is orientation rather\nthan a registry, so a future gap reads as expected rather than as a claim.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GYbc8aoorHsVeNQLsofiQU\n\n* chore: dedupe repeated facts in AGENTS.md to one canonical home\n\nFacts stated in N places rot in N places, and three copies here were already\nwrong. Each cluster below now has one canonical description; the other files\ncarry a pointer, which cannot go stale because it states no facts.\n\nCorrections found while consolidating:\n\n- The adapter re-export does not copy `dist/`. `sync-exported-npm-with-cli.js`\n  resolves the file list with `npm-packlist` — the files npm would publish, per\n  the `files` key — wipes `cli/<name>/`, copies them, then rewrites the `exports`\n  map in `cli/package.json`. Five of the seven copies said `dist/`, and\n  mount-utils claimed a second destination that the script never writes.\n- `npm/webpack-dev-server` said cypress-in-cypress needs \"special env vars\"\n  without naming any; `npm/vite-dev-server` named one without its value. There\n  are two vars, not one: outer `CYPRESS_INTERNAL_E2E_TESTING_SELF_PARENT_PROJECT=1`\n  and inner `INTERNAL_E2E_TESTING_SELF_PARENT_PROJECT=true` via `--expose`.\n- `packages/AGENTS.md` said nohoist was set in `driver` and `frontend-shared`.\n  It is also set in `proxy`, `server`, `socket`, and `types`.\n- The v8-snapshot build command was quoted two different ways, neither complete.\n  The missing `rimraf` is precisely what makes the stale-blueprint failure mode\n  possible, and `ensure-typedefs` was absent from both.\n\nLeft deliberately duplicated: the per-package command blocks, which are\nparameterized by package name rather than copies of one statement, and the\n\"generated by tsc, do not edit\" lines, where the generator legitimately differs\nper package. Short invariants stated identically in two or three files are also\nleft in place — a pointer would be no shorter and less useful at the point of\nreading; where those disagreed, the wording is now aligned instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GYbc8aoorHsVeNQLsofiQU\n\n* chore: derive the user-Node floor instead of hardcoding it\n\nThe rule restated the `engines.node` range, the major derived from it, and the\n`.node-version` value, three lines below a link to the file that owns all three.\nA stale floor here is worse than no floor: it answers \"is this API safe\" with a\nnumber nobody rechecked.\n\nThe durable part is the derivation — the floor is the lowest major in\n`engines.node`, and it sits deliberately below the dev Node — so that is what\nthe rule now says, with the one-liner to read the current value. This matches\nhow the Runtime targets section of AGENTS.md already stated the same fact.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GYbc8aoorHsVeNQLsofiQU\n\n* chore: drop the driver spec extension from the test-runner rule\n\ndevelop is converting driver specs from `.cy.js` to `.cy.ts`, and the count has\nalready crossed over. Naming an extension and a count in the prose was the same\ncaching mistake the rule itself warns about, so it now just says \"its Cypress\nspecs under cypress/e2e\". The `paths:` glob already matched both extensions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GYbc8aoorHsVeNQLsofiQU\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqVSuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzFwQAIuftxOVZ81ZqDzbNDXjOdK5\nkQJxmtRlBQHe3NERegEiCetH+RzDECjUTmB4QnNnrx5E6FCX7emfiHbfEis2eF7L\nyGWZrfxufG20Gn9xACHDP31qvtWrMsmjjueYm9X58T17wEfWC1xLBRPW097dgrJ0\nK/5wte94l2qd6XrtF9AkqbffFWxC672NLZQw1P0profEwo5FFQfVj0Pic+zl+/60\n0WNTEIUGoWJaGOXBDtrLYxEg8Hl3vL7tb6AkBUFIWxNq4jcb/SulezWdM0Y1b4jq\nLUMHKf/L+33p9h3XMn26Uwr85HvEUGMoZsQWmPwzWwRbG2k4Gxwm2hJHyrVWe/QF\nqeC3yxlTtxVYie3HehCc6vS2EoOArTfp7z8Fg7AEU6RHq7nnSWBXMhQWd0yi1QTB\nSKtyUoiGOTEdTRa72T5VABq3WDDgj7MZhc5/rxz5ndX4g6koQpDvG6nY/Z9NrQ+8\ntgIWSUZd/rViSib94Z7UTQ3Otb4RA8VV+sHdfJ/PkU6dUw1j8cwdBGgRnJ4ruQGT\ng4Uw3pl72fM9jAip1K4S75jWqcOEqfDxuarKDS9C7M80X6tnXVixVZw3BufJd3cu\nA+tWkfqg26NedIUSMzeTAeQyFTu1rSRX12fUyPOu8uvrZ7+AcxFgcz987eFfFRIs\n0ZxErqZqfLXrdbFL2Tlx\n=4fFQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T14:22:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/a1b69653f1fca97228bde651e304e7d7d01682a1","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKGExYjY5NjUzZjFmY2E5NzIyOGJkZTY1MWUzMDRlN2Q3ZDAxNjgyYTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/ce6f8fbf58b98b25527e99069029a15f022cb155","sha":"ce6f8fbf58b98b25527e99069029a15f022cb155","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/ce6f8fbf58b98b25527e99069029a15f022cb155"}],"sha":"a1b69653f1fca97228bde651e304e7d7d01682a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/a1b69653f1fca97228bde651e304e7d7d01682a1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/ce6f8fbf58b98b25527e99069029a15f022cb155/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T13:24:25Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":2,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T13:24:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: convert three driver specs to TypeScript (#34854)\n\n* chore: convert driver navigation spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/cy/navigation.cy.js to .ts. No other\nspec imports it, so the conversion lands on its own.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GQXzB5ap9FEzbAocw5QRrM\n\n* chore: type the navigation spec state with StateFunc\n\n$SetterGetter.create infers a two-argument call signature, so reading a\nkey back with a single argument does not type-check. Cast through\nStateFunc, the same type Cypress.state uses.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GQXzB5ap9FEzbAocw5QRrM\n\n* chore: convert driver currentTest spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/cypress/currentTest.cy.js to .ts. The\nspec type-checks as-is; no source changes were needed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GQXzB5ap9FEzbAocw5QRrM\n\n* chore: convert driver script_utils spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/cypress/script_utils.cy.js to .ts and\nswap the require calls for imports, keeping the module specifiers so the\nstubs still patch the instances script_utils itself loads.\n\nrunScripts is typed for the real spec-loading inputs, while these tests\nfeed it partial browser, window and script fakes, so calls route through\na helper that casts once. The created-script fakes declare src, which a\nreal script element carries.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GQXzB5ap9FEzbAocw5QRrM\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"96ec75dca35fbd480b8ec95fc5babe019cbcf1d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/96ec75dca35fbd480b8ec95fc5babe019cbcf1d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/ce6f8fbf58b98b25527e99069029a15f022cb155","verification":{"payload":"tree 96ec75dca35fbd480b8ec95fc5babe019cbcf1d5\nparent 4d374e0009de8563c434bf9ea3502bc0b9eedbbe\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1789478665 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789478665 -0400\n\nchore: convert three driver specs to TypeScript (#34854)\n\n* chore: convert driver navigation spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/cy/navigation.cy.js to .ts. No other\nspec imports it, so the conversion lands on its own.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GQXzB5ap9FEzbAocw5QRrM\n\n* chore: type the navigation spec state with StateFunc\n\n$SetterGetter.create infers a two-argument call signature, so reading a\nkey back with a single argument does not type-check. Cast through\nStateFunc, the same type Cypress.state uses.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GQXzB5ap9FEzbAocw5QRrM\n\n* chore: convert driver currentTest spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/cypress/currentTest.cy.js to .ts. The\nspec type-checks as-is; no source changes were needed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GQXzB5ap9FEzbAocw5QRrM\n\n* chore: convert driver script_utils spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/cypress/script_utils.cy.js to .ts and\nswap the require calls for imports, keeping the module specifiers so the\nstubs still patch the instances script_utils itself loads.\n\nrunScripts is typed for the real spec-loading inputs, while these tests\nfeed it partial browser, window and script fakes, so calls route through\na helper that casts once. The created-script fakes declare src, which a\nreal script element carries.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GQXzB5ap9FEzbAocw5QRrM\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqUcJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAM8AQAAmK1FfZ9glGSsz383bmdE+p\nDQM7qyZXu3BTqF3JTetDZad3ca6FbLI8HkD5+kSx7iqPSKHh2lIVyYJq2UW54+bG\nIifliqmhfxzyqeSdUCep4Oac5gbq/4KGASQ0dL8ZyWXCNZqQ0NqlBu6fWtW+5oqG\nM51FLeCxn7rfpDKAPTgITw7ZnHY0Miks1VZ8WB7ttDG2/cCmD13SdECWxQYZdgUg\n1OG/MO4Qd2SnASkGIt/+UQqGp/FwBNOYbnDVgGk58wZKLElwHv4xbHxwiKTP0sr8\ne2vsFglA9mrdAkGmbxHqkZPC5nUmFPZj+i4yNrm3+wb4jdDsx04eQ5DEboO/mbqP\neW2T2PJ9poQPIS+IYv0gJsf56wn8wdanljKcZp0F0G1QU2D8EX6oQai5mvPjd0z6\nOObSh0CINCfF58UefLKQN73fjPeHNo1X/Mg4lFneGR07QgrXvpLFQhVvt4ypNx4a\nloUYSIYiJtuAG5s/9+83/G6o7beFU3MtCv0qHqmC59lyiv3ytdEr1IiDCTL6vk7R\n0Od/AIBuSsSPZCEukUNQJHlkObOydY6vwf0ycT4Sa7/9FH8lAvtE1gbNZVv7XSPC\nOfsRRqb28Fv6mN5eclDJ2wgf55nfMc5Fopdg0Tl08y63QY7BDvRwPdE62gbsQffI\nbeELlFJ0cE/XIla4w7cr\n=JEoq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T13:24:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/ce6f8fbf58b98b25527e99069029a15f022cb155","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKGNlNmY4ZmJmNThiOThiMjU1MjdlOTkwNjkwMjlhMTVmMDIyY2IxNTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/4d374e0009de8563c434bf9ea3502bc0b9eedbbe","sha":"4d374e0009de8563c434bf9ea3502bc0b9eedbbe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/4d374e0009de8563c434bf9ea3502bc0b9eedbbe"}],"sha":"ce6f8fbf58b98b25527e99069029a15f022cb155","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/ce6f8fbf58b98b25527e99069029a15f022cb155"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/4d374e0009de8563c434bf9ea3502bc0b9eedbbe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T13:24:08Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":2,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T13:24:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: convert three driver cypress specs to TypeScript (#34853)\n\n* chore: convert driver command spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/cypress/command.cy.js to .ts.\n\n`Cypress.Command` is assigned at runtime but is not part of the public\n`Cypress` type, so destructuring it does not type check. Import the\n`$Command` class from the driver source instead, matching the sibling\ncommand_queue spec.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013ETepm3daiynD4mpaWdXmM\n\n* chore: convert driver network_utils spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/cypress/network_utils.cy.js to .ts and\nreplace the `require` of the driver source with a relative import, matching\nthe sibling specs already on TypeScript.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013ETepm3daiynD4mpaWdXmM\n\n* chore: convert driver runner spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/cypress/runner.cy.js to .ts and resolve\nthe type errors the rename surfaced:\n\n- Mark the spec as a module so the top-level `const { _ } = Cypress` no\n  longer collides with the global lodash declaration.\n- Type the collected `test:after:run` attributes as `Cypress.ObjectLike[]`,\n  which otherwise infer as `never[]`.\n- Drop the `return` from the event handler, whose value is unused, to\n  satisfy `noImplicitReturns`.\n- Guard the `_.last` lookup in the root after hook, which is optional.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013ETepm3daiynD4mpaWdXmM\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f064ab8a9866ceb6435473392f8c2e5d645c32e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/f064ab8a9866ceb6435473392f8c2e5d645c32e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/4d374e0009de8563c434bf9ea3502bc0b9eedbbe","verification":{"payload":"tree f064ab8a9866ceb6435473392f8c2e5d645c32e0\nparent eeba28d83089027ea61cf67b806550606d65dc19\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1789478648 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789478648 -0400\n\ntest: convert three driver cypress specs to TypeScript (#34853)\n\n* chore: convert driver command spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/cypress/command.cy.js to .ts.\n\n`Cypress.Command` is assigned at runtime but is not part of the public\n`Cypress` type, so destructuring it does not type check. Import the\n`$Command` class from the driver source instead, matching the sibling\ncommand_queue spec.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013ETepm3daiynD4mpaWdXmM\n\n* chore: convert driver network_utils spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/cypress/network_utils.cy.js to .ts and\nreplace the `require` of the driver source with a relative import, matching\nthe sibling specs already on TypeScript.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013ETepm3daiynD4mpaWdXmM\n\n* chore: convert driver runner spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/cypress/runner.cy.js to .ts and resolve\nthe type errors the rename surfaced:\n\n- Mark the spec as a module so the top-level `const { _ } = Cypress` no\n  longer collides with the global lodash declaration.\n- Type the collected `test:after:run` attributes as `Cypress.ObjectLike[]`,\n  which otherwise infer as `never[]`.\n- Drop the `return` from the event handler, whose value is unused, to\n  satisfy `noImplicitReturns`.\n- Guard the `_.last` lookup in the root after hook, which is optional.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013ETepm3daiynD4mpaWdXmM\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqUb4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8twQAJLCnl/ywmLlp4u0t/wMayAI\niaoi/rUJdT6pN7kVTWrRb9peBpa2/QQ3/DqCNdiqvXtGBcT/kDp01USDebaa+Ms4\nj7eo/xNDLe0tJMz3a1t0loLf0pkJnt7j4huOcUs0GZZFsaIca+wznJz8VSrj+FJz\niPnirovqvD21lsj2D57+VJgoWt8Pa96m8gBkw37EHbaHv1of/3SAP2AvnI4gjWpq\nL+GlkoWSJXQnH+yzhmes52RqcMXQjBwqxXqBFOZuVu+wJ+4MFq9CTRwmQe4zNpWc\n1Bj+Vm9uaMlmsMK78NLysd7KhXNfUIUnFBbjKSWkAjla91Ev2PYg9w+sBd6NW/YB\nbQgF3B5aZBHhQvUm5S1nuhB6YXrrsbAamcAHVLc361PSByWEhKTLLNHe3uGDyDBa\nlLeyZdGsUn75el7Ah6eBqsbUjceSDijp3H0Wa/rxHVZSuxkXqq/uxI0FGeipx1vF\nhajmYV9O1fMW+NtKFSBhsdCk8gFiVMQ8kIfFbA0Sg0qh1abyX5lgX1AJl6NRWYEY\n1DjSWy3s33aIPplNpM6hCJl498mxG6ZgQc4/CBVh35vQ7cVwcUXwowIM/YK8W7ba\nQflXgWcA6eCFXde4qywE7868j5FI95g1Qhn49GAK7vY2zuTGbv9LVKZDHXGan8gB\nqIQsFVDKjVIvFGwocA5W\n=KGkX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T13:24:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/4d374e0009de8563c434bf9ea3502bc0b9eedbbe","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDRkMzc0ZTAwMDlkZTg1NjNjNDM0YmY5ZWEzNTAyYmMwYjllZWRiYmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/eeba28d83089027ea61cf67b806550606d65dc19","sha":"eeba28d83089027ea61cf67b806550606d65dc19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/eeba28d83089027ea61cf67b806550606d65dc19"}],"sha":"4d374e0009de8563c434bf9ea3502bc0b9eedbbe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/4d374e0009de8563c434bf9ea3502bc0b9eedbbe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/eeba28d83089027ea61cf67b806550606d65dc19/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T13:23:44Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":2,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T13:23:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: convert four driver specs to TypeScript and take the cookie prefix tests offline (#34852)\n\n* test: convert the driver e2e cookies spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `e2e_cookies.cy.js` to `.ts` and resolve the type errors that\nsurfaced:\n\n- `cy.getCookie(''foo'', ''bar'')` passed a value where `CookieOptions` is\n  expected. The second argument was never used, so drop it.\n- `cy.getCookie()` resolves to `Cookie | null`, and `expect(cookie).exist`\n  does not narrow the type, so assert non-null before reading properties.\n- Type the `cleanse` parameter as `Cypress.Cookie[]`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Urz2XAX5MQvG8nQMm3Mh8u\n\n* test: resolve remaining type errors in the e2e cookies spec\n\n`const { _ } = Cypress` collides with the global lodash `_` in a file with\nno imports, since TypeScript treats it as a script rather than a module.\n`_` was used once, so read it off `Cypress` at the call site instead.\n\nGive the `cloneDeepWith` customizer an explicit `undefined` branch to\nsatisfy `noImplicitReturns`; returning `undefined` is already what the\nimplicit path did, and it is what tells lodash to clone the value normally.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Urz2XAX5MQvG8nQMm3Mh8u\n\n* test: convert the driver limited map spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `limited_map.cy.js` to `.ts` and replace the `require()` of\n`@packages/driver/src/util/limited_map` with a relative `import`, matching\nthe other specs in this directory. The import also makes the file a module,\nso `const _ = Cypress._` no longer collides with the global lodash `_`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Urz2XAX5MQvG8nQMm3Mh8u\n\n* test: convert the driver buffer spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `buffer.cy.js` to `.ts`. No code changes are needed: `Encodings`\nalready admits `null`, so the `cy.readFile(path, null)` overload resolves\nand yields the `any` that `Cypress.Buffer.isBuffer()` accepts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Urz2XAX5MQvG8nQMm3Mh8u\n\n* test: convert the driver security spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `security.cy.js` to `.ts`. The spec is three statements against the\nglobal `cy`, so the rename alone type-checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Urz2XAX5MQvG8nQMm3Mh8u\n\n* test: point the cookie prefix tests at a local https origin\n\nThe `__Host-` and `__Secure-` tests visited `https://example.com`, so they\nneeded live internet access to run at all.\n\nThe driver suite already serves every fixture over https on ports 3502/3503,\nand `cypress.config.ts` maps `*.foobar.com` to 127.0.0.1, so\n`https://www.foobar.com:3502` is a same-origin https target that the sibling\ncookie specs already use.\n\nThe behavior under test is unchanged. The prefix validation in\n`cy.setCookie()` reads only its options, never the current origin, so the\nthree error cases are origin-independent. The two cases that do set a cookie\nneed a real https origin because the CDP converter swaps `domain` for `url` on\n`__Host-` cookies, and a local https origin satisfies that the same way\n`example.com` did.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Urz2XAX5MQvG8nQMm3Mh8u\n\n* test: drop the retry overrides from the cookie prefix tests\n\nThese five tests carried `{ retries: 15 }` and a flake TODO because they\ndepended on reaching `https://example.com`. Now that they run against the\nlocal https server, the retry budget is no longer earning anything: the spec\npassed 20 consecutive runs with `retries=0`, in 16-18s each.\n\nThey fall back to the suite-wide `retries: 2` that every other driver spec\ngets, set in `cypress/support/defaults.ts`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Urz2XAX5MQvG8nQMm3Mh8u\n\n* test: use the apex domain in the cookie prefix tests\n\n`example.com` is an apex domain, so `www.foobar.com` changed the shape of what\nthese tests assert against: a subdomain resolves to a different superdomain\nthan the host itself.\n\n`foobar.com` is mapped in `hosts` alongside `*.foobar.com`, and the apex\nreturns the same cookie shapes the original did — `foobar.com` (dotless,\nhost-only) for `__Host-` and `.foobar.com` for `__Secure-`, which is what the\noptional leading dot in the assertions is there to accept.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Urz2XAX5MQvG8nQMm3Mh8u\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3d2b200fd556e0febd762d9f2fc9b5452ee385de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/3d2b200fd556e0febd762d9f2fc9b5452ee385de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/eeba28d83089027ea61cf67b806550606d65dc19","verification":{"payload":"tree 3d2b200fd556e0febd762d9f2fc9b5452ee385de\nparent 83902dc838d4a242e88df8cfa3da8a196c681731\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1789478624 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789478624 -0400\n\ntest: convert four driver specs to TypeScript and take the cookie prefix tests offline (#34852)\n\n* test: convert the driver e2e cookies spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `e2e_cookies.cy.js` to `.ts` and resolve the type errors that\nsurfaced:\n\n- `cy.getCookie(''foo'', ''bar'')` passed a value where `CookieOptions` is\n  expected. The second argument was never used, so drop it.\n- `cy.getCookie()` resolves to `Cookie | null`, and `expect(cookie).exist`\n  does not narrow the type, so assert non-null before reading properties.\n- Type the `cleanse` parameter as `Cypress.Cookie[]`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Urz2XAX5MQvG8nQMm3Mh8u\n\n* test: resolve remaining type errors in the e2e cookies spec\n\n`const { _ } = Cypress` collides with the global lodash `_` in a file with\nno imports, since TypeScript treats it as a script rather than a module.\n`_` was used once, so read it off `Cypress` at the call site instead.\n\nGive the `cloneDeepWith` customizer an explicit `undefined` branch to\nsatisfy `noImplicitReturns`; returning `undefined` is already what the\nimplicit path did, and it is what tells lodash to clone the value normally.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Urz2XAX5MQvG8nQMm3Mh8u\n\n* test: convert the driver limited map spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `limited_map.cy.js` to `.ts` and replace the `require()` of\n`@packages/driver/src/util/limited_map` with a relative `import`, matching\nthe other specs in this directory. The import also makes the file a module,\nso `const _ = Cypress._` no longer collides with the global lodash `_`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Urz2XAX5MQvG8nQMm3Mh8u\n\n* test: convert the driver buffer spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `buffer.cy.js` to `.ts`. No code changes are needed: `Encodings`\nalready admits `null`, so the `cy.readFile(path, null)` overload resolves\nand yields the `any` that `Cypress.Buffer.isBuffer()` accepts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Urz2XAX5MQvG8nQMm3Mh8u\n\n* test: convert the driver security spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `security.cy.js` to `.ts`. The spec is three statements against the\nglobal `cy`, so the rename alone type-checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Urz2XAX5MQvG8nQMm3Mh8u\n\n* test: point the cookie prefix tests at a local https origin\n\nThe `__Host-` and `__Secure-` tests visited `https://example.com`, so they\nneeded live internet access to run at all.\n\nThe driver suite already serves every fixture over https on ports 3502/3503,\nand `cypress.config.ts` maps `*.foobar.com` to 127.0.0.1, so\n`https://www.foobar.com:3502` is a same-origin https target that the sibling\ncookie specs already use.\n\nThe behavior under test is unchanged. The prefix validation in\n`cy.setCookie()` reads only its options, never the current origin, so the\nthree error cases are origin-independent. The two cases that do set a cookie\nneed a real https origin because the CDP converter swaps `domain` for `url` on\n`__Host-` cookies, and a local https origin satisfies that the same way\n`example.com` did.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Urz2XAX5MQvG8nQMm3Mh8u\n\n* test: drop the retry overrides from the cookie prefix tests\n\nThese five tests carried `{ retries: 15 }` and a flake TODO because they\ndepended on reaching `https://example.com`. Now that they run against the\nlocal https server, the retry budget is no longer earning anything: the spec\npassed 20 consecutive runs with `retries=0`, in 16-18s each.\n\nThey fall back to the suite-wide `retries: 2` that every other driver spec\ngets, set in `cypress/support/defaults.ts`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Urz2XAX5MQvG8nQMm3Mh8u\n\n* test: use the apex domain in the cookie prefix tests\n\n`example.com` is an apex domain, so `www.foobar.com` changed the shape of what\nthese tests assert against: a subdomain resolves to a different superdomain\nthan the host itself.\n\n`foobar.com` is mapped in `hosts` alongside `*.foobar.com`, and the apex\nreturns the same cookie shapes the original did — `foobar.com` (dotless,\nhost-only) for `__Host-` and `.foobar.com` for `__Secure-`, which is what the\noptional leading dot in the assertions is there to accept.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Urz2XAX5MQvG8nQMm3Mh8u\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqUbgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZL4QACbbzroObcpo4BXsIbZmvtdz\nbedC3sTcfy1d01vsQimsgjC85Z+s9HRR6kd70Pm3hkWpBBUPVn4kjEFVU1kElaQb\nxAfOunof3Mpu2ot7b26rcGUMmcAxxHF7u8MymqUacHP21FjlKle441qLjlgNQ47d\na7t8gNSKqD5FPW6lWAimCNAienPZ0zjGuOOiURWiKSwHZijz0HX4MrqU+SEOynrU\ntmIGaAQNkeoEkp4gfJYP0ni51r93/M/IW6fo4vtOaeqa37CiTR/tE1Pa/kd51W1n\nV/zfr8eGy440tJePAC/gdgewSvNDpPgJ4bSQrMA+QWXb2cILyLwt50P8gTrSj2ma\ne0ZCDiBP7XclLwH4lcRtZu7GBERHl6thxwXlZ4Vl517hgy96quKjxYWK1ZtSqMQZ\ngUco0QPvfHfXQlzoN/h6QitNSBpUhI/NS+yThZoSCbM3kSPkFbz9uxS+aed10KoR\n41J01XbO+2IfvfaLNbrg2In9+3oVOm0cNplXlXs2hhgO5Hjjh+tp5wQT0Ots0brq\nVuzD3abpbVYU6E5SKQWO+sXdF9+5Tp0whx+BLf8C3RFN6+wOUA4lDFAeqZzZ353X\n0P3iJAnesoL3W0aeZCO0mOBStpr9RB0Vbi8z/DCs7oW/gEBBPyxbIePuFhEN1iqU\nCkWmgxwCdsXTOwjrhs4t\n=WndR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T13:23:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/eeba28d83089027ea61cf67b806550606d65dc19","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKGVlYmEyOGQ4MzA4OTAyN2VhNjFjZjY3YjgwNjU1MDYwNmQ2NWRjMTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/83902dc838d4a242e88df8cfa3da8a196c681731","sha":"83902dc838d4a242e88df8cfa3da8a196c681731","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/83902dc838d4a242e88df8cfa3da8a196c681731"}],"sha":"eeba28d83089027ea61cf67b806550606d65dc19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/eeba28d83089027ea61cf67b806550606d65dc19"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/83902dc838d4a242e88df8cfa3da8a196c681731/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T01:16:53Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":9,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T01:16:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: convert driver e2e, memory, and Keyboard specs to TypeScript (#34848)\n\n* chore: convert ended_early and keyboard driver specs to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/ended_early.cy.js and\nkeyboard.cy.js to .ts.\n\nended_early needed no changes. In keyboard, the `characters` table\ninferred as (string | number)[][], so the destructured `char` was not\nassignable to cy.type(). Annotating it as a labelled tuple keeps the\nthree columns self-documenting at the call site.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QodC2Tbhqdime1pTbxpo6q\n\n* chore: convert memory driver specs to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/memory/dom-stress-test.cy.js and\nmemory.cy.js to .ts.\n\nmemory needed no changes. In dom-stress-test, `counts` infers as\nnumber[], so the count was not assignable to cy.type(). Interpolate it\ninstead, matching the template-literal form used elsewhere in the driver\nspecs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QodC2Tbhqdime1pTbxpo6q\n\n* chore: convert Cypress.Keyboard API spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/cypress/keyboard.cy.js to .ts.\n\nThe published Cypress.Keyboard type describes only the documented\ndefaults() and Keys, while this spec drives the internal surface, so\nnarrow it once at the top rather than casting at each call site.\n\nThe two negative tests pass deliberately invalid arguments to assert the\nruntime guards, so they need @ts-expect-error.\n\n@types/chai declares `eql` on the root assertion but not on `deep`, so\n`expect(result).to.deep.eql(...)` does not type-check. The chainer works\nat runtime and the assertion was never skipped; `eql` is already a deep\ncomparison, so call it directly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QodC2Tbhqdime1pTbxpo6q\n\n* chore: make the driver''s InternalKeyboard type usable\n\nInternalKeyboard was inert. It was merged onto Cypress.Cypress as\n`Keyboard`, which the published cypress.d.ts already declares, and a\nduplicate interface member must be declared with an identical type. The\nmismatch is an error inside a .d.ts, which skipLibCheck drops, so the\npublished declaration silently won and Cypress.Keyboard.reset() did not\ntype-check anywhere.\n\nIt was also inaccurate three ways: it extended Partial<Keyboard>, which\nresolves to the DOM Keyboard (getLayoutMap/lock/unlock) rather than\nanything Cypress; it declared getMap, while the export is getKeymap; and\nit truncated Keys to TAB.\n\nDerive it from the module Cypress.Keyboard is actually assigned so it\ncannot drift, and drop the merge that never applied. Callers cast to it\nexplicitly, which is what the keyboard spec now does.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QodC2Tbhqdime1pTbxpo6q\n\n* chore: tighten comments on the keyboard spec and internal type\n\nThe @ts-expect-error reasons restated the test titles directly above\nthem. Say instead that the argument is deliberately invalid, which is\nthe part the code does not already express.\n\nState the InternalKeyboard constraint in the present tense rather than\nas an alternative that was ruled out.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QodC2Tbhqdime1pTbxpo6q\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"11f50a8447eb9692f7a9577a56511a9a50e2fc54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/11f50a8447eb9692f7a9577a56511a9a50e2fc54"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/83902dc838d4a242e88df8cfa3da8a196c681731","verification":{"payload":"tree 11f50a8447eb9692f7a9577a56511a9a50e2fc54\nparent 5c4226b04285a578d2cfc98ca54725fc9042e6a7\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1789435013 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789435013 -0400\n\ntest: convert driver e2e, memory, and Keyboard specs to TypeScript (#34848)\n\n* chore: convert ended_early and keyboard driver specs to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/ended_early.cy.js and\nkeyboard.cy.js to .ts.\n\nended_early needed no changes. In keyboard, the `characters` table\ninferred as (string | number)[][], so the destructured `char` was not\nassignable to cy.type(). Annotating it as a labelled tuple keeps the\nthree columns self-documenting at the call site.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QodC2Tbhqdime1pTbxpo6q\n\n* chore: convert memory driver specs to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/memory/dom-stress-test.cy.js and\nmemory.cy.js to .ts.\n\nmemory needed no changes. In dom-stress-test, `counts` infers as\nnumber[], so the count was not assignable to cy.type(). Interpolate it\ninstead, matching the template-literal form used elsewhere in the driver\nspecs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QodC2Tbhqdime1pTbxpo6q\n\n* chore: convert Cypress.Keyboard API spec to TypeScript\n\nRename packages/driver/cypress/e2e/cypress/keyboard.cy.js to .ts.\n\nThe published Cypress.Keyboard type describes only the documented\ndefaults() and Keys, while this spec drives the internal surface, so\nnarrow it once at the top rather than casting at each call site.\n\nThe two negative tests pass deliberately invalid arguments to assert the\nruntime guards, so they need @ts-expect-error.\n\n@types/chai declares `eql` on the root assertion but not on `deep`, so\n`expect(result).to.deep.eql(...)` does not type-check. The chainer works\nat runtime and the assertion was never skipped; `eql` is already a deep\ncomparison, so call it directly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QodC2Tbhqdime1pTbxpo6q\n\n* chore: make the driver''s InternalKeyboard type usable\n\nInternalKeyboard was inert. It was merged onto Cypress.Cypress as\n`Keyboard`, which the published cypress.d.ts already declares, and a\nduplicate interface member must be declared with an identical type. The\nmismatch is an error inside a .d.ts, which skipLibCheck drops, so the\npublished declaration silently won and Cypress.Keyboard.reset() did not\ntype-check anywhere.\n\nIt was also inaccurate three ways: it extended Partial<Keyboard>, which\nresolves to the DOM Keyboard (getLayoutMap/lock/unlock) rather than\nanything Cypress; it declared getMap, while the export is getKeymap; and\nit truncated Keys to TAB.\n\nDerive it from the module Cypress.Keyboard is actually assigned so it\ncannot drift, and drop the merge that never applied. Callers cast to it\nexplicitly, which is what the keyboard spec now does.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QodC2Tbhqdime1pTbxpo6q\n\n* chore: tighten comments on the keyboard spec and internal type\n\nThe @ts-expect-error reasons restated the test titles directly above\nthem. Say instead that the argument is deliberately invalid, which is\nthe part the code does not already express.\n\nState the InternalKeyboard constraint in the present tense rather than\nas an alternative that was ruled out.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QodC2Tbhqdime1pTbxpo6q\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","sign