jCC3sJGtDiNXCIJlKqip8uGwbLOn\n5deD3sHT62YqdaPKAHnm\n=8mIY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T19:37:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/898db843544b446a95eb4ff72908c8d19ab89d2a","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDg5OGRiODQzNTQ0YjQ0NmE5NWViNGZmNzI5MDhjOGQxOWFiODlkMmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/025716642e69ef2c6dd72e4564e523d6c691db5a","sha":"025716642e69ef2c6dd72e4564e523d6c691db5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/025716642e69ef2c6dd72e4564e523d6c691db5a"}],"sha":"898db843544b446a95eb4ff72908c8d19ab89d2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/898db843544b446a95eb4ff72908c8d19ab89d2a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/025716642e69ef2c6dd72e4564e523d6c691db5a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T19:29:53Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":4,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T19:29:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: restore run mode Electron window size on Windows (#34773)\n\n* fix: restore run mode Electron window size on Windows\n\nElectron 41.3+ reserves part of the client area of a frameless window\nwith a thick frame for resize hit targets on Windows, which shrinks the\nweb contents - and with it every failure screenshot and video frame -\nbelow the size the browser was launched with. The hidden run mode window\nis never resized by hand, so it no longer asks for a thick frame.\n\nAdds an integration spec that measures the content size of a real\nElectron window created from the run mode options, and runs it on\nWindows in CI, where no job currently runs package tests.\n\nFixes #34771\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R3mxeHZHkXgKJSiQBvXqUu\n\n* test(server): resolve the electron executable from its dist directory\n\nThe electron package''s path.txt is relative to dist, so the spec spawned\na path that does not exist. Reads it asynchronously as well, which the\nserver''s lint rules prefer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R3mxeHZHkXgKJSiQBvXqUu\n\n* chore(server): drop the Electron window CI job and integration spec\n\nThe spec only has teeth on Windows, and with the Electron browser\ndeprecated a dedicated Windows job does not carry its weight. The unit\nspec covers the window options through the existing create() seam.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R3mxeHZHkXgKJSiQBvXqUu\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"22796ee4991bc0bdd8a2094823b221a635a44be1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/22796ee4991bc0bdd8a2094823b221a635a44be1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/025716642e69ef2c6dd72e4564e523d6c691db5a","verification":{"payload":"tree 22796ee4991bc0bdd8a2094823b221a635a44be1\nparent aa7d40a0fabed62cd41809086b33329d95ed29c1\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1789414193 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789414193 -0400\n\nfix: restore run mode Electron window size on Windows (#34773)\n\n* fix: restore run mode Electron window size on Windows\n\nElectron 41.3+ reserves part of the client area of a frameless window\nwith a thick frame for resize hit targets on Windows, which shrinks the\nweb contents - and with it every failure screenshot and video frame -\nbelow the size the browser was launched with. The hidden run mode window\nis never resized by hand, so it no longer asks for a thick frame.\n\nAdds an integration spec that measures the content size of a real\nElectron window created from the run mode options, and runs it on\nWindows in CI, where no job currently runs package tests.\n\nFixes #34771\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R3mxeHZHkXgKJSiQBvXqUu\n\n* test(server): resolve the electron executable from its dist directory\n\nThe electron package''s path.txt is relative to dist, so the spec spawned\na path that does not exist. Reads it asynchronously as well, which the\nserver''s lint rules prefer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R3mxeHZHkXgKJSiQBvXqUu\n\n* chore(server): drop the Electron window CI job and integration spec\n\nThe spec only has teeth on Windows, and with the Electron browser\ndeprecated a dedicated Windows job does not carry its weight. The unit\nspec covers the window options through the existing create() seam.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R3mxeHZHkXgKJSiQBvXqUu\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqEsxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAJ4QAESjMaCUXwduJ7VJhpcv8vYb\nmD8HV3mspO++rFSJMzAxVFef9rMlQl1tiTY+xoSz+nV0otxxpGeWAdaKnZuXB00p\nT14LOU2gpOV8ucgvxSs/0c4NeXjnOM7u4X+r7pLws9npfetqVuB+P+aKI00bu+eB\nFBj775I5sUmi4CTdGvsnoG+qubK+zgD0tmpqgv7KmKv1qszG2XPVJhNbjPwHfzun\nLHszeoleEo6T60bSOgJjORNKzFKPQ1/EWzX1DEeT/ZCz8wJgbiayRqK4noYH028k\nXQZczgy2/SWKaxBNEZXIGn+9QbmCLid/vAW2dF9XWDJ7E3ZXU//a0jUAkN04wca0\nhuRFzFh8vIFsmOyzLdiuw5hPo5RA6/VKkDrHzIyJNC2cLWQfaxavkWC1J9JwxlOE\nQ+aSy28ovBCRksHFA2AcdpkwQE742cfaEHjvSzA8fbBPwx4AJCdsAgHipqlH3Klh\n07tRAhnsMsC3gYMeoON0NrlOaJAhtks4MYLjjhvGrG+WaaZB6aEEr1oMR3ES7k9m\nsaSeZqsSXiA9uUxmslX7Wy0QK0GLgQP+zj1nmSFgeFpZ+cAgR7gHhroz79gdtm+0\n1G0W1whqIJc1Vcgr3KGh5zjYBuwG+s59wXJjtlo/YUkhLbbrlI+90pR1u8sq6Ied\nhlW7VrBT3TGX8P2hv1Rv\n=hIFp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T19:29:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/025716642e69ef2c6dd72e4564e523d6c691db5a","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDAyNTcxNjY0MmU2OWVmMmM2ZGQ3MmU0NTY0ZTUyM2Q2YzY5MWRiNWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/aa7d40a0fabed62cd41809086b33329d95ed29c1","sha":"aa7d40a0fabed62cd41809086b33329d95ed29c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/aa7d40a0fabed62cd41809086b33329d95ed29c1"}],"sha":"025716642e69ef2c6dd72e4564e523d6c691db5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/025716642e69ef2c6dd72e4564e523d6c691db5a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/aa7d40a0fabed62cd41809086b33329d95ed29c1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T18:30:19Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":4,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T18:30:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: convert three driver e2e specs to TypeScript (#34845)\n\n* chore: convert cancelation and csp_headers driver specs to TypeScript\n\nRenames both e2e specs from .js to .ts. csp_headers needed no code\nchanges; cancelation needed three:\n\n- `const { Promise } = Cypress` collided with the global Promise, since\n  this spec has no imports and so is a script rather than a module. That\n  redeclaration made TypeScript resolve `.delay()` and\n  `.onPossiblyUnhandledRejection()` against PromiseConstructor instead of\n  Bluebird, so use `Cypress.Promise` directly at each call site.\n- Bluebird''s `cancel()` takes no arguments, so `cancel.apply(this, args)`\n  fails `strictBindCallApply`; call it with no arguments instead.\n- `cy.isStopped()` was never typed, so declare it alongside the other\n  driver-internal APIs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LR5k9rcrVTwpqB2ockioRh\n\n* chore: convert blob driver spec to TypeScript\n\nRenames the spec from .js to .ts. No code changes were needed: the\n`const { Blob, Promise } = Cypress` destructure sits inside the describe\ncallback, so it shadows the globals in function scope rather than\ncolliding with them, and indexing `Blob` by a string method name is\nallowed under the shared `noImplicitAny: false` setting.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LR5k9rcrVTwpqB2ockioRh\n\n* chore: correct spelling of the cancellation driver spec filename\n\nNothing referenced the spec by name, so this is a rename only; the\ndriver''s default specPattern picks it up either way.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LR5k9rcrVTwpqB2ockioRh\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9b9d6aa5a5ca595de95dd0b1e09d9d7c4f556bd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/9b9d6aa5a5ca595de95dd0b1e09d9d7c4f556bd8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/aa7d40a0fabed62cd41809086b33329d95ed29c1","verification":{"payload":"tree 9b9d6aa5a5ca595de95dd0b1e09d9d7c4f556bd8\nparent e581fac2997929a3219c9a6a678c683762be959d\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1789410619 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789410619 -0400\n\nchore: convert three driver e2e specs to TypeScript (#34845)\n\n* chore: convert cancelation and csp_headers driver specs to TypeScript\n\nRenames both e2e specs from .js to .ts. csp_headers needed no code\nchanges; cancelation needed three:\n\n- `const { Promise } = Cypress` collided with the global Promise, since\n  this spec has no imports and so is a script rather than a module. That\n  redeclaration made TypeScript resolve `.delay()` and\n  `.onPossiblyUnhandledRejection()` against PromiseConstructor instead of\n  Bluebird, so use `Cypress.Promise` directly at each call site.\n- Bluebird''s `cancel()` takes no arguments, so `cancel.apply(this, args)`\n  fails `strictBindCallApply`; call it with no arguments instead.\n- `cy.isStopped()` was never typed, so declare it alongside the other\n  driver-internal APIs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LR5k9rcrVTwpqB2ockioRh\n\n* chore: convert blob driver spec to TypeScript\n\nRenames the spec from .js to .ts. No code changes were needed: the\n`const { Blob, Promise } = Cypress` destructure sits inside the describe\ncallback, so it shadows the globals in function scope rather than\ncolliding with them, and indexing `Blob` by a string method name is\nallowed under the shared `noImplicitAny: false` setting.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LR5k9rcrVTwpqB2ockioRh\n\n* chore: correct spelling of the cancellation driver spec filename\n\nNothing referenced the spec by name, so this is a rename only; the\ndriver''s default specPattern picks it up either way.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LR5k9rcrVTwpqB2ockioRh\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqD07CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFbIQAG2UiC+LLynOAQ2SI8PP9xI4\ntIy2JNhlXtXjhlKVcQ0EilQC6RtPbE53FeyM4XpiaNJIu1gcKpkF4yGf197WRBb4\nF7NINpYyYS+9uWyxtfReesSRdRESc3fH37iNWyDdCxNe6ewSXfZmWBKLXw7p8zT6\nbUmd0NSMTrsuhW/y4dXcpwUnXG+U7tVrlzad4PYKyUp/uVTkech4a3NNMpQ/lMuO\nSSLQh87KQdkaBHXVrFAK1U9CXL9/Sa3qvAmTRrjrF3ZKM12qr1fIbc+1EW6zzIxk\n7CzPJzroSCxyDs0hsvzSfezUcc+LboIQevb+mKdRBT9iSPoeLqEmenBqfre1qTZ/\nDogYOleF61cDL+iiea97oBrOE8JdrOawM+GmcGSJgITLvyu0jRtuJNz70oD8psAf\nKTzCNkOXcFfdngPPTYE6RBrtFQK8J11+m25bgL1ulB4hxI/CYTyQIerFIFfYgnDI\n8Gj/rdO8hDRJKATLpf03x/aEjfpluCj9/2l5MvVQ9U81EgkgNZFpsDHY08Nn4Y5C\nkqOh80/lB6f6VBpPDZUXZp4N4Y34raSxZWjKeandck4PbGrLnNyTDYlKYEZkEjWM\ngqzW3MgW5eRPp6v1xJNVmiCtKYWNh+EUNKoZEEuNWpJXhUdkpLn+ZcDBDFRHpVZY\nFeiGyAeJ8sFfo4813qLg\n=/nJ8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T18:30:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.gith