":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/e581fac2997929a3219c9a6a678c683762be959d","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKGU1ODFmYWMyOTk3OTI5YTMyMTljOWE2YTY3OGM2ODM3NjJiZTk1OWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/0947d25e2d5e9bcc6446307cbcec466d69b9f6ac","sha":"0947d25e2d5e9bcc6446307cbcec466d69b9f6ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/0947d25e2d5e9bcc6446307cbcec466d69b9f6ac"}],"sha":"e581fac2997929a3219c9a6a678c683762be959d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/e581fac2997929a3219c9a6a678c683762be959d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/0947d25e2d5e9bcc6446307cbcec466d69b9f6ac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T15:30:07Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":2,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T15:30:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: correct stale Node version and host-specific claims in AGENTS.md (#34838)\n\n* docs: correct the Node version floor in AGENTS.md\n\nThe cloud environment notes stated that Node.js >= 22.19.0 is pre-installed.\nThe bundled Node has since moved to 24.15.0, and the root package.json now\nsets engines.node to >=24.15.0, so yarn refuses to run any script on an\nolder Node. An agent reading the old line concludes 22.x is sufficient and\nthen hits a hard failure on the first yarn command.\n\nReplace the stale floor with a pointer to .node-version and document how to\ninstall the required version, including two things that are easy to get\nwrong: sourcing nvm.sh with && swallows the install because it exits\nnon-zero when no default is aliased, and nvm use does not survive into a new\nshell when the container puts its own Node first on PATH.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017zj8MmKJ499ygaGQL7XdoH\n\n* docs: scope the cloud environment section beyond one host\n\nThe section was titled for Cursor Cloud, but most of it applies to any\nhosted container, and the parts that do not were stated as facts about all\nof them. Claude Code on the web has no Xvfb, no DISPLAY and no system\nChrome, only the Chromium Playwright bundles, so an agent following the\nbrowser bullet there runs a command that cannot work.\n\nRetitle the section, say up front that host-specific bullets name their\nhost, and mark which environment supplies a display and a browser.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017zj8MmKJ499ygaGQL7XdoH\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"11fd32fabcad2c81529740609468132eeaecf8c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/11fd32fabcad2c81529740609468132eeaecf8c2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/0947d25e2d5e9bcc6446307cbcec466d69b9f6ac","verification":{"payload":"tree 11fd32fabcad2c81529740609468132eeaecf8c2\nparent 0621c985ea64ff690a201424fb9a648f361f0e45\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1789399807 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789399807 -0400\n\ndocs: correct stale Node version and host-specific claims in AGENTS.md (#34838)\n\n* docs: correct the Node version floor in AGENTS.md\n\nThe cloud environment notes stated that Node.js >= 22.19.0 is pre-installed.\nThe bundled Node has since moved to 24.15.0, and the root package.json now\nsets engines.node to >=24.15.0, so yarn refuses to run any script on an\nolder Node. An agent reading the old line concludes 22.x is sufficient and\nthen hits a hard failure on the first yarn command.\n\nReplace the stale floor with a pointer to .node-version and document how to\ninstall the required version, including two things that are easy to get\nwrong: sourcing nvm.sh with && swallows the install because it exits\nnon-zero when no default is aliased, and nvm use does not survive into a new\nshell when the container puts its own Node first on PATH.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017zj8MmKJ499ygaGQL7XdoH\n\n* docs: scope the cloud environment section beyond one host\n\nThe section was titled for Cursor Cloud, but most of it applies to any\nhosted container, and the parts that do not were stated as facts about all\nof them. Claude Code on the web has no Xvfb, no DISPLAY and no system\nChrome, only the Chromium Playwright bundles, so an agent following the\nbrowser bullet there runs a command that cannot work.\n\nRetitle the section, say up front that host-specific bullets name their\nhost, and mark which environment supplies a display and a browser.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017zj8MmKJ499ygaGQL7XdoH\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqBL/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1HAQAIvrxHFnlBi2mGaAXcGGUWPd\n5HdtVCBX5cRkpcoeCqTNFvkFMx75b00Jc4Yb/mLOjROGhYdufdOXozqnA2k1HOUb\nn8Le6LnrLRX6Ymz0huwFAy37JvQr2SBIlpYQTqIm5p2RG4yLjrK9tGj1SxcwO56X\nICy2gYvFp7NOP6WrOD8wzQK94pxCeBxXSCt7gVcM2M555HQlGpt01IO3nWaNk2kK\n8qpqxymsK8S2zEuqUrcnoUk4LeQz8rgjEkd0WLBjkkLBm3Ngb+pkpjryw0O0QQx/\ntAXvBxYZr/7pr2mAaqaCLv39pIwtIsBIbYLnwf1z+VN8J8PyssW1y8qPvHv7/N+e\n1W7IGvkYWgclusXscGgYyPUP7hfwVqjVnrk89A/zGToGPjHynbg9GllISIbMiszD\nTqfBFy2eUz7RYAxYUu9FjVeNnNnSx/XOalHUwev6O9Nx5y2he2n9t66lSueDhqSs\nE391rW34TLDSiTiAOA8gJt8Gb9IiCXWD5BOzIYc/GgF+aJr+v7Pp9lopg8j46h4u\nQsIhXtIo38CDUIxU6p+NE2zzBM98YS/Iax/JKmGAsqYFnlF5DhoT3WIhIYSY1+uL\nffZZsx2z60/9Qfi7Exq6CzqPTAdWqw76obvNiGMEXT26a1urZCKzUCmUMInndAya\n2iNXrGpmG9HLN0qHVbdU\n=vD6f\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T15:30:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/0947d25e2d5e9bcc6446307cbcec466d69b9f6ac","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDA5NDdkMjVlMmQ1ZTliY2M2NDQ2MzA3Y2JjZWM0NjZkNjliOWY2YWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/0621c985ea64ff690a201424fb9a648f361f0e45","sha":"0621c985ea64ff690a201424fb9a648f361f0e45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/0621c985ea64ff690a201424fb9a648f361f0e45"}],"sha":"0947d25e2d5e9bcc6446307cbcec466d69b9f6ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/0947d25e2d5e9bcc6446307cbcec466d69b9f6ac"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/0621c985ea64ff690a201424fb9a648f361f0e45/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T15:29:55Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":2,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T15:29:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: stop downgrading ESLint rules in the cypress package (#34839)\n\n* chore: silence the four no-var warnings in cli/types\n\n`cy`, `Cypress`, `expect` and `assert` are declared in ambient global script\nfiles, where only `var` puts a name on `typeof globalThis`. Converting them to\n`let`/`const` would drop `window.Cypress` and `globalThis.expect` from the\npublished type surface, which the `CypressGlobalsTests` block in\ncli/types/tests/cypress-tests.ts already guards against.\n\nKeep `var` and scope an eslint-disable to each declaration instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QD7BBchiEkBTKjsykUDSXt\n\n* chore: tighten the no-var justification comments in cli/types\n\nLead with the reason `var` is required rather than restating the declaration,\nstate it in terms of the present code instead of what `let`/`const` would do,\nand leave the existing chai comment untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QD7BBchiEkBTKjsykUDSXt\n\n* chore: enforce no-var in the CLI package\n\nThe four ambient global declarations in `cli/types` were the only violations,\nand each now carries a scoped disable explaining why `var` is required there.\n\nDrop the downgrade so the package inherits `no-var: ''error''` from the shared\nconfig, matching how the other promoted rules are handled.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QD7BBchiEkBTKjsykUDSXt\n\n* chore: assert types in the global declaration guard\n\n`CypressGlobalsTests` is the only thing in the dtslint suite that fails when\n`cy`, `Cypress`, `expect` or `assert` stop being `declare var`, but it was bare\nreferences with nothing marking it as a guard.\n\nName what it defends and promote the entries to `$ExpectType`, which also covers\n`expect` and `assert` degrading to `any` -- previously caught by nothing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QD7BBchiEkBTKjsykUDSXt\n\n* chore: stop linting the generated net-stubbing type definitions\n\nsync-typedefs copies external-types.ts in from @packages/network-interception,\nwhere it is already linted. Its `no-unused-vars` disable is load-bearing there\nbut reads as an unused directive against the CLI config.\n\nIgnore the copy, matching the exclusion dtslint already carries for it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QD7BBchiEkBTKjsykUDSXt\n\n* chore: enforce the remaining stylistic rules in the CLI package\n\nEvery rule left in the downgrade block was already clean apart from one missing\nspace in cy-minimatch.d.ts. Fix that and drop the block so the package inherits\nthe shared config, where `stylistic.configs.customize` and the explicit\n`space-before-function-paren` override both sit at error.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QD7BBchiEkBTKjsykUDSXt\n\n* chore: correct the lint comments in the CLI package\n\nEach `.d.ts` comment paired one global with one access path, reading as though\n`window.assert` and `globalThis.expect` were not covered. Name the globals and\nthe two objects separately, and match the wording across both files.\n\nThe net-stubbing ignore referred to disable directives; the file carries one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QD7BBchiEkBTKjsykUDSXt\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e814552e44d22589f96ce01f0041deea8c3b9bf3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/e814552e44d22589f96ce01f0041deea8c3b9bf3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/0621c985ea64ff690a201424fb9a648f361f0e45","verification":{"payload":"tree e814552e44d22589f96ce01f0041deea8c3b9bf3\nparent fed00f5477afc7225ea06a08d445c68b9a92f1b8\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1789399795 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789399795 -0400\n\nchore: stop downgrading ESLint rules in the cypress package (#34839)\n\n* chore: silence the four no-var warnings in cli/types\n\n`cy`, `Cypress`, `expect` and `assert` are declared in ambient global script\nfiles, where only `var` puts a name on `typeof globalThis`. Converting them to\n`let`/`const` would drop `window.Cypress` and `globalThis.expect` from the\npublished type surface, which the `CypressGlobalsTests` block in\ncli/types/tests/cypress-tests.ts already guards against.\n\nKeep `var` and scope an eslint-disable to each declaration instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QD7BBchiEkBTKjsykUDSXt\n\n* chore: tighten the no-var justification comments in cli/types\n\nLead with the reason `var` is required rather than restating the declaration,\nstate it in terms of the present code instead of what `let`/`const` would do,\nand leave the existing chai comment untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QD7BBchiEkBTKjsykUDSXt\n\n* chore: enforce no-var in the CLI package\n\nThe four ambient global declarations in `cli/types` were the only violations,\nand each now carries a scoped disable explaining why `var` is required there.\n\nDrop the downgrade so the package inherits `no-var: ''error''` from the shared\nconfig, matching how the other promoted rules are handled.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QD7BBchiEkBTKjsykUDSXt\n\n* chore: assert types in the global declaration guard\n\n`CypressGlobalsTests` is the only thing in the dtslint suite that fails when\n`cy`, `Cypress`, `expect` or `assert` stop being `declare var`, but it was bare\nreferences with nothing marking it as a guard.\n\nName what it defends and promote the entries to `$ExpectType`, which also covers\n`expect` and `assert` degrading to `any` -- previously caught by nothing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QD7BBchiEkBTKjsykUDSXt\n\n* chore: stop linting the generated net-stubbing type definitions\n\nsync-typedefs copies external-types.ts in from @packages/network-interception,\nwhere it is already linted. Its `no-unused-vars` disable is load-bearing there\nbut reads as an unused directive against the CLI config.\n\nIgnore the copy, matching the exclusion dtslint already carries for it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QD7BBchiEkBTKjsykUDSXt\n\n* chore: enforce the remaining stylistic rules in the CLI package\n\nEvery rule left in the downgrade block was already clean apart from one missing\nspace in cy-minimatch.d.ts. Fix that and drop the block so the package inherits\nthe shared config, where `stylistic.configs.customize` and the explicit\n`space-before-function-paren` override both sit at error.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QD7BBchiEkBTKjsykUDSXt\n\n* chore: correct the lint comments in the CLI package\n\nEach `.d.ts` comment paired one global with one access path, reading as though\n`window.assert` and `globalThis.expect` were not covered. Name the globals and\nthe two objects separately, and match the wording across both files.\n\nThe net-stubbing ignore referred to disable directives; the file carries one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QD7BBchiEkBTKjsykUDSXt\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqBLzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAv2cQAC87ULuPkS9I4d5PGGEpJT84\no5dPR+Zw/sNWInLBnalWWq8Zydvn1rraXTMqx+5I1hyd32JYUMKCTVffWbJo1crc\nYz27oVkXStJPNo3xdyJ2vaRuCLlf1Wx0UNboHLFk42uByvSq9rF2KSrBnmqI/Oxp\n86173DUNC1+lGG6u5Z4SxJBB64TDVOEzJJ3FlpmbyO2Cd5v2Vvh/9H52UkB+KXyO\neD7HJxi2/doR6m9qRqYi1zo4/kHBgGDZ+78tIhkHZ1kMKVJ+rwRMJfD4NYBqs4Dd\n/Ej3bA7C9uHvwJwrw9DNzYIKpJA0gHuC68z7crNxWiaKaTXbRhz6yKmqI9ArnPqG\nxwQG5k0/TPeBX0AzQq9wInFsKKyilFOaul60Nq0kgHC38nqCqf9yBvhUnfnzYU68\nCM9t5aCzxGzx6iXMWobB/CdecQIsFUqAIEGn32BT1avoFBM+xLJiDiIcSx2Nb9nD\ndzO4SDOzU3qY3EC1RUYFEI91NpRiCC80qXRo8tSQ5F+NdicgNOMBxjJXFOfdx18a\nR0CEymsL1rmER5MlLtLd5y4JyBRkkun/4lF2K/p/vO0TIWKU5LlAJWaq/N2oPypF\n+3hrAjBBPxLPbJDtUnDGgvxXUgHcrTsC1Oc6UeLEY8sv0h6aX2ehJi/y+QaoTn2U\nodSavYNs/SQfjO6lMO9y\n=q7F/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T15:29:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/0621c985ea64ff690a201424fb9a648f361f0e45","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDA2MjFjOTg1ZWE2NGZmNjkwYTIwMTQyNGZiOWE2NDhmMzYxZjBlNDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/fed00f5477afc7225ea06a08d445c68b9a92f1b8","sha":"fed00f5477afc7225ea06a08d445c68b9a92f1b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/fed00f5477afc7225ea06a08d445c68b9a92f1b8"}],"sha":"0621c985ea64ff690a201424fb9a648f361f0e45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/0621c985ea64ff690a201424fb9a648f361f0e45"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/fed00f5477afc7225ea06a08d445c68b9a92f1b8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T15:29:23Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":2,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T15:29:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: convert dom_hitbox.cy.js to TypeScript (#34840)\n\nRename the driver''s rect-highlight e2e spec to .ts and add the annotations\nit needs to type-check:\n\n- Swap the `require` of `clickCommandLog` for an `import`, now that\n  `cypress/support/utils` is itself TypeScript.\n- Add a local `RectLike` interface for the rect helpers. `DOMRect` alone\n  will not do, since `ensureCorrectTargetPosition` builds a plain object\n  literal that has no `x`, `y` or `toJSON`.\n- Type `contentHighlightCenter` as a tuple so it spreads into the two\n  parameters of `elementFromPoint`.\n- Let `ensureCorrectHighlightPositions` take `string | null | undefined`,\n  covering both the omitted argument and the explicit `null` call site.\n- Give `clickAndPin` optional `x`/`y` parameters and branch on them. A\n  rest tuple resolves against `click(options?)` rather than\n  `click(x, y, options?)`, which reads the coordinates as click options.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019fb127i5EBCcYH5cawVsng\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"26fef9e720a02a6bbf577d818e4746a2e8a8ee0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/26fef9e720a02a6bbf577d818e4746a2e8a8ee0e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/fed00f5477afc7225ea06a08d445c68b9a92f1b8","verification":{"payload":"tree 26fef9e720a02a6bbf577d818e4746a2e8a8ee0e\nparent 1aad838c3ad37f679034d1df477e7b7a5231a3f7\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1789399763 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789399763 -0400\n\nchore: convert dom_hitbox.cy.js to TypeScript (#34840)\n\nRename the driver''s rect-highlight e2e spec to .ts and add the annotations\nit needs to type-check:\n\n- Swap the `require` of `clickCommandLog` for an `import`, now that\n  `cypress/support/utils` is itself TypeScript.\n- Add a local `RectLike` interface for the rect helpers. `DOMRect` alone\n  will not do, since `ensureCorrectTargetPosition` builds a plain object\n  literal that has no `x`, `y` or `toJSON`.\n- Type `contentHighlightCenter` as a tuple so it spreads into the two\n  parameters of `elementFromPoint`.\n- Let `ensureCorrectHighlightPositions` take `string | null | undefined`,\n  covering both the omitted argument and the explicit `null` call site.\n- Give `clickAndPin` optional `x`/`y` parameters and branch on them. A\n  rest tuple resolves against `click(options?)` rather than\n  `click(x, y, options?)`, which reads the coordinates as click options.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019fb127i5EBCcYH5cawVsng\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqBLTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsfUQAKXOiYHhHaGfA/TLbyib2oCU\n3C2ZOCwL4H+ic37Ud9gfKVnCP1TCblmQzxfyaGJgaKitRODy/4ITosUzLg16cI8X\nCXCeunNg5AZzw0H0woNSMi9l7KEmjr30YUugj45qIEHbS8bHPIDQye5u68XZchew\nbA19PzkG34GVkYZNCkaGjVhZcUKOYnzjFCVLhrgEVkBqeSKz/dlIwPGOHsKoMVRS\n0CU3Eh+B8tVhTnmU17w+ZOZcdElU52Pw6Qej/U/7UjMJH9HIPygBL+e4RxvIO4Zf\nMiKFbnBRDaop/kK/8Wrsd9Aivk/rMPQrnluYPwVHzojFbwgjpO4Mb9mDoS/jONQp\n06K7sWtO9TIhS9RCpLo779MNDvyHBssJ+6qMZYlt9AMgGpwTM2YTKn73Dj8QCUAC\nCHmNrfYdqDJjk6Ybw0yK6mk7LFRkBX37QVuLpvyooL45iTPrItMGbrpVo5feWqEW\ntgZsjQoq1oewyo4SNa82SUgJeUF2Y3FT7d46GYaFnXvFCQv3pcafAO4uCnlkGClM\nvr/aGc5iLAC42g6ARIXJJCd8TBnKxuMOwpzIKiQV8YY65x1W0ha/Iu9VUFiDQmwo\nuJP10efqr9LynWHnwwfr4jkLgYZhSIyOViC16wzztO2YUeydN/ioh5ZSMFVGNQWm\nGJEowvbl9ostxApda+/Z\n=C286\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T15:29:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/fed00f5477afc7225ea06a08d445c68b9a92f1b8","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKGZlZDAwZjU0NzdhZmM3MjI1ZWEwNmEwOGQ0NDVjNjhiOWE5MmYxYjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/1aad838c3ad37f679034d1df477e7b7a5231a3f7","sha":"1aad838c3ad37f679034d1df477e7b7a5231a3f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/1aad838c3ad37f679034d1df477e7b7a5231a3f7"}],"sha":"fed00f5477afc7225ea06a08d445c68b9a92f1b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/fed00f5477afc7225ea06a08d445c68b9a92f1b8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/1aad838c3ad37f679034d1df477e7b7a5231a3f7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T15:27:45Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":2,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T15:27:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: make process.geteuid usage in specs Windows-safe and enforce the rule (#34841)\n\n* chore: make process.geteuid usage in specs Windows-safe and enforce the rule\n\n`process.geteuid` does not exist on Windows, so calling it throws and\n`vi.spyOn` on it fails outright. Both sites were reported by the\n`no-restricted-properties` ESLint rule.\n\npackages/electron/test/open.spec.ts stubs `process.geteuid` through a\nproperty descriptor instead of `vi.spyOn`, and restores the original\ndescriptor, deleting the stub when the host never had the property. This\nalso covers the two sibling cases that previously spied on it, which threw\n`geteuid does not exist` on Windows.\n\npackages/server/test/integration/cypress_spec.js reads the euid through an\noptional call inside a try/catch and treats an unreadable euid the same as\nroot, matching the guard already used in packages/server/lib/util/file.ts.\n\nWith every remaining call site guarded, `no-restricted-properties` moves\nfrom ''warn'' to ''error'' in the flat config, matching the severity the\neslintrc config has always used.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RRetMZaQBDvbzJNZURQCnE\n\n* chore: pin the electron paths spec to POSIX path semantics\n\n`paths.spec.ts` asserts on POSIX literals such as `/package/dist/Cypress/test`\nwhile its `path` mocks delegated to the host implementation, so the\nexpectations could only ever match on a POSIX host.\n\n`path.join` was not mocked at all, which mattered most: `pkgRoot` calls\n`path.join(currentDir, ''package.json'')` and the `existsSync` mock matches a\n`/`-joined literal, so on Windows the package root would never be found and\nthe walk would continue to the filesystem root.\n\nThe mocks now delegate to `path.posix`, which makes the spec produce the same\npaths on every host. The `path.dirname` comparison stays on the host\nimplementation, since both sides of it derive from a real `__dirname`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RRetMZaQBDvbzJNZURQCnE\n\n* chore: type-check the electron specs\n\n`tsconfig.base.json` listed `test/**/*` in `include` and `test` in `exclude`.\nExclude wins, so no spec in the package was type-checked. Both build configs\nalready override `exclude` with `test/**/*` of their own, so dropping `test`\nfrom the base leaves `dist` unchanged and only affects the `noEmit` config.\n\nTwo errors that were hidden by this come with it:\n\n- `process.exit` returns `never`, so the `void` callbacks standing in for it in\n  `open.spec.ts` were not assignable. One of the two was suppressed with a\n  blanket `@ts-expect-error`; both now cast to `() => never`.\n- `paths.spec.ts` spread the result of an untyped `vi.importActual`.\n\n`@packages/electron` had no `check-ts` script, which left it out of\n`lerna run check-ts` entirely. It has one now, pointed at the `noEmit` config\nso the specs are covered.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RRetMZaQBDvbzJNZURQCnE\n\n* chore: tighten two comments in the electron specs\n\nOne described the approach it replaced rather than the code as it stands, the\nother restated the `path.posix` delegation already visible on the next line.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RRetMZaQBDvbzJNZURQCnE\n\n* chore: stop the electron open spec leaking state between tests\n\n`os.platform` and the stubbed env vars outlived the blocks that set them, so a\ntest''s result depended on which block ran before it. Under\n`--sequence.shuffle` two tests failed where the sandbox flag or the stderr\npath leaked forward.\n\n`os` is automocked, so `platform` now gets a default alongside the other happy\npath defaults, and `vi.unstubAllEnvs` joins `clearAllMocks` in the teardown.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RRetMZaQBDvbzJNZURQCnE\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"79d0f4d6884192d2dc8c16caf54b9bedbb9305b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/79d0f4d6884192d2dc8c16caf54b9bedbb9305b2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/1aad838c3ad37f679034d1df477e7b7a5231a3f7","verification":{"payload":"tree 79d0f4d6884192d2dc8c16caf54b9bedbb9305b2\nparent fff1a3fbd7d4b6451f97303869cf6a1447362661\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1789399665 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789399665 -0400\n\nchore: make process.geteuid usage in specs Windows-safe and enforce the rule (#34841)\n\n* chore: make process.geteuid usage in specs Windows-safe and enforce the rule\n\n`process.geteuid` does not exist on Windows, so calling it throws and\n`vi.spyOn` on it fails outright. Both sites were reported by the\n`no-restricted-properties` ESLint rule.\n\npackages/electron/test/open.spec.ts stubs `process.geteuid` through a\nproperty descriptor instead of `vi.spyOn`, and restores the original\ndescriptor, deleting the stub when the host never had the property. This\nalso covers the two sibling cases that previously spied on it, which threw\n`geteuid does not exist` on Windows.\n\npackages/server/test/integration/cypress_spec.js reads the euid through an\noptional call inside a try/catch and treats an unreadable euid the same as\nroot, matching the guard already used in packages/server/lib/util/file.ts.\n\nWith every remaining call site guarded, `no-restricted-properties` moves\nfrom ''warn'' to ''error'' in the flat config, matching the severity the\neslintrc config has always used.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RRetMZaQBDvbzJNZURQCnE\n\n* chore: pin the electron paths spec to POSIX path semantics\n\n`paths.spec.ts` asserts on POSIX literals such as `/package/dist/Cypress/test`\nwhile its `path` mocks delegated to the host implementation, so the\nexpectations could only ever match on a POSIX host.\n\n`path.join` was not mocked at all, which mattered most: `pkgRoot` calls\n`path.join(currentDir, ''package.json'')` and the `existsSync` mock matches a\n`/`-joined literal, so on Windows the package root would never be found and\nthe walk would continue to the filesystem root.\n\nThe mocks now delegate to `path.posix`, which makes the spec produce the same\npaths on every host. The `path.dirname` comparison stays on the host\nimplementation, since both sides of it derive from a real `__dirname`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RRetMZaQBDvbzJNZURQCnE\n\n* chore: type-check the electron specs\n\n`tsconfig.base.json` listed `test/**/*` in `include` and `test` in `exclude`.\nExclude wins, so no spec in the package was type-checked. Both build configs\nalready override `exclude` with `test/**/*` of their own, so dropping `test`\nfrom the base leaves `dist` unchanged and only affects the `noEmit` config.\n\nTwo errors that were hidden by this come with it:\n\n- `process.exit` returns `never`, so the `void` callbacks standing in for it in\n  `open.spec.ts` were not assignable. One of the two was suppressed with a\n  blanket `@ts-expect-error`; both now cast to `() => never`.\n- `paths.spec.ts` spread the result of an untyped `vi.importActual`.\n\n`@packages/electron` had no `check-ts` script, which left it out of\n`lerna run check-ts` entirely. It has one now, pointed at the `noEmit` config\nso the specs are covered.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RRetMZaQBDvbzJNZURQCnE\n\n* chore: tighten two comments in the electron specs\n\nOne described the approach it replaced rather than the code as it stands, the\nother restated the `path.posix` delegation already visible on the next line.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RRetMZaQBDvbzJNZURQCnE\n\n* chore: stop the electron open spec leaking state between tests\n\n`os.platform` and the stubbed env vars outlived the blocks that set them, so a\ntest''s result depended on which block ran before it. Under\n`--sequence.shuffle` two tests failed where the sandbox flag or the stderr\npath leaked forward.\n\n`os` is automocked, so `platform` now gets a default alongside the other happy\npath defaults, and `vi.unstubAllEnvs` joins `clearAllMocks` in the teardown.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RRetMZaQBDvbzJNZURQCnE\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqBJxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3vwQAHShgkWYJF9J+SWezBy86jWt\nUCAmjVzAo2dmNieIJknPBkYRgYSrxfcYQuCQv010WnBjJQRmJGBr2A163o3J/g4E\n3W80loc72tjGjZIJNySBQqKr/aX6gyV2GiFVLLi5ItyTK2Ui4W+w6cusgq5WJkgA\nxZNJILypV6uM9lFMrgVd9eSOpcPUsHC1Sw1KQQfOviGEVXIww2u60vhhWnNiWeFT\n5TXlSYhcHW+M4eiP7JE3lN+DIIQb9d77++SH3YzbcjDfO63w5LfbxQSEhhNDv5vz\n6PsKp57R5HumMqCZghaedRc3bgwNzqo6A9E1uL0et7mpOUe+O6+7vhLl1VKX/V6E\nMX2ikUBqCZ1or1uMGmjxM+rZHIA/iLgpYYcPuBdzgnq3pHvoGC6Lt5w+QphkmbEj\nAvjy0guJ0xuZ3m/pptXGO/2m105eBnqyOO4kToMwPIMU+NIapATtdy2TelrkYf4O\nJ37M+yt836E6BRQWP/TuhZ6rx48feD4p+G5dyHw+KooJ28ZdEt+I+uSX/HLcnjuu\n/wd6wU9nZisceJqlPBv2SgEfW23f4aI41M8stqJAQE1awf/w9r/MX+pXgOzlNcXK\nS95YDIIrOP6WF8edXugm6NXrKQ7kP1DttXW/iPd+NYzgIEzmtXt/UbrMCwtTK6LW\nmsYKtbxJmEcc9/eVrE0J\n=D8bz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T15:27:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/1aad838c3ad37f679034d1df477e7b7a5231a3f7","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDFhYWQ4MzhjM2FkMzdmNjc5MDM0ZDFkZjQ3N2U3YjdhNTIzMWEzZjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/fff1a3fbd7d4b6451f97303869cf6a1447362661","sha":"fff1a3fbd7d4b6451f97303869cf6a1447362661","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/fff1a3fbd7d4b6451f97303869cf6a1447362661"}],"sha":"1aad838c3ad37f679034d1df477e7b7a5231a3f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/1aad838c3ad37f679034d1df477e7b7a5231a3f7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/fff1a3fbd7d4b6451f97303869cf6a1447362661/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T15:27:19Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":2,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T15:27:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: convert promises.cy.js to TypeScript (#34842)\n\n* chore: convert promises driver spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `promises.cy.js` to `promises.cy.ts` and resolve the type errors it\nsurfaced:\n\n- capture the `top.console.warn` spy in a local rather than reading\n  `firstCall` back off the console method, which is not typed as a spy\n- widen the top frame before reaching for `console`, which lives on the\n  global scope rather than on `Window`\n- annotate the `logs` arrays and mark the intentionally untyped `cy.foo()`\n  custom command with `@ts-expect-error`, matching the convention in the\n  neighbouring driver specs\n\nNo behaviour change: all 7 tests still pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0141tUsAgkvsxEb3B1Me8Dn3\n\n* chore: name the Bluebird internal instead of casting it to `any`\n\n`cy.spy` only requires that the method be a key of the object handed to it,\nso the `_warn` spy can keep the prototype''s real type and add just the\ninternal method''s signature to it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0141tUsAgkvsxEb3B1Me8Dn3\n\n* chore: scope the promises spec''s declarations to the file\n\nWithout a top-level import or export the spec is a script, so `topWindow`\nand `PromiseInternals` land in the driver project''s global TS scope and\ncollide with any later spec reusing those names.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0141tUsAgkvsxEb3B1Me8Dn3\n\n* chore: state the promises spec''s suppression reason once\n\nThe justification for the `@ts-expect-error` directives was repeated at all\nsix sites. Explain `cy.foo()` once on the suite and leave the directives\nbare, and trim the `topWindow` comment to the part the cast cannot express.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0141tUsAgkvsxEb3B1Me8Dn3\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"78587fbee8763c5de87f457b04d5c04a15126fca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/78587fbee8763c5de87f457b04d5c04a15126fca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/fff1a3fbd7d4b6451f97303869cf6a1447362661","verification":{"payload":"tree 78587fbee8763c5de87f457b04d5c04a15126fca\nparent 59c64c1fb9a3f91239fcea900f50bd150e855dd1\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1789399639 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789399639 -0400\n\ntest: convert promises.cy.js to TypeScript (#34842)\n\n* chore: convert promises driver spec to TypeScript\n\nRename `promises.cy.js` to `promises.cy.ts` and resolve the type errors it\nsurfaced:\n\n- capture the `top.console.warn` spy in a local rather than reading\n  `firstCall` back off the console method, which is not typed as a spy\n- widen the top frame before reaching for `console`, which lives on the\n  global scope rather than on `Window`\n- annotate the `logs` arrays and mark the intentionally untyped `cy.foo()`\n  custom command with `@ts-expect-error`, matching the convention in the\n  neighbouring driver specs\n\nNo behaviour change: all 7 tests still pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0141tUsAgkvsxEb3B1Me8Dn3\n\n* chore: name the Bluebird internal instead of casting it to `any`\n\n`cy.spy` only requires that the method be a key of the object handed to it,\nso the `_warn` spy can keep the prototype''s real type and add just the\ninternal method''s signature to it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0141tUsAgkvsxEb3B1Me8Dn3\n\n* chore: scope the promises spec''s declarations to the file\n\nWithout a top-level import or export the spec is a script, so `topWindow`\nand `PromiseInternals` land in the driver project''s global TS scope and\ncollide with any later spec reusing those names.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0141tUsAgkvsxEb3B1Me8Dn3\n\n* chore: state the promises spec''s suppression reason once\n\nThe justification for the `@ts-expect-error` directives was repeated at all\nsix sites. Explain `cy.foo()` once on the suite and leave the directives\nbare, and trim the `topWindow` comment to the part the cast cannot express.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0141tUsAgkvsxEb3B1Me8Dn3\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqBJXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMrwQAESu+yU5SOSeSLQMMAGX5TKk\nZGsfjYy0oz/GbTHF2yoYbaddr+4VwPDq3DONJ8J08yB