00f50bd150e855dd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/59c64c1fb9a3f91239fcea900f50bd150e855dd1"}],"sha":"fff1a3fbd7d4b6451f97303869cf6a1447362661","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/fff1a3fbd7d4b6451f97303869cf6a1447362661"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/59c64c1fb9a3f91239fcea900f50bd150e855dd1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T15:27:03Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":3,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T15:27:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: convert the react driver specs to TypeScript and swap React 15 for React 19 (#34843)\n\n* chore: convert react-15 and react-16 driver specs to TypeScript\n\nBoth specs type-check as-is: `.its(''onChangeEvents'')` resolves through the\nstring propertyPath overload, so the rename needed no source changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LECgPBs4RbyYkxFZh5MZd5\n\n* chore: replace the React 15 driver spec with React 19\n\nThe driver''s react specs guard cy.type() against React''s _valueTracker: React\ncaches an input''s last value on the node, so assigning through the property it\npatches leaves the tracker in sync and onChange never fires. setNativeProp\nreaches past it for the prototype setter, which the tracker misses.\n\nReact 15 predates every version Cypress supports, while React 19 -- the current\nmajor -- had no coverage at all. Swap it. React 16 stays as the legacy canary.\n\nReact 19 dropped its UMD builds, so the fixture evaluates the CommonJS bundles\nagainst a small loader. Each module gets its own exports binding because the\nbundles read exports lazily, and a shared global resolves to whichever module\nloaded last.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LECgPBs4RbyYkxFZh5MZd5\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a34928c81e03cdad565b522a2f603ebc5349b9a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/a34928c81e03cdad565b522a2f603ebc5349b9a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/59c64c1fb9a3f91239fcea900f50bd150e855dd1","verification":{"payload":"tree a34928c81e03cdad565b522a2f603ebc5349b9a6\nparent 6511c6bb7cc33f565d4477fb139f0965c4883fcc\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1789399623 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789399623 -0400\n\ntest: convert the react driver specs to TypeScript and swap React 15 for React 19 (#34843)\n\n* chore: convert react-15 and react-16 driver specs to TypeScript\n\nBoth specs type-check as-is: `.its(''onChangeEvents'')` resolves through the\nstring propertyPath overload, so the rename needed no source changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LECgPBs4RbyYkxFZh5MZd5\n\n* chore: replace the React 15 driver spec with React 19\n\nThe driver''s react specs guard cy.type() against React''s _valueTracker: React\ncaches an input''s last value on the node, so assigning through the property it\npatches leaves the tracker in sync and onChange never fires. setNativeProp\nreaches past it for the prototype setter, which the tracker misses.\n\nReact 15 predates every version Cypress supports, while React 19 -- the current\nmajor -- had no coverage at all. Swap it. React 16 stays as the legacy canary.\n\nReact 19 dropped its UMD builds, so the fixture evaluates the CommonJS bundles\nagainst a small loader. Each module gets its own exports binding because the\nbundles read exports lazily, and a shared global resolves to whichever module\nloaded last.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LECgPBs4RbyYkxFZh5MZd5\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqBJHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqDUQAJui6BbMR0VDIKktgn4U2BpZ\ni2T59tPKOK16UKBAW4DeaARBpE7Wck3xhUit+N0e0o7Jvc/SV+k4yPINQlXY8NXW\n1sgy/Uxi1zY8Dch9Qd4CSeWLSrbMimQBonhdHX2xKZaiWF2WHOHuPbjfPCFnvAej\nAym9R7gPyE5DitiXuXwFuz1iOlHg/tySWWwGCk5G1c4QqnHdyBqmFZg1etaE8g1g\nazaS5dTBS+l7Lwv0TzeiljO9I17i314aOUnQFV/g9SW42MOPPg3WO3fkJUAF2Mv9\n5Dqif+6/xGrVL0V4LD5OALqfF7J/jhFX25h2g0dIYwwqbYgGMcLGzklZr2N+taaB\n3Ua5ZgFw0NUho+B12q0K/ADNm4SKqCBRlGLn2SqWBzIh4mP9B4yZp82cFwvQv79A\nNg+LbxmQt3ecSYgPQgTUvLbTOKfvVD3U/OeBnJ7g1ednrZEKwmnICxyNvh2+cib0\n10AEjR0UisWZz91MahaRn66CG67ByfQ/SNDnRDzwgO1LflfJxRJwGKdf5GDE8E1T\npmcJwOp2FP2n5+lFP5flt/vwYxHyQ2+m6igl+s3AZJOywDcgI1WgLJfQpsgIrt7J\n/BkW0N1ZwMhM7QN8kw4Ap5AYVIXFqBu6tBqnS5rCKNKirkQhbRpNHWnzS2rhBMhy\n/izRPyAAUuNbdCT0gB4w\n=Cq+W\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T15:27:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/59c64c1fb9a3f91239fcea900f50bd150e855dd1","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDU5YzY0YzFmYjlhM2Y5MTIzOWZjZWE5MDBmNTBiZDE1MGU4NTVkZDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/6511c6bb7cc33f565d4477fb139f0965c4883fcc","sha":"6511c6bb7cc33f565d4477fb139f0965c4883fcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/6511c6bb7cc33f565d4477fb139f0965c4883fcc"}],"sha":"59c64c1fb9a3f91239fcea900f50bd150e855dd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/59c64c1fb9a3f91239fcea900f50bd150e855dd1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3980464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AtofStryker","id":3980464,"login":"AtofStryker","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5ODA0NjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtofStryker","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/6511c6bb7cc33f565d4477fb139f0965c4883fcc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:29:15Z","email":"bglesias@gmail.com","name":"Bill Glesias"},"comment_count":2,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:29:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: enforce blockHosts on the browser network path in Chrome (#34788)\n\nThe synthetic response used on the CDP Fetch path auto-destroys after\nend(), so a 503 written by the blocked-hosts policy read as a browser\ncancel. The pipeline threw and the transport released the paused request\nuntouched, so blocked hosts loaded from the real origin. Only treat a\nresponse destroyed before it finished as a cancel.\n\nRun the blockHosts system specs on Chrome as well as Electron; they were\nskipped in the system-tests-chrome job.\n\nCloses #34785\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e547fdc6206999d7b38c98c5f51cbb4330131cfb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/e547fdc6206999d7b38c98c5f51cbb4330131cfb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/6511c6bb7cc33f565d4477fb139f0965c4883fcc","verification":{"payload":"tree e547fdc6206999d7b38c98c5f51cbb4330131cfb\nparent 2a65ae9fe99d3b99d0c7af1859131ce7ad8555af\nauthor Bill Glesias <bglesias@gmail.com> 1789396155 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789396155 -0400\n\nfix: enforce blockHosts on the browser network path in Chrome (#34788)\n\nThe synthetic response used on the CDP Fetch path auto-destroys after\nend(), so a 503 written by the blocked-hosts policy read as a browser\ncancel. The pipeline threw and the transport released the paused request\nuntouched, so blocked hosts loaded from the real origin. Only treat a\nresponse destroyed before it finished as a cancel.\n\nRun the blockHosts system specs on Chrome as well as Electron; they were\nskipped in the system-tests-chrome job.\n\nCloses #34785\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqAS7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbuIQAA9Ch4vBEg+byIHZMDpfo3fz\nORTrJOd+UTsdK9dNKoCWcvyeJvUF2YYZCXYD8sjeaDQVBgUMKUmxj1Fu/U61DwXV\nB9nF4kCb3ke/ZAdPkxFMaSpH9mJ/RM4ju8xnrNkSHtwQZech81ytbO98tkrWgw0k\nspNVZM1/p/1NZ9KoAaU5/Sqjw3RxmoH2iqd3fb88Cdg+AoPppBR7O4DBNNvhV3O/\nLedCdV2qINnbwzPObJWywyFZBohTg+eMyg64BC84Oof1MDHFGg7Y37wvkrLmhJPj\nMDkzaA/SxKd3SuUtcQKMsSmQlQloKUWpwHkF/rsJGwGrzAru2w3JK/edcw7S08Z5\nVJ/L80VznNJzRJxBIoonVdiqQfQgj9bezWburOnKzMCmm8s71z0yFsiYLLsPFKzm\nZDtWEo4Fix6faVr5vf52+yd5A87oGC97tE1s7rsamWaCvSlqEkn+NnZXWlOa0EMn\nf1/CzH28LTV0i1FndDPkvaXzALRY5aubHoLxhau/Ga1UM6vD2BrAZ3m7S4Q4M1Xu\nOBDkdwqG5pjimAdF4zjuoLhIapwO0wZW1n5YEf9SNQ7wdRolFpE932DZi92MCdou\ndVfPHtI3P9e/2FzxwGUv/RvhqspPd9A3bEHMiH/ygMtuvg8WbJ89D5LxXc0jRD3Y\n/qlIexNBbZzrXp1QrOA7\n=LVq0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T14:29:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/6511c6bb7cc33f565d4477fb139f0965c4883fcc","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDY1MTFjNmJiN2NjMzNmNTY1ZDQ0NzdmYjEzOWYwOTY1YzQ4ODNmY2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/2a65ae9fe99d3b99d0c7af1859131ce7ad8555af","sha":"2a65ae9fe99d3b99d0c7af1859131ce7ad8555af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/2a65ae9fe99d3b99d0c7af1859131ce7ad8555af"}],"sha":"6511c6bb7cc33f565d4477fb139f0965c4883fcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/6511c6bb7cc33f565d4477fb139f0965c4883fcc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/142877?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cacieprins","id":142877,"login":"cacieprins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Mjg3Nw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cacieprins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/2a65ae9fe99d3b99d0c7af1859131ce7ad8555af/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T13:00:50Z","email":"cacieprins@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Cacie Prins"},"comment_count":4,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T13:00:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add trustedCertificates option for the native browser network path (#34791)\n\n* fix: validate TLS certificates on the native browser network path\n\nOn the CDP netstack (Chrome, Chromium, Edge), Cypress no longer passes\nthe blanket --ignore-certificate-errors flag, which silently accepted\ninvalid certificates and, as a side effect, prevented the browser from\ncaching static assets across navigations. The browser now validates\ncertificates as it does in production.\n\nAdds a `trustedCertificates` config option so users can declare a\nself-signed or private-CA certificate their app under test presents;\neach entry''s SubjectPublicKeyInfo fingerprint is passed to Chrome via\n--ignore-certificate-errors-spki-list. Firefox, WebKit, Electron, and\nforceHttp1 runs are unaffected and keep the legacy behavior.\n\nAddresses #34760.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: add system smoke test for trustedCertificates on the native browser network path\n\nExercises the end-to-end plumbing on Chrome: a self-signed HTTPS origin\nwhose leaf certificate is declared in `trustedCertificates` loads because\nits SPKI fingerprint reaches Chrome via --ignore-certificate-errors-spki-list,\nwith the blanket --ignore-certificate-errors no longer passed.\n\nDeliberately does not assert the disk-cache behavior the feature restores,\nwhich is unobservable from a system test: Cypress''s security-reducing\nlaunch flags load invalid certs regardless of trust, the same-renderer\nmemory cache masks the disk cache within a spec, and the browser cache is\nreset between specs. That behavior is covered by lower-level verification.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: convert trustedCertificates system-test fixtures to TypeScript\n\nReplaces the .js fixture config and spec with cypress.config.ts (a plain\nexport default, since lightweight fixtures have no node_modules to resolve\n`cypress` from) and a .cy.ts spec, and adds the tsconfig.json a .cy.ts\nfixture requires — the batteries-included preprocessor throws\nTsConfigNotFoundError without one (house precedent: projects/ts-proj).\n\nRecords the \"TypeScript for all new code\" convention in AGENTS.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: keep --ignore-certificate-errors on the native network path; trustedCertificates is additive\n\nDropping the blanket flag on the native browser network path broke real\nself-signed HTTPS setups beyond caching: Chrome refuses service-worker\nregistration on a page with a genuine certificate error, and cross-origin\nnavigation to a hosts-mapped self-signed origin timed out\n(system-tests-chrome: service_worker_spec, web_security_spec). Those are\nuser-visible breaks for a common local-dev configuration.\n\nThe blanket flag now stays. `trustedCertificates` layers an\n--ignore-certificate-errors-spki-list on top; Chrome honors that list over\nthe blanket flag, so a declared cert''s origin is genuinely trusted and its\nassets cache, while undeclared origins behave exactly as before. Tightening\nthe blanket flag can be a deliberate change in a major version.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: restore web_security snapshots pruned by a local system-test run\n\nRunning `yarn test web_security --browser chrome` locally let snap-shot-it\nprune the Firefox-gated snapshot key from __snapshots__/web_security_spec.js,\nand it was swept into the previous commit. CI then failed the Firefox test\nwith \"Cannot store new snapshot value\". Restores the file from develop and\nrecords the gotcha in system-tests/AGENTS.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: reframe the trustedCertificates changelog entry as a feature\n\nMoves the entry from Bugfixes to Features and bumps the release heading to\n16.1.0, matching the PR''s `feat:` semantic prefix (a new configuration option\nthat enables browser caching for origins with self-signed or private-CA\ncertificates; purely additive).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add a TRUSTED_CERTIFICATES_LOAD_ERROR Cypress error\n\nA missing file or unparsable PEM previously threw a plain Error out of\nopenProject.launch(). Run mode only maps timeouts and the Firefox connect\ncase, so it reached the user as a generic unexpected error with a stack.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: trust every certificate in a trustedCertificates PEM bundle\n\nA filePath or pem value holding several certificates now yields one SPKI\nfingerprint per certificate instead of silently trusting only the first,\nand load or parse failures throw TRUSTED_CERTIFICATES_LOAD_ERROR naming\nthe offending entry.\n\nAlso verb-leads the two exports to match the other lib/util helpers:\nspkiFingerprintFromPem -> generateSpkiFingerprint and\ntrustedCertificateFingerprints -> resolveTrustedCertificateFingerprints.\nThe trustedCertificateFingerprints launch-option property keeps its name.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: accept an absolute filePath in trustedCertificates\n\nInternal CA certs usually live outside the project, and clientCertificates\nalready accepts absolute paths. path.resolve() in the server handles both\nforms. Also switches the entry loop to value.entries().\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: correct the trustedCertificates type docstrings\n\nA filePath is resolved against the project root, so it may be absolute,\nand a PEM bundle trusts every certificate it holds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: assert the spki flag reaches Chrome in the trusted certs system test\n\nThe blanket --ignore-certificate-errors made the spec pass with an empty\ntrustedCertificates, so the fixture now fails the launch unless Chrome is\ngiven --ignore-certificate-errors-spki-list for the leaf it presents. The\nexpected fingerprint is a literal computed with openssl, independent of\nthe helper under test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: link cy.visit() in the trustedCertificates changelog entry\n\nRule 10 of guides/writing-the-cypress-changelog.md asks for parens and a\ndocs link on a command''s first mention. Also drops the repo-wide\nTypeScript convention bullet, which belongs in its own chore PR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: pin the trusted certificates system test to the browser network path\n\nThe full-suite forceHttp1 CI jobs export CYPRESS_forceHttp1=true for the\nwhole job. The fixture''s before:browser:launch check only holds on the\nbrowser network path, and CLI config beats env, so pass forceHttp1: false\nexplicitly. Verified locally: passes by default and under\nCYPRESS_forceHttp1=true with the pin, fails under that env without it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: regenerate the cypress-sessions GraphQL types for TRUSTED_CERTIFICATES_LOAD_ERROR\n\nThe data-context build regenerates both schema.graphql and\npackages/cypress-sessions/lib/generated/graphql.ts; the errors AGENTS.md\nnote named only the first, so the second was left out. Name both.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: address review on trustedCertificates scoping, args binding, and cert drift\n\n- cypress.d.ts: say that entries are not URL-scoped, unlike clientCertificates,\n  and that relative paths resolve against the project root.\n- chrome.ts: args is never rebound in _getArgs, so it is const again.\n- trusted_certificates_spec: a before hook asserts the fixture cert is still a\n  byte copy of the https-proxy server cert. The fixture''s hardcoded SPKI keeps\n  satisfying its own launch hook after a regeneration, so this is the only\n  check that catches the drift. Verified it fails when the fixture differs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: match the TRUSTED_CERTIFICATES_LOAD_ERROR text to the supported entry shapes\n\nThe message described `filePath` as resolved from the project root and\nomitted `spki`. Absolute paths are supported and `spki` is a valid entry,\nso the text now mirrors the `trustedCertificates` docstring.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Bill Glesias <bglesias@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"1f8dc1257900f8d39186bca53805cd11f6895a30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/1f8dc1257900f8d39186bca53805cd11f6895a30"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/2a65ae9fe99d3b99d0c7af1859131ce7ad8555af","verification":{"payload":"tree 1f8dc1257900f8d39186bca53805cd11f6895a30\nparent 48e8b3757b5dc13ecaf7be8051f2bb65f31c5398\nauthor Cacie Prins <cacieprins@users.noreply.github.com> 1789390850 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789390850 -0400\n\nfeat: add trustedCertificates option for the native browser network path (#34791)\n\n* fix: validate TLS certificates on the native browser network path\n\nOn the CDP netstack (Chrome, Chromium, Edge), Cypress no longer passes\nthe blanket --ignore-certificate-errors flag, which silently accepted\ninvalid certificates and, as a side effect, prevented the browser from\ncaching static assets across navigations. The browser now validates\ncertificates as it does in production.\n\nAdds a `trustedCertificates` config option so users can declare a\nself-signed or private-CA certificate their app under test presents;\neach entry''s SubjectPublicKeyInfo fingerprint is passed to Chrome via\n--ignore-certificate-errors-spki-list. Firefox, WebKit, Electron, and\nforceHttp1 runs are unaffected and keep the legacy behavior.\n\nAddresses #34760.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: add system smoke test for trustedCertificates on the native browser network path\n\nExercises the end-to-end plumbing on Chrome: a self-signed HTTPS origin\nwhose leaf certificate is declared in `trustedCertificates` loads because\nits SPKI fingerprint reaches Chrome via --ignore-certificate-errors-spki-list,\nwith the blanket --ignore-certificate-errors no longer passed.\n\nDeliberately does not assert the disk-cache behavior the feature restores,\nwhich is unobservable from a system test: Cypress''s security-reducing\nlaunch flags load invalid certs regardless of trust, the same-renderer\nmemory cache masks the disk cache within a spec, and the browser cache is\nreset between specs. That behavior is covered by lower-level verification.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: convert trustedCertificates system-test fixtures to TypeScript\n\nReplaces the .js fixture config and spec with cypress.config.ts (a plain\nexport default, since lightweight fixtures have no node_modules to resolve\n`cypress` from) and a .cy.ts spec, and adds the tsconfig.json a .cy.ts\nfixture requires — the batteries-included preprocessor throws\nTsConfigNotFoundError without one (house precedent: projects/ts-proj).\n\nRecords the \"TypeScript for all new code\" convention in AGENTS.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: keep --ignore-certificate-errors on the native network path; trustedCertificates is additive\n\nDropping the blanket flag on the native browser network path broke real\nself-signed HTTPS setups beyond caching: Chrome refuses service-worker\nregistration on a page with a genuine certificate error, and cross-origin\nnavigation to a hosts-mapped self-signed origin timed out\n(system-tests-chrome: service_worker_spec, web_security_spec). Those are\nuser-visible breaks for a common local-dev configuration.\n\nThe blanket flag now stays. `trustedCertificates` layers an\n--ignore-certificate-errors-spki-list on top; Chrome honors that list over\nthe blanket flag, so a declared cert''s origin is genuinely trusted and its\nassets cache, while undeclared origins behave exactly as before. Tightening\nthe blanket flag can be a deliberate change in a major version.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: restore web_security snapshots pruned by a local system-test run\n\nRunning `yarn test web_security --browser chrome` locally let snap-shot-it\nprune the Firefox-gated snapshot key from __snapshots__/web_security_spec.js,\nand it was swept into the previous commit. CI then failed the Firefox test\nwith \"Cannot store new snapshot value\". Restores the file from develop and\nrecords the gotcha in system-tests/AGENTS.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: reframe the trustedCertificates changelog entry as a feature\n\nMoves the entry from Bugfixes to Features and bumps the release heading to\n16.1.0, matching the PR''s `feat:` semantic prefix (a new configuration option\nthat enables browser caching for origins with self-signed or private-CA\ncertificates; purely additive).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add a TRUSTED_CERTIFICATES_LOAD_ERROR Cypress error\n\nA missing file or unparsable PEM previously threw a plain Error out of\nopenProject.launch(). Run mode only maps timeouts and the Firefox connect\ncase, so it reached the user as a generic unexpected error with a stack.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: trust every certificate in a trustedCertificates PEM bundle\n\nA filePath or pem value holding several certificates now yields one SPKI\nfingerprint per certificate instead of silently trusting only the first,\nand load or parse failures throw TRUSTED_CERTIFICATES_LOAD_ERROR naming\nthe offending entry.\n\nAlso verb-leads the two exports to match the other lib/util helpers:\nspkiFingerprintFromPem -> generateSpkiFingerprint and\ntrustedCertificateFingerprints -> resolveTrustedCertificateFingerprints.\nThe trustedCertificateFingerprints launch-option property keeps its name.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: accept an absolute filePath in trustedCertificates\n\nInternal CA certs usually live outside the project, and clientCertificates\nalready accepts absolute paths. path.resolve() in the server handles both\nforms. Also switches the entry loop to value.entries().\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: correct the trustedCertificates type docstrings\n\nA filePath is resolved against the project root, so it may be absolute,\nand a PEM bundle trusts every certificate it holds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: assert the spki flag reaches Chrome in the trusted certs system test\n\nThe blanket --ignore-certificate-errors made the spec pass with an empty\ntrustedCertificates, so the fixture now fails the launch unless Chrome is\ngiven --ignore-certificate-errors-spki-list for the leaf it presents. The\nexpected fingerprint is a literal computed with openssl, independent of\nthe helper under test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: link cy.visit() in the trustedCertificates changelog entry\n\nRule 10 of guides/writing-the-cypress-changelog.md asks for parens and a\ndocs link on a command''s first mention. Also drops the repo-wide\nTypeScript convention bullet, which belongs in its own chore PR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: pin the trusted certificates system test to the browser network path\n\nThe full-suite forceHttp1 CI jobs export CYPRESS_forceHttp1=true for the\nwhole job. The fixture''s before:browser:launch check only holds on the\nbrowser network path, and CLI config beats env, so pass forceHttp1: false\nexplicitly. Verified locally: passes by default and under\nCYPRESS_forceHttp1=true with the pin, fails under that env without it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: regenerate the cypress-sessions GraphQL types for TRUSTED_CERTIFICATES_LOAD_ERROR\n\nThe data-context build regenerates both schema.graphql and\npackages/cypress-sessions/lib/generated/graphql.ts; the errors AGENTS.md\nnote named only the first, so the second was left out. Name both.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: address review on trustedCertificates scoping, args binding, and cert drift\n\n- cypress.d.ts: say that entries are not URL-scoped, unlike clientCertificates,\n  and that relative paths resolve against the project root.\n- chrome.ts: args is never rebound in _getArgs, so it is const again.\n- trusted_certificates_spec: a before hook asserts the fixture cert is still a\n  byte copy of the https-proxy server cert. The fixture''s hardcoded SPKI keeps\n  satisfying its own launch hook after a regeneration, so this is the only\n  check that catches the drift. Verified it fails when the fixture differs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: match the TRUSTED_CERTIFICATES_LOAD_ERROR text to the supported entry shapes\n\nThe message described `filePath` as resolved from the project root and\nomitted `spki`. Absolute paths are supported and `spki` is a valid entry,\nso the text now mirrors the `trustedCertificates` docstring.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Bill Glesias <bglesias@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp/ACCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPhMQAKIHJVMcWpOkDkIWZHmT6djJ\nbie4Fe1C9xuMFeF4T0jtqos7DFstrg7C+ftCkXhEHZ0flOmjYVOQkBKPjNbvlXCK\nddu5LlUOEnxqbfgrriSPSeZPP+ZsCmU4ugtYRSI7ScON9fbSNxRQ8u/5k8cyb9a7\nEUcdhqqKBsfocgwNlxiDaGffy6hrR+w+JCtpLOIZWoA1V3Or0HPIf1X6ABei+Xf5\nNYHSqxUnjXIWjyTMBIPsDuNBg+sPnLBIL6C3AsNjc/sRW7RGdA61DgR5osgYv+ns\nDj0RtnRkaxoPgMYOKR54nBfRa4zpkgfFzjROF+PsyIPnAD/vX7CDzq6NxMM15v7f\nuFYKxK+F0gwL2I8Fxy13vB72Cy2gOA1j6ZGBVJNedFpEaw9r8qfmjFPcKi9892sx\nPGFTN0T1XgpgErT/e8rKDH0iz5tattxacgFZCcksFbm87VMaX7JFncmVQLZVNN8K\nui1zGWdasGYoLoO6C14NgcKAAyABAxtQHgp1dQZzDryj0r/6FeswdrDg6BdMQyQu\nVArslZ7KWTHC0Qq8Z846N5AvcXDBEWzihzi71uaJyqT4Tfgx5JnSnWL4SQ4dlcJ+\njUm51963coLRHZdoi9S9LwOFzA6QrPUE3CDZGluL/RsOkrz/un3XiSjcnZglKIsc\n8BafZRSd0fTu+TnPZtoP\n=TcBl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T13:00:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/2a65ae9fe99d3b99d0c7af1859131ce7ad8555af","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDJhNjVhZTlmZTk5ZDNiOTlkMGM3YWYxODU5MTMxY2U3YWQ4NTU1YWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/48e8b3757b5dc13ecaf7be8051f2bb65f31c5398","sha":"48e8b3757b5dc13ecaf7be8051f2bb65f31c5398","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/48e8b3757b5dc13ecaf7be8051f2bb65f31c5398"}],"sha":"2a65ae9fe99d3b99d0c7af1859131ce7ad8555af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/2a65ae9fe99d3b99d0c7af1859131ce7ad8555af"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/48e8b3757b5dc13ecaf7be8051f2bb65f31c5398/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T11:28:59Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":4,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T11:28:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: convert four driver specs to TypeScript (#34837)\n\n* test: convert popups.cy.js to TypeScript\n\nRename the popups driver spec to `.ts` and switch the `assertLogLength`\nimport to ESM, matching the sibling specs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DNnGX8VnGS44GyLxTiAETT\n\n* test: convert timeouts.cy.js to TypeScript\n\nRename the timeouts driver spec to `.ts`. The stub state passed to\n`create` is a bare function, so cast it to `StateFunc` to satisfy the\ncallable interface while still yielding no runnable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DNnGX8VnGS44GyLxTiAETT\n\n* test: convert browser.cy.js to TypeScript\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DNnGX8VnGS44GyLxTiAETT\n\n* test: fix dead assertion in browser isBrowser throw test\n\nThe `.to.throw` was chained inside the arrow passed to `expect`, so the\nfunction was never invoked and the test asserted nothing. Move it onto the\nouter `expect` and match the message `browser.invalid_arg` actually throws.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DNnGX8VnGS44GyLxTiAETT\n\n* test: type the browser spec''s commands helper\n\nThe helper hung off the mocha context, so `this.commands()` resolved to `any`\nthrough the `Context` index signature and nothing downstream was checked.\nMoving it to a typed local restores checking on `.browser` and `.isBrowser`,\nwhich surfaces the calls that exceed the public types: `family` cannot carry\nan `!` exclusion prefix, and the throw test passes a deliberately invalid arg.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DNnGX8VnGS44GyLxTiAETT\n\n* test: keep browser spec formatting closer to the original\n\nRestore the `function ()` callback form and the multi-line matcher arrays so\nthe diff is limited to the lines the typed helper actually required.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DNnGX8VnGS44GyLxTiAETT\n\n* Revert \"test: type the browser spec''s commands helper\"\n\nReverts the typed local and the formatting follow-up. Dropping `this.commands`\nrewrote roughly a third of the file, which pushed rename similarity to 31% and\nmade GitHub render the spec as a delete plus an add rather than a rename.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DNnGX8VnGS44GyLxTiAETT\n\n* test: convert cypress.cy.js to TypeScript\n\nSwap the lodash `require` for an import so the file is treated as a module\nrather than a script, which also stops `$` and `Promise` colliding with the\nglobals and resolves `Promise` to Cypress''s bluebird. Cast the internal and\ndeliberately invalid calls the public types do not cover.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DNnGX8VnGS44GyLxTiAETT\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"14fb5287fb4287c955fc22911a82b1564bb483a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/14fb5287fb4287c955fc22911a82b1564bb483a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/48e8b3757b5dc13ecaf7be8051f2bb65f31c5398","verification":{"payload":"tree 14fb5287fb4287c955fc22911a82b1564bb483a2\nparent fe1998c95f5c8323653fb2e7a35b3916299a5921\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1789385339 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789385339 -0400\n\ntest: convert four driver specs to TypeScript (#34837)\n\n* test: convert popups.cy.js to TypeScript\n\nRename the popups driver spec to `.ts` and switch the `assertLogLength`\nimport to ESM, matching the sibling specs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DNnGX8VnGS44GyLxTiAETT\n\n* test: convert timeouts.cy.js to TypeScript\n\nRename the timeouts driver spec to `.ts`. The stub state passed to\n`create` is a bare function, so cast it to `StateFunc` to satisfy the\ncallable interface while still yielding no runnable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DNnGX8VnGS44GyLxTiAETT\n\n* test: convert browser.cy.js to TypeScript\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DNnGX8VnGS44GyLxTiAETT\n\n* test: fix dead assertion in browser isBrowser throw test\n\nThe `.to.throw` was chained inside the arrow passed to `expect`, so the\nfunction was never invoked and the test asserted nothing. Move it onto the\nouter `expect` and match the message `browser.invalid_arg` actually throws.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DNnGX8VnGS44GyLxTiAETT\n\n* test: type the browser spec''s commands helper\n\nThe helper hung off the mocha context, so `this.commands()` resolved to `any`\nthrough the `Context` index signature and nothing downstream was checked.\nMoving it to a typed local restores checking on `.browser` and `.isBrowser`,\nwhich surfaces the calls that exceed the public types: `family` cannot carry\nan `!` exclusion prefix, and the throw test passes a deliberately invalid arg.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DNnGX8VnGS44GyLxTiAETT\n\n* test: keep browser spec formatting closer to the original\n\nRestore the `function ()` callback form and the multi-line matcher arrays so\nthe diff is limited to the lines the typed helper actually required.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DNnGX8VnGS44GyLxTiAETT\n\n* Revert \"test: type the browser spec''s commands helper\"\n\nReverts the typed local and the formatting follow-up. Dropping `this.commands`\nrewrote roughly a third of the file, which pushed rename similarity to 31% and\nmade GitHub render the spec as a delete plus an add rather than a rename.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DNnGX8VnGS44GyLxTiAETT\n\n* test: convert cypress.cy.js to TypeScript\n\nSwap the lodash `require` for an import so the file is treated as a module\nrather than a script, which also stops `$` and `Promise` colliding with the\nglobals and resolves `Promise` to Cypress''s bluebird. Cast the internal and\ndeliberately invalid calls the public types do not cover.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DNnGX8VnGS44GyLxTiAETT\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp9p7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdlkQAIBjalT+hM99Dao85rXoJznd\nj5ae+huAu9rfOo5/G9c1w++QHAm7p6VpoaCiK6u2GwoRGDdGCql0BFtXIVbBX251\n4s8sNSgEXubYURIwJOiG2rJk5bCQyoyqvpgPh8lo5DHP7CtA54DnNfDLZiqfpITj\nj9Sp/LAg3L9V25rJbotUlCN67v3F1RdLz+yyzfTWEWfXAqkVAnxcfCfI07DmYPu1\nWWRtPYEZsd/o7B9FlW7ruQDv+TZK5TzdFyZV9E1ataPBE/ta2/GgZW8DZ7QJxWK5\ngiMJIRTN9iHv7uhmLzLdt6MOWxsJ4jWSA+nhcYI8p84s1nAek7MNLAcljuWYG2KZ\nHccb8bYUxW1LNtR7puiE72KKjaHi44d0iJYNToE83s0rf20PN1HNGk2S3PtwkQwe\nnI2F3lJDDNCjBEWxCvuNo4vUUx86Ad3JKsC6hPZCFBQIe1xmQWdBBe8EX6IVTEUO\ncT2mjPxGT+qOl7+6UMi43ZpS/3Hbgm34qFDDN6AfJuQqSSUF9hfnxodJ3vX7GJxe\nQm8QL3QfNRmC2jIM+j/LTXbKcvH0wSnFKr125/Zj3vwtZsOzSlXTAVTvhxLQ3PdP\npv6kIYb9/HtHO4tQF1E/mINgEjB187zHvcmDb11kERZKCbtb4cCQh9gdFz+5UTh1\nr5lr6XzZ/LGy4lxEe3bo\n=hHy6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T11:29:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/48e8b3757b5dc13ecaf7be8051f2bb65f31c5398","node_id":"C_kwDOAeKht9oAKDQ4ZThiMzc1N2I1ZGMxM2VjYWY3YmU4MDUxZjJiYjY1ZjMxYzUzOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/commit/fe1998c95f5c8323653fb2e7a35b3916299a5921","sha":"fe1998c95f5c8323653fb2e7a35b3916299a5921","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/fe1998c95f5c8323653fb2e7a35b3916299a5921"}],"sha":"48e8b3757b5dc13ecaf7be8051f2bb65f31c5398","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/48e8b3757b5dc13ecaf7be8051f2bb65f31c5398"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1271364?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jennifer-shehane","id":1271364,"login":"jennifer-shehane","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzEzNjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jennifer-shehane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/commits/fe1998c95f5c8323653fb2e7a35b3916299a5921/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T23:55:43Z","email":"jennifer@cypress.io","name":"Jennifer Shehane"},"comment_count":4,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T23:55:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: use spread instead of .apply() and promote prefer-spread to error (#34835)\n\n* chore: replace .apply() with spread to resolve prefer-spread warnings\n\nEach of these call sites passed the receiving object as the `thisArg` to\n`.apply()`, so spreading the argument array preserves both the receiver and\nthe argument list exactly.\n\nThe manager helpers call into implementations that ship from the Cloud\n(AppCaptureProtocol, StudioServer, CyPromptServer). Those are plain class\ninstances, so the structural contract of method names and signatures is\nuntouched. One nuance worth noting: when version skew leaves a method\nmissing, the caught TypeError now reads \"<method> is not a function\"\nrather than blaming `apply`. Both paths are still caught and reported the\nsame way, and the new message names the method.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016p5wVMTydRJqNYEVM4ezXC\n\n* chore: replace .apply() with spread in state spec\n\nThe `thisArg` was already the object the method was read off, so spreading\nthe argument array preserves both the receiver and the argument list.\n\nThis was the last remaining prefer-spread warning in the monorepo.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016p5wVMTydRJqNYEVM4ezXC\n\n* test: cover receiver binding and argument forwarding for Cloud invocations\n\nThe protocol, studio and cy prompt managers reach implementations that ship\nfrom the Cloud as class instances whose methods rely on `this`. Argument\nforwarding was already well covered, but nothing asserted which object the\nmethod is invoked on, so detaching one from its instance passed every test.\n\nAdds receiver assertions to each manager, plus the first coverage of the\nsocket `mocha` handler, whose variadic forwarding to onMocha had none.\n\nVerified by mutation: detaching the method from its receiver, and passing the\nargument array instead of spreading it, each fail the new tests. Under the\nreceiver mutation every pre-existing test in protocol_spec still passed, and\nunder the onMocha mutation all 71 pre-existing socket tests still passed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016p5wVMTydRJqNYEVM4ezXC\n\n* test: tighten comments on Cloud invocation tests\n\nReduce the receiver rationale to the one fact the code does not already\nconvey: the Cloud ships these servers as class instances that rely on `this`.\nThe test names carry the rest.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016p5wVMTydRJqNYEVM4ezXC\n\n* chore: promote prefer-spread from warn to error\n\nThe monorepo no longer violates the rule, so new .apply() calls that a spread\nwould replace can be caught rather than accumulating as warnings.\n\nMoves the rule into the enabled-rules block; it had been sitting under a\ncomment describing rules that are off pending enablement.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016p5wVMTydRJqNYEVM4ezXC\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"acc3751c10a4a28b3604d6eaca2768dad823539d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/trees/acc3751c10a4a28b3604d6eaca2768dad823539d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/git/commits/fe1998c95f5c8323653fb2e7a35b3916299a5921","verification":{"payload":"tree acc3751c10a4a28b3604d6eaca2768dad823539d\nparent 1a43c716dadce9e46500df20ca7528b22b4e862d\nauthor Jennifer Shehane <jennifer@cypress.io> 1789343743 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789343743 -0400\n\nchore: use spread instead of .apply() and promote prefer-spread to error (#34835)\n\n* chore: replace .apply() with spread to resolve prefer-spread warnings\n\nEach of these call sites passed the receiving object as the `thisArg` to\n`.apply()`, so spreading the argument array preserves both the receiver and\nthe argument list exactly.\n\nThe manager helpers call into implementations that ship from the Cloud\n(AppCaptureProtocol, StudioServer, CyPromptServer). Those are plain class\ninstances, so the structural contract of method names and signatures is\nuntouched. One nuance worth noting: when version skew leaves a method\nmissing, the caught TypeError now reads \"<method> is not a function\"\nrather than blaming `apply`. Both paths are still caught and reported the\nsame way, and the new message names the method.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016p5wVMTydRJqNYEVM4ezXC\n\n* chore: replace .apply() with spread in state spec\n\nThe `thisArg` was already the object the method was read off, so spreading\nthe argument array preserves both the receiver and the argument list.\n\nThis was the last remaining prefer-spread warning in the monorepo.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016p5wVMTydRJqNYEVM4ezXC\n\n* test: cover receiver binding and argument forwarding for Cloud invocations\n\nThe protocol, studio and cy prompt managers reach implementations that ship\nfrom the Cloud as class instances whose methods rely on `this`. Argument\nforwarding was already well covered, but nothing asserted which object the\nmethod is invoked on, so detaching one from its instance passed every test.\n\nAdds receiver assertions to each manager, plus the first coverage of the\nsocket `mocha` handler, whose variadic forwarding to onMocha had none.\n\nVerified by mutation: detaching the method from its receiver, and passing the\nargument array instead of spreading it, each fail the new tests. Under the\nreceiver mutation every pre-existing test in protocol_spec still passed, and\nunder the onMocha mutation all 71 pre-existing socket tests still passed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016p5wVMTydRJqNYEVM4ezXC\n\n* test: tighten comments on Cloud invocation tests\n\nReduce the receiver rationale to the one fact the code does not already\nconvey: the Cloud ships these servers as class instances that rely on `this`.\nThe test names carry the rest.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016p5wVMTydRJqNYEVM4ezXC\n\n* chore: promote prefer-spread from warn to error\n\nThe monorepo no longer violates the rule, so new .apply() calls that a spread\nwould replace can be caught rather than accumulating as warnings.\n\nMoves the rule into the enabled-rules block; it had been sitting under a\ncomment describing rules that are off pending enablement.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016p5wVMTydRJqNYEVM4ezXC\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpzf/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA50sQAENONpLUDeqEIANar2QrGjFk\n+LF+IlaKq9bHB1VDlXurBGgBsYA1thEw3o8NZrJcPo9GNkPM8H2MPVeqOqEjm0Bx\nQWsCWaa2iA+EiMjw93Pw9xyHHf5b6LIpIqcFVMXUqoIYgr1TlpAqpJ3immlE43OU\nKd56yxfpDrLaI0IyFwMLYzxPWRdzXYuhakzoSHXiTG7MKuSA5jQ85MAzUSuRfPD3\naRx5iP2mH48J5UK0nrYQkEaM73g2nsHFGm78SRzGLsXYjxt5M+OxdKxCeRO/6uum\nwy4JNB7wU+MZGa/Na1P4N8qXvLlFiXYUsEkFXqrdJ20H3sB1i+w4QwzqOH/1pOLS\n546mjxDdbBFvBVEOSA6XWw3b7wQdGvu+cOIUUIhmRshJIL2CKDvzJrtEvrQcT4bi\nrtoj2hhurklOePM8pd8pqzEem6ASk7pNvLLYHOZ+MDIQJQ9