rs/esarafianou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/esarafianou","id":17114347,"login":"esarafianou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MTE0MzQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/e32d8734cb082a1cc4ffed6eb827342d28b1fc8f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T08:40:33Z","email":"eva.sarafianou@gmail.com","name":"Eva Sarafianou"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T08:40:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Request docs-draft review from a human when the source PR author is a bot (#38987)\n\n* When a bot authors the source PR, request docs-draft review from a human reviewer of that PR instead of the bot.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Keep the docs draft running if GitHub reviewer lookup fails.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"4dc7176ec286e7f362189185c5e0d87915066e5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/trees/4dc7176ec286e7f362189185c5e0d87915066e5e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/commits/e32d8734cb082a1cc4ffed6eb827342d28b1fc8f","verification":{"payload":"tree 4dc7176ec286e7f362189185c5e0d87915066e5e\nparent 9e386cb9937f05f97cb42c9fef5b1c0d13832c42\nauthor Eva Sarafianou <eva.sarafianou@gmail.com> 1791189633 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791189633 +0200\n\nRequest docs-draft review from a human when the source PR author is a bot (#38987)\n\n* When a bot authors the source PR, request docs-draft review from a human reviewer of that PR instead of the bot.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Keep the docs draft running if GitHub reviewer lookup fails.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw2KBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoNUQAIl33pSPLyD+AoqTPQBjTxyx\n28QEwfZtCN3Qt5PORzoFVzYZBSRHb5sUNDQ7n39XbuBg7UaD41FSMOObHLkdr/5W\nQ9QbotVdrLGRPpAmnUDGXQNFDk9ViYhtx+2R+91S7Uyod3BcKgDvutxWmfuubJXx\n5RIsns7zUQLl4jjB1rofdp4WlrUrkcGz7PK29hb5jsT+9cUtkqmBxNmyDIXIBCil\n5zsc5gBeYkdVTtlTU/TTs3CmCfWAU6NkzOCHp2vv38KU1VYhaV2Bx9NQgEiG5iUM\nci4Ag9pSLxCv0EfIwFC+l1AJc7vMyAnSHiOoTFoVPVoXcZlyPEwi26w3t3jm5TYk\ns5lGMk2hrQ/e5u6rPlEJMgZZ9HhCIiVxaHvJ2pgrYdu1v39vkX8YyWzyrWsDEyJV\nEDnT8P3eH4bkEO6FlL5ljfy92Fseh8+X/jQr7w6POpvc7sYnUvlZ8+8mghNpVNO8\nFHEcppLxXxtkPNnW0Iycr/XbfK3bI0qzbdwUo8xqcSazMDrA+dfbZCU9wna72uS/\nlB7fblkxEkXqnsmKIWLamQITmUxg4rvDAgMfIwlc5ItaQPL3WHwi+ahFGbIcxNSH\nSfELkfKWQpnOVIujh9WPrafJ5K+6cUlrxgb2FLoHo3WxGtKeHZqas3f31jC5EFrk\nvqKSwyMQmKv1Twmx2VTF\n=80A4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T08:40:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/e32d8734cb082a1cc4ffed6eb827342d28b1fc8f","node_id":"C_kwDOAjtrA9oAKGUzMmQ4NzM0Y2IwODJhMWNjNGZmZWQ2ZWI4MjczNDJkMjhiMWZjOGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/9e386cb9937f05f97cb42c9fef5b1c0d13832c42","sha":"9e386cb9937f05f97cb42c9fef5b1c0d13832c42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/9e386cb9937f05f97cb42c9fef5b1c0d13832c42"}],"sha":"e32d8734cb082a1cc4ffed6eb827342d28b1fc8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/e32d8734cb082a1cc4ffed6eb827342d28b1fc8f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17114347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/esarafianou","id":17114347,"login":"esarafianou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MTE0MzQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/9e386cb9937f05f97cb42c9fef5b1c0d13832c42/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T09:01:13Z","email":"eva.sarafianou@gmail.com","name":"Eva Sarafianou"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T09:01:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: resolve raw HTML link and image paths through useBaseUrl (#38958)\n\n* docs: resolve raw HTML link and image paths through useBaseUrl\n\nDocusaurus prepends `baseUrl` to markdown-syntax links (`[text](/path)`) but\nnever to site-absolute paths written in raw HTML/JSX attributes. Those values\nship verbatim, which is correct only while `baseUrl` is `/`.\n\nConvert the 221 raw `<a href=\"/...\">` anchors across 22 files under docs/main\nand the 3 raw `<img src=\"/img/...\">` tags in docs/develop to\n`useBaseUrl(''/...'')`, matching how images in the same table rows already\nresolve their paths. Link targets, link text and table structure are unchanged.\n\nAdd scripts/check-base-url-attrs.mjs and run it as the first step of\n`prebuild` so the build fails fast on any new occurrence.\n\n* docs(site): match CommonMark fence closing in baseUrl attr check\n\nToggle on any fence-like line could exit a block early; track the\nopening marker and only close with the same character of sufficient length.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs(site): also flag JSX string-literal href/src in baseUrl check\n\nQuoted attributes alone miss href={\"/path\"} / src={''/path''}, which\nbypass baseUrl the same way. Scan both forms through one validation path.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"484eb94a36a812401c825999c8ec7bf6bbb3fec3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/trees/484eb94a36a812401c825999c8ec7bf6bbb3fec3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/commits/9e386cb9937f05f97cb42c9fef5b1c0d13832c42","verification":{"payload":"tree 484eb94a36a812401c825999c8ec7bf6bbb3fec3\nparent 05a293c603f9909565a8793148a5f7a08b4d3274\nauthor Eva Sarafianou <eva.sarafianou@gmail.com> 1791104473 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791104473 +0200\n\ndocs: resolve raw HTML link and image paths through useBaseUrl (#38958)\n\n* docs: resolve raw HTML link and image paths through useBaseUrl\n\nDocusaurus prepends `baseUrl` to markdown-syntax links (`[text](/path)`) but\nnever to site-absolute paths written in raw HTML/JSX attributes. Those values\nship verbatim, which is correct only while `baseUrl` is `/`.\n\nConvert the 221 raw `<a href=\"/...\">` anchors across 22 files under docs/main\nand the 3 raw `<img src=\"/img/...\">` tags in docs/develop to\n`useBaseUrl(''/...'')`, matching how images in the same table rows already\nresolve their paths. Link targets, link text and table structure are unchanged.\n\nAdd scripts/check-base-url-attrs.mjs and run it as the first step of\n`prebuild` so the build fails fast on any new occurrence.\n\n* docs(site): match CommonMark fence closing in baseUrl attr check\n\nToggle on any fence-like line could exit a block early; track the\nopening marker and only close with the same character of sufficient length.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs(site): also flag JSX string-literal href/src in baseUrl check\n\nQuoted attributes alone miss href={\"/path\"} / src={''/path''}, which\nbypass baseUrl the same way. Scan both forms through one validation path.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwhXZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAg1sQAJjiX+CB20U9x4IEFV7cZvZ/\nDNUdjYZyHHYgUUK3K8vtpO9QbOY3LVVU6N+sV1qYQJBHztnpqv5ZCuyVMV8cSA5m\nj68bJo0KD/TvdiLT6bUDxygU0gXNkYQTUClJJzDVE8h6Nz9mhv/Gj4Cd/Zdnnbto\nC