/05a293c603f9909565a8793148a5f7a08b4d3274"}],"sha":"9e386cb9937f05f97cb42c9fef5b1c0d13832c42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/9e386cb9937f05f97cb42c9fef5b1c0d13832c42"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5334504?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saturninoabril/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saturninoabril/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saturninoabril/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saturninoabril/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/saturninoabril","id":5334504,"login":"saturninoabril","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMzQ1MDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saturninoabril/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saturninoabril/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saturninoabril/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saturninoabril/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saturninoabril/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saturninoabril","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/05a293c603f9909565a8793148a5f7a08b4d3274/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T04:35:53Z","email":"5334504+saturninoabril@users.noreply.github.com","name":"sabril"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T04:35:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"E2E/Test: Fix failing tests (#38981)\n\n* playwright: allow ensureFeatureFlag to set multiple flags, remove skipIfFeatureFlagNotSet\n\nensureFeatureFlag now accepts either a single (flagName, value) pair or a\n{flagName: value} map, so prerequisites like\n''await pw.skipIfFeatureFlagNotSet(\"ChannelAttributes\", true)'' can be\ncombined with other flag prerequisites into a single server restart\ninstead of one restart per flag.\n\nskipIfFeatureFlagNotSet is removed entirely (definition, export, and\nfixture wiring): it only ever skipped a test when a flag was off rather\nthan turning it on, which silently left specs gated on a flag that\ndefaults off (e.g. DiscoverableChannels, ManagedChannelCategories)\npermanently un-exercised in CI.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: migrate skipIfFeatureFlagNotSet call sites to ensureFeatureFlag\n\nMechanical rename of skipIfFeatureFlagNotSet(flag, true) to\nensureFeatureFlag(flag, true) across channel_attributes, global_attributes,\nboard_attributes, channel_perm_rules, and abac specs/helpers. Adjacent\nsingle-flag calls within the same test are merged into one\nensureFeatureFlag({flagA: true, flagB: true}) call so the server restarts\nonce per test instead of once per flag.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: mark tests broken by real DiscoverableChannels/ManagedChannelCategories as known issues\n\nBoth DiscoverableChannels and ManagedChannelCategories default to off and\nwere never set in the testcontainers CI baseline, so every spec gated on\nskipIfFeatureFlagNotSet(flag, true) for these flags silently self-skipped\nand never actually ran. Migrating them to ensureFeatureFlag makes the\nserver restart with the flag genuinely on, which surfaces pre-existing\nproduct bugs:\n\n- discoverable_channels.spec.ts: Browse Channels'' search results race the\n  typed-search fetch against the discoverable-only loadDiscoverableChannels()\n  fetch, intermittently dropping the ''Request to join'' button. The sibling\n  Find Channels flow is unaffected and still passes.\n- managed_categories.spec.ts: assigning a managed_category_name to a\n  channel has no effect on the sidebar in this server build - channels\n  stay under the regular CHANNELS group and no managed category header is\n  ever rendered, so every behavior that depends on being in a managed\n  category (grouping, sorting, real-time updates, disabled Favorite/Move\n  To/context-menu, and the System Console setting) fails.\n\nMark the affected tests with test.fixme and a @knownIssue comment so they\nreport as skipped rather than failing CI, while the two tests that don''t\ndepend on the broken behavior keep running normally.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: force ChannelAttributes off in channel_classification.spec.ts\n\nChannelAttributes now defaults on (#38937), which hides the legacy\nclassification toggle this suite exercises (gated on\n!channelAttributes.enabled in new_channel_modal.tsx and\nchannel_settings_configuration_tab.tsx). Force the flag off via\nensureFeatureFlag so the toggle renders again.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: force ChannelAttributes off in channel_banner.spec.ts\n\nSame root cause as channel_classification.spec.ts: with ChannelAttributes\non by default, channel_settings_configuration_tab.tsx renders the\nattribute-aware BannerTextEditor instead of the legacy AdvancedTextbox\n(testid channel_banner_banner_text_textbox) this suite drives. Force the\nflag off via ensureFeatureFlag so the legacy control renders again.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: give permalink preview wait more headroom in initial_scroll_read.spec.ts\n\nThe ''with multiple pages of post previews'' case waits on a .post-preview\nlocator with Playwright''s implicit 30s default timeout while 120\npermalink previews resolve. Under full 30-way parallel CI load this\nconsistently took 39-44s (observed across two separate dispatch leases\nin CI run 37112179268), timing out even though the behavior itself is\ncorrect. Explicitly extend the wait to 60s and the per-test timeout to\n90s for this case only.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* eslint-plugin: add playwright-ensure-feature-flag-top-level rule\n\nEnforces that a Playwright spec file calls ensureFeatureFlag at most\nonce, and only from a top-level test.beforeAll(). This keeps the\nintent of a spec''s feature-flag combination explicit at the top of\nthe file instead of scattered through individual tests, and bounds\neach spec file to at most one server restart.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: enable ensure-feature-flag-top-level rule, grandfather pre-existing files\n\nTurns the new rule on as an error for the whole specs/ tree, and\ncarves out the 14 files that already called ensureFeatureFlag more\nthan once per file or outside a top-level beforeAll before this rule\nexisted. Those predate this change and are unrelated to it; each\nneeds its own migration pass to a single top-level beforeAll.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: hoist ensureFeatureFlag to a single top-level beforeAll in channel_attributes specs\n\nConsolidates the per-test ensureFeatureFlag calls in\nchannel_attribute_assignment, channel_attribute_banner,\nchannel_attribute_banner_settings, channel_attribute_lifecycle, and\nchannel_attribute_settings_modal into one top-level beforeAll each,\nper the new playwright-ensure-feature-flag-top-level rule.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: hoist ensureFeatureFlag to a single top-level beforeAll in channel_attribute_display/editing specs\n\nConsolidates per-test ensureFeatureFlag calls into one top-level\nbeforeAll per file. The flag-off scenario in channel_attribute_display\nneeds the opposite ChannelAttributes value from every other test in\nthat file, so it moves to its own channel_attribute_display_flag_off.spec.ts.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: add channel_attribute_display_flag_off.spec.ts\n\nSplit out of channel_attribute_display.spec.ts: the flag-off scenario\nneeds the opposite ChannelAttributes value from every other test in\nthat file.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: mark 3 channel attribute chip-overflow tests as known issues\n\nThese three tests fail on master independent of this PR (reproduced\nagainst the committed baseline via git stash, and live against a\nTestcontainers server), each from a distinct bug in the\nChannelAttributeLabels/useLabelsOverflow chip-collapse feature:\n\n- ''collapses the thread header chips into +N without moving the\n  thread controls'': availableWidthForLabels only measures the chip\n  row''s own flex ancestor, which in the thread pane has no visibility\n  into how much room the separate Follow/popout/menu controls need.\n- ''collapses overflowing chips into +N without moving header\n  controls'': channel-header__icons'' deliberate min-width:0 lets it\n  shrink below what its own non-shrinking icon buttons need, and the\n  chip row is forced to show one chip even with zero room left,\n  spilling ~12px past the header.\n- ''adds and removes a multiselect option, and the header chips\n  follow'': removing one of two multiselect values leaves the chip\n  container permanently visibility:hidden -- useLabelsOverflow''s\n  debounced recalculation after the ids change never completes.\n\nEach is documented with a @knownIssue explaining the root cause found\nvia live reproduction, matching the convention already used for the\nmanaged categories known issues.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: split managed_categories.spec.ts flag-off test into its own file\n\nManagedChannelCategories true/false needs two separate server\nrestarts, so the one test needing the flag off moves to\nmanaged_categories_flag_off.spec.ts, leaving a single top-level\nbeforeAll(true) in managed_categories.spec.ts per the new\nplaywright-ensure-feature-flag-top-level rule.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: hoist ensureFeatureFlag to a single top-level beforeAll in misc specs\n\nConsolidates per-test ensureFeatureFlag calls into one top-level\nbeforeAll each in channel_perm_rules_v0_4, discoverable_channels,\nabac/policies/graph_operators, abac/resource_attributes/graph_sync,\nand abac/resource_attributes/masking, per the new\nplaywright-ensure-feature-flag-top-level rule.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: split channel_attributes_required_kill_switch.spec.ts by flag value\n\nChannelAttributesRequired true/false needs two separate server\nrestarts, so the file splits into\nchannel_attributes_required_kill_switch_on.spec.ts and\nchannel_attributes_required_kill_switch_off.spec.ts, each with a\nsingle top-level beforeAll, per the new\nplaywright-ensure-feature-flag-top-level rule.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: hoist ensureFeatureFlag to a single top-level beforeAll in global_attributes_form.spec.ts\n\nConsolidates the per-test flag combinations (ChannelAttributes,\nPostAttributes, PropertyFieldGraph) into one superset beforeAll: all\nthree are purely additive, so the superset covers every test here\nwith a single restart. Also stops requireHierarchicalAttributesEnabled\nin global_attributes_helpers.ts from hiding an indirect\nensureFeatureFlag call of its own.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: hoist ensureFeatureFlag and split classification markings test\n\nAdds a single top-level beforeAll(PropertyFieldGraph: true) to\nglobal_attributes_listing.spec.ts, needed after\nrequireHierarchicalAttributesEnabled stopped setting the flag itself.\nSplits the Classification Markings row test, which needs\nClassificationMarkings on, into its own\nglobal_attributes_listing_classification_markings.spec.ts, per the\nnew playwright-ensure-feature-flag-top-level rule.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: hoist ensureFeatureFlag to a single top-level beforeAll in remaining global_attributes specs\n\nConsolidates per-test ensureFeatureFlag calls into one top-level\nbeforeAll each in channel_resource_configuration.spec.ts and\nclassification_attribute.spec.ts, per the new\nplaywright-ensure-feature-flag-top-level rule.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* eslint-plugin: revert playwright-ensure-feature-flag-top-level rule\n\nDrop the custom rule enforcing ensureFeatureFlag at the top level of a\nspec file. A guideline in AGENTS.md and the function''s own doc comment\nis enough; tooling to enforce it is unnecessary overhead. Also reverts\neslint.config.mjs''s enablement of the rule and its grandfather list.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: support multiple flags in ensureFeatureFlag, refresh client after restart\n\nensureFeatureFlag now also accepts a {flagName: value} map so a test\ncan combine several prerequisite flags into a single restart instead\nof one per flag.\n\nAlso fixes a stale-client bug in its own post-restart verification:\nrestartMattermostContainer() points the server at a new container and\nclears the cached client, so the pre-restart adminClient was stale by\nthe time it was used to verify the flags took effect. Fetch a fresh\nclient instead.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: call ensureFeatureFlag per test, remove skipIfNoEnterpriseLicense, fix stale adminClient reuse\n\nRevert the top-level beforeAll/bare-import ensureFeatureFlag calls back\nto per-test pw.ensureFeatureFlag() calls, since pw is a test-scoped\nfixture and unavailable in beforeAll. Every test in a given spec file\npasses the same parameters, so the Testcontainers server still restarts\nat most once per file.\n\nReplace the local skipIfNoEnterpriseLicense helper with\npw.skipIfNoLicense().\n\nFix several places where an adminClient obtained before\nensureFeatureFlag''s restart was reused afterward: the restart points the\nserver at a new container, leaving that client stale. Reorder calls so\nensureFeatureFlag runs first, or refresh the client afterward when\nreordering is not possible.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: restore ChannelAttributes=false override in channel_classification.spec.ts\n\nLost during the top-level-to-per-test ensureFeatureFlag revert. Without\nit, ChannelAttributes defaulting on hides the legacy classification\ntoggle this suite exercises (gated on !channelAttributes.enabled in\nnew_channel_modal.tsx and channel_settings_configuration_tab.tsx),\nfailing every test with a timeout waiting for\nchannelClassificationToggle-button.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: give permalink preview wait more headroom in initial_scroll_read.spec.ts\n\n120 permalink previews each resolve their own lookup, which can exceed\nthe default test timeout under loaded CI. Extend the timeout for that\ncase to leave headroom on top of the one-minute postPreview.waitFor.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: document ensureFeatureFlag convention and PW_WORKERS in AGENTS.md\n\nAdd e2e-tests/playwright/AGENTS.md covering the single-worker-per-server\nparallelism model, the ensureFeatureFlag one-restart-per-file convention,\nand pw.skipIfNoLicense(). Import it from the root AGENTS.md.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: stop custom profile attribute fields leaking across spec files\n\nattribute_settings_behavior.spec.ts''s MM-T5749 test created a custom\nprofile attribute field named \"Cancel Test <id>\" and never deleted it,\nunlike its sibling spec files. Since CI runs many spec files against\none shared server per job, the field persisted and leaked into every\nlater test''s Profile modal in that job.\n\nIts Edit button''s computed accessible name becomes \"Cancel Test <id>\nEdit\" (title + button text via aria-labelledby), which\ngetByRole(''button'', {name: ''Cancel''})''s substring match also picked up\nalongside the real Cancel button, causing a strict-mode violation in\nlocked_profile_fields.spec.ts whenever both specs ran in the same job\n(reproduced locally by running them back-to-back on one server).\n\nFixes it two ways:\n- Track and delete the fields attribute_settings_behavior.spec.ts owns,\n  matching the deleteCustomProfileAttributes cleanup convention already\n  used by its sibling spec files.\n- Switch profile_modal.ts''s cancelButton to getByTestId(''cancelButton'')\n  instead of a substring role-name match, so this class of bug can''t\n  recur from any other attribute name.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: give long post-preview show-more check more headroom\n\nThe permalink preview needs a second render pass once the linked\npost''s content arrives before it knows whether to show the collapsed\n''Show more'' treatment. The default 10s expect timeout left no margin\nfor that extra round trip under loaded CI, causing this case alone\n(out of 26 in the same file) to fail intermittently. Extend to 20s,\nmirroring the same permalink-preview timing fix already applied to\ninitial_scroll_read.spec.ts.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: fix prettier formatting in attribute_settings_behavior.spec.ts\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>","tree":{"sha":"f12240d86c18b126ada8a15c3b30f7331f910645","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/trees/f12240d86c18b126ada8a15c3b30f7331f910645"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/commits/05a293c603f9909565a8793148a5f7a08b4d3274","verification":{"payload":"tree f12240d86c18b126ada8a15c3b30f7331f910645\nparent af4c3cfde668e006981efa29ba740791eb03fb13\nauthor sabril <5334504+saturninoabril@users.noreply.github.com> 1791088553 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791088553 +0800\n\nE2E/Test: Fix failing tests (#38981)\n\n* playwright: allow ensureFeatureFlag to set multiple flags, remove skipIfFeatureFlagNotSet\n\nensureFeatureFlag now accepts either a single (flagName, value) pair or a\n{flagName: value} map, so prerequisites like\n''await pw.skipIfFeatureFlagNotSet(\"ChannelAttributes\", true)'' can be\ncombined with other flag prerequisites into a single server restart\ninstead of one restart per flag.\n\nskipIfFeatureFlagNotSet is removed entirely (definition, export, and\nfixture wiring): it only ever skipped a test when a flag was off rather\nthan turning it on, which silently left specs gated on a flag that\ndefaults off (e.g. DiscoverableChannels, ManagedChannelCategories)\npermanently un-exercised in CI.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: migrate skipIfFeatureFlagNotSet call sites to ensureFeatureFlag\n\nMechanical rename of skipIfFeatureFlagNotSet(flag, true) to\nensureFeatureFlag(flag, true) across channel_attributes, global_attributes,\nboard_attributes, channel_perm_rules, and abac specs/helpers. Adjacent\nsingle-flag calls within the same test are merged into one\nensureFeatureFlag({flagA: true, flagB: true}) call so the server restarts\nonce per test instead of once per flag.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: mark tests broken by real DiscoverableChannels/ManagedChannelCategories as known issues\n\nBoth DiscoverableChannels and ManagedChannelCategories default to off and\nwere never set in the testcontainers CI baseline, so every spec gated on\nskipIfFeatureFlagNotSet(flag, true) for these flags silently self-skipped\nand never actually ran. Migrating them to ensureFeatureFlag makes the\nserver restart with the flag genuinely on, which surfaces pre-existing\nproduct bugs:\n\n- discoverable_channels.spec.ts: Browse Channels'' search results race the\n  typed-search fetch against the discoverable-only loadDiscoverableChannels()\n  fetch, intermittently dropping the ''Request to join'' button. The sibling\n  Find Channels flow is unaffected and still passes.\n- managed_categories.spec.ts: assigning a managed_category_name to a\n  channel has no effect on the sidebar in this server build - channels\n  stay under the regular CHANNELS group and no managed category header is\n  ever rendered, so every behavior that depends on being in a managed\n  category (grouping, sorting, real-time updates, disabled Favorite/Move\n  To/context-menu, and the System Console setting) fails.\n\nMark the affected tests with test.fixme and a @knownIssue comment so they\nreport as skipped rather than failing CI, while the two tests that don''t\ndepend on the broken behavior keep running normally.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: force ChannelAttributes off in channel_classification.spec.ts\n\nChannelAttributes now defaults on (#38937), which hides the legacy\nclassification toggle this suite exercises (gated on\n!channelAttributes.enabled in new_channel_modal.tsx and\nchannel_settings_configuration_tab.tsx). Force the flag off via\nensureFeatureFlag so the toggle renders again.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: force ChannelAttributes off in channel_banner.spec.ts\n\nSame root cause as channel_classification.spec.ts: with ChannelAttributes\non by default, channel_settings_configuration_tab.tsx renders the\nattribute-aware BannerTextEditor instead of the legacy AdvancedTextbox\n(testid channel_banner_banner_text_textbox) this suite drives. Force the\nflag off via ensureFeatureFlag so the legacy control renders again.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: give permalink preview wait more headroom in initial_scroll_read.spec.ts\n\nThe ''with multiple pages of post previews'' case waits on a .post-preview\nlocator with Playwright''s implicit 30s default timeout while 120\npermalink previews resolve. Under full 30-way parallel CI load this\nconsistently took 39-44s (observed across two separate dispatch leases\nin CI run 37112179268), timing out even though the behavior itself is\ncorrect. Explicitly extend the wait to 60s and the per-test timeout to\n90s for this case only.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* eslint-plugin: add playwright-ensure-feature-flag-top-level rule\n\nEnforces that a Playwright spec file calls ensureFeatureFlag at most\nonce, and only from a top-level test.beforeAll(). This keeps the\nintent of a spec''s feature-flag combination explicit at the top of\nthe file instead of scattered through individual tests, and bounds\neach spec file to at most one server restart.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: enable ensure-feature-flag-top-level rule, grandfather pre-existing files\n\nTurns the new rule on as an error for the whole specs/ tree, and\ncarves out the 14 files that already called ensureFeatureFlag more\nthan once per file or outside a top-level beforeAll before this rule\nexisted. Those predate this change and are unrelated to it; each\nneeds its own migration pass to a single top-level beforeAll.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: hoist ensureFeatureFlag to a single top-level beforeAll in channel_attributes specs\n\nConsolidates the per-test ensureFeatureFlag calls in\nchannel_attribute_assignment, channel_attribute_banner,\nchannel_attribute_banner_settings, channel_attribute_lifecycle, and\nchannel_attribute_settings_modal into one top-level beforeAll each,\nper the new playwright-ensure-feature-flag-top-level rule.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: hoist ensureFeatureFlag to a single top-level beforeAll in channel_attribute_display/editing specs\n\nConsolidates per-test ensureFeatureFlag calls into one top-level\nbeforeAll per file. The flag-off scenario in channel_attribute_display\nneeds the opposite ChannelAttributes value from every other test in\nthat file, so it moves to its own channel_attribute_display_flag_off.spec.ts.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: add channel_attribute_display_flag_off.spec.ts\n\nSplit out of channel_attribute_display.spec.ts: the flag-off scenario\nneeds the opposite ChannelAttributes value from every other test in\nthat file.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: mark 3 channel attribute chip-overflow tests as known issues\n\nThese three tests fail on master independent of this PR (reproduced\nagainst the committed baseline via git stash, and live against a\nTestcontainers server), each from a distinct bug in the\nChannelAttributeLabels/useLabelsOverflow chip-collapse feature:\n\n- ''collapses the thread header chips into +N without moving the\n  thread controls'': availableWidthForLabels only measures the chip\n  row''s own flex ancestor, which in the thread pane has no visibility\n  into how much room the separate Follow/popout/menu controls need.\n- ''collapses overflowing chips into +N without moving header\n  controls'': channel-header__icons'' deliberate min-width:0 lets it\n  shrink below what its own non-shrinking icon buttons need, and the\n  chip row is forced to show one chip even with zero room left,\n  spilling ~12px past the header.\n- ''adds and removes a multiselect option, and the header chips\n  follow'': removing one of two multiselect values leaves the chip\n  container permanently visibility:hidden -- useLabelsOverflow''s\n  debounced recalculation after the ids change never completes.\n\nEach is documented with a @knownIssue explaining the root cause found\nvia live reproduction, matching the convention already used for the\nmanaged categories known issues.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: split managed_categories.spec.ts flag-off test into its own file\n\nManagedChannelCategories true/false needs two separate server\nrestarts, so the one test needing the flag off moves to\nmanaged_categories_flag_off.spec.ts, leaving a single top-level\nbeforeAll(true) in managed_categories.spec.ts per the new\nplaywright-ensure-feature-flag-top-level rule.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: hoist ensureFeatureFlag to a single top-level beforeAll in misc specs\n\nConsolidates per-test ensureFeatureFlag calls into one top-level\nbeforeAll each in channel_perm_rules_v0_4, discoverable_channels,\nabac/policies/graph_operators, abac/resource_attributes/graph_sync,\nand abac/resource_attributes/masking, per the new\nplaywright-ensure-feature-flag-top-level rule.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: split channel_attributes_required_kill_switch.spec.ts by flag value\n\nChannelAttributesRequired true/false needs two separate server\nrestarts, so the file splits into\nchannel_attributes_required_kill_switch_on.spec.ts and\nchannel_attributes_required_kill_switch_off.spec.ts, each with a\nsingle top-level beforeAll, per the new\nplaywright-ensure-feature-flag-top-level rule.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: hoist ensureFeatureFlag to a single top-level beforeAll in global_attributes_form.spec.ts\n\nConsolidates the per-test flag combinations (ChannelAttributes,\nPostAttributes, PropertyFieldGraph) into one superset beforeAll: all\nthree are purely additive, so the superset covers every test here\nwith a single restart. Also stops requireHierarchicalAttributesEnabled\nin global_attributes_helpers.ts from hiding an indirect\nensureFeatureFlag call of its own.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: hoist ensureFeatureFlag and split classification markings test\n\nAdds a single top-level beforeAll(PropertyFieldGraph: true) to\nglobal_attributes_listing.spec.ts, needed after\nrequireHierarchicalAttributesEnabled stopped setting the flag itself.\nSplits the Classification Markings row test, which needs\nClassificationMarkings on, into its own\nglobal_attributes_listing_classification_markings.spec.ts, per the\nnew playwright-ensure-feature-flag-top-level rule.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: hoist ensureFeatureFlag to a single top-level beforeAll in remaining global_attributes specs\n\nConsolidates per-test ensureFeatureFlag calls into one top-level\nbeforeAll each in channel_resource_configuration.spec.ts and\nclassification_attribute.spec.ts, per the new\nplaywright-ensure-feature-flag-top-level rule.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* eslint-plugin: revert playwright-ensure-feature-flag-top-level rule\n\nDrop the custom rule enforcing ensureFeatureFlag at the top level of a\nspec file. A guideline in AGENTS.md and the function''s own doc comment\nis enough; tooling to enforce it is unnecessary overhead. Also reverts\neslint.config.mjs''s enablement of the rule and its grandfather list.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: support multiple flags in ensureFeatureFlag, refresh client after restart\n\nensureFeatureFlag now also accepts a {flagName: value} map so a test\ncan combine several prerequisite flags into a single restart instead\nof one per flag.\n\nAlso fixes a stale-client bug in its own post-restart verification:\nrestartMattermostContainer() points the server at a new container and\nclears the cached client, so the pre-restart adminClient was stale by\nthe time it was used to verify the flags took effect. Fetch a fresh\nclient instead.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: call ensureFeatureFlag per test, remove skipIfNoEnterpriseLicense, fix stale adminClient reuse\n\nRevert the top-level beforeAll/bare-import ensureFeatureFlag calls back\nto per-test pw.ensureFeatureFlag() calls, since pw is a test-scoped\nfixture and unavailable in beforeAll. Every test in a given spec file\npasses the same parameters, so the Testcontainers server still restarts\nat most once per file.\n\nReplace the local skipIfNoEnterpriseLicense helper with\npw.skipIfNoLicense().\n\nFix several places where an adminClient obtained before\nensureFeatureFlag''s restart was reused afterward: the restart points the\nserver at a new container, leaving that client stale. Reorder calls so\nensureFeatureFlag runs first, or refresh the client afterward when\nreordering is not possible.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: restore ChannelAttributes=false override in channel_classification.spec.ts\n\nLost during the top-level-to-per-test ensureFeatureFlag revert. Without\nit, ChannelAttributes defaulting on hides the legacy classification\ntoggle this suite exercises (gated on !channelAttributes.enabled in\nnew_channel_modal.tsx and channel_settings_configuration_tab.tsx),\nfailing every test with a timeout waiting for\nchannelClassificationToggle-button.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: give permalink preview wait more headroom in initial_scroll_read.spec.ts\n\n120 permalink previews each resolve their own lookup, which can exceed\nthe default test timeout under loaded CI. Extend the timeout for that\ncase to leave headroom on top of the one-minute postPreview.waitFor.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: document ensureFeatureFlag convention and PW_WORKERS in AGENTS.md\n\nAdd e2e-tests/playwright/AGENTS.md covering the single-worker-per-server\nparallelism model, the ensureFeatureFlag one-restart-per-file convention,\nand pw.skipIfNoLicense(). Import it from the root AGENTS.md.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: stop custom profile attribute fields leaking across spec files\n\nattribute_settings_behavior.spec.ts''s MM-T5749 test created a custom\nprofile attribute field named \"Cancel Test <id>\" and never deleted it,\nunlike its sibling spec files. Since CI runs many spec files against\none shared server per job, the field persisted and leaked into every\nlater test''s Profile modal in that job.\n\nIts Edit button''s computed accessible name becomes \"Cancel Test <id>\nEdit\" (title + button text via aria-labelledby), which\ngetByRole(''button'', {name: ''Cancel''})''s substring match also picked up\nalongside the real Cancel button, causing a strict-mode violation in\nlocked_profile_fields.spec.ts whenever both specs ran in the same job\n(reproduced locally by running them back-to-back on one server).\n\nFixes it two ways:\n- Track and delete the fields attribute_settings_behavior.spec.ts owns,\n  matching the deleteCustomProfileAttributes cleanup convention already\n  used by its sibling spec files.\n- Switch profile_modal.ts''s cancelButton to getByTestId(''cancelButton'')\n  instead of a substring role-name match, so this class of bug can''t\n  recur from any other attribute name.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: give long post-preview show-more check more headroom\n\nThe permalink preview needs a second render pass once the linked\npost''s content arrives before it knows whether to show the collapsed\n''Show more'' treatment. The default 10s expect timeout left no margin\nfor that extra round trip under loaded CI, causing this case alone\n(out of 26 in the same file) to fail intermittently. Extend to 20s,\nmirroring the same permalink-preview timing fix already applied to\ninitial_scroll_read.spec.ts.\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n* playwright: fix prettier formatting in attribute_settings_behavior.spec.ts\n\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: saturnino <saturnino@mattermost.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwdepCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnykQAJT7UgKd5j8lzqYImErPLmUL\neBJVYfrlZfgtwn