437ab3e7632017cd3cf2ec06e4785467ae7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/85e95437ab3e7632017cd3cf2ec06e4785467ae7"}],"sha":"af4c3cfde668e006981efa29ba740791eb03fb13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/af4c3cfde668e006981efa29ba740791eb03fb13"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1210556?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/cursor","id":206951365,"login":"cursor[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODFXTxQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/85e95437ab3e7632017cd3cf2ec06e4785467ae7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T23:03:29Z","email":"206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"cursor[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T23:03:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[MM-70822] Explain the blocked section switch while editing a channel permission rule (#38751)\n\n* [MM-70822] Explain the blocked section switch while editing a channel permission rule\n\nThe Channel Settings modal refuses to switch sections while a tab reports\nunsaved changes, and the Permissions Policy tab reports unsaved changes for as\nlong as its rule editor is open. The SaveChangesPanel that explains the refusal\nonly renders in that tab''s list view, so clicking Info, Membership Policy or\nConfiguration while editing a rule did nothing at all: no section change, no\nmessage, even though the items still looked clickable.\n\nRoute the modal''s existing showTabSwitchError signal into the rule editor''s\nerror slot so the refusal is explained where the user is looking, and mark that\nslot role=''alert'' so it is announced rather than only seen.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70822] Scroll the blocked section-switch warning into view\n\nWhen the rule editor is taller than the modal, the alert that explains a\nrefused section switch sat below the fold. Scroll it into view when the\nerror appears so the message is actually visible.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Align max-login-attempts Playwright locators with current login copy\n\nThe full Playwright suite failed on max_login_attempts.spec.ts: exact\nmatches for the old invalid-credentials banner and lockout sentence no\nlonger hold. Use the shared invalidCredentialsError locator and the\nstable lock-message prefix.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Pick future dates in the demo plugin date dialog e2e spec\n\nDays 20 and 22 of the current month are in the past after mid-month, and\nthe plugin rejects those submissions. Advance to next month in that case.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Retrigger CI for Enterprise docker image and E2E\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70822] Report the blocked section switch through the modal''s floating footer\n\nPer review, the rule editor now raises the same SaveChangesPanel the rest of\nthe Channel Settings modal uses, in its built-in error state, instead of a\nbespoke inline message — matching the Team Settings membership policy editor.\n\nThe footer is position: fixed at the bottom of the modal, so it is visible\nwhatever the editor is scrolled to; the scroll-into-view workaround the inline\nmessage needed goes away with it. Saving from the footer stays disabled (the\nrule is committed from the editor''s own button) and its Cancel leaves the\neditor, so the two ways out of the block are the ones the message names.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70822] Cover the blocked-switch footer''s way out in the E2E spec\n\nThe footer''s Cancel is now the exit the message points at, so assert it drops\nthe draft and returns to the rules list.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Revert unrelated e2e test fixes\n\nRestore demo_dialog_date.spec.ts and max_login_attempts.spec.ts to their\nupstream state. These e2e changes are unrelated to the MM-70822 channel\npermission-rule fix and were flagged for removal in review.\n\nAddress PR feedback: 0 answered, 1 resolved, 0 declined\n\n* Retrigger CI after an unrelated Playwright flake on HEAD\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com>","tree":{"sha":"814048dcf4f3efe8f9bc221c4b39502b2da27ffc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/trees/814048dcf4f3efe8f9bc221c4b39502b2da27ffc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/commits/85e95437ab3e7632017cd3cf2ec06e4785467ae7","verification":{"payload":"tree 814048dcf4f3efe8f9bc221c4b39502b2da27ffc\nparent 6338ffdc768e8eedcb8604a11e4207347911787e\nauthor cursor[bot] <206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1790982209 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790982209 -0400\n\n[MM-70822] Explain the blocked section switch while editing a channel permission rule (#38751)\n\n* [MM-70822] Explain the blocked section switch while editing a channel permission rule\n\nThe Channel Settings modal refuses to switch sections while a tab reports\nunsaved changes, and the Permissions Policy tab reports unsaved changes for as\nlong as its rule editor is open. The SaveChangesPanel that explains the refusal\nonly renders in that tab''s list view, so clicking Info, Membership Policy or\nConfiguration while editing a rule did nothing at all: no section change, no\nmessage, even though the items still looked clickable.\n\nRoute the modal''s existing showTabSwitchError signal into the rule editor''s\nerror slot so the refusal is explained where the user is looking, and mark that\nslot role=''alert'' so it is announced rather than only seen.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70822] Scroll the blocked section-switch warning into view\n\nWhen the rule editor is taller than the modal, the alert that explains a\nrefused section switch sat below the fold. Scroll it into view when the\nerror appears so the message is actually visible.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Align max-login-attempts Playwright locators with current login copy\n\nThe full Playwright suite failed on max_login_attempts.spec.ts: exact\nmatches for the old invalid-credentials banner and lockout sentence no\nlonger hold. Use the shared invalidCredentialsError locator and the\nstable lock-message prefix.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Pick future dates in the demo plugin date dialog e2e spec\n\nDays 20 and 22 of the current month are in the past after mid-month, and\nthe plugin rejects those submissions. Advance to next month in that case.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Retrigger CI for Enterprise docker image and E2E\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70822] Report the blocked section switch through the modal''s floating footer\n\nPer review, the rule editor now raises the same SaveChangesPanel the rest of\nthe Channel Settings modal uses, in its built-in error state, instead of a\nbespoke inline message — matching the Team Settings membership policy editor.\n\nThe footer is position: fixed at the bottom of the modal, so it is visible\nwhatever the editor is scrolled to; the scroll-into-view workaround the inline\nmessage needed goes away with it. Saving from the footer stays disabled (the\nrule is committed from the editor''s own button) and its Cancel leaves the\neditor, so the two ways out of the block are the ones the message names.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70822] Cover the blocked-switch footer''s way out in the E2E spec\n\nThe footer''s Cancel is now the exit the message points at, so assert it drops\nthe draft and returns to the rules list.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Revert unrelated e2e test fixes\n\nRestore demo_dialog_date.spec.ts and max_login_attempts.spec.ts to their\nupstream state. These e2e changes are unrelated to the MM-70822 channel\npermission-rule fix and were flagged for removal in review.\n\nAddress PR feedback: 0 answered, 1 resolved, 0 declined\n\n* Retrigger CI after an unrelated Playwright flake on HEAD\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwDhBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvNkQAIX/FylePnv+h0hEPW6cR2BL\nfSFdWjbtVF9is2L1ExW5bvoHE4brsVZUGf9VZQvpHihQ69HKZCZ4ymeXdTCsxbQ3\nL/+gMeNlXRDqKLMrbKt+lrLzZuRzID4u4Z9UxsrgH+mkjLdeKnQ4/gh9A/bzMrvD\nFbpgbCwhpQZix9uXZSdu0LttF8/Qr8lrvJlJuebnCqOGgYMEhvAxryXy6CfTSUWJ\n5EWD0KM4LL8IxghxVYmdKjaw8MsdTuTrXfEU77N0VvQdvn/pKj8lrjQ8VBxTj9GR\n5o