2Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Align channel attribute chips and fix header label flicker (#38841)\n\n* Align channel attribute chips and stop header label flicker.\n\nMake hierarchical and select/rank chips share AttributeChip chrome in channel info, and stabilize header overflow measurement so squeezed channel names do not re-expand chips.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Hide channel attribute chip dismiss until the value menu is open.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Collapse hidden chip dismiss so resting chips do not reserve trailing space.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Keep text attribute edit size aligned with the resting value.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Fix stylelint property order in channel attribute SCSS.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Cache chip widths before collapsing on zero available space.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Fix multiselect outside-click close and chip-remove keyboard activation.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Fix stylelint property order on AttributeChip remove control.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Fix graph picker disabled assertions and label activation.\n\nDiv Menu triggers use aria-disabled (jest-dom toBeDisabled only covers form controls), and label htmlFor cannot activate a non-labelable div, so forward the field-name click.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Align select attribute triggers with inline chips and clear via chip X.\n\nSelect/rank fields were still using the boxed input+chevron trigger and a Clear menu item, while Channel Info graph/multiselect chrome is borderless chips with in-chip remove.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Remove unused channel_attributes.info.clear i18n string.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Unify channel attribute chip size so classification matches other chips.\n\nChannel Info had been forcing AttributeChip to 24px with zero vertical padding (a leftover graph-picker metric), and medium chips still uppercased non-dismissible values — solid TOP SECRET / UNCLASSIFIED pills read taller than severity and multiselect chips sharing the same component.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Remove stale channel_attributes.info.clear keys from locale files.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Clamp channel attribute chips to 148px and lock medium height.\n\nLong multiselect values were overflowing Channel Info because medium chips only had max-width 100%, and the 14px remove control’s flex auto-minimum still pushed dismissible classification chips past 22px.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Cap attribute value dropdown items at 320px with ellipsis truncation.\n\nLong hierarchical and Channel Info select option labels were stretching the popover; clamp the menu/paper and keep checkbox/chevron usable.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Fix stylelint property order and empty comment in attribute chip styles.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Revert non-English locale edits; keep clear-string removal in en.json only.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Remove orphan channel_attributes.info.clear keys from non-en locales.\n\ni18n CI rejects keys absent from en.json; the Clear control was removed so the English string is gone and translations of it must go too.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Point Learn More / help links at mattermost.com without www.\n\nwww.mattermost.com returns HTTP 401 to the external-links CI crawler; the apex host resolves normally and matches the pl/ permalink used elsewhere.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com>","tree":{"sha":"0a35b6fef961715f9e380f8d430635c2cd416470","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/trees/0a35b6fef961715f9e380f8d430635c2cd416470"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/commits/cb7a69a1b8b845c4e65f0736307d322252c4d3f5","verification":{"payload":"tree 0a35b6fef961715f9e380f8d430635c2cd416470\nparent 60328d1ed00f5d95cece4f476d3ca1b0e2966975\nauthor Asaad Mahmood <asaadmahmood@users.noreply.github.com> 1790946662 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790946662 +0500\n\nAlign channel attribute chips and fix header label flicker (#38841)\n\n* Align channel attribute chips and stop header label flicker.\n\nMake hierarchical and select/rank chips share AttributeChip chrome in channel info, and stabilize header overflow measurement so squeezed channel names do not re-expand chips.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Hide channel attribute chip dismiss until the value menu is open.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Collapse hidden chip dismiss so resting chips do not reserve trailing space.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Keep text attribute edit size aligned with the resting value.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Fix stylelint property order in channel attribute SCSS.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Cache chip widths before collapsing on zero available space.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Fix multiselect outside-click close and chip-remove keyboard activation.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Fix stylelint property order on AttributeChip remove control.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Fix graph picker disabled assertions and label activation.\n\nDiv Menu triggers use aria-disabled (jest-dom toBeDisabled only covers form controls), and label htmlFor cannot activate a non-labelable div, so forward the field-name click.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Align select attribute triggers with inline chips and clear via chip X.\n\nSelect/rank fields were still using the boxed input+chevron trigger and a Clear menu item, while Channel Info graph/multiselect chrome is borderless chips with in-chip remove.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Remove unused channel_attributes.info.clear i18n string.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Unify channel attribute chip size so classification matches other chips.\n\nChannel Info had been forcing AttributeChip to 24px with zero vertical padding (a leftover graph-picker metric), and medium chips still uppercased non-dismissible values — solid TOP SECRET / UNCLASSIFIED pills read taller than severity and multiselect chips sharing the same component.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Remove stale channel_attributes.info.clear keys from locale files.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Clamp channel attribute chips to 148px and lock medium height.\n\nLong multiselect values were overflowing Channel Info because medium chips only had max-width 100%, and the 14px remove control’s flex auto-minimum still pushed dismissible classification chips past 22px.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Cap attribute value dropdown items at 320px with ellipsis truncation.\n\nLong hierarchical and Channel Info select option labels were stretching the popover; clamp the menu/paper and keep checkbox/chevron usable.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Fix stylelint property order and empty comment in attribute chip styles.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Revert non-English locale edits; keep clear-string removal in en.json only.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Remove orphan channel_attributes.info.clear keys from non-en locales.\n\ni18n CI rejects keys absent from en.json; the Clear control was removed so the English string is gone and translations of it must go too.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Point Learn More / help links at mattermost.com without www.\n\nwww.mattermost.com returns HTTP 401 to the external-links CI crawler; the apex host resolves normally and matches the pl/ permalink used elsewhere.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv61mCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAST8QAI55SUpdqjS+LJ++zmYxsJkF\nWQoFuxaAGX9ViMiCEH/IuxEWYSzqJz5chlXSgdZQEUjUQNGdpjqbNmjJavZ0jC0o\njbS+p3s1BgAn2sjSkO8Bqs+jZdCjT6U8cLlalXI5pk8/utLOPPJEpkBuDnHGchjz\nozJW/QWWm5siHYh/siFCxA8ZWrAwRUBPS3yako+GiHwX4lpKW+dXzcYCO/d5IxcV\nOEfw6gQ5grvS74s+GTzePnrqRd0R8umngKcWrZ/JY/np7RJcVwlcy0FwbBkGxFKF\nRnnepjtH4OqJHN+qKQS2EBxHq100qikQ1TFy6UmbHpKZOhFZt6/1M3AYMYtP4uM/\nijNedxPqvN14eTC2D++o/lbSa5AUerOoylNsMO0PgUAzJ+xGJ20zfvPegcOt0GwB\nUALB3ZPgZAbYvIZ324f0DCrSGyQMZb5Cj+XQq9PGEZpe3R8Vex8DE/OuC6nP887O\n6qcRQxQXzGaz+TgrEcdkcAbim6wL880ITOOC9lknjLy5ZoI8yQYePe/56wdsuyEG\nK0rztjeiYAhfKCH/e1AB2GOPGJKi5vOuDZkKJmIVUoP0uY2hv9J/4VKaZanP5P04\nRGH2tgdDrgOKrUqCjxGMGz6Tlk7HUfjX+3kO/B8OZVbXb/gPaeWDncOkJckKciij\nkLPxMqjizZxf3WnrNLyy\n=kEx+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T13:11:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/u