:"ede699c3c6596c5bc6fc8d2d20b97a49ee7e4405","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/ede699c3c6596c5bc6fc8d2d20b97a49ee7e4405"}],"sha":"1638ff81b52bc950db5f96a664866ec9b6f37d32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/1638ff81b52bc950db5f96a664866ec9b6f37d32"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16541325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hanzei","id":16541325,"login":"hanzei","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTQxMzI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/ede699c3c6596c5bc6fc8d2d20b97a49ee7e4405/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T07:26:41Z","email":"ben.schumacher@mattermost.com","name":"Ben Schumacher"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T07:26:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[MM-70909] Health Dashboard PR13: MVP config rules (push notifications + SiteURL) (#38769)\n\n* [MM-70909] Rename health rule Summary to Title\n\nRuleText.SummaryID becomes TitleID (json \"title_id\") and\nHealthFinding.Summary becomes Title (json \"title\"); the registry now\nrequires health.rule.<code>.title. Nothing stores rendered prose, so\nno migration is needed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* [MM-70909] Add healthcheck.TranslationId\n\nA no-op marker so the i18n extractor can find the rule catalog''s\ntranslation ids without the healthcheck package importing\npublic/shared/i18n.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* [MM-70909] Add English strings for health rules and reasons\n\nWraps the health reason ids in TranslationId so the extractor sees\nthem, adds health.reason.config_unavailable for rules that cannot read\ntheir config, and adds en.json text for the push notification and\nSiteURL rules.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* [MM-70909] Add push notification and SiteURL health rules\n\nPUSH_EMPTY_URL, PUSH_BAD_SCHEME and PUSH_TEST_PROXY share the\nPushNotificationServer subject and differ by code so each condition\ncan be muted on its own. SITE_URL_EMPTY and SITE_URL_HTTP cover\nServiceSettings.SiteURL. Every code emits a result each cycle.\n\nThe rules package aggregates the catalog and is imported by the health\ncheck service so Builtin() is populated in production.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* [MM-70909] Align renamed RuleText field in Render test\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* fix: match the push test proxy by parsed hostname\n\nA substring check fired on URLs that only mention the test proxy in a\nquery string or a lookalike domain.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [MM-70909] Add translator descriptions for health rule strings\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"e63126e23ca891750af381ffb745a03b699c5922","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/trees/e63126e23ca891750af381ffb745a03b699c5922"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/commits/ede699c3c6596c5bc6fc8d2d20b97a49ee7e4405","verification":{"payload":"tree e63126e23ca891750af381ffb745a03b699c5922\nparent 964b09b8b925e9f1398c0481ccb6b60b444538f9\nauthor Ben Schumacher <ben.schumacher@mattermost.com> 1790926001 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790926001 +0200\n\n[MM-70909] Health Dashboard PR13: MVP config rules (push notifications + SiteURL) (#38769)\n\n* [MM-70909] Rename health rule Summary to Title\n\nRuleText.SummaryID becomes TitleID (json \"title_id\") and\nHealthFinding.Summary becomes Title (json \"title\"); the registry now\nrequires health.rule.<code>.title. Nothing stores rendered prose, so\nno migration is needed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* [MM-70909] Add healthcheck.TranslationId\n\nA no-op marker so the i18n extractor can find the rule catalog''s\ntranslation ids without the healthcheck package importing\npublic/shared/i18n.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* [MM-70909] Add English strings for health rules and reasons\n\nWraps the health reason ids in TranslationId so the extractor sees\nthem, adds health.reason.config_unavailable for rules that cannot read\ntheir config, and adds en.json text for the push notification and\nSiteURL rules.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* [MM-70909] Add push notification and SiteURL health rules\n\nPUSH_EMPTY_URL, PUSH_BAD_SCHEME and PUSH_TEST_PROXY share the\nPushNotificationServer subject and differ by code so each condition\ncan be muted on its own. SITE_URL_EMPTY and SITE_URL_HTTP cover\nServiceSettings.SiteURL. Every code emits a result each cycle.\n\nThe rules package aggregates the catalog and is imported by the health\ncheck service so Builtin() is populated in production.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* [MM-70909] Align renamed RuleText field in Render test\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* fix: match the push test proxy by parsed hostname\n\nA substring check fired on URLs that only mention the test proxy in a\nquery string or a lookalike domain.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [MM-70909] Add translator descriptions for health rule strings\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv1yxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvusQAKGo6/JiHu9zj+ikvxxcchf0\nMYvOPAUpRTMisk20/+2CZ96sGkNcaY9nT8K+mc+C6wtvYGwlTBftaa11vaFy90lP\niTbMZUfHyOrENW+tHIwb/sMLbp3vJPHbbjdop2MhtQYHyObwM2BwZnU1bDKIq4gb\nIKtJ5dz7+0noUifPriK5bFNZtch5A8fVnjmoYQUNiP8m4FFVMpsu8BOH40g5pno1\nviIEd1/vedni0f0/ByMRkIPn83alZtE2McZrbbfAXKvKGoDL9dVuZeb78P6/MU8u\ndKu8uBNC8S/ZAa3b7AEwdHUdLnQCswPhq52xKFfiD1TqpZA8eU7T9Q8H4Su3JQDw\nDQUa82HzxxKH12KjQ1V/NEdZtKGfF4yegdVWjwblhQeMPrQED924Cl3uKelAGuHS\nfELiOhhQjF7FgOAdfQmodpxPXDMEq1aCYZGnYYwzsfDyaTEHjEm01+JfeUmCjA52\n3DYBC4d6MPcmuBu70NHdABdApjCXiVkgJ9xsbNW+DOnfoAqvFlx/m4NSOkSBAtA1\nBqctzF7PgaGBc1kG4sed8WeKuYfczAySgxxgeLOtyMuFZjCOp0y00gAyjkRWy6/X\nYDexGw1jhJMMOb4HfBWcySlIzZEsW1WPrcgtBzlF15072PNemmjKyU9u2rZpRfRx\n/lrTxvR0skeCKFR3VAwf\n=iNWQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T07:26