:"hanzei","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTQxMzI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/964b09b8b925e9f1398c0481ccb6b60b444538f9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T07:26:41Z","email":"ben.schumacher@mattermost.com","name":"Ben Schumacher"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T07:26:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[MM-70903] Health Dashboard PR12: leader-only hourly health check task (#38761)\n\n* [MM-70903] Run the health check hourly on the cluster leader\n\nAdd the HealthDashboard feature flag (off by default) and a leader-only\nrecurring task that builds a health snapshot, evaluates it, reconciles\nfindings and garbage-collects expired ones. The cycle is a no-op unless\nthe flag is on and the license is at least Enterprise.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Build the health check service on first use\n\nNewChannels also runs over mock stores that do not stub HealthFinding(), which\npanicked every server started from them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Trim HealthDashboard feature flag comment\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add HealthDashboard to the sanitized config golden\n\nThe new feature flag is part of every support packet''s sanitized config.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Let a health check panic crash the server like other tasks\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Drop the concurrent health check test\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Drop the health check Stop test\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Cover the health check task with the leader task tests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"9cf444bf2d25ab2addc51db21603f13d0383b656","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/trees/9cf444bf2d25ab2addc51db21603f13d0383b656"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/commits/964b09b8b925e9f1398c0481ccb6b60b444538f9","verification":{"payload":"tree 9cf444bf2d25ab2addc51db21603f13d0383b656\nparent 2e6262768eccdb47be1ca2caaef00e61826d5f1c\nauthor Ben Schumacher <ben.schumacher@mattermost.com> 1790926001 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790926001 +0200\n\n[MM-70903] Health Dashboard PR12: leader-only hourly health check task (#38761)\n\n* [MM-70903] Run the health check hourly on the cluster leader\n\nAdd the HealthDashboard feature flag (off by default) and a leader-only\nrecurring task that builds a health snapshot, evaluates it, reconciles\nfindings and garbage-collects expired ones. The cycle is a no-op unless\nthe flag is on and the license is at least Enterprise.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Build the health check service on first use\n\nNewChannels also runs over mock stores that do not stub HealthFinding(), which\npanicked every server started from them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Trim HealthDashboard feature flag comment\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add HealthDashboard to the sanitized config golden\n\nThe new feature flag is part of every support packet''s sanitized config.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Let a health check panic crash the server like other tasks\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Drop the concurrent health check test\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Drop the health check Stop test\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Cover the health check task with the leader task tests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv1yxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPowQAFILspEqcfoEXWVKIBGTG/0j\npX4viqKBb/qbdp3rLIusbyvrBDxHya7ODKkW95dY/VormwoOS1eCc4Va88jhnAGB\nywH9CqvlW0TeOhuoc5OytZDQblWFT/U3cwFXZPnj9CVEJKWie+kMwi1pZdUoJals\nOhzTEvHjhfEq/Tz6vfhuEMhWrDL8Ws7a+pK8LQIten3Mr0FUq8VGIMCL/0UCkWGI\n3S7Ep+/WEYiyZQaCHGULHtl/XDUKUBIBCZcUNEUaD5d7OIMfU3WFa/F0ss7sS3bW\nU1UafmuAVWRcq0sC4zeXD/kjJl8FDYro7y7NJXoNFUS/taREoOlgzruOn1b2dkzX\nK6Ehn1uUOB0zQesRYNKv3RNgW1KggV6xzIlwu6ZhfF+6yjGpHvXgbFZDgZtrpr9W\nVWsbGpUjeJ3C7/dopIHYq2Jy2AY0tPznioUCyzzbOPDfhpkSMjxuXFO5c4Lz6vKj\nqMV8jx2/Q5SNmCWqoCEGdp1AMZsugVIIDXKVGCXNXa/skzJde0Y2klvUkWRqs2Dc\nSFaXEGNySJ+doalSJqtHOSmqvLgJAN5zopi0n9SWzumgrEOA48IkIr7X8jufa5dV\nSXgZsnCxRq6ItuVEag0i01O5eAbeOVFUO3qL9m5+CAdryWbNMVRQWBGN3KUKA8Xt\nV5Fqp4ZYhPb8pSa3V2p/\n=mNYg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T07:26:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/964b09b8b925e9f1398c0481ccb6b60b444538f9","node_id":"C_kwDOAjtrA9oAKDk2NGIwOWI4YjkyNWU5ZjEzOThjMDQ4MWNjYjZiNjBiNDQ0NTM4Zjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/2e6262768eccdb47be1ca2caaef00e61826d5f1c","sha":"2e6262768eccdb47be1ca2caaef00e61826d5f1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/2e6262768eccdb47be1ca2caaef00e61826d5f1c"}],"sha":"964b09b8b925e9f1398c0481ccb6b60b444538f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/964b09b8b925e9f1398c0481ccb6b60b444538f9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/812088?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fmartingr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fmartingr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fmartingr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fmartingr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fmartingr","id":812088,"login":"fmartingr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMjA4OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fmartingr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fmartingr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fmartingr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fmartingr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fmartingr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fmartingr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/2e6262768eccdb47be1ca2caaef00e61826d5f1c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T16:08:19Z","email":"812088+fmartingr@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Felipe Martin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T16:08:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Restructure Slack migration guide end to end (#37911)\n\n* MM-69567: Document what does and doesn''t migrate from Slack.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* MM-69567: Clarify Slack migration coverage from review feedback.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* MM-69562–MM-69570: Restructure Slack migration guide end to end.\n\nRewrite migrate-from-slack into a prepare → export → transform → import flow with coverage, Grid, emails, guests, and large-import guidance.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Fix mmctl channel-move link to use extensionless docs URL.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* MM-69562: Document org-wide DM handling in grid-transform.\n\nAdd a FAQ entry explaining that grid-transform has no special handling\nfor org-wide conversations: root-level dms.json and mpims.json entries\nare assigned to the workspace named on the first post carrying a team\nfield, so a cross-workspace DM lands in exactly one Mattermost team.\n\nCover the two practical consequences: participants from the other\nworkspace import as deactivated <USERID>@local placeholder accounts,\nand conversations that cannot be assigned are logged to\ngrid-transform-slack.log and dropped from every per-workspace zip.\n\nAlso replace the Enterprise Grid section''s pointer to the multi-party\nDM section, which never covered org-wide DMs, with a summary and a link\nto the new FAQ entry.\n\n* Address Slack migration documentation review feedback\n\n* Document mmetl dry-run validation for migrations\n\n* Simplify Slack migration overview\n\n* Group Slack export formats with export step\n\n* Put Slack migration feature mapping first\n\n* Number Slack migration action sections\n\n* Nest multiple Slack exports under transform\n\n* Add final Slack migration validation step\n\n* Clarify what migrates from Slack and move reference detail into appendices.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: Eric Sethna <14333569+esethna@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"65d87d2e8db1c6f8b0a48e2dbaf944edaa482d40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/trees/65d87d2e8db1c6f8b0a48e2dbaf944edaa482d40"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/commits/2e6262768eccdb47be1ca2caaef00e61826d5f1c","verification":{"payload":"tree 65d87d2e8db1c6f8b0a48e2dbaf944edaa482d40\nparent ac3b331878d44700bdb2feeed81d2c2709577ed4\nauthor Felipe Martin <812088+fmartingr@users.noreply.github.com> 1790870899 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790870899 -0700\n\nRestructure Slack migration guide end to end (#37911)\n\n* MM-69567: Document what does and doesn''t migrate from Slack.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* MM-69567: Clarify Slack migration coverage from review feedback.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* MM-69562–MM-69570: Restructure Slack migration guide end to end.\n\nRewrite migrate-from-slack into a prepare → export → transform → import flow with coverage, Grid, emails, guests, and large-import guidance.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Fix mmctl channel-move link to use extensionless docs URL.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* MM-69562: Document org-wide DM handling in grid-transform.\n\nAdd a FAQ entry explaining that grid-transform has no special handling\nfor org-wide conversations: root-level dms.json and mpims.json entries\nare assigned to the workspace named on the first post carrying a team\nfield, so a cross-workspace DM lands in exactly one Mattermost team.\n\nCover the two practical consequences: participants from the other\nworkspace import as deactivated <USERID>@local placeholder accounts,\nand conversations that cannot be assigned are logged to\ngrid-transform-slack.log and dropped from every per-workspace zip.\n\nAlso replace the Enterprise Grid section''s pointer to the multi-party\nDM section, which never covered org-wide DMs, with a summary and a link\nto the new FAQ entry.\n\n* Address Slack migration documentation review feedback\n\n* Document mmetl dry-run validation for migrations\n\n* Simplify Slack migration overview\n\n* Group Slack export formats with export step\n\n* Put Slack migration feature mapping first\n\n* Number Slack migration action sections\n\n* Nest multiple Slack exports under transform\n\n* Add final Slack migration validation step\n\n* Clarify what migrates from Slack and move reference detail into appendices.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: Eric Sethna <14333569+esethna@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvoVzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmD4QAG1mU10Z0dv+Nrx0mXz0Vyf/\n47a4YQ5S9XV1Ns3vXPHgAiT0FNOPz0pdTsZLshTxucXu3URu2qUr0Qh/z/afpbNq\nWEK1c7cc1tLTqkiiKDj13ePxfvyhry+ErhwWN8PS9o1igrCULIyfpR03Sr/sRhXV\nNNxuqgScuKl14GJ7f8tPYa8LNfOUet7qvx+oNI3NhTkFmQJvVtkD4WfGTgMtsDE8\nY5V2gZ9MgpgmQMnBi8zIQPdj8ttnTMQYuI2AzCk5Vryoebz7vuEDbmeC+BAN9wlX\nBCAGhmRHW1AtroQGowcFR5w2Ks5ce53YVWktNOG7Nene9jbp6KXGY2J52PV/zXzh\nweD/jCSMfsy3M4P1K/6eavgqHbWcE/T8ppXk1Ru+ASFoNl68+9+QYRpX8Bj2VPkb\njx1ebwYZ+J6NcKeQg2Wl37E4P4NG22rkvkKjWa3fBti/OwnA0+QQL