commits/751b8cb67b946baecb991b6ce5c04a5caecc39fe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/785518?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JulienTant","id":785518,"login":"JulienTant","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4NTUxOA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/1a6759a60f4826387f9250e031f558c9b39a6ede/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T03:43:49Z","email":"785518+JulienTant@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Julien Tant"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T03:43:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Make CPA create/patch/delete template-aware (#38834)\n\n* Make CPA create/patch/delete template-aware\n\ncreateCPAField now creates a template field (canonical schema) plus a\nlinked user field, returning the user field ID for backwards compat.\npatchCPAField routes schema attrs (options, ldap, saml) through the\ntemplate for linked fields; type changes unlink + delete the template\nfirst to work around the service-layer constraint that blocks template\ntype changes while dependents exist. deleteCPAField cleans up the\nlinked template after removing the user field.\n\nmmctl: remove the hardcoded TargetType:\"user\" from cpaFieldCreateCmdF\nnow that the server stamps both fields authoritatively.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add TestCPATemplateSystem to verify the two-field architecture\n\nSix integration subtests verify the internal template+linked-user-field\ninvariants introduced by the template-aware CPA handlers:\n\n- create builds a template field and a linked user field; the returned\n  ID is always the user field''s\n- list never exposes template fields (ObjectType=template)\n- schema attrs (options) are stored on the template, not the user field\n- display attrs (visibility, managed) stay on the user field and are\n  absent from the template\n- deleting a user field also soft-deletes its linked template\n- a type-change clears LinkedFieldID on the user field and soft-deletes\n  the orphaned template\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Address CodeRabbit review: logging and attr routing fixes\n\n- createCPAField: log rollback failure when template cleanup fails after\n  user-field creation error (previously silently discarded)\n- patchCPAField type-change path: log template deletion failure instead\n  of discarding it, so orphaned templates are visible in operator logs\n- patchCPAField non-type-change path: use splitCPAAttrs() for the\n  user-field patch instead of manual option-key deletion; this prevents\n  schema attrs (ldap, saml) from leaking onto the user field and ensures\n  only display attrs (visibility, managed, sort_order, display_name,\n  value_type) are applied there\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix TestCPATemplateSystem failures: stale-options guard and template visibility\n\nFix 1 (options test): after updating the template''s options, syncPropertyField-\nOptions propagates them to the user field''s option rows. Calling\nUpdatePropertyField on the user field immediately after triggered the\nlinked-field options-change guard because existingField still held the stale\npre-propagation snapshot. Now, when the attrs-only patch has nothing left to\napply to the user field (all attrs were schema-only, no name change), we skip\nUpdatePropertyField and re-fetch the field so hydratePropertyFieldOptions reads\nthe freshly-propagated option rows.\n\nFix 2 (display-attrs test): sanitizeAndValidateFieldAttrs sets a default\nvisibility=\"when_set\" on any field with an empty visibility. Template fields are\nschema-only definitions that must not carry display attrs; the guard now skips\nthe visibility default for ObjectType=template.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix mmctl TargetType and stale-options on mixed CPA patch\n\nmmctl: restore TargetType:\"user\" in cpaFieldCreateCmdF; commit 8cc7789213\nremoved it assuming the server stamps it, but the unit test mock still\nexpected it, causing a mock-argument mismatch failure.\n\napi4: after updating the CPA template field, always re-fetch existingField\nbefore applying the remaining user-field patch. The previous fix only\nskipped UpdatePropertyField when patch.Attrs==nil && patch.Name==nil, but\na mixed patch (schema attrs + display attrs or name) would still call\nUpdatePropertyField with the stale pre-propagation options snapshot,\ntriggering the linked-field options-change guard. Re-fetching immediately\nafter the template update covers all cases.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix owner-managed CPA field: propagate owners to user field in splitCPAAttrs\n\nTwo issues in TestOwnerManagedCPAFieldHumanValueWrites and\nTestSysadminManagesCPAFieldOwners:\n\n1. PermissionValues not pinned to sysadmin on owner-managed user fields:\n   enforceGroupPermissions checks HasPropertyFieldOwners on the field being\n   created/updated. Since owners are schema attrs (routed to the template by\n   splitCPAAttrs), the user field had no owners in its Attrs and the sysadmin\n   pin never fired. Fix: add explicit pin in createCPAField when the raw input\n   has owners, so the nil-fill is already at sysadmin before CreatePropertyField\n   runs.\n\n2. GetPropertyFieldOwners returned empty on the user field returned from\n   create/patch: callers read owners from the CPAField (backed by the user\n   field), but owners were only stored on the template. Fix: extend\n   splitCPAAttrs to also copy owners to the display map (like display_name and\n   value_type), so the user field stores them and all reads are consistent.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d3bbeb79c2a037c8a5e3ed962550af622b5c12b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/trees/d3bbeb79c2a037c8a5e3ed962550af622b5c12b2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/commits/1a6759a60f4826387f9250e031f558c9b39a6ede","verification":{"payload":"tree d3bbeb79c2a037c8a5e3ed962550af622b5c12b2\nparent 2ab94ccaabe9a7d9595cc31376e37c5f127a8956\nauthor Julien Tant <785518+JulienTant@users.noreply.github.com> 1790826229 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790826229 +0000\n\nMake CPA create/patch/delete template-aware (#38834)\n\n* Make CPA create/patch/delete template-aware\n\ncreateCPAField now creates a template field (canonical schema) plus a\nlinked user field, returning the user field ID for backwards compat.\npatchCPAField routes schema attrs (options, ldap, saml) through the\ntemplate for linked fields; type changes unlink + delete the template\nfirst to work around the service-layer constraint that blocks template\ntype changes while dependents exist. deleteCPAField cleans up the\nlinked template after removing the user field.\n\nmmctl: remove the hardcoded TargetType:\"user\" from cpaFieldCreateCmdF\nnow that the server stamps both fields authoritatively.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add TestCPATemplateSystem to verify the two-field architecture\n\nSix integration subtests verify the internal template+linked-user-field\ninvariants introduced by the template-aware CPA handlers:\n\n- create builds a template field and a linked user field; the returned\n  ID is always the user field''s\n- list never exposes template fields (ObjectType=template)\n- schema attrs (options) are stored on the template, not the user field\n- display attrs (visibility, managed) stay on the user field and are\n  absent from the template\n- deleting a user field also soft-deletes its linked template\n- a type-change clears LinkedFieldID on the user field and soft-deletes\n  the orphaned template\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Address CodeRabbit review: logging and attr routing fixes\n\n- createCPAField: log rollback failure when template cleanup fails after\n  user-field creation error (previously silently discarded)\n- patchCPAField type-change path: log template deletion failure instead\n  of discarding it, so orphaned templates are visible in operator logs\n- patchCPAField non-type-change path: use splitCPAAttrs() for the\n  user-field patch instead of manual option-key deletion; this prevents\n  schema attrs (ldap, saml) from leaking onto the user field and ensures\n  only display attrs (visibility, managed, sort_order, display_name,\n  value_type) are applied there\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix TestCPATemplateSystem failures: stale-options guard and template visibility\n\nFix 1 (options test): after updating the template''s options, syncPropertyField-\nOptions propagates them to the user field''s option rows. Calling\nUpdatePropertyField on the user field immediately after triggered the\nlinked-field options-change guard because existingField still held the stale\npre-propagation snapshot. Now, when the attrs-only patch has nothing left to\napply to the user field (all attrs were schema-only, no name change), we skip\nUpdatePropertyField and re-fetch the field so hydratePropertyFieldOptions reads\nthe freshly-propagated option rows.\n\nFix 2 (display-attrs test): sanitizeAndValidateFieldAttrs sets a default\nvisibility=\"when_set\" on any field with an empty visibility. Template fields are\nschema-only definitions that must not carry display attrs; the guard now skips\nthe visibility default for ObjectType=template.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix mmctl TargetType and stale-options on mixed CPA patch\n\nmmctl: restore TargetType:\"user\" in cpaFieldCreateCmdF; commit 8cc7789213\nremoved it assuming the server stamps it, but the unit test mock still\nexpected it, causing a mock-argument mismatch failure.\n\napi4: after updating the CPA template field, always re-fetch existingField\nbefore applying the remaining user-field patch. The previous fix only\nskipped UpdatePropertyField when patch.Attrs==nil && patch.Name==nil, but\na mixed patch (schema attrs + display attrs or name) would still call\nUpdatePropertyField with the stale pre-propagation options snapshot,\ntriggering the linked-field options-change guard. Re-fetching immediately\nafter the template update covers all cases.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix owner-managed CPA field: propagate owners to user field in splitCPAAttrs\n\nTwo issues in TestOwnerManagedCPAFieldHumanValueWrites and\nTestSysadminManagesCPAFieldOwners:\n\n1. PermissionValues not pinned to sysadmin on owner-managed user fields:\n   enforceGroupPermissions checks HasPropertyFieldOwners on the field being\n   created/updated. Since owners are schema attrs (routed to the template by\n   splitCPAAttrs), the user field had no owners in its Attrs and the sysadmin\n   pin never fired. Fix: add explicit pin in createCPAField when the raw input\n   has owners, so the nil-fill is already at sysadmin before CreatePropertyField\n   runs.\n\n2. GetPropertyFieldOwners returned empty on the user field returned from\n   create/patch: callers read owners from the CPAField (backed by the user\n   field), but owners were only stored on the template. Fix: extend\n   splitCPAAttrs to also copy owners to the display map (like display_name and\n   value_type), so the user field stores them and all reads are consistent.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvdb1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXjwQABriS4DbSc3iswoZb8uQKLfX\n1jVIawHBcovYOcZkQsC/3QbmJJ0pcgLBzj/+PMuefoAayXI2LmzsxjzH0F5en6wS\nhLjJv5+5ie8TtFUPvnADtQ626GSa1a1c2ih5K0NI/fLZ/9bIKs6xwYe2Nze1wABj\ng8HZAZxRgx/UlZGftMatyGcOTOZoxdyPGmXcmBaGW5wZts1nC6HJzQC6CKDrysTS\njHFubGSiZuY0gySXU08MpiqvaokswVHZerievHCF4ab2Ei4vPW5LlZZUATkvu44D\nLDARj7LFQqIlmt9RGd6W4GTeZ4Qbq8BgT81XnZ9+ttAXWdUy5JhF2usjPFCMYPLq\nIQGAQyRpMR3Rm4Wg39EnkijAwb0gdqnP3BzdeDB3VYB3mQ8dRNcpJUPIwVyInIeA\nmYJIS8TkaWdvyWhGLQAMoau5HwqmEg7/l+N7opDfxIt/mTQpw2MytbIs51DZzlWq\n8a5/19+qjX5NzCam17NmfsoTlXSpOws9K/cVcCXQf80MHCjJd7CCQHyzvi6HBaI8\nNcWaQrfYPb/2/F26I50QadSNhAwnxFzaCIx/8SpLNRGuzgl0y6YVy6UH0AzrJUPf\nm4zX0fCJjqaO9mCDu1Jyx1iYxI1pOUWkhrc/uKonb+eFBaLFwaPZNE6IkiZgoU9V\n8IlgG4DBoAk6Qiw/ci35\n=Hg4D\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T03:43:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.