thub.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/91b4450e49cd6e6b427fac629a71705aed793a75","node_id":"C_kwDOAjtrA9oAKDkxYjQ0NTBlNDljZDZlNmI0MjdmYWM2MjlhNzE3MDVhZWQ3OTNhNzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/24ef18fda7ca58b8ef59c8dd880fd17bccabe12b","sha":"24ef18fda7ca58b8ef59c8dd880fd17bccabe12b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/24ef18fda7ca58b8ef59c8dd880fd17bccabe12b"}],"sha":"91b4450e49cd6e6b427fac629a71705aed793a75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/91b4450e49cd6e6b427fac629a71705aed793a75"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1210556?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/cursor","id":206951365,"login":"cursor[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODFXTxQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/24ef18fda7ca58b8ef59c8dd880fd17bccabe12b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T19:29:44Z","email":"206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"cursor[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T19:29:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"MM-70812: Lock integration-managed channel attribute values in the channel RHS (#38802)\n\n* MM-70812: Lock plugin-managed channel attribute values in the channel RHS\n\nThe Channel Attributes panel in Channel Info decided a row was editable from\npermission_values alone. The server refuses every session write to a field\nwhose values an integration owns -- attrs.protected with a source_plugin_id,\nor a non-empty attrs.owners list -- before permission_values is consulted, so\na channel admin was offered a dropdown that could only end in \"Couldn''t save\".\n\nMirror that gate client-side and show the row''s padlock, so the attribute\nreads as deliberately read-only rather than broken.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Tidy comments and typing in the source-managed attribute lock\n\nName the gate source-managed rather than plugin-managed, since it also\ncovers ldap/saml sync, drop a comment that repeated the hook''s own doc,\nannotate the ownership table instead of asserting its type, and wrap the\nnew spec''s objective to match the ones beside it.\n\n* Format the new channel attribute spec to prettier''s liking\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Add the MM-70812 walkthrough artifacts and ticket link\n\nThe PR description could not be amended after it was opened, so the\nbefore/after evidence and the ticket link live here instead.\n\nTicket: https://mattermost.atlassian.net/browse/MM-70812\n\nReproduced on a real server against a protected channel attribute created\nby a purpose-built plugin (the only caller the server lets set\nattrs.protected), holding the value NOFORN on Town Square. Before, the\nvalue opened an option menu and the save came back 403\napp.property.access_denied.app_request. After, it is a read-only chip\nbehind a padlock.\n\nSide-by-side crop:\nhttps://cursor-plugin-pr-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/cursor/cursor/jira-bug-fix-agent-workflow-5926/before-after-comparison.png\n\nBefore, save failed:\nhttps://cursor-plugin-pr-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/cursor/cursor/jira-bug-fix-agent-workflow-5926/before-save-failed.webp\nBefore, full walkthrough:\nhttps://cursor-plugin-pr-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/cursor/cursor/jira-bug-fix-agent-workflow-5926/before-protected-attr-editable.mp4\n\nAfter, locked read-only chip:\nhttps://cursor-plugin-pr-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/cursor/cursor/jira-bug-fix-agent-workflow-5926/after-readonly-chip.webp\nAfter, full walkthrough:\nhttps://cursor-plugin-pr-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/cursor/cursor/jira-bug-fix-agent-workflow-5926/after-protected-attr-readonly.mp4\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* e2e: set MM-T622 override flags via config patch\n\nThe admin-console Save control stays disabled when the radios already\nmatch leftover Integration Management config. Patch the two override\nflags and store a stable hook-level icon instead.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* e2e: align Session Attributes type labels with String/Boolean/Enum\n\nThe listing Type column is getDisplayType (String | Boolean | Enum).\nIP/Version labels were removed from the product.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* e2e: stage dirty-nav via Enable instead of the TTL submenu\n\nThe nested Time-to-live submenu is racy under MUI. Staging Enable is\nenough to dirty the page, and enable() now waits for the menu to close.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Address PR feedback: 0 answered, 2 resolved, 0 declined\n\nRevert unrelated e2e test changes flagged by reviewer:\n- disallow_username_profile_override_spec.js (incoming webhook icon setup)\n- session_attributes.spec.ts + session_attributes.ts helper (dirty-check tweak)\n\nThese were unrelated to the channel-attributes locking fix (MM-70812) and\nare restored to their master state.\n\n* Add the translator description for the large-emoji processing error\n\nEnterprise i18n extract writes a description for every en.json entry. The new emoji processing error was missing one, so the check failed.\n\nCo-authored-by: maria.nunez <maria.nunez@mattermost.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\nCo-authored-by: Maria A Nunez <maria.nunez@mattermost.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com>","tree":{"sha":"92aac31fec26b31f1c3caeb32f15b4f147a585a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/trees/92aac31fec26b31f1c3caeb32f15b4f147a585a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/commits/24ef18fda7ca58b8ef59c8dd880fd17bccabe12b","verification":{"payload":"tree 92aac31fec26b31f1c3caeb32f15b4f147a585a3\nparent f747d6242a6d32eb9ac406f0b992384bf2f7857d\nauthor cursor[bot] <206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1790796584 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790796584 +0000\n\nMM-70812: Lock integration-managed channel attribute values in the channel RHS (#38802)\n\n* MM-70812: Lock plugin-managed channel attribute values in the channel RHS\n\nThe Channel Attributes panel in Channel Info decided a row was editable from\npermission_values alone. The server refuses every session write to a field\nwhose values an integration owns -- attrs.protected with a source_plugin_id,\nor a non-empty attrs.owners list -- before permission_values is consulted, so\na channel admin was offered a dropdown that could only end in \"Couldn''t save\".\n\nMirror that gate client-side and show the row''s padlock, so the attribute\nreads as deliberately read-only rather than broken.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Tidy comments and typing in the source-managed attribute lock\n\nName the gate source-managed rather than plugin-managed, since it also\ncovers ldap/saml sync, drop a comment that repeated the hook''s own doc,\nannotate the ownership table instead of asserting its type, and wrap the\nnew spec''s objective to match the ones beside it.\n\n* Format the new channel attribute spec to prettier''s liking\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Add the MM-70812 walkthrough artifacts and ticket link\n\nThe PR description could not be amended after it was opened, so the\nbefore/after evidence and the ticket link live here instead.\n\nTicket: https://mattermost.atlassian.net/browse/MM-70812\n\nReproduced on a real server against a protected channel attribute created\nby a purpose-built plugin (the only caller the server lets set\nattrs.protected), holding the value NOFORN on Town Square. Before, the\nvalue opened an option menu and the save came back 403\napp.property.access_denied.app_request. After, it is a read-only chip\nbehind a padlock.\n\nSide-by-side crop:\nhttps://cursor-plugin-pr-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/cursor/cursor/jira-bug-fix-agent-workflow-5926/before-after-comparison.png\n\nBefore, save failed:\nhttps://cursor-plugin-pr-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/cursor/cursor/jira-bug-fix-agent-workflow-5926/before-save-failed.webp\nBefore, full walkthrough:\nhttps://cursor-plugin-pr-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/cursor/cursor/jira-bug-fix-agent-workflow-5926/before-protected-attr-editable.mp4\n\nAfter, locked read-only chip:\nhttps://cursor-plugin-pr-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/cursor/cursor/jira-bug-fix-agent-workflow-5926/after-readonly-chip.webp\nAfter, full walkthrough:\nhttps://cursor-plugin-pr-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/cursor/cursor/jira-bug-fix-agent-workflow-5926/after-protected-attr-readonly.mp4\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* e2e: set MM-T622 override flags via config patch\n\nThe admin-console Save control stays disabled when the radios already\nmatch leftover Integration Management config. Patch the two override\nflags and store a stable hook-level icon instead.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* e2e: align Session Attributes type labels with String/Boolean/Enum\n\nThe listing Type column is getDisplayType (String | Boolean | Enum).\nIP/Version labels were removed from the product.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* e2e: stage dirty-nav via Enable instead of the TTL submenu\n\nThe nested Time-to-live submenu is racy under MUI. Staging Enable is\nenough to dirty the page, and enable() now waits for the menu to close.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Address PR feedback: 0 answered, 2 resolved, 0 declined\n\nRevert unrelated e2e test changes flagged by reviewer:\n- disallow_username_profile_override_spec.js (incoming webhook icon setup)\n- session_attributes.spec.ts + session_attributes.ts helper (dirty-check tweak)\n\nThese were unrelated to the channel-attributes locking fix (MM-70812) and\nare restored to their master state.\n\n* Add the translator description for the large-emoji processing error\n\nEnterprise i18n extract writes a description for every en.json entry. The new emoji processing error was missing one, so the check failed.\n\nCo-authored-by: maria.nunez <maria.nunez@mattermost.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\nCo-authored-by: Maria A Nunez <maria.nunez@mattermost.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvWMoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAW2AQAJ/iNsLO+FN7yp4CqIfqIqai\n+UidcBw0Ny/jc60MfANWrWYcomg5avnTP0QWwHAocE9Upnrufq6C4HBsO3z8126F\n+CUckqkbVJPgJZCqdB0FCDT1c0qQA1AXP1/c4dzgfMW/hpi8MOix4Z7nyPC2Rmkw\n1XicBwNeIwdQrG1wtqzgLLEsZX0E35Wl/K1Ojagg7WHGuY9qLfCGJdfTczl5Q6y0\nPGav51HdjtRjQqi0Z5mo2SpbZSw3hbTRlNHDajhcjvrQKdUENzhcdATSFg/yu6E5\nU870DwCu82Dpv