or":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1023171?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lieut-data","id":1023171,"login":"lieut-data","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjMxNzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/4aa82f6f13868bc328761cc4ba1cefc251a4186e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:05:50Z","email":"jesse.hallam@gmail.com","name":"Jesse Hallam"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:05:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Don''t ship empty strings as valid translations (#38412)\n\n* Format the admin console exact-time tooltip as one message\n\nThe tooltip spliced a translated \"at\" into a moment format string, so a locale\nthat needs no connecting word had no way to say so: \"\" falls back to the\nEnglish, and zh-CN had settled on \" \". It is now a single message formatting the\ndate and time for the reader''s locale, and translators can reorder or drop the\nconnecting word.\n\nEach existing translation of \"at\" is carried into the new message as it\nrendered before; ja''s was untranslated English and is left to fall back.\n\n* Remove the whitespace-only server translations\n\n438 entries across es, fr, it and ja held \" \" in place of a full English\nsentence, mostly error messages. go-i18n renders that as-is, so the user saw a\nblank message where a missing id would at least have fallen back to English.\nRemoved with `mmgotool i18n clean-empty`.\n\n* Report a blank translation the way a missing one is reported\n\nBoth runtimes treat an empty translation as missing: react-intl falls back to\nthe English, and go-i18n returns the id. A whitespace-only one is worse: it\nrenders, and the user sees nothing. Both checkers now report either as a missing\nkey, under the same --warn-missing-keys / --warn-missing-ids flags, and\n`mmgotool i18n clean-empty` removes both.\n\nclean-empty also now writes the two-space indent the catalogs use.\n\n* Correct the connecting word in six exact-time translations\n\nThe carried-over \"at\" was wrong in ko, pl, ru, nl, tr and zh-TW: Korean\nattaches 에 to the date, Polish, Russian and Dutch take o, в and om before a\nclock time, and Turkish \"zaman\" and the spaced zh-TW 於 read as noise, so both\ndrop the word as zh-CN already does.","tree":{"sha":"9f9e7967736c840d9e8118b7a5473ee3fa0132dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/trees/9f9e7967736c840d9e8118b7a5473ee3fa0132dd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/commits/4aa82f6f13868bc328761cc4ba1cefc251a4186e","verification":{"payload":"tree 9f9e7967736c840d9e8118b7a5473ee3fa0132dd\nparent 7206a38470ee4091dc594859b1a4055a60e56362\nauthor Jesse Hallam <jesse.hallam@gmail.com> 1790773550 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790773550 -0300\n\nDon''t ship empty strings as valid translations (#38412)\n\n* Format the admin console exact-time tooltip as one message\n\nThe tooltip spliced a translated \"at\" into a moment format string, so a locale\nthat needs no connecting word had no way to say so: \"\" falls back to the\nEnglish, and zh-CN had settled on \" \". It is now a single message formatting the\ndate and time for the reader''s locale, and translators can reorder or drop the\nconnecting word.\n\nEach existing translation of \"at\" is carried into the new message as it\nrendered before; ja''s was untranslated English and is left to fall back.\n\n* Remove the whitespace-only server translations\n\n438 entries across es, fr, it and ja held \" \" in place of a full English\nsentence, mostly error messages. go-i18n renders that as-is, so the user saw a\nblank message where a missing id would at least have fallen back to English.\nRemoved with `mmgotool i18n clean-empty`.\n\n* Report a blank translation the way a missing one is reported\n\nBoth runtimes treat an empty translation as missing: react-intl falls back to\nthe English, and go-i18n returns the id. A whitespace-only one is worse: it\nrenders, and the user sees nothing. Both checkers now report either as a missing\nkey, under the same --warn-missing-keys / --warn-missing-ids flags, and\n`mmgotool i18n clean-empty` removes both.\n\nclean-empty also now writes the two-space indent the catalogs use.\n\n* Correct the connecting word in six exact-time translations\n\nThe carried-over \"at\" was wrong in ko, pl, ru, nl, tr and zh-TW: Korean\nattaches 에 to the date, Polish, Russian and Dutch take o, в and om before a\nclock time, and Turkish \"zaman\" and the spaced zh-TW 於 read as noise, so both\ndrop the word as zh-CN already does.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvQkuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgJwQAJgjfywsE6R7CY+5YBJo/Aj3\nZBDvCF9/Bq7FejQ61jN+rjaEJBuZ94c2Bb525UoAi+1SeZvKJMmEIpl2iotDgxUx\n4bDjZ4stgIfnIOLS+lzItWmaUOLxgPgUYJlubkPYux/7JTNH+ceGXCLqNLtMfLku\nUmWEE2NGHLKfJMG5GHMB7yp6eNFaNs2EP2284YZzN+wvAXcMrjJ1rS56CKnd9SAx\n6UeaL/+ov1eBb0ZAOF13++sd88evb5wqPKlBvLsNGVdTAlJ3ZhKlXWrh4YpNMkcf\nvnS/qPe6gl1LmTXmUuqajWZQJ49guq5tTkoobllLOi7xxhJfjtjOewmoFzrY6dZg\n+M8wYlzLeTtu3UD1X6Ff+pqqJ5BduIME9MhDxptuOagSVC4Wr3W9p2a1G9d/0+NU\n/YWeV4C8CfAAQLuXnAUfqFhe313BarST4dRK23NRuvEt1dfEBWxdf4jLcD9C0sXR\n4ZbhhVJpF28qzKaxc4rn5VVoJFJunG8araOEn2d3NqOn7ppzrsy7UKfFERENWhdV\nJkCsUr+1JI4TwvGmp/XLExIg4Cgur9jdAYPwxB1Ae8AfvDwCbjAAChHzDRvvG1aL\n+P014M+0Vp1dfscCFg5Vo9eMRQEKrZF71jnW+iMOcfOpDRv43Lh1LDnaFOx4wjSV\ntd60JeJmUIBXAJYFvTWW\n=wQjT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:05:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/4aa82f6f13868bc328761cc4ba1cefc251a4186e","node_id":"C_kwDOAjtrA9oAKDRhYTgyZjZmMTM4NjhiYzMyODc2MWNjNGJhMWNlZmMyNTFhNDE4NmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/7206a38470ee4091dc594859b1a4055a60e56362","sha":"7206a38470ee4091dc594859b1a4055a60e56362","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/7206a38470ee4091dc594859b1a4055a60e56362"}],"sha":"4aa82f6f13868bc328761cc4ba1cefc251a4186e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/4aa82f6f13868bc328761cc4ba1cefc251a4186e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10082627?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pvev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pvev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pvev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pvev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pvev","id":10082627,"login":"pvev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDgyNjI3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pvev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pvev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pvev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pvev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pvev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pvev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/7206a38470ee4091dc594859b1a4055a60e56362/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:39:38Z","email":"pablovv2012@gmail.com","name":"Pablo Vélez"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:39:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Mm 70889 channel attributes fix (#38747)\n\n* Polish channel attributes admin and channel settings UX.\n\nHide Channel Info display as UI-only, add attributes to the Info tab, and improve empty banner preview messaging.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Edit channel attributes from channel settings and allow emptying the banner\n\n* Fix multiselect display to render individual chips for each value\n\n* Fix alignment of elements in attribute details and classification attribute styles\n\n* Fix channel attribute banner settings and rendering\n\nPersist banner opt-outs, validate required text, preserve template punctuation, avoid double rendering, and prevent duplicate chip removal. Update regression tests and E2E selectors.\n\n* Enhance banner token controls with unset value indicators\n\n* Refactor channel attributes and banner handling\n\n* Preserve authored classification banners when legacy banner info reports disabled\n\n* Refactor tests for channel attributes and banner handling\n\n* Fix styling and scrolling behavior in channel attributes and settings modal\n\n* Fix banner fallback behavior for empty authored text in channel classification\n\n* fix unit test\n\n* update snapshot, adjust text margin and show error message correctly for clasification\n\n* adjust snapshots\n\n* Revert \"adjust snapshots\"\n\nThis reverts commit 77bd1df4cabb5173895a7a8e51bbae9d0467a25d.\n\n* fix error message marging\n\n* adjust snapshot\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Asaad Mahmood <asaadmahmood@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: coderabbitai[bot] <136622811+coderabbitai[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com>","tree":{"sha":"d1db1b85abb46f46b6dd47ec96e1bbe4b04bf298","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/trees/d1db1b85abb46f46b6dd47ec96e1bbe4b04bf298"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/commits/7206a38470ee4091dc594859b1a4055a60e56362","verification":{"payload":"tree d1db1b85abb46f46b6dd47ec96e1bbe4b04bf298\nparent 3ba2add35efe861a7b4c07dd8dc3202a1f3e4c67\nauthor Pablo Vélez <pablovv2012@gmail.com> 1790768378 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790768378 +0200\n\nMm 70889 channel attributes fix (#38747)\n\n* Polish channel attributes admin and channel settings UX.\n\nHide Channel Info display as UI-only, add attributes to the Info tab, and improve empty banner preview messaging.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Edit channel attributes from channel settings and allow emptying the banner\n\n* Fix multiselect display to render individual chips for each value\n\n* Fix alignment of elements in attribute details and classification attribute styles\n\n* Fix channel attribute banner settings and rendering\n\nPersist banner opt-outs, validate required text, preserve template punctuation, avoid double rendering, and prevent duplicate chip removal. Update regression tests and E2E selectors.\n\n* Enhance banner token controls with unset value indicators\n\n* Refactor channel attributes and banner handling\n\n* Preserve authored classification banners when legacy banner info reports disabled\n\n* Refactor tests for channel attributes and banner handling\n\n* Fix styling and scrolling behavior in channel attributes and settings modal\n\n* Fix banner fallback behavior for empty authored text in channel classification\n\n* fix unit test\n\n* update snapshot, adjust text margin and show error message correctly for clasification\n\n* adjust snapshots\n\n* Revert \"adjust snapshots\"\n\nThis reverts commit 77bd1df4cabb5173895a7a8e51bbae9d0467a25d.\n\n* fix error message marging\n\n* adjust snapshot\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Asaad Mahmood <asaadmahmood@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: coderabbitai[bot] <136622811+coderabbitai[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvPT6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiH4QAF6lYPpLeJ2ZHjxZJJ/id98w\nHTSWZhmkQTCFsBJVPx3vXfpq9hKEZ/LaRqzisifIp8r1Fx1wy0x9i8IThnxcoouR\nXjdI7KlA1AoYpmg4FU50x7silYp9NEI6U8gwNVz1OovuogXzyQxIokVUl48eF64e\nyUuwJwhoigRWP++TC/yeCmoZ8RJQdh0FDzlbX9yUO4liKEMG8isIdKnlhkZ1Y1iL\nGI0kBGbeiQIjcpnSxUxIUuocKb8zLPtdn3SbrTycRKU5cxut33tOCVCU4WnevlYj\ngW1S9/AKjApJ098T5ZKD+V9ebRrNk01ffAIq1kVUFWkvkGJsUBi9/F59UqnYV5dB\naXk+oseVVhlesFZPgOlM+tVOCqjkWaZTEUXbWHftNcrypyTZ2MAkGEGpntPcvdWW\nUYxl0gXUA/HmvtPUN9TmfQxXRltU4/uw/Khw2jimOGduXhHwmiuIpk1suttE7IWX\n6J8bPL8GPVMlJ7tJjQfDd8wK+U3XsK9cVl4lQqMuXtv4j9ISq4InlIGGQengnm0Z\nwRSDsOx8RAXqDzZqjHsfhkUAibu5nmGPSejFISz4broguwUF4ZvON1q41uGJTQUI\nAD1q2XHacycDsnSg8eTmUlxkS6IJxPthmIGBW1nBGNTQ+BSVyWkXro2Ps+0iuBsE\nDImBLxWL7VSNENWahKrc\n=iTdB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T11:39:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/7206a38470ee4091dc594859b1a4055a60e56362","node_id":"C_kwDOAjtrA9oAKDcyMDZhMzg0NzBlZTQwOTFkYzU5NDg1OWIxYTQwNTVhNjBlNTYzNjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/3ba2add35efe861a7b4c07dd8dc3202a1f3e4c67","sha":"3ba2add35efe861a7b4c07dd8dc3202a1f3e4c67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/3ba2add35efe861a7b4c07dd8dc3202a1f3e4c67"}],"sha":"7206a38470ee4091dc594859b1a4055a60e56362","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/7206a38470ee4091dc594859b1a4055a60e56362"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16541325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hanzei","id":16541325,"login":"hanzei","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTQxMzI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/3ba2add35efe861a7b4c07dd8dc3202a1f3e4c67/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:04:28Z","email":"ben.schumacher@mattermost.com","name":"Ben Schumacher"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:04:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[MM-70902] Health Dashboard PR11b: leader diagnostics with per-section errors (#38758)\n\n* [MM-70902] Attach leader diagnostics with per-section errors to health snapshot\n\nGetSupportPacketDiagnostics now returns a NodeDiagnostics envelope whose\nErrors map records every node section, with each collection failure also\nset on its section. The support packet still marshals only the\ndiagnostics, so diagnostics.yaml and warning.txt are unchanged.\nBuildHealthSnapshot attaches the envelope to the leader node only.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Drop unreachable nil check on the diagnostics envelope\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Allow background cluster publishes in the leader-diagnostics test\n\nSetup''s config-change publishes can reach the strict cluster mock and panic\nthe test binary intermittently.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Install the three-node cluster at setup instead of swapping it\n\nSetCluster on a running server races with background config publishes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Allow background cluster publishes in the section-errors cluster subtest\n\nThe strict cluster mock rejected Setup''s config-change publish from a\nPlatformService.Go goroutine, which exited without decrementing the\ngoroutine count and hung Shutdown until the package timed out.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"309dbc9e0ba711b1b59c24458a9e720158f2e730","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/trees/309dbc9e0ba711b1b59c24458a9e720158f2e730"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/commits/3ba2add35efe861a7b4c07dd8dc3202a1f3e4c67","verification":{"payload":"tree 309dbc9e0ba711b1b59c24458a9e720158f2e730\nparent d2914954e068b23012853a3ce16073408f27d653\nauthor Ben Schumacher <ben.schumacher@mattermost.com> 1790766268 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790766268 +0200\n\n[MM-70902] Health Dashboard PR11b: leader diagnostics with per-section errors (#38758)\n\n* [MM-70902] Attach leader diagnostics with per-section errors to health snapshot\n\nGetSupportPacketDiagnostics now returns a NodeDiagnostics envelope whose\nErrors map records every node section, with each collection failure also\nset on its section. The support packet still marshals only the\ndiagnostics, so diagnostics.yaml and warning.txt are unchanged.\nBuildHealthSnapshot attaches the envelope to the leader node only.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Drop unreachable nil check on the diagnostics envelope\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Allow background cluster publishes in the leader-diagnostics test\n\nSetup''s config-change publishes can reach the strict cluster mock and panic\nthe test binary intermittently.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Install the three-node cluster at setup instead of swapping it\n\nSetCluster on a running server races with background config publishes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Allow background cluster publishes in the section-errors cluster subtest\n\nThe strict cluster mock rejected Setup''s config-change publish from a\nPlatformService.Go goroutine, which exited without decrementing the\ngoroutine count and hung Shutdown until the package timed out.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvOy8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAP1UQAIaBTz6e8w0ghHReflw1zS5b\nkVDOGSSLYQnLbZEk9swFSw26MUJLi5D/6ILbE4JM8G+e9z4Wr3QTkamu1G/nxlns\nK+7HksChUz8FtGy0dixDqMMtEhMAbegRrXnhRixR4Y1phtCxXWK+etnp1EcKPlW9\nT9IHzSO6WsyxNTPTTNThHwmbWz/dW9r85p+F59Xa4g4UJQxf2qhOx3KCHOClSij7\n80/+XN9KF2nYgD/7ncmHs5JgtJf5zaSQzY3yRFBpz15HOXCFdT6d/fdG5X/JU0+9\ntfy460Sfd5J6Y5f9yAuATgUy+NPGivwzZwrjtjgycYdk9SQt1vAcg33uMg+fykHK\nWHNyZ/XvJnB6xgEG5OHjy9V1oRBwT0xMOKSKHYxl+by1Pnns3Q7mUNVIbu6Kl+Fc\nwmqbeJVpwo17zEp2Ob+Z8bCq2xB9Wv1nVj9HERGF1IbAvM6XT9FyFH+KpwANKGw7\nlaOiODD9KIkDqpYOGXLu0iFnTFCCPRLpFjbNxbNI1o54QjXUJfWfZWwFWgQNY0r6\neZF225ufuOz/n3uadzAaAkqSms0L3t2do5jfDf1T8PSj3ZTlTy1yhyAeB2OLKw4F\nlOb21BgPUIBSviOHJPCV7BNMXswiLVU2vneZHjrkDLkVmp1wQmptP8m/RyOcH6A/\ndz7i3P+EYi+lycxm5mmI\n=DBm9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T11:04:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_ur