name shadowed test helper in stats subtests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvOy7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaJ4QADUOCvNE7HMrQ2Bl1pnPuhut\nBWappZ0xHqrjbq58ErD9/HKR6BrWk2DfOYrsd1HXM0dofGVyWfqYmx67RHkY2YQb\ncHCrcco9clobANKZnWyQIetZe+1spw3WzrWJqCDasrxwvrLccvfuA7dOlyzR27Bq\nmNs+uwyG/TmsojUMxcXMXQFZ+G7R5XbONUwRrgLpHtQfIyZb4mzTDNad1epbdE9q\n4R1m2GJbDg3lLsZXHUZn7QEapcamscK9nhJpaJiGwqFO2qVoY3uydSBz11SUIwpP\nBgMPNojW5bHLdgCXOzg+3WznXBY1eFuSG6Zx/UyPF2Jhdf0U/DLv/t20l4ZWMXBF\noKhf9OQ3E7H+OXfVbgKNtEwa5UIAEgHKwonb4VBHbpc3mL4hNPPL94irlQSUyIXJ\n8pQe1T6jgLo4nQ6IDuwMBnE9vFpcG0ZCSpmHG5FX01NbhFN0nmlibNruv00dSK+z\nZ6xuNNAbbVauhh3BdD8ze7OhzuO23P1mqBDQE+Me3pLGlfkkiAggmxZKxV81rphT\nuPsEeYcsMQ47UHZZfDd55lSN1aMukWoho/QzGfKm6z7RkJqDM/HIwQktMFrUfOPO\n2exuZgRNDP3t3o32PX3Y+5ik2NBmMv4TazRCX7z1MbFe9WfPbERhiTgCqNhuux1E\nN6ontYiS4XEWPHdSG3wF\n=yeEm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T11:04:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/1bd281bfbace2000dbd102e17fdb1f2b205720b6","node_id":"C_kwDOAjtrA9oAKDFiZDI4MWJmYmFjZTIwMDBkYmQxMDJlMTdmZGIxZjJiMjA1NzIwYjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/73562bd08c7428bf8a7caab5424e24565a20bd0c","sha":"73562bd08c7428bf8a7caab5424e24565a20bd0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/73562bd08c7428bf8a7caab5424e24565a20bd0c"}],"sha":"1bd281bfbace2000dbd102e17fdb1f2b205720b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/1bd281bfbace2000dbd102e17fdb1f2b205720b6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14200393?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bgardner8008/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bgardner8008/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bgardner8008/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bgardner8008/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bgardner8008","id":14200393,"login":"bgardner8008","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MjAwMzkz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bgardner8008/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bgardner8008/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bgardner8008/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bgardner8008/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bgardner8008/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bgardner8008","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/73562bd08c7428bf8a7caab5424e24565a20bd0c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T09:16:57Z","email":"billg@wavearts.com","name":"Bill Gardner"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T09:16:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"MM-70272: Add aggregate size and depth limits to archive and Slack import extraction (#38009)\n\n* Add aggregate size and depth limits to archive and Slack import extraction\n\n- Add ExtractionBudget to docextractor interface; thread shared byte budget\n  and max depth through all extractors so nested archives share one pool\n- Cap archive walk at 1000 entries per level and maxArchiveDepth levels\n- Cap Slack import at 500MB total decompressed across all ZIP entries\n\n* Add depth-limit and aggregate-size tests\n\nAdd TestArchiveExtractorDepthLimit to verify that nested archive\nextraction stops at maxDepth levels. Add TestSlackImportTotalSizeLimit\nto verify that the aggregate byte cap halts Slack import entry\nprocessing once the limit is reached.\n\nConvert slackImportMaxTotalSize from const to var so tests can lower\nthe threshold without creating multi-hundred-megabyte fixtures.\n\n* Cap subtext to remaining budget before appending\n\n* Restore Ctx field in ExtractSettings for API compatibility\n\n* Honor caller context cancellation in extractWithTimeout\n\nExtractSettings.Ctx was restored for API compatibility but was never\nobserved by extractWithTimeout. A cancelled request context could wait\nfor the full extraction timeout (or forever when Timeout <= 0).\n\nNow, when Ctx is set, extractWithTimeout runs on a goroutine and selects\non resultCh, timer.C (if Timeout > 0), and ctx.Done() — returning a\ncancellation error as soon as the caller context is cancelled. A nil\nchannel for timer.C means the timeout case simply never fires when\nTimeout <= 0. The fast synchronous path is retained for the common case\nwhere neither Ctx nor Timeout is set.\n\nAdds TestExtractContextCancellation covering: already-cancelled context,\nmid-extraction cancellation, and ctx vs timeout race (ctx wins first).\n\n* Update pdf.go to use github.com/mattermost/pdf fork\n\nThe go.mod was updated upstream to replace github.com/ledongthuc/pdf\nwith the Mattermost fork github.com/mattermost/pdf. The pdf.go import\nwas not updated during the rebase because git kept our version of the\nfile. Also pass context.Background() to GetPlainText, which the fork\nextended to take a context.Context.\n\n* Don''t log archive entry path in extraction error\n\nEntry paths from user-uploaded archives should not appear in\nerror messages, per the pattern established in #37987.\n\n* Restore ctx to Extractor interface alongside budget\n\nAdds context.Context back as the first parameter to Extractor.Extract,\nalongside the existing ExtractionBudget parameter. This restores\nAlejandro''s MM-69725 fix: pdfExtractor passes the context down to\nGetPlainText(ctx), so when extractWithTimeout returns (timeout or parent\ncancellation), the derived context is cancelled and the PDF goroutine\nstops at the next page rather than running to completion.\n\nmmPreviewExtractor also gains context propagation via\nhttp.NewRequestWithContext so its outbound HTTP call can be cancelled.\nContext-unaware extractors (document, plain) accept and ignore it.\n\n* Fix test extractors to implement updated Extractor interface\n\n* Fix remaining test extractors to implement updated Extractor interface\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Edgar <edgar.bellotmico@mattermost.com>","tree":{"sha":"9a210f95dfdd18b2ae2974e69adad74f94747721","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/trees/9a210f95dfdd18b2ae2974e69adad74f94747721"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/commits/73562bd08c7428bf8a7caab5424e24565a20bd0c","verification":{"payload":"tree 9a210f95dfdd18b2ae2974e69adad74f94747721\nparent 9176425f82c265e2fceef0e5010a8bc1e0a94264\nauthor Bill Gardner <billg@wavearts.com> 1790759817 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790759817 +0000\n\nMM-70272: Add aggregate size and depth limits to archive and Slack import extraction (#38009)\n\n* Add aggregate size and depth limits to archive and Slack import extraction\n\n- Add ExtractionBudget to docextractor interface; thread shared byte budget\n  and max depth through all extractors so nested archives share one pool\n- Cap archive walk at 1000 entries per level and maxArchiveDepth levels\n- Cap Slack import at 500MB total decompressed across all ZIP entries\n\n* Add depth-limit and aggregate-size tests\n\nAdd TestArchiveExtractorDepthLimit to verify that nested archive\nextraction stops at maxDepth levels. Add TestSlackImportTotalSizeLimit\nto verify that the aggregate byte cap halts Slack import entry\nprocessing once the limit is reached.\n\nConvert slackImportMaxTotalSize from const to var so tests can lower\nthe threshold without creating multi-hundred-megabyte fixtures.\n\n* Cap subtext to remaining budget before appending\n\n* Restore Ctx field in ExtractSettings for API compatibility\n\n* Honor caller context cancellation in extractWithTimeout\n\nExtractSettings.Ctx was restored for API compatibility but was never\nobserved by extractWithTimeout. A cancelled request context could wait\nfor the full extraction timeout (or forever when Timeout <= 0).\n\nNow, when Ctx is set, extractWithTimeout runs on a goroutine and selects\non resultCh, timer.C (if Timeout > 0), and ctx.Done() — returning a\ncancellation error as soon as the caller context is cancelled. A nil\nchannel for timer.C means the timeout case simply never fires when\nTimeout <= 0. The fast synchronous path is retained for the common case\nwhere neither Ctx nor Timeout is set.\n\nAdds TestExtractContextCancellation covering: already-cancelled context,\nmid-extraction cancellation, and ctx vs timeout race (ctx wins first).\n\n* Update pdf.go to use github.com/mattermost/pdf fork\n\nThe go.mod was updated upstream to replace github.com/ledongthuc/pdf\nwith the Mattermost fork github.com/mattermost/pdf. The pdf.go import\nwas not updated during the rebase because git kept our version of the\nfile. Also pass context.Background() to GetPlainText, which the fork\nextended to take a context.Context.\n\n* Don''t log archive entry path in extraction error\n\nEntry paths from user-uploaded archives should not appear in\nerror messages, per the pattern established in #37987.\n\n* Restore ctx to Extractor interface alongside budget\n\nAdds context.Context back as the first parameter to Extractor.Extract,\nalongside the existing ExtractionBudget parameter. This restores\nAlejandro''s MM-69725 fix: pdfExtractor passes the context down to\nGetPlainText(ctx), so when extractWithTimeout returns (timeout or parent\ncancellation), the derived context is cancelled and the PDF goroutine\nstops at the next page rather than running to completion.\n\nmmPreviewExtractor also gains context propagation via\nhttp.NewRequestWithContext so its outbound HTTP call can be cancelled.\nContext-unaware extractors (document, plain) accept and ignore it.\n\n* Fix test extractors to implement updated Extractor interface\n\n* Fix remaining test extractors to implement updated Extractor interface\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Edgar <edgar.bellotmico@mattermost.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvNOJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAulsQAK5nIc4II3oFbKy3ES5pPFSE\nVzmnwoKwhSX4SUvUZqo9CiZ9ETFZPhp32mcqY0EQG112BwQPZDJ9flnANXdo+zYO\n//yo2Gf7CUHsXvLSIQwQSyHkyviwyNf7siqUh28KtNEZj/MGxnr1htAdNbBTMruV\nhAE+IiuQoi5MpaGtQda0YfQRJEAV0q9wMz8d5pyi9rzShcHCPZEsxv1Idoz/ZcP8\nutB/O9vggESn9F4zr02QAOmyKeonDP4tHbv1WKyBYfV7IYVW31JwPaIsNuOV5UMY\nvLgHab3UogMrLSu/vgRupHtc0O7Dlwhuu+Av+gDw5BpE0CUPpfyUVpZOy2tNu4hv\nYRFZMNeS1cyHYTIl/DG+BeKpF0rQ6biDjq9NEZavwMD7QSGGbRur0xUIcTQqCWs5\nWhS+ecNbEkHqSt6E6ZtGrm21PszNzsKbA95kzKJg1vHfEPe0+/6/7AlHRxVemKdp\nEahTHkmEMic1x0DUlLezFmXVl6sd2WtePgqi3a+ThW6GzDM1eS14F5OL1cAPeVe4\nOxVhbqF8GdEqFcGpSQc27nKG1tODWUcFNo3cj7xFP5w9p/jAha/cbQt+Srg9RZZO\nxNxQuD16lAtN2dJVRtRrolZSe852LZNRG9KROkMPLz9G0SQd8ogMpSoRNRf6VOn4\nO6HWKLc+pT72ibGYGn4z\n=EgiO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T09:16:58Z"}