ml_url":"https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/0d48bb838aaa25e451968e3de7d4532b477f2456","node_id":"C_kwDOAjtrA9oAKDBkNDhiYjgzOGFhYTI1ZTQ1MTk2OGUzZGU3ZDQ1MzJiNDc3ZjI0NTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/c7ae0e632138639da734be3ac480e087f314bd18","sha":"c7ae0e632138639da734be3ac480e087f314bd18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/c7ae0e632138639da734be3ac480e087f314bd18"}],"sha":"0d48bb838aaa25e451968e3de7d4532b477f2456","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/0d48bb838aaa25e451968e3de7d4532b477f2456"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1210556?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/cursor","id":206951365,"login":"cursor[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODFXTxQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/c7ae0e632138639da734be3ac480e087f314bd18/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T19:37:09Z","email":"206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"cursor[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T19:37:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[MM-60727] Update relative date separators when the local day changes (#38832)\n\n* [MM-60727] Refresh relative timestamps when the local day changes\n\nTimestamp only scheduled a re-render when the matched range carried an\nexplicit refresh interval, which the Today/Yesterday ranges do not. A\nchannel left open across local midnight therefore kept rendering a stale\n\"Today\" date separator, and posting afterwards produced a second \"Today\"\nseparator instead of relabelling the older one as \"Yesterday\".\n\nSchedule a re-render at the next local day boundary whenever the rendered\noutput was derived from a calendar-day comparison with the current time.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Refresh week, month, quarter and year ranges at the day boundary too\n\nThose ranges are compared as whole calendar periods and carry no refresh\ninterval either, so a \"last week\" label left on screen went stale in the\nsame way \"Today\" did. Threads, post previews and pending join requests\nall render timestamps with those units.\n\nAlso harden the test suite following review: probe a timezone whose\nmidnight never happens, sweep the day-boundary arithmetic across every\ntimezone, assert the pending refresh is released on unmount, and drive\nthe date separator through a non-UTC user timezone.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Add a Playwright spec for the date separator day rollover\n\nDrives a real channel across local midnight with page.clock, which is\nthe only part jsdom cannot vouch for: that the refresh timer survives\ninside the virtualized post list with a real server and a real Intl.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Keep the new-messages toast sentence in step with its own date label\n\nTimestamp now refreshes itself at the day boundary, but the toast\ncomputed the \"since\" connective in the parent, so at midnight the\nsentence became \"15 new messages yesterday\" with the connective missing.\nBuild the sentence inside Timestamp''s render prop, which is re-invoked\non each refresh, so the label and the wording come from one pass.\n\nAlso cover the refresh-interval branch, the stale-now reset, and each\ncalendar unit in the rollover set, all of which survived mutation.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Tidy comments and drop a redundant Boolean cast\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Advance the schedule-message calendar when the target date is next month\n\nThe helper skipped \"next month\" whenever the same day-of-month was already\nvisible. Near month-end that day is the current month''s past (disabled) date,\nso selecting two days ahead clicked a disabled cell. Always advance when the\ntarget month differs.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Navigate the date picker until the visible month matches the target\n\nA single next-month click is not enough when the offset spans more than\none month, or when the calendar opens on a previously selected month.\nKeep stepping until the caption matches the target month and year.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>","tree":{"sha":"eb934bd0adb61a9c533721b1971a7dfeb23bdc34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/trees/eb934bd0adb61a9c533721b1971a7dfeb23bdc34"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/commits/c7ae0e632138639da734be3ac480e087f314bd18","verification":{"payload":"tree eb934bd0adb61a9c533721b1971a7dfeb23bdc34\nparent 2a6eba426feacbea5267a5af452f91affbe82e05\nauthor cursor[bot] <206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1790710629 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790710629 -0400\n\n[MM-60727] Update relative date separators when the local day changes (#38832)\n\n* [MM-60727] Refresh relative timestamps when the local day changes\n\nTimestamp only scheduled a re-render when the matched range carried an\nexplicit refresh interval, which the Today/Yesterday ranges do not. A\nchannel left open across local midnight therefore kept rendering a stale\n\"Today\" date separator, and posting afterwards produced a second \"Today\"\nseparator instead of relabelling the older one as \"Yesterday\".\n\nSchedule a re-render at the next local day boundary whenever the rendered\noutput was derived from a calendar-day comparison with the current time.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Refresh week, month, quarter and year ranges at the day boundary too\n\nThose ranges are compared as whole calendar periods and carry no refresh\ninterval either, so a \"last week\" label left on screen went stale in the\nsame way \"Today\" did. Threads, post previews and pending join requests\nall render timestamps with those units.\n\nAlso harden the test suite following review: probe a timezone whose\nmidnight never happens, sweep the day-boundary arithmetic across every\ntimezone, assert the pending refresh is released on unmount, and drive\nthe date separator through a non-UTC user timezone.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Add a Playwright spec for the date separator day rollover\n\nDrives a real channel across local midnight with page.clock, which is\nthe only part jsdom cannot vouch for: that the refresh timer survives\ninside the virtualized post list with a real server and a real Intl.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Keep the new-messages toast sentence in step with its own date label\n\nTimestamp now refreshes itself at the day boundary, but the toast\ncomputed the \"since\" connective in the parent, so at midnight the\nsentence became \"15 new messages yesterday\" with the connective missing.\nBuild the sentence inside Timestamp''s render prop, which is re-invoked\non each refresh, so the label and the wording come from one pass.\n\nAlso cover the refresh-interval branch, the stale-now reset, and each\ncalendar unit in the rollover set, all of which survived mutation.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Tidy comments and drop a redundant Boolean cast\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Advance the schedule-message calendar when the target date is next month\n\nThe helper skipped \"next month\" whenever the same day-of-month was already\nvisible. Near month-end that day is the current month''s past (disabled) date,\nso selecting two days ahead clicked a disabled cell. Always advance when the\ntarget month differs.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Navigate the date picker until the visible month matches the target\n\nA single next-month click is not enough when the offset spans more than\none month, or when the calendar opens on a previously selected month.\nKeep stepping until the caption matches the target month and year.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvBNlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWBIQAGD9kLadG3FhoMEf/G4kh2RH\n0nPqrYNvRNYaRa2IMb3VK3qNqCmYXKvx1olDwFhvdPLK7V5DqTdP2vNwP5a7MzQc\njxr/R61Rq/x1JhtUV6T9jsjLS7u5vX/7Wy1DDfsS0/ubI6+xjT4eWTBMdt6G6nf+\n8FjCHMiwMn+R7mi4L7bYckDa27xpftyR06aUaqPcRTN8oCRnA8Uc1nBSnzqZ5Zgh\nli+wYG/HQxb4A0pJ/tIRQWyGNnSP2PVtxXhnPG8vtAs3fD2FIFbVPTMkFrj3ffL1\n5TSqbn1rCsDhdcJv8gCVqTraVQiLIErE94T+KWBDye6cpUyB1nnvTvsMteM3Siq6\n+W1C/oXHcatwK/quH0ciVhc4BZBOtEY+StFRABf/geiPm8WU535wQPD0IOj7WuM2\nvsy7qkQyyItTJShhpEbsYlutQNDzKI/k5kvJdsFB+Ich37IkdKctaj9RnDklFm6G\nX8/OPLVN3DVItzIzgFrW4OqnNsuZJlz44vh9lGWvP2QiMHRVi+RFQWhrsOuXTjjY\nkbnnOu+9Fl8Ag58yb4gqK3hSEsjg1LCWSVUcuaZ5erUcatuRYW3xSYa