rl":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/2a6eba426feacbea5267a5af452f91affbe82e05","node_id":"C_kwDOAjtrA9oAKDJhNmViYTQyNmZlYWNiZWE1MjY3YTVhZjQ1MmY5MWFmZmJlODJlMDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/47b00703d1cb4853bdb7492f78338b77df1bd0c4","sha":"47b00703d1cb4853bdb7492f78338b77df1bd0c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/47b00703d1cb4853bdb7492f78338b77df1bd0c4"}],"sha":"2a6eba426feacbea5267a5af452f91affbe82e05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/2a6eba426feacbea5267a5af452f91affbe82e05"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1023171?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lieut-data","id":1023171,"login":"lieut-data","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjMxNzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/47b00703d1cb4853bdb7492f78338b77df1bd0c4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T16:43:54Z","email":"jesse.hallam@gmail.com","name":"Jesse Hallam"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T16:43:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Give every en.json entry a translator-facing description (#38411)\n\n* Give every en.json entry a translator-facing description\n\nA translator handed `channel_header.directchannel.you` and the word \"you\" has no\nway to know whether that is a label, a suffix, or the second person pronoun.\nen.json carries the string and nothing else, and the context that would answer\nthe question lives only in the source.\n\nEach entry in en.json now carries a `description` of where the string appears\nand how it is used, on both surfaces:\n\n- server: `{\"id\", \"translation\", \"description\"}`. go-i18n reads only id and\n  translation, so the server ignores it.\n- webapp: `{\"defaultMessage\", \"description\"}` in place of the bare string.\n  Nothing in the bundle imports en.json any more -- English renders from each\n  call site''s defaultMessage -- so the descriptions never reach the client.\n\n`make i18n-extract` and `npm run i18n-extract` carry existing descriptions\nforward, so the only thing a person writes is the description. A new id arrives\nwith an empty one to fill in; a removed id is dropped. On the webapp a\n`description` written in source wins over the recorded one.\n\nThe webapp formatter now fails on a defaultMessage that is not a string literal:\nwith en.json no longer shipped there is no English to fall back to, and the id\nwould render as itself. That rejects the commercial support modal''s per-row\nlabel, which was never translatable under its single shared id, so it renders\nthe label directly.\n\ncheck_icu.mjs flattens the new source shape before comparing, so the locale\ncatalogs stay flat `key -> string`.\n\n* Describe the en.json entries added since the descriptions were written","tree":{"sha":"a716833cc5b25e491250993b5c7c39d8ad3ec356","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/trees/a716833cc5b25e491250993b5c7c39d8ad3ec356"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/commits/47b00703d1cb4853bdb7492f78338b77df1bd0c4","verification":{"payload":"tree a716833cc5b25e491250993b5c7c39d8ad3ec356\nparent d038ccd2aa7ba98c8ba73c96eefca6e831980319\nauthor Jesse Hallam <jesse.hallam@gmail.com> 1790700234 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790700234 -0300\n\nGive every en.json entry a translator-facing description (#38411)\n\n* Give every en.json entry a translator-facing description\n\nA translator handed `channel_header.directchannel.you` and the word \"you\" has no\nway to know whether that is a label, a suffix, or the second person pronoun.\nen.json carries the string and nothing else, and the context that would answer\nthe question lives only in the source.\n\nEach entry in en.json now carries a `description` of where the string appears\nand how it is used, on both surfaces:\n\n- server: `{\"id\", \"translation\", \"description\"}`. go-i18n reads only id and\n  translation, so the server ignores it.\n- webapp: `{\"defaultMessage\", \"description\"}` in place of the bare string.\n  Nothing in the bundle imports en.json any more -- English renders from each\n  call site''s defaultMessage -- so the descriptions never reach the client.\n\n`make i18n-extract` and `npm run i18n-extract` carry existing descriptions\nforward, so the only thing a person writes is the description. A new id arrives\nwith an empty one to fill in; a removed id is dropped. On the webapp a\n`description` written in source wins over the recorded one.\n\nThe webapp formatter now fails on a defaultMessage that is not a string literal:\nwith en.json no longer shipped there is no English to fall back to, and the id\nwould render as itself. That rejects the commercial support modal''s per-row\nlabel, which was never translatable under its single shared id, so it renders\nthe label directly.\n\ncheck_icu.mjs flattens the new source shape before comparing, so the locale\ncatalogs stay flat `key -> string`.\n\n* Describe the en.json entries added since the descriptions were written","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu+rKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJt8QAALwkMIRtT0U98d0rRT3Zkwc\n9z/Yxg0yJoYwmeB9XNLlxWhs2jd0Dxi/jRSyxugZ0HwZQw1L/xvsuYFmGLnJgFD5\nGpSu3fxatI/AZHQbyuLnvzswLzuV97XcooElV+bOYB3aJClgX9gwQ1A6DHK+7V2i\nXYaGnrh2xbhoqKURrZBBG7o18VBS/8hf7uBLW83GHR0iaD5JQih4nnf2fOrJnbeB\nPh85awJiaAf5fnYT/WUfAb3maaOJTHsyr5SFQYh1kstn1OTPhr7wRAPUkzvdDy+8\nRQDjjSABrL1RM8r2Bj0Q+w/4KQaec3p9oN6dw4UljNn8CnanHLdvnU6cLaZn6iAu\nP+NEiZLTSd1DZqMG9pCmn9C9xxmDm8KwlYfFZCjI1oFtEDvtpaUi9aS6vM0atqIq\nvH/JpZc0iOCYgqV4ISr49J3ibVFWqO/QSWLQ2Zk1l+PiXdZS/IkUQvMfCXFAhydT\noHVDs9Ibiezz0nQrDLjs9Oq9WTy/lqZMJTJLu2YhslmjerYN5k/qaZeJMng4ymkh\ng3Zyz7AhL6ftmmBNUwCioZPw+dCeRzJIz4hN+BAaH7OYwDTyD5Iq97LVdgUI578i\ntZAOjUnfqpDmyNZ8dJaPVyj500WhjGRb+xeCtNkH9hirmeoqW33BPoZiK+0Pm8KN\n8SBakJ6MhPDS51Aden10\n=B7e8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T16:43:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/47b00703d1cb4853bdb7492f78338b77df1bd0c4","node_id":"C_kwDOAjtrA9oAKDQ3YjAwNzAzZDFjYjQ4NTNiZGI3NDkyZjc4MzM4Yjc3ZGYxYmQwYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/d038ccd2aa7ba98c8ba73c96eefca6e831980319","sha":"d038ccd2aa7ba98c8ba73c96eefca6e831980319","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/d038ccd2aa7ba98c8ba73c96eefca6e831980319"}],"sha":"47b00703d1cb4853bdb7492f78338b77df1bd0c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/47b00703d1cb4853bdb7492f78338b77df1bd0c4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1023171?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lieut-data","id":1023171,"login":"lieut-data","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjMxNzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/d038ccd2aa7ba98c8ba73c96eefca6e831980319/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T14:32:24Z","email":"jesse.hallam@gmail.com","name":"Jesse Hallam"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T14:32:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Render English from each message''s defaultMessage, not en.json (#38494)\n\n* Render English from each message''s defaultMessage, not en.json\n\nThe webapp bundles i18n/en.json into the main chunk and merges it into every\nlocale''s message map, so each English string ships twice: once as the\ndefaultMessage compiled into its call site, and again as a catalog entry.\nDropping the import saves ~167KB gzipped and changes nothing on screen.\nreact-intl already falls back to the defaultMessage when a key is missing, and\nan id only reaches en.json because formatjs found a literal defaultMessage at\nits call site -- a literal nothing then strips from the bundle, since no babel\nconfig enables removeDefaultMessage.\n\nen.json was also merged into the non-English catalogs, which sit between 39%\nand 91% complete. Without it those keys resolve through the defaultMessage\ninstead, so react-intl reports a MissingTranslationError -- and it constructs\nthat error, stack trace and all, before any onError handler can filter it, at\nroughly 4.4us a call. Naming the current locale as defaultLocale skips the\nbranch outright and formats the fallback under the reader''s locale, which is\nwhat merging en.json used to do. A descriptor carrying no defaultMessage at\nall still reports, which is the case worth hearing about.\n\nThe six tests that handed en.json to createIntl now pass {} explicitly. They\nwere already getting {} at runtime -- jest maps every i18n catalog to an empty\nmock -- so the whole suite has been exercising this fallback all along. An\nESLint rule keeps the import from creeping back.\n\n* Index admin console messages from their raw text\n\nreact-intl returns a catalog string verbatim when no values are passed, but\nalways formats a defaultMessage. With en.json gone the search index hit the\nsecond path, and every message with a rich-text tag or placeholder failed to\nformat. Index the raw string, as it did before, and stop the test loading\nen.json through a path the jest catalog mock does not match.","tree":{"sha":"b11c4b89bebe55b159078ad6c453e2dff0159136","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/trees/b11c4b89bebe55b159078ad6c453e2dff0159136"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/commits/d038ccd2aa7ba98c8ba73c96eefca6e831980319","verification":{"payload":"tree b11c4b89bebe55b159078ad6c453e2dff0159136\nparent 258d6ce8c1e045c3a92b6aaa68ede818ff44dbc8\nauthor Jesse Hallam <jesse.hallam@gmail.com> 1790692344 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790692344 +0000\n\nRender English from each message''s defaultMessage, not en.json (#38494)\n\n* Render English from each message''s defaultMessage, not en.json\n\nThe webapp bundles i18n/en.json into the main chunk and merges it into every\nlocale''s message map, so each English string ships twice: once as the\ndefaultMessage compiled into its call site, and again as a catalog entry.\nDropping the import saves ~167KB gzipped and changes nothing on screen.\nreact-intl already falls back to the defaultMessage when a key is missing, and\nan id only reaches en.json because formatjs found a literal defaultMessage at\nits call site -- a literal nothing then strips from the bundle, since no babel\nconfig enables removeDefaultMessage.\n\nen.json was also merged into the non-English catalogs, which sit between 39%\nand 91% complete. Without it those keys resolve through the defaultMessage\ninstead, so react-intl reports a MissingTranslationError -- and it constructs\nthat error, stack trace and all, before any onError handler can filter it, at\nroughly 4.4us a call. Naming the current locale as defaultLocale skips the\nbranch outright and formats the fallback under the reader''s locale, which is\nwhat merging en.json used to do. A descriptor carrying no defaultMessage at\nall still reports, which is the case worth hearing about.\n\nThe six tests that handed en.json to createIntl now pass {} explicitly. They\nwere already getting {} at runtime -- jest maps every i18n catalog to an empty\nmock -- so the whole suite has been exercising this fallback all along. An\nESLint rule keeps the import from creeping back.\n\n* Index admin console messages from their raw text\n\nreact-intl returns a catalog string verbatim when no values are passed, but\nalways formats a defaultMessage. With en.json gone the search index hit the\nsecond path, and every message with a rich-text tag or placeholder failed to\nformat. Index the raw string, as it did before, and stop the test loading\nen.json through a path the jest catalog mock does not match.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu8v4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgfIQAGPz9aU1uP8v3Ii3G8WJCpMn\nksEpT3mhHskorHDS6LXhQmXj9xArTKx0/eTKFCwsTEAwbLCqs4wSOBx6AQrtGaiE\nfgSs/eKZR9vqsU0HPzu/I80/Wf7nnghvLQlogXYzEQlYDl5Ye6bufSGLERSME75w\njkV5yW30ZN7Ap3eMd/KCa3i3LWKGlg+e5LVdKBSmoVstQDRcdYdVUqZSFP72VVEk\nTTMEFiEY3T5SLw9OOVih3oHs/Jizwrkt8RIdrAI1fNpxqWvuSwE9afw41seFFCF6\n8Bj6ITgHWWxfWFSwe2nq5i84UlXEaFMgpYd6UppgIvGR6buu2nJXpG2TtDhUWWrl\nvwdLsSeyg/ptND/YdGAAUYnBpFusuJpmkc1mekczbrvYvW7Rz2OnzFO/en419D66\nOuJj4Xqcq2oFniMLGgyhNYpFtlm94lEFbKS3p5jhUKP5Oo8mYIQE7v5NiQZlOkWJ\n0YgG1BDtzVg+aH0t62ov1ahuZtBD5P2D5QIZXVZrfoy6Wu6cczMgZ10cHVBbyHVp\nwoTZH+683VKWMDwdQU756tytmtfUoDuc/mATfeKWGxRdPPAUOwfrE7RjBrxREThq\nec6HaLTKxq8J19YhYkS3ecWnNapj0Ev3B4JKCv8bOXv/NnXlO0zZmvtDI/O3Pm7g\ng6X9SgNyqwB9wpVyyV64\n=RLgc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T14:32:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/d038ccd2aa7ba98c8ba73c96eefca6e831980319","node_id":"C_kwDOAjtrA9oAKGQwMzhjY2QyYWE3YmE5OGM4YmE3M2M5NmVlZmNhNmU4MzE5ODAzMTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/258d6ce8c1e045c3a92b6aaa68ede818ff44dbc8","sha":"258d6ce8c1e045c3a92b6aaa68ede818ff44dbc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/258d6ce8c1e045c3a92b6aaa68ede818ff44dbc8"}],"sha":"d038ccd2aa7ba98c8ba73c96eefca6e831980319","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/d038ccd2aa7ba98c8ba73c96eefca6e831980319"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/239766337?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edgarbellot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edgarbellot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edgarbellot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edgarbellot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/edgarbellot","id":239766337,"login":"edgarbellot","node_id":"U_kgDODkqLQQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edgarbellot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edgarbellot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edgarbellot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edgarbellot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edgarbellot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/edgarbellot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/258d6ce8c1e045c3a92b6aaa68ede818ff44dbc8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T14:26:52Z","email":"edgar.bellotmico@mattermost.com","name":"Edgar Bellot Micó"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T14:26:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"MM-70676: Rework file metadata preparation for post retrieval, channel bookmarks, and notification delivery (#38444)\n\n* MM-70636: Rework file metadata preparation in bulk post retrieval\n\n* Avoid variable shadowing in getPostsByIds loop\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* MM-70636: Extend metadata preparation to channel bookmarks and notification events\n\n* Simplify slice lookup in bookmark broadcast test helper\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Skip redundant evaluation when no bookmark carries file info\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Tighten ABAC access-evaluation test mocks to match subject and resource\n\n* Assert ABAC access-evaluation mock is actually invoked in bulk post retrieval tests\n\n* Extend file metadata preparation to the remaining bookmark endpoints\n\nRoute the bookmark payloads returned by the create, update, sort-order and\ndelete handlers through the same shared preparation helper the listing\nendpoint already uses, so all five handlers share one code path instead of\nrepeating it. The helper also tolerates nil entries consistently.\n\nPrepare the persistent notification attachment hints per recipient, matching\nhow the rest of that event payload is already prepared, and reuse the\nexisting policy-state helper instead of keeping a second copy of it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"44b89ecbd66926a7fdbe4691244470c05d61fceb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/trees/44b89ecbd66926a7fdbe4691244470c05d61fceb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/commits/258d6ce8c1e045c3a92b6aaa68ede818ff44dbc8","verification":{"payload":"tree 44b89ecbd66926a7fdbe4691244470c05d61fceb\nparent 7dc8c5f72bc1e2e3a180ce23d72f0815dab6a189\nauthor Edgar Bellot Micó <edgar.bellotmico@mattermost.com> 1790692012 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790692012 +0200\n\nMM-70676: Rework file metadata preparation for post retrieval, channel bookmarks, and notification delivery (#38444)\n\n* MM-70636: Rework file metadata preparation in bulk post retrieval\n\n* Avoid variable shadowing in getPostsByIds loop\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* MM-70636: Extend metadata preparation to channel bookmarks and notification events\n\n* Simplify slice lookup in bookmark broadcast test helper\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Skip redundant evaluation when no bookmark carries file info\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Tighten ABAC access-evaluation test mocks to match subject and resource\n\n* Assert ABAC access-evaluation mock is actually invoked in bulk post retrieval tests\n\n* Extend file metadata preparation to the remaining bookmark endpoints\n\nRoute the bookmark payloads returned by the create, update, sort-order and\ndelete handlers through the same shared preparation helper the listing\nendpoint already uses, so all five handlers share one code path instead of\nrepeating it. The helper also tolerates nil entries consistently.\n\nPrepare the persistent notification attachment hints per recipient, matching\nhow the rest of that event payload is already prepared, and reuse the\nexisting policy-state helper instead of keeping a second copy of it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu8qsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYEYQAD9y+LvCxxi77yDFYKWGtG5x\nrGwODeVby3drdkTVeV6/fW3swLP5bwwINDFu5qjpgpNHIJVZWWiQL5jDG2Bcc2Er\nA2to+byfO3i8MqVBcxpw2Ql9SsBAIBCTU9wev83mstu6q9irTo/70GhWtaER/+V5\nxjCi60h6f3CNpWXWtkZhj+7xmdaQIi21BlF1JNSzXH/C2qRMJh2m5m03qjvEG+AU\ndu+S/w3kcvQc3r+3SC8BIX231aLUBUoXnpaDYhV+jz6JT48tQ9R3saO+hcqToxyY\nHIDVqFz5QADYeIsGPwezlaFia9cCV5M5YKmkMwK+RMgVvMUJh8EVzG9EnTZabPJV\n4O0+rXmrXAGtv77TP2MkhyXj4OaduHornXJaGfY6FepbR5PiLsOcBJ1wKtqu6HaD\nH1x/iW1BH3Km84aycOC5SQeYkqj0jUDBTFXkHamEigC5uFKB3oTqAZFRJYzRo7Ev\nV2gMoI469VllWFk9qgXKgbA4ZiTJCQ6DLKQ6yOvE8mhuOuvX2LepYeE2L5YPH2Rn\nPy9xftTso9XqGofTILtuFP7LeCcPXzfdA8CGOwbE+fCi5BtR6/UYvmtc5XHxSw22\njLkB0QKjCN0ZEyRf5nBKEDCctZkw3SvCECwEQavvCajZ+8mg73SIjkEUIfALZkyg\nwWVn/8p34BSX0cgzNRYg\n=x1WT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T14:26:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repo