t.com/u/785518?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JulienTant","id":785518,"login":"JulienTant","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4NTUxOA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/6e4c923eb2f1ceafcc9491c607396060d9ec405b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T21:34:55Z","email":"785518+JulienTant@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Julien Tant"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T21:34:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"MM-70890: Don''t copy ldap/saml sync attrs to non-user linked fields (#38774)\n\n* MM-70890: Don''t copy ldap/saml sync attrs to non-user linked fields\n\nSAML and LDAP sync services only ever write user-targeted property\nvalues. Copying attrs.ldap/attrs.saml onto channel, team, or post\nlinked fields causes checkSyncLock to block all writes to those fields\nwith 403, since no caller other than the sync service is allowed to\nwrite to a synced field — and the sync service never targets channels.\n\nFix CreatePropertyField to only propagate sync attrs when the linked\nfield''s ObjectType is ''user''. Add a migration to strip the incorrectly\ncopied attrs from existing non-user, non-template fields in production.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* MM-70890: Address CodeRabbit findings\n\n- Strip caller-supplied ldap/saml attrs from non-user linked fields (else\n  branch) so checkSyncLock cannot treat direct caller input as a sync lock\n- Bump UpdateAt in migration so since-based polling picks up corrected fields\n- Add type: ''text'' to E2E regression test template to pass field validation\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* MM-70890: Remove redundant loop variable copy (Go 1.22+)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix e2e override workflows: --slurp incompatible with --jq in gh CLI\n\nBoth e2e-tests-override-status.yml and e2e-tests-verified-label.yml used\n--paginate --slurp --jq together. Newer gh CLI versions reject that\ncombination; pipe through jq separately instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com>","tree":{"sha":"bf996d40d7284ce329abf7ea26023b89aca81792","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/trees/bf996d40d7284ce329abf7ea26023b89aca81792"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/commits/6e4c923eb2f1ceafcc9491c607396060d9ec405b","verification":{"payload":"tree bf996d40d7284ce329abf7ea26023b89aca81792\nparent 03e5d9083d2de65f5e0c43287f092fc04f8138a9\nauthor Julien Tant <785518+JulienTant@users.noreply.github.com> 1790631295 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790631295 +0000\n\nMM-70890: Don''t copy ldap/saml sync attrs to non-user linked fields (#38774)\n\n* MM-70890: Don''t copy ldap/saml sync attrs to non-user linked fields\n\nSAML and LDAP sync services only ever write user-targeted property\nvalues. Copying attrs.ldap/attrs.saml onto channel, team, or post\nlinked fields causes checkSyncLock to block all writes to those fields\nwith 403, since no caller other than the sync service is allowed to\nwrite to a synced field — and the sync service never targets channels.\n\nFix CreatePropertyField to only propagate sync attrs when the linked\nfield''s ObjectType is ''user''. Add a migration to strip the incorrectly\ncopied attrs from existing non-user, non-template fields in production.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* MM-70890: Address CodeRabbit findings\n\n- Strip caller-supplied ldap/saml attrs from non-user linked fields (else\n  branch) so checkSyncLock cannot treat direct caller input as a sync lock\n- Bump UpdateAt in migration so since-based polling picks up corrected fields\n- Add type: ''text'' to E2E regression test template to pass field validation\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* MM-70890: Remove redundant loop variable copy (Go 1.22+)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix e2e override workflows: --slurp incompatible with --jq in gh CLI\n\nBoth e2e-tests-override-status.yml and e2e-tests-verified-label.yml used\n--paginate --slurp --jq together. Newer gh CLI versions reject that\ncombination; pipe through jq separately instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqut1/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQIIQAA6Og90xex5EYY/obg06Xd/C\nOuA72eH4jgI7rl2EYjOpgs9MXy2Yc7x7NVktsELQMuPK7txN9qWGZfQQ5jsvnQX+\nTm8500FnkCu7biJlNMqOR9iRm9M6VRrRer6agA1A5wvdZthw5gBFQMEC3I+lGYCB\nmVp8tUupWig2ywC3AjwaWQF1EgtOVu1ERVAcRtAIZZefomFmtjszTx3szEtpolfa\n9n/IvZWmNpuixM9HGgyw+hPqTQqVEYHMG0Y+PXwJhSAAVGtIzgow2ZZ+7UsTqerN\nX0vIalduNeKi/8A92YJjaxFA1q7Fma6kgWm7llN8BF5G4PuddnqhummfDBn8V1YP\n6J3wE2dzMaY3I0Ai/b6XgmbTy5dq/fhHQPWWgUq2utfU58Oq8+JcCvYJ6LP5NdvP\nLZ0pkoOEOYRpQnmv7JgIsxTDJqqpmDPXXRe8qt7gKGl0jwio/9+Vg4v763053wsn\n9bE6pCbK7wU0IJdQRIwRjzZa