u/17114347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/esarafianou","id":17114347,"login":"esarafianou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MTE0MzQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/27c501d217266608a917c163690505d14d75df66/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T09:49:16Z","email":"eva.sarafianou@gmail.com","name":"Eva Sarafianou"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T09:49:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Replace docs impact review with self-clearing gap detection (#38177)\n\n* Replace docs impact review with self-clearing gap detection\n\nThe old workflow sparse-checked-out mattermost/docs and cited source/**.rst\npaths that no longer exist, so it was judging the current PR against a docs\ntree this repo replaced. It also applied Docs/Needed and never removed it,\nwhich made the label a permanent record of a gap rather than a statement about\nthe PR as it stands.\n\ndocs-gap.yml reads both sides of the diff — the code and whatever docs the PR\nalready carries — so a later push that documents the change flips the verdict\nto none and clears the label. The label follows the verdict, not the presence\nof a docs diff, or clearing it would be an escape hatch anyone could take by\nediting an unrelated page. Prior state travels in the sticky comment, so a\nlabel a human applied survives a none verdict.\n\nThe audience personas come from the same frontmatter the review router reads\ninstead of being restated in workflow YAML, which is what keeps the two halves\nof the pipeline from disagreeing about who reads what.\n\nBoth are added and removed in one commit: they share a trigger, so running\nthem together would double-comment and race the label.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Tune docs-gap prompt, CAP limits, and Action pins\n\nCorrect API docs publish scope, size wrap caps for ~10k/1k LoC and ~100 paths, and bump checkout/setup-node to v7.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Split docs-ai into review/, gap/, and shared lib/\n\nMake which pipeline owns which scripts obvious; keep one package and shared helpers.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Trim docs-gap comments to non-obvious rationale\n\nKeep the why for label lifecycle, soft-fail, and secrets gating; drop restated narration.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Fix gap-report footer, label-remove restore, and cancelled report job\n\nAddress CodeRabbit: hide opt-out on none, restore sticky if removeLabel fails, shell-safe dry-run example, skip report on concurrency cancel.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Harden sticky author match and pin claude-code-action v1.0.235\n\nMatch stickies to github-actions[bot] only, use the job GITHUB_TOKEN\ninstead of Claude App OIDC on analyze, and bump the action pin.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"74632bc744add0179dc07314533e29b5669b2dd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/trees/74632bc744add0179dc07314533e29b5669b2dd0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/commits/27c501d217266608a917c163690505d14d75df66","verification":{"payload":"tree 74632bc744add0179dc07314533e29b5669b2dd0\nparent 8bfa298a54cba976311164492f4be9e62a039389\nauthor Eva Sarafianou <eva.sarafianou@gmail.com> 1790588956 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790588956 +0300\n\nReplace docs impact review with self-clearing gap detection (#38177)\n\n* Replace docs impact review with self-clearing gap detection\n\nThe old workflow sparse-checked-out mattermost/docs and cited source/**.rst\npaths that no longer exist, so it was judging the current PR against a docs\ntree this repo replaced. It also applied Docs/Needed and never removed it,\nwhich made the label a permanent record of a gap rather than a statement about\nthe PR as it stands.\n\ndocs-gap.yml reads both sides of the diff — the code and whatever docs the PR\nalready carries — so a later push that documents the change flips the verdict\nto none and clears the label. The label follows the verdict, not the presence\nof a docs diff, or clearing it would be an escape hatch anyone could take by\nediting an unrelated page. Prior state travels in the sticky comment, so a\nlabel a human applied survives a none verdict.\n\nThe audience personas come from the same frontmatter the review router reads\ninstead of being restated in workflow YAML, which is what keeps the two halves\nof the pipeline from disagreeing about who reads what.\n\nBoth are added and removed in one commit: they share a trigger, so running\nthem together would double-comment and race the label.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Tune docs-gap prompt, CAP limits, and Action pins\n\nCorrect API docs publish scope, size wrap caps for ~10k/1k LoC and ~100 paths, and bump checkout/setup-node to v7.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Split docs-ai into review/, gap/, and shared lib/\n\nMake which pipeline owns which scripts obvious; keep one package and shared helpers.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Trim docs-gap comments to non-obvious rationale\n\nKeep the why for label lifecycle, soft-fail, and secrets gating; drop restated narration.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Fix gap-report footer, label-remove restore, and cancelled report job\n\nAddress CodeRabbit: hide opt-out on none, restore sticky if removeLabel fails, shell-safe dry-run example, skip report on concurrency cancel.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Harden sticky author match and pin claude-code-action v1.0.235\n\nMatch stickies to github-actions[bot] only, use the job GITHUB_TOKEN\ninstead of Claude App OIDC on analyze, and bump the action pin.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqujgcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+84QAIQCT+4fcmd9pvXZHQcYjzfo\nU8YZOG0hLQfD2GrQQTupoflu3mybpcr3Vv0l3HgWxYrNw88pjrJ99J6eYUefWint\nCFy77UOChJzhOtOnxPgW+oFEub7syz9oariTx5kZV0l4W7rYF4zLJa3NNz1GZKm3\n/x7e9CqSsDcyJAkRHUUvRw+baOraCGIElVc19oNdppJDikK6qQDJ9JmPnyOVJepf\nOpk5GfAjZf5o0OlpRYK81lB433BLQ9/a/3dN1e3TNI4auY+IFt+5gS94JSFXbMiZ\n2s10SBg8dNkbXCyP6fysg6h/U5c7ESFb2nn2K497DHlYYEQJqCpCNMB1Z+wefwUO\nTL5mm2ES7aedn3t/XpJ5ngeeUzEv3SSiOSV4QCEyg+t9/NQXOvXDgAWRCBRHQ+4i\nSIKbUAwQVRGsWgTwCOcmfwwmzUbDOnDBMiLVBv5PUBgJR+WnY9lohtcyDjb6POw2\nfXD9ZI1k8RVzBklkquzh2UQu7WWBGkeFqnIQaZOIwVt82zFelGL94i38Uk7x8Iqa\nqHDkjTACSsb/mTnQXqsE27JI5ZZLSHNPKTKnV+SVEM5TivmbBu83K2JstKUU0pRt\nLejiyfswAVhQmU5FzFb/83upzMF8NDCpjhN/W2pcpFbl092s3NYI3T6rEh0jskFA\ne6C8+ZvhSRf85Q3nC7q7\n=/NZ8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T09:49:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/