unused tokens, and add focus-visible\nstyling to the header menu trigger.\n\nCo-authored-by: Matthew Birtch <mattbirtch@gmail.com>\n\n* Fix lint issues in admin navbar dropdown\n\nCo-authored-by: Matthew Birtch <mattbirtch@gmail.com>\n\n* Fix import order in admin navbar dropdown test\n\nCo-authored-by: Matthew Birtch <mattbirtch@gmail.com>\n\n* Fix Stylelint property order in admin sidebar active state\n\nCo-authored-by: Matthew Birtch <mattbirtch@gmail.com>\n\n* Wait for menu close before asserting dropdown actions in tests\n\nCo-authored-by: Matthew Birtch <mattbirtch@gmail.com>\n\n* Ensure single-team setup for MM-T909 system console menu test\n\nCo-authored-by: Matthew Birtch <mattbirtch@gmail.com>\n\n* Fix admin navbar dropdown tests for deferred menu onClick\n\nUse WithTestMenuContext instead of Menu.Container so menu close\ncallbacks fire synchronously in Jest. Assert modal dialogType against\nthe connected modal components rather than expect.any(Function).\n\nCo-authored-by: Matthew Birtch <mattbirtch@gmail.com>\n\n* Restore Team Selection label for zero-team admin menu\n\nUse admin.nav.switch when the user belongs to no teams, matching\npre-migration copy. Keep Switch teams for the multi-team submenu.\n\nCo-authored-by: Matthew Birtch <mattbirtch@gmail.com>\n\n* Simplify admin navbar dropdown test menu wrapper\n\nUse WithTestMenuContext directly, matching other menu item unit tests,\ninstead of wrapping with MuiMenuList and CompassDesignProvider.\n\nCo-authored-by: Matthew Birtch <mattbirtch@gmail.com>\n\n* Remove unused clearfix from admin sidebar header\n\nThe flex-based header already handles overflow on child elements; the\nlegacy clearfix mixin only applied overflow: hidden.\n\nCo-authored-by: Matthew Birtch <mattbirtch@gmail.com>\n\n* Remove dead admin console sidebar styling and sectionClass\n\nDrop unused sections--settings CSS, misplaced admin-console__header\nAvatar rules, and the orphaned sass:color import. Remove the unused\nsectionClass prop and rely on Avatar-lg for sidebar header sizing.\n\nCo-authored-by: Matthew Birtch <mattbirtch@gmail.com>\n\n* Align admin header menu positioning with Menu.Container props\n\nUse transformOrigin horizontal offset like other LHS menus instead of\nMuiPopover :has() CSS. Set main menu width via menu.width and scope\nSwitch teams submenu min-width to its MenuList id.\n\nCo-authored-by: Matthew Birtch <mattbirtch@gmail.com>\n\n* Rename admin sidebar header team__name to header__title\n\nThe primary header line shows System Console, not a team name.\n\nCo-authored-by: Matthew Birtch <mattbirtch@gmail.com>\n\n* Use flex layout for admin sidebar nav scroll area\n\nGive the Scrollbars wrapper flex: 1 instead of a fixed height calc on\nnav-pills__container. Size the console grid main row with minmax(0, 1fr)\nand remove the unused --admin-sidebar-nav-offset token.\n\nCo-authored-by: Matthew Birtch <mattbirtch@gmail.com>\n\n* Use lowercase hex for sys-sidebar-bg token\n\nCo-authored-by: Matthew Birtch <mattbirtch@gmail.com>\n\n* Revert unrelated MenuIcon changes from system console PR\n\nThe admin sidebar header uses ChevronDownIcon from compass-icons; the\nshared MenuIcon widget is still used by mobile channel header buttons.\n\nCo-authored-by: Matthew Birtch <mattbirtch@gmail.com>\n\n* Fix Stylelint property order in admin sidebar scroll rule\n\nCo-authored-by: Matthew Birtch <mattbirtch@gmail.com>\n\n* Improve admin console team submenu truncation and scrollbar hover.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Fix Stylelint property order on submenu paper styles.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Remove obsolete team-switch i18n keys from non-English locales.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Revert \"Remove obsolete team-switch i18n keys from non-English locales.\"\n\nThis reverts commit be37f063dfb2946d0ceb5c700e25780176c6f155.\n\n* Restore unused team-switch strings in en.json to satisfy i18n CI.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Keep en.json team-switch key restore minimal without resorting the file.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Sync en.json with i18n-extract after removing unused team-switch strings.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Close admin header menu before clicking BackstageNavbar in e2e.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Remove obsolete team-switch i18n keys from non-English locales.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* retain clip, menu portals so no longer gets clipped within anyway\n\n* Fix Stylelint property order: move overflow before flex-direction in .admin-sidebar\n\n* Fix e2e sidebar header menu button locator after portal-based menu migration\n\nThe #admin-sidebar-header ID is on the button element itself; scoping\ngetByRole(''button'') inside it searched for a button within a button.\nUse container directly since it resolves to the button. Also remove the\nstale comment describing the overflow-x/y split (no longer applicable\nsince portals render the menu outside the sidebar''s clip region).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix hover on active state\n\n* padding tweak on nav items to tighten a bit\n\n* Rename the System Console header menu accessible name to match the visible label.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Restore native external links in the System Console header menu.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Add Menu.ItemExternalLink and use it for System Console header links.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Fix keyboard focus and Enter/Space on System Console header menu links.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Point the System Console header menu overflow spec at the Switch teams submenu.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Tighten System Console LHS letter-spacing.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Matthew Birtch <2040554+matthewbirtch@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt/PhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiPwQABHC1bZ8nvmNu54kp5v6SJjp\nbH+ZVhlY+TZ7P59Wl6rL/UMetUfnHF63uZIW3cvHT1hYLzni8XN1WRIt0lY4FFlh\n2cLFw4rFk71sGNlF3R9GSwYrwuFNl8GGNpR88cMaAjHb3uChbx30ZZJCzW4L73Il\nwOwDcvjCcATlAEXV3a9XhxVo8o/JPistPBTpbJ+wuKIT2KrfLFRhO9OHcpbdFJ1W\nlt62rWpRmUVc7TyrOaaea+ouSCBX+wBcf6tSPUkzPXN05sVXviqyrRrfz3ZxlEno\nkdcNTODRjYEd6jXfpl1JFwAIXRq2NXsd4Ihut303cNm3scvyYvfyE7djWsVvvVn/\ntNG8P+oGFU5SyS0hqX55Ex8q9zren3rHlfEqF2GSNoLLzHASEyxkcgYMq+hae7at\n/lGfhMNFvRjhJHOkUxAc12h78CxuDFDOYtd2e7A88JM+Qogp85zMosail0eq9Fi/\neyV6/ZRqlROvfsFJANU3glXMHCjxmki2v1Y5I+ZboQUo4iW2C/UhQJxRllACeFA1\ngmCFN2QOIdPMN+VGEBtPmZEKH3jtvp0c509CLdH/Aem0fbqmP3eXia/gxpedaNNY\nk7lycGygztB5aY52CZuRLerfVu6GPV/jLh0peGrFq9B32JvS53q8EmzQ2atbndo5\nEYGApzsHrya2tNh+D//e\n=WUMO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T16:33:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/1f33d75c0c2f9d26cd9be109ae66b24c0bc3f28b","node_id":"C_kwDOAjtrA9oAKDFmMzNkNzVjMGMyZjlkMjZjZDliZTEwOWFlNjZiMjRjMGJjM2YyOGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/3a1f5f0da1868dd2d67a7b8d91ffd6333357354f","sha":"3a1f5f0da1868dd2d67a7b8d91ffd6333357354f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/3a1f5f0da1868dd2d67a7b8d91ffd6333357354f"}],"sha":"1f33d75c0c2f9d26cd9be109ae66b24c0bc3f28b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/1f33d75c0c2f9d26cd9be109ae66b24c0bc3f28b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17114347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/esarafianou","id":17114347,"login":"esarafianou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MTE0MzQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/3a1f5f0da1868dd2d67a7b8d91ffd6333357354f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T18:21:11Z","email":"eva.sarafianou@gmail.com","name":"Eva Sarafianou"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T18:21:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add AI persona review pipeline for docs PRs (#38144)\n\n* Add AI persona review pipeline for docs PRs\n\nSix reader personas review changes under docs/main, docs/develop and\ndocs/api, and one sticky comment per PR carries their verdicts. Advisory\nonly: nothing blocks a merge, and the review is a no-op when\nANTHROPIC_API_KEY is unset, so forks and unconfigured checkouts are\nunaffected.\n\nThe registry is the set of files in .github/prompts/personas/, each\ncarrying its metadata in frontmatter, so adding a persona means adding a\nfile. Rules that don''t vary by audience live in conventions.md and\nreview-contract.md instead of being restated six times, and they form a\nbyte-identical prefix across personas so they hit the prompt cache.\n\nConventions were derived by measuring docs/ rather than ported from the\nmigration PoC, which corrected three wrong assumptions: title is the only\nrequired frontmatter key, plan gating is <PlanAvailability slug>, and\ninternal links are absolute site paths.\n\nNo prose linter runs. The Vale config already in the repo comes from the\nPoC and has never been run against this corpus; it produces ~8,375\nfindings, most of them false positives, so brand-voice judges heading case\nand terminology in context instead. This change leaves those files\nuntouched and records the measurement in the docs-ai README, so whether\nthey should stay at all can be decided separately.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Fix version anchoring rules and drop the milestone from docs review\n\nThe milestone was a no-op. Assigning one is not a workflow trigger, and the\nvalue comes from the event payload, so a milestone set late in the cycle —\nwhich is when release management sets them — never reached a review at all.\nRemoved end to end: the workflow env var, the script flag, and both prompt\nbranches. Authoring keeps its milestone rule, since docs-needed.yml guarantees\none is set before the writer runs.\n\nVersion anchoring is now split by role rather than by who wrote the change. A\nreviewer cannot tell whether a person or a generator produced a diff, so the\nprevious framing was undecidable at the point of use. Reviewers check that an\nanchor exists, accept one the author states — developers ship docs with the\ncode and know their target release — and always flag the authoring placeholder,\nwhich only a human can clear.\n\nReviewers also no longer defer findings. The old budget guidance had\nbrand-voice drop lesser categories to fit three slots, which surfaced them one\npush at a time as earlier ones were fixed, indistinguishable from the standard\nmoving. Findings are pattern-collapsed instead, and a truncated list names its\nremainder in the summary so an author can fix everything in one pass.\n\nDrops dry-run.mjs and lib/diff.mjs, which nothing else consumed, and the README\nlink from the comment footer. Comments trimmed throughout.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Tighten docs AI prompts and harden the review comment\n\nScope brand-voice''s consistency check to the diff: it cannot see pages\noutside the change, so asking it to compare against neighbours invites\nclaims about content it never read.\n\nOnly adopt a bot-authored comment when updating the review. The marker\nrenders invisibly, so anyone able to comment could plant it and have the\nnext run overwrite their post.\n\nMake the verdict example valid JSON, replace the frontmatter regex with\nan explicit split, and cut the README back to the persona format and the\nconstraints a contributor can unknowingly break.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Validate persona docs_paths and code_signals at load\n\nA docs_paths entry that no longer exists matches nothing, so the persona\nsilently stops being selected for the content it owns; an impact-scoped\npersona with no code_signals silently gates on nothing. Both were only\ncaught by the test suite. Check them where the registry is built, so\nediting a persona locally fails with the offending path named.\n\nCode paths are deliberately not checked on disk: they are matched as\nprefixes and move far more often than docs directories.\n\nAlso say in the README that the file body is the persona''s system prompt.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Test the model-output and frontmatter edge cases\n\nparseJson and withRetry had no coverage at all, and they sit either side\nof every model call: one turns fenced or prose-wrapped output into a\nverdict, the other decides whether a failure costs one API call or three.\nThe frontmatter rules were covered only for the personas we ship, so the\nvalidation itself — id mismatch, unknown scope, a docs_paths entry that\ndoes not exist — went unexercised.\n\nTwo seams were needed. parsePersona now takes the file contents instead\nof reading them, because fixtures cannot live in the personas directory:\nthat directory is the registry, so a fixture in it would be a reviewer.\nwithRetry takes an injectable wait, so the retry path is tested without\n3.5s of real backoff.\n\nEach new test was checked by mutating the code it covers.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Validate the persona registry on master, and co-locate the unit tests\n\nThe registry resolves docs_paths against the working tree, so a docs\nrename that lands between a PR''s last run and its merge breaks master\nwith neither PR going red. Run validate on push as well; prepare now\ngates on the event, and review and report follow it, so a push costs one\njob and no model calls.\n\nMove the three unit tests beside the modules they cover, matching how the\nwebapp places its tests. registry.test.mjs stays at the top level: it\nchecks the personas and prompts we ship rather than any one module.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Find the sticky review comment past the first page of a PR thread\n\nreport.mjs read one page of issue comments and stopped. That endpoint returns\noldest-first and takes no ordering parameter, so a sticky comment created once a\nthread already held 100 comments fell outside the only page ever fetched, and\nevery later push posted a duplicate instead of editing it. The GitHub client\nmoves to lib/github.mjs, where the comment walk is a lazy generator that stops\nat the first match: unchanged single request on a short thread, and no\nduplicates on a long one.\n\nAlso drops docs/api from review scope. Its reference pages are generated from\nthe OpenAPI spec, so a finding there can only ever be fixed in api/v4/source/,\nand the workflow, the personas and the README now say so. The workflow excludes\ndocs/main/agents/docs for the same reason.\n\ncomplete() takes userPrompt rather than user, so the argument reads as the\nprompt it is next to the system prompt.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Run docs persona review on pull requests only\n\nThe push trigger only ever ran `validate`; the sticky comment the rest of\nthe workflow exists to produce has nowhere to land outside a PR. A registry\nbreak now surfaces on the next docs PR instead of on the merge that caused\nit, which costs a little latency and saves a run on every merge to master.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Run docs AI review via workflow_dispatch as a single job\n\nThe pull_request matrix attached a check per persona plus validate /\nprepare / report, which flooded the PR checks list before we had tuned\nthe personas. Manual dispatch with a PR number lets us exercise real\ndiffs without an audience; collapsing to one job keeps the later\npull_request restore to a single check.\n\nScripts and prompts come from the workflow ref, so a same-repo branch\ncannot rewrite the pipeline that reviews it. Also bump @anthropic-ai/sdk\nto 0.127.0 (was 0.40) and js-yaml to 4.3.2 for the merge-keys advisory,\nand disable the SDK''s own retries so they do not stack on withRetry.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Trim docs-review workflow comments to the non-obvious\n\nKeep only why dispatch is manual/single-job, why PR metadata\navoids GITHUB_OUTPUT, the merge-ref fallback, fail-soft persona\nwaits, and why SDK retries are disabled.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"49dab8381baf9a71dd957de770d3b1f0f32cf3f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/trees/49dab8381baf9a71dd957de770d3b1f0f32cf3f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/commits/3a1f5f0da1868dd2d67a7b8d91ffd6333357354f","verification":{"payload":"tree 49dab8381baf9a71dd957de770d3b1f0f32cf3f9\nparent 3b20966b6108e4fdb58773d8409ae4e37ca31001\nauthor Eva Sarafianou <eva.sarafianou@gmail.com> 1790360471 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790360471 +0300\n\nAdd AI persona review pipeline for docs PRs (#38144)\n\n* Add AI persona review pipeline for docs PRs\n\nSix reader personas review changes under docs/main, docs/develop and\ndocs/api, and one sticky comment per PR carries their verdicts. Advisory\nonly: nothing blocks a merge, and the review is a no-op when\nANTHROPIC_API_KEY is unset, so forks and unconfigured checkouts are\nunaffected.\n\nThe registry is the set of files in .github/prompts/personas/, each\ncarrying its metadata in frontmatter, so adding a persona means adding a\nfile. Rules that don''t vary by audience live in conventions.md and\nreview-contract.md instead of being restated six times, and they form a\nbyte-identical prefix across personas so they hit the prompt cache.\n\nConventions were derived by measuring docs/ rather than ported from the\nmigration PoC, which corrected three wrong assumptions: title is the only\nrequired frontmatter key, plan gating is <PlanAvailability slug>, and\ninternal links are absolute site paths.\n\nNo prose linter runs. The Vale config already in the repo comes from the\nPoC and has never been run against this corpus; it produces ~8,375\nfindings, most of them false positives, so brand-voice judges heading case\nand terminology in context instead. This change leaves those files\nuntouched and records the measurement in the docs-ai README, so whether\nthey should stay at all can be decided separately.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Fix version anchoring rules and drop the milestone from docs review\n\nThe milestone was a no-op. Assigning one is not a workflow trigger, and the\nvalue comes from the event payload, so a milestone set late in the cycle —\nwhich is when release management sets them — never reached a review at all.\nRemoved end to end: the workflow env var, the script flag, and both prompt\nbranches. Authoring keeps its milestone rule, since docs-needed.yml guarantees\none is set before the writer runs.\n\nVersion anchoring is now split by role rather than by who wrote the change. A\nreviewer cannot tell whether a person or a generator produced a diff, so the\nprevious framing was undecidable at the point of use. Reviewers check that an\nanchor exists, accept one the author states — developers ship docs with the\ncode and know their target release — and always flag the authoring placeholder,\nwhich only a human can clear.\n\nReviewers also no longer defer findings. The old budget guidance had\nbrand-voice drop lesser categories to fit three slots, which surfaced them one\npush at a time as earlier ones were fixed, indistinguishable from the standard\nmoving. Findings are pattern-collapsed instead, and a truncated list names its\nremainder in the summary so an author can fix everything in one pass.\n\nDrops dry-run.mjs and lib/diff.mjs, which nothing else consumed, and the README\nlink from the comment footer. Comments trimmed throughout.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Tighten docs AI prompts and harden the review comment\n\nScope brand-voice''s consistency check to the diff: it cannot see pages\noutside the change, so asking it to compare against neighbours invites\nclaims about content it never read.\n\nOnly adopt a bot-authored comment when updating the review. The marker\nrenders invisibly, so anyone able to comment could plant it and have the\nnext run overwrite their post.\n\nMake the verdict example valid JSON, replace the frontmatter regex with\nan explicit split, and cut the README back to the persona format and the\nconstraints a contributor can unknowingly break.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Validate persona docs_paths and code_signals at load\n\nA docs_paths entry that no longer exists matches nothing, so the persona\nsilently stops being selected for the content it owns; an impact-scoped\npersona with no code_signals silently gates on nothing. Both were only\ncaught by the test suite. Check them where the registry is built, so\nediting a persona locally fails with the offending path named.\n\nCode paths are deliberately not checked on disk: they are matched as\nprefixes and move far more often than docs directories.\n\nAlso say in the README that the file body is the persona''s system prompt.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Test the model-output and frontmatter edge cases\n\nparseJson and withRetry had no coverage at all, and they sit either side\nof every model call: one turns fenced or prose-wrapped output into a\nverdict, the other decides whether a failure costs one API call or three.\nThe frontmatter rules were covered only for the personas we ship, so the\nvalidation itself — id mismatch, unknown scope, a docs_paths entry that\ndoes not exist — went unexercised.\n\nTwo seams were needed. parsePersona now takes the file contents instead\nof reading them, because fixtures cannot live in the personas directory:\nthat directory is the registry, so a fixture in it would be a reviewer.\nwithRetry takes an injectable wait, so the retry path is tested without\n3.5s of real backoff.\n\nEach new test was checked by mutating the code it covers.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Validate the persona registry on master, and co-locate the unit tests\n\nThe registry resolves docs_paths against the working tree, so a docs\nrename that lands between a PR''s last run and its merge breaks master\nwith neither PR going red. Run validate on push as well; prepare now\ngates on the event, and review and report follow it, so a push costs one\njob and no model calls.\n\nMove the three unit tests beside the modules they cover, matching how the\nwebapp places its tests. registry.test.mjs stays at the top level: it\nchecks the personas and prompts we ship rather than any one module.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Find the sticky review comment past the first page of a PR thread\n\nreport.mjs read one page of issue comments and stopped. That endpoint returns\noldest-first and takes no ordering parameter, so a sticky comment created once a\nthread already held 100 comments fell outside the only page ever fetched, and\nevery later push posted a duplicate instead of editing it. The GitHub client\nmoves to lib/github.mjs, where the comment walk is a lazy generator that stops\nat the first match: unchanged single request on a short thread, and no\nduplicates on a long one.\n\nAlso drops docs/api from review scope. Its reference pages are generated from\nthe OpenAPI spec, so a finding there can only ever be fixed in api/v4/source/,\nand the workflow, the personas and the README now say so. The workflow excludes\ndocs/main/agents/docs for the same reason.\n\ncomplete() takes userPrompt rather than user, so the argument reads as the\nprompt it is next to the system prompt.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Run docs persona review on pull requests only\n\nThe push trigger only ever ran `validate`; the sticky comment the rest of\nthe workflow exists to produce has nowhere to land outside a PR. A registry\nbreak now surfaces on the next docs PR instead of on the merge that caused\nit, which costs a little latency and saves a run on every merge to master.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Run docs AI review via workflow_dispatch as a single job\n\nThe pull_request matrix attached a check per persona plus validate /\nprepare / report, which flooded the PR checks list before we had tuned\nthe personas. Manual dispatch with a PR number lets us exercise real\ndiffs without an audience; collapsing to one job keeps the later\npull_request restore to a single check.\n\nScripts and prompts come from the workflow ref, so a same-repo branch\ncannot rewrite the pipeline that reviews it. Also bump @anthropic-ai/sdk\nto 0.127.0 (was 0.40) and js-yaml to 4.3.2 for the merge-keys advisory,\nand disable the SDK''s own retries so they do not stack on withRetry.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Trim docs-review workflow comments to the non-obvious\n\nKeep only why dispatch is manual/single-job, why PR metadata\navoids GITHUB_OUTPUT, the merge-ref fallback, fail-soft persona\nwaits, and why SDK retries are disabled.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtruXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAd6IQABELsZC6bIIMzSNYo7AsVnci\noGLOCqv/J5p3qKMCbrtvJkkWc4VmVd4b57jmBfuJV2Cl6VFj3BXQSPHsLJZLltQj\nq5vhrcyAyJYrnmQc1vEI5SX64xM6DlXvBd8CquFTjgxt2dcKJYThivQ+X0cjmO1/\ntrrvXvsROdwwBc/EDsYyoihmDTeXyYzNUSz2gGjnPKn9k9jtjyVwQaUzyGic2h0N\ny9TR9ormTUgSESxhi45rtklX98YzJD2H8QpZUiUpA9fKP6ameDEHBh4Ejwh7jDnT\n+r4rqWXQ3MgEfoJW1nc8XpfDCtY6PuaLmXl7ixj5gkdHEPj3VDdVLsocNba9Kkj1\nEEkx4j4QxqTPlsMJYRquRryp2Osq5xG8hKn8hAnUiafIq/KobazdDOktahEKa59w\nRmnWW1ibKXDkw+BVpGPLo/Sh71NTN7yfB8m4xb9T6/8z99OcMIuutyVXyiIkUsJ8\nVf1lwdRTCag8u0Stpl/5fcpr5hyZN+Se9GECz2U124jaCMmWVnUOdYA7gcl0riHP\nFUe1fUMRdr2FiYePHUxCV6errgyz1+oTGfWBsdNUiY9sIcZd5EB7+Mdl