gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/devinbinnie","id":52460000,"login":"devinbinnie","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDYwMDAw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devinbinnie/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devinbinnie/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devinbinnie/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devinbinnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devinbinnie/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/devinbinnie","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/5b398474642e8c63dd30e71445046fd2e3392b2b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T12:33:38Z","email":"52460000+devinbinnie@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Devin Binnie"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T12:33:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Session attributes docs (#38553)\n\n* Session attributes docs\n\n* PR feedback\n\n* Clarify Desktop-only os_platform availability in ABAC rule documentation\n\n* Reorder\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: coderabbitai[bot] <136622811+coderabbitai[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"1324e3e1ba414cd8effeeee84e8475963d7676f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/trees/1324e3e1ba414cd8effeeee84e8475963d7676f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/commits/5b398474642e8c63dd30e71445046fd2e3392b2b","verification":{"payload":"tree 1324e3e1ba414cd8effeeee84e8475963d7676f9\nparent f76792bb97038c37d09639803f67c0c8675744ca\nauthor Devin Binnie <52460000+devinbinnie@users.noreply.github.com> 1790339618 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790339618 -0400\n\nSession attributes docs (#38553)\n\n* Session attributes docs\n\n* PR feedback\n\n* Clarify Desktop-only os_platform availability in ABAC rule documentation\n\n* Reorder\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: coderabbitai[bot] <136622811+coderabbitai[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtmoiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgmUQAJUC9rstAKsz2dXjUrdCZQ2o\n3q6KD02gMqqdPy2u86I6PKnFO2Gd2EoXWTkb3dt/7QlNNL0/LhLwcmpk9Pt+gzz+\n85oohLBxi13NxydLK3KHxneuw2h8vR+jPNBODpgRBzUlf//A40QPKQPoVf2H8CLU\nRuGsW9SKt7f3ThqsZ/RuxunhtAW2p5p54S6k2GK3vxUaHLLXLCA7vf2WBFZbXNkZ\nkvgrQjrDi075+sNbm35kUJ4mQ2bph7gDPthDBTp5n0dWVJa8k6Hcm0LHLJQxY2zD\nVaDNEchyuPvZEI8aOlkUK/8G9CHWizJH096PE4j6o5wcoHrkoE80Vtj8Hg4MqKIO\nTfTDh3kMf4I/sMV0v/iyGYs106WwqO+qKOO1v6HFivqktZZV5qljS2N4AtrPpEqF\nHvnDxDMZawn1QpS7993EoHcjF4jBxquVl68qHS9wrsa1I6MvY6HsoryRCGPSMI7v\nilw38k+rCsokDUle8Vt2UzQn1YkNomcc+5xUCR87LEmMGv8brJ5d8qmVXv110XL9\nEqcLfi78ksRWgwnlMrw/npsFdZaCF8AKOArSzMPSqpKBch7UCDCMU0cwKNflSM6j\nLtFl3IGoEsVFh0EIgr5Dk4fVfL2U7IagVd6wjOkFT3Kk9KaSOAqShK4VcTsGi5jj\nmEvpUDq3/5Sf+TEcSAC6\n=sMmj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T12:33:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/5b398474642e8c63dd30e71445046fd2e3392b2b","node_id":"C_kwDOAjtrA9oAKDViMzk4NDc0NjQyZThjNjNkZDMwZTcxNDQ1MDQ2ZmQyZTMzOTJiMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/f76792bb97038c37d09639803f67c0c8675744ca","sha":"f76792bb97038c37d09639803f67c0c8675744ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/f76792bb97038c37d09639803f67c0c8675744ca"}],"sha":"5b398474642e8c63dd30e71445046fd2e3392b2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/5b398474642e8c63dd30e71445046fd2e3392b2b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17114347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/esarafianou","id":17114347,"login":"esarafianou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MTE0MzQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/commits/f76792bb97038c37d09639803f67c0c8675744ca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T09:17:19Z","email":"eva.sarafianou@gmail.com","name":"Eva Sarafianou"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T09:17:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(site): make IMEDiagram content-driven with variant toggle (#38593)\n\n* docs(site): make IMEDiagram content-driven with variant toggle\n\nRefactor the Intelligent Mission Environment diagram so all copy,\nicons, and layout live in typed content modules under\n''components/IMEDiagram/content/''. The React component is now a pure\nrenderer over an ''IMEContent'' object.\n\nAdds a second ''mission'' variant that mirrors the National Security /\nFedGov marketing infographic (title + tagline, 6 application cards,\nInteroperability row with ABAC / classification / federation controls,\n3-column Deployment row with brand logo strips).\n\nThe default export shows an audience toggle above the diagram when\nneither ''variant'' nor ''content'' props are passed, so visitors can\nswitch between General and National Security views at read time. The\nexisting ''<IMEDiagram />'' call site in docs/main/index.mdx picks this\nup automatically.\n\nAlso adds ''scripts/render-ime.mjs'', a Playwright script that navigates\nto ''/?imeVariant=<id>&imeExport=1'' (a mode that hides the toggle) and\nscreenshots each variant to ''static/img/ime/<id>.png'', so marketing\ncan reuse the docs as the single source of truth for the infographic.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs(site): point IMEDiagram Advanced Information Controls at zero-trust\n\nThe Zero Trust security guide covers ABAC, ICAM, session enforcement,\nand dynamic policies — a much closer match to this cell''s bullets than\nthe generic security-guide index.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs(site): use real brand assets from FY27 sales deck in IMEDiagram mission variant\n\nExtracts icons and brand marks from slide 7 of the FY27 Platform Pitch\nSales Deck and wires them into the mission variant of the IMEDiagram:\n\n* Product-card icons (Messaging/Workflow/Audio/Project/Human-Machine\n  Teaming) — the marigold outline icons from the deck instead of the\n  generic inline SVGs.\n* Application client strip logos — Windows, macOS, Linux, iOS,\n  Android, Microsoft Teams.\n* Application supply-chain strip logos — PostgreSQL, Kubernetes,\n  React Native, GitHub, Go, Argo.\n* Deployment ''Enterprise to Edge with Sovereign AI'' cloud logos —\n  Azure, Oracle, AWS, GCP.\n* Deployment ''Layered Extensibility'' integration logos — GitHub,\n  GitLab, Jira, Confluence, Splunk.\n\nSchema changes:\n\n* ''Cell'' and ''Intro'' gain an optional ''iconSrc'' path; when set it\n  takes precedence over the named ''icon'' key. This keeps the general\n  variant''s inline SVG icons working while letting the mission variant\n  reference PNGs.\n* Renderer adds a small ''CellIcon'' helper that picks ''iconSrc'' vs.\n  the SVG icon.\n* Adds ''.iconImg'' / ''.introIconImg'' styles (larger 2rem/1.5rem to\n  match the deck''s baked-in padding) and tightens the ''.logoImg''\n  sizing so wordmarks (Oracle, AWS) don''t overwhelm the sentence\n  text next to them.\n\nAlso corrects a few strings on the mission variant to match the\ncanonical deck wording exactly (''Air-Gapped & Sovereign Deployment &\nIntegration'', ''Secure Federation & Interoperability'', ''Scales to 200K+\nconcurrent users'', ''NATO & US PL3, IL4/5, 6/7 proven'').\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs(site): add IME banner, widen to 16:9, and add remaining deck logos\n\nMatches the FY27 Platform Pitch deck (slide 7) more faithfully:\n\n* Blue camo banner with title + tagline replaces the plain text\n  header. Uses the deck''s own background image (banner-bg.jpg) with\n  a marigold underline for brand rhythm.\n* Diagram widens rightward on \\u2265 1200px viewports to hit the deck''s\n  native 1280x720 (16:9) dimensions. Uses ''--doc-sidebar-width'' so it\n  never overlaps the docs sidebar. This dramatically reduces the\n  vertical whitespace inside each cell (product cards no longer stack\n  tall).\n* Adds 14 more brand assets extracted from the same slide:\n  AI vendors (Meta, Mistral, Ask Sage, OpenAI, Elastic, Perplexity),\n  federation partners (MS Defender, MS Entra ID, Global Relay, Tines,\n  MS sync/devices), and misc (webhook, plus, generic-O federation\n  badge).\n* Populates the mission variant''s logo constellations to match the\n  deck: Interop \\u2192 Secure Federation cell gains a federation partner\n  strip, Deployment intro gains the AI vendor row (OpenAI, Meta,\n  Elastic, Perplexity, Ask Sage, Mistral), Deployment \\u2192 Layered\n  Extensibility grows to the full 9-logo mix.\n* Swaps intro icons for deck-branded PNGs: Applications gets the\n  MS sync/devices icon, Interop gets the MS Defender shield,\n  Deployment gets the Mattermost mark.\n\nSchema: ''Intro'' gains an optional ''logos'' field so intro columns can\ncarry their own decorative badge row (used by Deployment''s AI vendor\nconstellation). Renderer picks it up via the existing ''LogoStrip''.\n\nGeneral variant is unaffected \\u2014 it has no title/tagline so no banner\nrenders, and it doesn''t set ''iconSrc'' anywhere so it keeps the\ninline SVG icons.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Address CodeRabbit review on IME diagram\n\n- Reset .markdown h2 spacing and marigold ::before bar on .bannerTitle\n  so the landing-page global doesn''t distort the mission banner.\n- Resolve mission image and banner-bg paths through useBaseUrl so they\n  work under non-root Docusaurus deployments.\n- Normalize every variant source (prop, URL, activeId) through\n  getVariant and derive aria-selected from the resolved variant so the\n  toggle can''t diverge from the rendered diagram; suppress the toggle\n  entirely when the parent controls the variant/content.\n- Drive .cellGrid and .footerRow columns from --ime-cols with a\n  data-cols attribute, so tablet breakpoints keep single-column layers\n  single-column without an inline-style vs !important fight.\n- Add data-variant + data-ready on the diagram <section> and have\n  render-ime.mjs wait on the variant-specific selector instead of the\n  first ''[aria-label\\$=\\\"overview\\\"]'' match.\n- Declare playwright as a devDependency (with matching lockfile entries)\n  and add an ''npm run render:ime'' script.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Center IME diagram in the reading column; drop General variant\n\n- Align the wrapper to the text column on both sides (max-width: 1280px,\n  width: 100%, margin: 0 auto) instead of breaking out rightward. The\n  previous wide breakout made the diagram''s left match the text column\n  but overflowed only to the right, producing asymmetric margins.\n- Keep the General content module in the tree but remove it from the\n  toggle so only the mission variant renders. Rename its label to\n  ''Enterprise Advanced''. New variants can be re-added to the array as\n  they land.\n- Auto-hide the toggle whenever only one variant is registered so we\n  don''t render a single-option ''tab'' row.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Narrow IME intro column to reclaim tile width\n\nThe intro column (Zero Trust..., Accelerates..., Air-Gapped...) was\nsized fractionally (1.1fr : 3.4fr) which ate ~24% of the diagram\nwidth. Fix at 150px so the 6-tile Applications row gets ~90px per\ntile instead of ~85px, and shrink the intro h3 slightly (0.95rem →\n0.88rem) so the title still wraps cleanly in the narrower column.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Widen IME diagram + match deck icon placement\n\nWidth: restore the wider-than-text layout on desktop (>= 1200px).\nThe wrapper breaks out of the reading column and extends rightward\ninto the space Docusaurus reserves for a ToC. The landing page hides\nits ToC in frontmatter, so that space is empty; the diagram never\nextends leftward, so it never overlaps the docs sidebar. Capped at\n1280px and viewport-safe via min().\n\nIcons per FY27 Platform Pitch deck (slide 7):\n- Accelerates Classified & Mission Partner Operations intro: drop\n  the leading icon (deck shows plain title text).\n- Air-Gapped & Sovereign Deployment & Integration intro: drop the\n  leading icon and the AI-vendor constellation (OpenAI, Meta,\n  Elastic, Perplexity, Ask Sage, Mistral).\n- Enterprise to Edge with Sovereign AI cell: absorb the AI vendor\n  logos the intro was carrying (OpenAI, Meta, Elastic, Ask Sage,\n  Mattermost) plus ''Tactical Edge'' and ''Local Datacenter'' text\n  badges, sitting above the existing Azure/Oracle/AWS/GCP row.\n- Secure Federation & Interoperability cell: drop the logo strip\n  (MS Teams, Entra, Matrix, Global Relay). Deck shows bullets only.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Position IME cell logos to match deck layout\n\nSchema:\n- Cell.cornerLogos: array of small logos pinned to the top-right of a\n  cell via absolute positioning. Used for the AI-vendor and\n  integration constellations that sit in the corner of the deck.\n- Cell.logoLayout (''strip'' | ''grid'') + Cell.logoColumns: opt-in CSS\n  grid layout for the main logo list (Layered Extensibility uses\n  a 4-column grid rather than a flow strip).\n- Layer.columnsTemplate: explicit grid-template-columns override so\n  a row can carry uneven-width cards (Deployment row uses\n  ''1.2fr 1.1fr 0.9fr'' to mirror the deck).\n\nMission content (deck slide 7):\n- Enterprise-to-Edge: OpenAI, Meta, Elastic, Ask Sage, Mattermost\n  logos in the top-right corner; Tactical Edge / Local Datacenter\n  text badges + Azure/Oracle/AWS/GCP logos remain as the bottom\n  strip.\n- Layered Extensibility: Jira, GitHub, GitLab, MS Defender, Splunk\n  as corner logos; Confluence, MS Teams, MS Sync, MS Entra, Tines,\n  Argo, Webhook, plus icon in a 4-column grid below the bullets.\n\nRenderer/CSS:\n- .cell becomes a positioning context (position: relative).\n- .cornerLogos: absolute top-right constellation with pointer-events\n  disabled so it never intercepts card clicks.\n- .logoGrid: CSS grid driven by --ime-logo-cols.\n- LayerBlock honours columnsTemplate before falling back to the\n  --ime-cols count.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Rename IME ''mission'' variant to ''entadv''; drop dead general variant\n\n- Rename content/mission.ts -> content/entadv.ts via git mv so history\n  is preserved. Update the exported constant (mission -> entadv), the\n  IMEContent.id (''mission'' -> ''entadv''), the JSDoc header, and the\n  variant registry in content/index.ts. The audience label stays\n  ''Enterprise Advanced''.\n- Remove content/general.ts. It was kept as a scaffold when we\n  narrowed the toggle down to a single variant, but the file is dead\n  code today and reintroducing a ''General'' audience will need fresh\n  copy anyway.\n- Re-tune the Layered Extensibility logo constellation to match the\n  slide more closely: swap Microsoft Defender out of the corner in\n  favour of Element/Matrix (enterprise-o), and rebalance the 4-column\n  grid to Elastic / MS Defender / MS Teams / MS Entra / MS Sync /\n  Global Relay / Confluence / Add.\n- Update render-ime.mjs VARIANTS list and the JSDoc example.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Render Layered Extensibility grid beside its bullets (deck parity)\n\nThe deck''s Layered Extensibility card places the ecosystem logos as\na 4×3 grid next to the bullet list, not below it and not split into\na corner constellation plus a bottom strip.\n\n- Add Cell.bodyLayout (''stack'' | ''side-by-side''). Default is ''stack''\n  (previous behaviour); ''side-by-side'' wraps the text block and the\n  logo grid in a two-column .cellSplit grid inside the cell body.\n- Add matching .cellSplit CSS and tighten the .logoGrid gaps when\n  it''s rendering inside a split (half the horizontal room).\n- Retarget Layered Extensibility content: drop the cornerLogos array\n  and merge those five icons into the main logos list, bringing the\n  grid to 12 items (Jira, GitHub, GitLab, Element, Splunk, Elastic,\n  MS Defender, MS Teams, MS Entra, MS Sync, Global Relay, Add).\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Drop title icons from IME Interoperability + Deployment cells\n\nThe source slide renders these cards as plain title + bullets; the\nmarigold SVG icons we were adding above each title (lock, users,\nserver, plug, shield) don''t exist on the deck. Removing them from\nAdvanced Information Controls, Secure Federation & Interoperability,\nEnterprise to Edge with Sovereign AI, Layered Extensibility, and\nHigh Availability & Scale.\n\nUse Cases + Applications rows keep their leading icons — those DO\nappear on the slide, and the Applications tiles use brand-mark PNGs\n(iconSrc) rather than the generic SVG registry.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Fix IME variant/toggle desync when URL preselects a variant\n\nPreviously, ?imeVariant=<id> both seeded activeId AND was stashed on\nurlOverride.variant, which then permanently won the resolve chain\n(variant ?? urlOverride.variant ?? activeId). Clicking a toggle tab\nmutated activeId but never affected what rendered, so the toggle\nlooked non-functional whenever the URL had picked a variant.\n\nDrop urlOverride.variant from state and let the URL seed activeId\nonce inside the useEffect. The resolve chain becomes\n(variant ?? activeId), so tab clicks take over from there.\nRenamed the remaining urlOverride.hideToggle to a boolean state for\nclarity.\n\nLatent today (only one variant is registered) but breaks the moment\na second variant lands.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME Applications tiles: center-align, underline product names, drop stray bold\n\nMatch the source slide for the Applications row:\n\n- Introduce `Cell.bodyLead`, an optional leading term rendered\n  underlined immediately before `body` (e.g. \"Channels\" in\n  \"Channels: ChatOps and automation\"). Applications cells split\n  their body copy into `bodyLead` + `body` so the product name gets\n  the deck''s underline treatment.\n- Center-align icon, title, and body copy in `.layer_applications`\n  tiles only. Use Cases and Deployment cards keep left-aligned\n  reading rhythm.\n- Force `.cellText` to `font-weight: 400` so nothing inherits bold\n  from surrounding markdown context; only `.cellTitle` stays bold.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME Interoperability cells: enlarged title on the left, bullets on the right\n\nMatch the source slide for the two Interoperability tiles (Advanced\nInformation Controls, Secure Federation & Interoperability):\n\n- Add `Cell.titlePlacement` (''top'' default | ''left''). When ''left'',\n  the cell body is a two-column grid: enlarged title in the left\n  column, body/bullets in the right.\n- Renderer emits a `.cellTitleSplit` wrapper for `titlePlacement:''left''`\n  cells; scoped `.cellTitleLeft .cellTitle` bumps the title to the\n  deck''s ~1.1rem size.\n- Interoperability content flips both cells to `titlePlacement:''left''`\n  and drops the (now-unused) leading icon.\n- Narrow-viewport fallback stacks title above bullets.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME Interoperability: center the title within its left column\n\nThe title was hugging the top-left of its column against the tall\nbullet list on the right. Set the aside to stretch to the row height\nand center its contents both axes, matching the deck.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME Interoperability: left-align title horizontally, keep vertical centering\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME Use Cases: drop leading icons, enlarge titles to match deck\n\nThe source slide''s Use Cases row has no leading icons and its titles\nread as the largest per-tile heading. Drop the shield/code/compass\nicons from all three cells and bump .layer_use-cases .cellTitle to\n1.15rem.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: match deck copy for Enterprise-to-Edge body\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Address CodeRabbit review: install chromium + wait for asset decode\n\n- npm script ''render:ime'' now runs ''playwright install chromium'' first\n  so a fresh checkout renders without a manual setup step (idempotent —\n  skipped when the browser is already downloaded).\n- render-ime.mjs waits for every <img> in the target section to load +\n  decode, and probes CSS background-image URLs (banner backdrop, etc.)\n  the same way, before screenshotting. data-ready fires as soon as\n  React commits the variant but images may still be decoding; without\n  this wait the exported PNG can be missing icons/logos/backgrounds.\n\nSkipped CodeRabbit findings that were already handled:\n- ''Resolve image paths against baseUrl'' — every image goes through the\n  <Img> helper (useBaseUrl) in index.tsx: CellIcon, IntroPanel,\n  LogoStrip, cornerLogos, and BannerHeader.\n- ''Toggle should change URL-selected variant'' — fixed in 152360aefb;\n  the URL now only seeds activeId on mount.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: drop Zero Trust icon and enlarge intro titles to fill the column\n\nApplications intro no longer renders the ms-sync icon (deck has no\nleading icon on any intro). Bumped .intro h3 from 0.88rem to 1.05rem\nso the three intro blocks fill the fixed 150px column instead of\nleaving a stripe of whitespace below.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: raise responsive-collapse breakpoint to match wrapper breakout\n\nThe wrapper breaks out of the reading column at >= 1200px, but the\ncollapse fallback only kicked in at <= 980px. Viewports in the\n981-1199px gap tried to render the full 6-tile grid + intro column\ninside a cramped ~700px reading column, so titles and body copy\noverlapped (visible with the docs sidebar open on ~1050px screens).\n\nRaise the breakpoint to 1199px so any viewport that doesn''t get the\nbreakout gets the 2-col fallback + stacked intro + stacked Interop\ntitle/bullets.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: fit within reading column + match deck copy on Use Cases\n\n- Wrapper: drop the >= 1200px breakout; the diagram now sits inside\n  the reading column, capped at 1280px. Add container-type: inline-size\n  so collapse triggers on wrapper width rather than viewport width.\n- Responsive: swap @media (max-width: 1199px) for @container\n  (max-width: 900px) — same collapse behavior but keyed to the\n  container so narrow reading columns (e.g. pages with a visible ToC)\n  collapse the same way narrow viewports do. Added !important on the\n  container-query grid-template-columns overrides so the Deployment\n  layer''s inline columnsTemplate still yields at narrow widths.\n- Use Cases copy trimmed to match the deck word-for-word.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: restore controlled breakout to recover the deck''s 16:9 ratio\n\nFitting the wrapper strictly to the reading column produced a\n~1.05:1 layout because Interoperability bullets wrapped tall. Bring\nback the breakout at >= 1300px viewports, capped at min(1280px,\nviewport - sidebar - gutters) so it never overlaps the sidebar and\nnever grows past the deck''s native width. Container query for\ncollapse stays in place, so narrow reading columns still collapse\ngracefully.\n\nResult on a 1728px viewport: 1280 x 750 (1.71:1) vs slide''s 1.78:1.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: drop unused SVG icons, strip entadv comments, retarget Agents\n\nKeep only the star glyph still referenced by Future Applications; point\nthe Agents tile at the admin agents guide.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: trim horizontal + vertical whitespace, cap wrapper at 1200px\n\nDiagram overflowed rightward more than needed and had extra padding\nthroughout. Trim proportionally so the ratio stays deck-shaped\n(~1.69:1 vs slide 1.78:1) with a smaller footprint.\n\n- Wrapper cap 1280 -> 1200 (breakout right edge shifts 80px inward).\n- Layer body padding 0.9rem 1rem -> 0.55rem 0.85rem.\n- Banner padding 1rem 1.5rem -> 0.7rem 1.25rem.\n- Banner title 1.6rem -> 1.4rem; tagline 0.9rem -> 0.82rem.\n- Intro column 150px -> 135px; intro h3 1.05rem -> 0.98rem.\n- Cell padding 0.6rem 0.7rem -> 0.5rem 0.6rem; cell gap 0.35rem -> 0.3rem.\n- .cellGrid gap 0.5rem -> 0.4rem.\n- .layerContentWithIntro gap 0.85rem -> 0.7rem.\n\nAt 1728px viewport: was 1280 x 750, now 1200 x 708. 42px shorter,\n80px narrower, wrapper right edge x=1612 -> 1532.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: grow banner, close visible white gap under it\n\nThe .layer_use-cases .layerBody top padding read as a visible white\nframe between the marigold banner border and the tinted (denim-50)\nUse Cases cells, while the same padding at the bottom of Deployment\nblended invisibly into its white cells. Geometry was symmetric, only\nthe perception was asymmetric.\n\n- .layer_use-cases .layerBody padding-top 0.55rem -> 0.2rem so the\n  first tinted row sits right under the marigold border.\n- .banner padding 0.7rem -> 1rem vertically to absorb the reclaimed\n  height.\n- Banner title 1.4rem -> 1.55rem, tagline 0.82rem -> 0.88rem so the\n  taller banner reads as intentional weight, not extra chrome.\n\nAt 1728px viewport: banner 73 -> 88, top-gap-below-banner 10 -> 4,\ndiagram 708 -> 724, ratio 1.69 -> 1.66.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: revert Use Cases top-padding trim, keep enlarged banner\n\nThe zero-gap look under the marigold border read as cramped. Restore\nthe standard .layerBody top padding on Use Cases (0.55rem) so the\ntinted tiles get their breathing room back. The banner keeps its\nenlarged size from the previous commit.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: trim Use Cases top padding to 0.35rem (7px gap under banner)\n\nMiddle ground between the too-tight 0.2rem (4px) and the too-loose\ndefault 0.55rem (10px). The tinted Use Cases tiles no longer read as\nfloating in a large white frame below the marigold rule, but keep\nenough breathing room to not look cramped.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: shrink layerLabel vertical padding so short lanes stop stretching\n\nThe extra ~28px of whitespace below the Use Cases tiles wasn''t from\n.layerBody padding — it was the vertical layerLabel (''USE CASES'')\ndemanding ~103px of row height (writing-mode: vertical-rl + heavy\nletter-spacing + padding: 0.85rem 0). Grid stretched the tile body\nto match, showing up as a big buffer below the tiles.\n\nTrim label padding to 0.15rem and letter-spacing 0.22em -> 0.18em so\nshort lanes size to their content instead of the label. Use Cases\ngap-above-tiles/gap-below-tiles is now 6px/8px (was 6px/34px).\nDiagram height at 1728px viewport: 724 -> 698.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: match deck 16:9 ratio, small banner bump\n\nBump wrapper cap 1200 -> 1240 and banner vertical padding\n1rem -> 1.1rem. At 1728px viewport the diagram is now 1240x701 =\n1.769:1, essentially matching the slide''s 1.778:1. Banner grew from\n88 -> 91px.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: fix phone breakpoint losing to container-query !important\n\nThe @container (max-width: 900px) rule uses\n''.cellGrid:not([data-cols=\"1\"]) { ... !important }'' to force multi-\ncolumn layers into 2 columns. That out-specificity''d the phone rule\n''.cellGrid { grid-template-columns: 1fr }'', so multi-column grids\nstayed 2-column at phone widths.\n\nMatch specificity + add !important on the phone selector for both\n.cellGrid and .footerRow. Verified at viewport 500px: all four\ngrids (data-cols 3, 6, 2, custom) now render as a single column.\n\nAddresses CodeRabbit review comment #4098042300.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Move IMEDiagram to asset-only icons; swap star to inline SVG\n\n- Delete icons.tsx SVG registry and IconName type; content modules now\n  reference icons purely via iconSrc.\n- Add /img/ime/logos/star.svg (marigold, transparent) for the\n  Future Applications tile; drop the SVG-specific CSS branches for\n  .icon, .introIcon, and .footerIcon.\n- Prune icon fields from Cell, Intro, and FooterStrip in types.ts and\n  simplify CellIcon, IntroPanel, and FooterCell accordingly.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Refresh render-ime.mjs setup notes\n\nPlaywright is now a direct devDependency and the render:ime npm script\nruns ''playwright install chromium'' before the render, so a fresh\ncheckout no longer needs the old ''npm i -D playwright'' instructions.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Switch IMEDiagram star to outlined stroke\n\nFilled marigold read as an off-tone accent next to the other tile\nicons. Match the previous SVG style: stroked marigold outline, no fill.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Match star.svg color to sibling icons\n\nStar was too yellow (#FFBC1F) next to the sparkle icon\n(Human-Machine Teaming), which renders as warm gold #D5A130.\nMatch that tone.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Restore brand logo legibility in IMEDiagram dark mode\n\nDark surfaces were swallowing near-black brand marks (GitHub, OpenAI,\nSplunk, Mattermost, React Native, Plus). Two scoped fixes:\n\n- footer strips: white background with denim text in dark mode\n  (mirrors the deck, which paints these strips white regardless of\n  surrounding tone).\n- brand logos on non-strip surfaces (corner logos, logo grids,\n  intro strips): small white chip so dark marks retain contrast on\n  the near-black cell background.\n\nLight mode is unaffected.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Fix IMEDiagram dark-mode brand icon legibility and alignment\n\nDark surfaces were swallowing near-black brand marks (GitHub, OpenAI,\nSplunk, Mattermost, React Native, Plus, Ask Sage, Meta) across three\ncarrier types: footer strips, corner logos on tiles, and the 3×4\nlogo matrix on Layered Extensibility.\n\n- Wrap each brand mark in a soft-grey chip (#e6e8ec) in dark mode.\n  Uses border-box padding so strip and grid dimensions stay identical\n  to light mode.\n- Tighten the chip padding for the dense 3×4 grid and the tiny\n  corner logos so the brand mark isn''t crowded out.\n- Drop the logoStrip top margin inside footer strips — it was intended\n  for stacking-context use in intro columns and pushed the icons ~7px\n  below the text baseline in the horizontal strip layout.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"d0f5481e02665bbaf1ba11c3bd331b961c53aa35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/trees/d0f5481e02665bbaf1ba11c3bd331b961c53aa35"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mattermost/mattermost/git/commits/f76792bb97038c37d09639803f67c0c8675744ca","verification":{"payload":"tree d0f5481e02665bbaf1ba11c3bd331b961c53aa35\nparent b20499b51166cfe20390b74b4ce890c6f3052438\nauthor Eva Sarafianou <eva.sarafianou@gmail.com> 1790327839 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790327839 +0300\n\ndocs(site): make IMEDiagram content-driven with variant toggle (#38593)\n\n* docs(site): make IMEDiagram content-driven with variant toggle\n\nRefactor the Intelligent Mission Environment diagram so all copy,\nicons, and layout live in typed content modules under\n''components/IMEDiagram/content/''. The React component is now a pure\nrenderer over an ''IMEContent'' object.\n\nAdds a second ''mission'' variant that mirrors the National Security /\nFedGov marketing infographic (title + tagline, 6 application cards,\nInteroperability row with ABAC / classification / federation controls,\n3-column Deployment row with brand logo strips).\n\nThe default export shows an audience toggle above the diagram when\nneither ''variant'' nor ''content'' props are passed, so visitors can\nswitch between General and National Security views at read time. The\nexisting ''<IMEDiagram />'' call site in docs/main/index.mdx picks this\nup automatically.\n\nAlso adds ''scripts/render-ime.mjs'', a Playwright script that navigates\nto ''/?imeVariant=<id>&imeExport=1'' (a mode that hides the toggle) and\nscreenshots each variant to ''static/img/ime/<id>.png'', so marketing\ncan reuse the docs as the single source of truth for the infographic.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs(site): point IMEDiagram Advanced Information Controls at zero-trust\n\nThe Zero Trust security guide covers ABAC, ICAM, session enforcement,\nand dynamic policies — a much closer match to this cell''s bullets than\nthe generic security-guide index.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs(site): use real brand assets from FY27 sales deck in IMEDiagram mission variant\n\nExtracts icons and brand marks from slide 7 of the FY27 Platform Pitch\nSales Deck and wires them into the mission variant of the IMEDiagram:\n\n* Product-card icons (Messaging/Workflow/Audio/Project/Human-Machine\n  Teaming) — the marigold outline icons from the deck instead of the\n  generic inline SVGs.\n* Application client strip logos — Windows, macOS, Linux, iOS,\n  Android, Microsoft Teams.\n* Application supply-chain strip logos — PostgreSQL, Kubernetes,\n  React Native, GitHub, Go, Argo.\n* Deployment ''Enterprise to Edge with Sovereign AI'' cloud logos —\n  Azure, Oracle, AWS, GCP.\n* Deployment ''Layered Extensibility'' integration logos — GitHub,\n  GitLab, Jira, Confluence, Splunk.\n\nSchema changes:\n\n* ''Cell'' and ''Intro'' gain an optional ''iconSrc'' path; when set it\n  takes precedence over the named ''icon'' key. This keeps the general\n  variant''s inline SVG icons working while letting the mission variant\n  reference PNGs.\n* Renderer adds a small ''CellIcon'' helper that picks ''iconSrc'' vs.\n  the SVG icon.\n* Adds ''.iconImg'' / ''.introIconImg'' styles (larger 2rem/1.5rem to\n  match the deck''s baked-in padding) and tightens the ''.logoImg''\n  sizing so wordmarks (Oracle, AWS) don''t overwhelm the sentence\n  text next to them.\n\nAlso corrects a few strings on the mission variant to match the\ncanonical deck wording exactly (''Air-Gapped & Sovereign Deployment &\nIntegration'', ''Secure Federation & Interoperability'', ''Scales to 200K+\nconcurrent users'', ''NATO & US PL3, IL4/5, 6/7 proven'').\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs(site): add IME banner, widen to 16:9, and add remaining deck logos\n\nMatches the FY27 Platform Pitch deck (slide 7) more faithfully:\n\n* Blue camo banner with title + tagline replaces the plain text\n  header. Uses the deck''s own background image (banner-bg.jpg) with\n  a marigold underline for brand rhythm.\n* Diagram widens rightward on \\u2265 1200px viewports to hit the deck''s\n  native 1280x720 (16:9) dimensions. Uses ''--doc-sidebar-width'' so it\n  never overlaps the docs sidebar. This dramatically reduces the\n  vertical whitespace inside each cell (product cards no longer stack\n  tall).\n* Adds 14 more brand assets extracted from the same slide:\n  AI vendors (Meta, Mistral, Ask Sage, OpenAI, Elastic, Perplexity),\n  federation partners (MS Defender, MS Entra ID, Global Relay, Tines,\n  MS sync/devices), and misc (webhook, plus, generic-O federation\n  badge).\n* Populates the mission variant''s logo constellations to match the\n  deck: Interop \\u2192 Secure Federation cell gains a federation partner\n  strip, Deployment intro gains the AI vendor row (OpenAI, Meta,\n  Elastic, Perplexity, Ask Sage, Mistral), Deployment \\u2192 Layered\n  Extensibility grows to the full 9-logo mix.\n* Swaps intro icons for deck-branded PNGs: Applications gets the\n  MS sync/devices icon, Interop gets the MS Defender shield,\n  Deployment gets the Mattermost mark.\n\nSchema: ''Intro'' gains an optional ''logos'' field so intro columns can\ncarry their own decorative badge row (used by Deployment''s AI vendor\nconstellation). Renderer picks it up via the existing ''LogoStrip''.\n\nGeneral variant is unaffected \\u2014 it has no title/tagline so no banner\nrenders, and it doesn''t set ''iconSrc'' anywhere so it keeps the\ninline SVG icons.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Address CodeRabbit review on IME diagram\n\n- Reset .markdown h2 spacing and marigold ::before bar on .bannerTitle\n  so the landing-page global doesn''t distort the mission banner.\n- Resolve mission image and banner-bg paths through useBaseUrl so they\n  work under non-root Docusaurus deployments.\n- Normalize every variant source (prop, URL, activeId) through\n  getVariant and derive aria-selected from the resolved variant so the\n  toggle can''t diverge from the rendered diagram; suppress the toggle\n  entirely when the parent controls the variant/content.\n- Drive .cellGrid and .footerRow columns from --ime-cols with a\n  data-cols attribute, so tablet breakpoints keep single-column layers\n  single-column without an inline-style vs !important fight.\n- Add data-variant + data-ready on the diagram <section> and have\n  render-ime.mjs wait on the variant-specific selector instead of the\n  first ''[aria-label\\$=\\\"overview\\\"]'' match.\n- Declare playwright as a devDependency (with matching lockfile entries)\n  and add an ''npm run render:ime'' script.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Center IME diagram in the reading column; drop General variant\n\n- Align the wrapper to the text column on both sides (max-width: 1280px,\n  width: 100%, margin: 0 auto) instead of breaking out rightward. The\n  previous wide breakout made the diagram''s left match the text column\n  but overflowed only to the right, producing asymmetric margins.\n- Keep the General content module in the tree but remove it from the\n  toggle so only the mission variant renders. Rename its label to\n  ''Enterprise Advanced''. New variants can be re-added to the array as\n  they land.\n- Auto-hide the toggle whenever only one variant is registered so we\n  don''t render a single-option ''tab'' row.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Narrow IME intro column to reclaim tile width\n\nThe intro column (Zero Trust..., Accelerates..., Air-Gapped...) was\nsized fractionally (1.1fr : 3.4fr) which ate ~24% of the diagram\nwidth. Fix at 150px so the 6-tile Applications row gets ~90px per\ntile instead of ~85px, and shrink the intro h3 slightly (0.95rem →\n0.88rem) so the title still wraps cleanly in the narrower column.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Widen IME diagram + match deck icon placement\n\nWidth: restore the wider-than-text layout on desktop (>= 1200px).\nThe wrapper breaks out of the reading column and extends rightward\ninto the space Docusaurus reserves for a ToC. The landing page hides\nits ToC in frontmatter, so that space is empty; the diagram never\nextends leftward, so it never overlaps the docs sidebar. Capped at\n1280px and viewport-safe via min().\n\nIcons per FY27 Platform Pitch deck (slide 7):\n- Accelerates Classified & Mission Partner Operations intro: drop\n  the leading icon (deck shows plain title text).\n- Air-Gapped & Sovereign Deployment & Integration intro: drop the\n  leading icon and the AI-vendor constellation (OpenAI, Meta,\n  Elastic, Perplexity, Ask Sage, Mistral).\n- Enterprise to Edge with Sovereign AI cell: absorb the AI vendor\n  logos the intro was carrying (OpenAI, Meta, Elastic, Ask Sage,\n  Mattermost) plus ''Tactical Edge'' and ''Local Datacenter'' text\n  badges, sitting above the existing Azure/Oracle/AWS/GCP row.\n- Secure Federation & Interoperability cell: drop the logo strip\n  (MS Teams, Entra, Matrix, Global Relay). Deck shows bullets only.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Position IME cell logos to match deck layout\n\nSchema:\n- Cell.cornerLogos: array of small logos pinned to the top-right of a\n  cell via absolute positioning. Used for the AI-vendor and\n  integration constellations that sit in the corner of the deck.\n- Cell.logoLayout (''strip'' | ''grid'') + Cell.logoColumns: opt-in CSS\n  grid layout for the main logo list (Layered Extensibility uses\n  a 4-column grid rather than a flow strip).\n- Layer.columnsTemplate: explicit grid-template-columns override so\n  a row can carry uneven-width cards (Deployment row uses\n  ''1.2fr 1.1fr 0.9fr'' to mirror the deck).\n\nMission content (deck slide 7):\n- Enterprise-to-Edge: OpenAI, Meta, Elastic, Ask Sage, Mattermost\n  logos in the top-right corner; Tactical Edge / Local Datacenter\n  text badges + Azure/Oracle/AWS/GCP logos remain as the bottom\n  strip.\n- Layered Extensibility: Jira, GitHub, GitLab, MS Defender, Splunk\n  as corner logos; Confluence, MS Teams, MS Sync, MS Entra, Tines,\n  Argo, Webhook, plus icon in a 4-column grid below the bullets.\n\nRenderer/CSS:\n- .cell becomes a positioning context (position: relative).\n- .cornerLogos: absolute top-right constellation with pointer-events\n  disabled so it never intercepts card clicks.\n- .logoGrid: CSS grid driven by --ime-logo-cols.\n- LayerBlock honours columnsTemplate before falling back to the\n  --ime-cols count.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Rename IME ''mission'' variant to ''entadv''; drop dead general variant\n\n- Rename content/mission.ts -> content/entadv.ts via git mv so history\n  is preserved. Update the exported constant (mission -> entadv), the\n  IMEContent.id (''mission'' -> ''entadv''), the JSDoc header, and the\n  variant registry in content/index.ts. The audience label stays\n  ''Enterprise Advanced''.\n- Remove content/general.ts. It was kept as a scaffold when we\n  narrowed the toggle down to a single variant, but the file is dead\n  code today and reintroducing a ''General'' audience will need fresh\n  copy anyway.\n- Re-tune the Layered Extensibility logo constellation to match the\n  slide more closely: swap Microsoft Defender out of the corner in\n  favour of Element/Matrix (enterprise-o), and rebalance the 4-column\n  grid to Elastic / MS Defender / MS Teams / MS Entra / MS Sync /\n  Global Relay / Confluence / Add.\n- Update render-ime.mjs VARIANTS list and the JSDoc example.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Render Layered Extensibility grid beside its bullets (deck parity)\n\nThe deck''s Layered Extensibility card places the ecosystem logos as\na 4×3 grid next to the bullet list, not below it and not split into\na corner constellation plus a bottom strip.\n\n- Add Cell.bodyLayout (''stack'' | ''side-by-side''). Default is ''stack''\n  (previous behaviour); ''side-by-side'' wraps the text block and the\n  logo grid in a two-column .cellSplit grid inside the cell body.\n- Add matching .cellSplit CSS and tighten the .logoGrid gaps when\n  it''s rendering inside a split (half the horizontal room).\n- Retarget Layered Extensibility content: drop the cornerLogos array\n  and merge those five icons into the main logos list, bringing the\n  grid to 12 items (Jira, GitHub, GitLab, Element, Splunk, Elastic,\n  MS Defender, MS Teams, MS Entra, MS Sync, Global Relay, Add).\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Drop title icons from IME Interoperability + Deployment cells\n\nThe source slide renders these cards as plain title + bullets; the\nmarigold SVG icons we were adding above each title (lock, users,\nserver, plug, shield) don''t exist on the deck. Removing them from\nAdvanced Information Controls, Secure Federation & Interoperability,\nEnterprise to Edge with Sovereign AI, Layered Extensibility, and\nHigh Availability & Scale.\n\nUse Cases + Applications rows keep their leading icons — those DO\nappear on the slide, and the Applications tiles use brand-mark PNGs\n(iconSrc) rather than the generic SVG registry.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Fix IME variant/toggle desync when URL preselects a variant\n\nPreviously, ?imeVariant=<id> both seeded activeId AND was stashed on\nurlOverride.variant, which then permanently won the resolve chain\n(variant ?? urlOverride.variant ?? activeId). Clicking a toggle tab\nmutated activeId but never affected what rendered, so the toggle\nlooked non-functional whenever the URL had picked a variant.\n\nDrop urlOverride.variant from state and let the URL seed activeId\nonce inside the useEffect. The resolve chain becomes\n(variant ?? activeId), so tab clicks take over from there.\nRenamed the remaining urlOverride.hideToggle to a boolean state for\nclarity.\n\nLatent today (only one variant is registered) but breaks the moment\na second variant lands.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME Applications tiles: center-align, underline product names, drop stray bold\n\nMatch the source slide for the Applications row:\n\n- Introduce `Cell.bodyLead`, an optional leading term rendered\n  underlined immediately before `body` (e.g. \"Channels\" in\n  \"Channels: ChatOps and automation\"). Applications cells split\n  their body copy into `bodyLead` + `body` so the product name gets\n  the deck''s underline treatment.\n- Center-align icon, title, and body copy in `.layer_applications`\n  tiles only. Use Cases and Deployment cards keep left-aligned\n  reading rhythm.\n- Force `.cellText` to `font-weight: 400` so nothing inherits bold\n  from surrounding markdown context; only `.cellTitle` stays bold.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME Interoperability cells: enlarged title on the left, bullets on the right\n\nMatch the source slide for the two Interoperability tiles (Advanced\nInformation Controls, Secure Federation & Interoperability):\n\n- Add `Cell.titlePlacement` (''top'' default | ''left''). When ''left'',\n  the cell body is a two-column grid: enlarged title in the left\n  column, body/bullets in the right.\n- Renderer emits a `.cellTitleSplit` wrapper for `titlePlacement:''left''`\n  cells; scoped `.cellTitleLeft .cellTitle` bumps the title to the\n  deck''s ~1.1rem size.\n- Interoperability content flips both cells to `titlePlacement:''left''`\n  and drops the (now-unused) leading icon.\n- Narrow-viewport fallback stacks title above bullets.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME Interoperability: center the title within its left column\n\nThe title was hugging the top-left of its column against the tall\nbullet list on the right. Set the aside to stretch to the row height\nand center its contents both axes, matching the deck.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME Interoperability: left-align title horizontally, keep vertical centering\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME Use Cases: drop leading icons, enlarge titles to match deck\n\nThe source slide''s Use Cases row has no leading icons and its titles\nread as the largest per-tile heading. Drop the shield/code/compass\nicons from all three cells and bump .layer_use-cases .cellTitle to\n1.15rem.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: match deck copy for Enterprise-to-Edge body\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Address CodeRabbit review: install chromium + wait for asset decode\n\n- npm script ''render:ime'' now runs ''playwright install chromium'' first\n  so a fresh checkout renders without a manual setup step (idempotent —\n  skipped when the browser is already downloaded).\n- render-ime.mjs waits for every <img> in the target section to load +\n  decode, and probes CSS background-image URLs (banner backdrop, etc.)\n  the same way, before screenshotting. data-ready fires as soon as\n  React commits the variant but images may still be decoding; without\n  this wait the exported PNG can be missing icons/logos/backgrounds.\n\nSkipped CodeRabbit findings that were already handled:\n- ''Resolve image paths against baseUrl'' — every image goes through the\n  <Img> helper (useBaseUrl) in index.tsx: CellIcon, IntroPanel,\n  LogoStrip, cornerLogos, and BannerHeader.\n- ''Toggle should change URL-selected variant'' — fixed in 152360aefb;\n  the URL now only seeds activeId on mount.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: drop Zero Trust icon and enlarge intro titles to fill the column\n\nApplications intro no longer renders the ms-sync icon (deck has no\nleading icon on any intro). Bumped .intro h3 from 0.88rem to 1.05rem\nso the three intro blocks fill the fixed 150px column instead of\nleaving a stripe of whitespace below.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: raise responsive-collapse breakpoint to match wrapper breakout\n\nThe wrapper breaks out of the reading column at >= 1200px, but the\ncollapse fallback only kicked in at <= 980px. Viewports in the\n981-1199px gap tried to render the full 6-tile grid + intro column\ninside a cramped ~700px reading column, so titles and body copy\noverlapped (visible with the docs sidebar open on ~1050px screens).\n\nRaise the breakpoint to 1199px so any viewport that doesn''t get the\nbreakout gets the 2-col fallback + stacked intro + stacked Interop\ntitle/bullets.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: fit within reading column + match deck copy on Use Cases\n\n- Wrapper: drop the >= 1200px breakout; the diagram now sits inside\n  the reading column, capped at 1280px. Add container-type: inline-size\n  so collapse triggers on wrapper width rather than viewport width.\n- Responsive: swap @media (max-width: 1199px) for @container\n  (max-width: 900px) — same collapse behavior but keyed to the\n  container so narrow reading columns (e.g. pages with a visible ToC)\n  collapse the same way narrow viewports do. Added !important on the\n  container-query grid-template-columns overrides so the Deployment\n  layer''s inline columnsTemplate still yields at narrow widths.\n- Use Cases copy trimmed to match the deck word-for-word.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: restore controlled breakout to recover the deck''s 16:9 ratio\n\nFitting the wrapper strictly to the reading column produced a\n~1.05:1 layout because Interoperability bullets wrapped tall. Bring\nback the breakout at >= 1300px viewports, capped at min(1280px,\nviewport - sidebar - gutters) so it never overlaps the sidebar and\nnever grows past the deck''s native width. Container query for\ncollapse stays in place, so narrow reading columns still collapse\ngracefully.\n\nResult on a 1728px viewport: 1280 x 750 (1.71:1) vs slide''s 1.78:1.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: drop unused SVG icons, strip entadv comments, retarget Agents\n\nKeep only the star glyph still referenced by Future Applications; point\nthe Agents tile at the admin agents guide.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: trim horizontal + vertical whitespace, cap wrapper at 1200px\n\nDiagram overflowed rightward more than needed and had extra padding\nthroughout. Trim proportionally so the ratio stays deck-shaped\n(~1.69:1 vs slide 1.78:1) with a smaller footprint.\n\n- Wrapper cap 1280 -> 1200 (breakout right edge shifts 80px inward).\n- Layer body padding 0.9rem 1rem -> 0.55rem 0.85rem.\n- Banner padding 1rem 1.5rem -> 0.7rem 1.25rem.\n- Banner title 1.6rem -> 1.4rem; tagline 0.9rem -> 0.82rem.\n- Intro column 150px -> 135px; intro h3 1.05rem -> 0.98rem.\n- Cell padding 0.6rem 0.7rem -> 0.5rem 0.6rem; cell gap 0.35rem -> 0.3rem.\n- .cellGrid gap 0.5rem -> 0.4rem.\n- .layerContentWithIntro gap 0.85rem -> 0.7rem.\n\nAt 1728px viewport: was 1280 x 750, now 1200 x 708. 42px shorter,\n80px narrower, wrapper right edge x=1612 -> 1532.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: grow banner, close visible white gap under it\n\nThe .layer_use-cases .layerBody top padding read as a visible white\nframe between the marigold banner border and the tinted (denim-50)\nUse Cases cells, while the same padding at the bottom of Deployment\nblended invisibly into its white cells. Geometry was symmetric, only\nthe perception was asymmetric.\n\n- .layer_use-cases .layerBody padding-top 0.55rem -> 0.2rem so the\n  first tinted row sits right under the marigold border.\n- .banner padding 0.7rem -> 1rem vertically to absorb the reclaimed\n  height.\n- Banner title 1.4rem -> 1.55rem, tagline 0.82rem -> 0.88rem so the\n  taller banner reads as intentional weight, not extra chrome.\n\nAt 1728px viewport: banner 73 -> 88, top-gap-below-banner 10 -> 4,\ndiagram 708 -> 724, ratio 1.69 -> 1.66.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: revert Use Cases top-padding trim, keep enlarged banner\n\nThe zero-gap look under the marigold border read as cramped. Restore\nthe standard .layerBody top padding on Use Cases (0.55rem) so the\ntinted tiles get their breathing room back. The banner keeps its\nenlarged size from the previous commit.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: trim Use Cases top padding to 0.35rem (7px gap under banner)\n\nMiddle ground between the too-tight 0.2rem (4px) and the too-loose\ndefault 0.55rem (10px). The tinted Use Cases tiles no longer read as\nfloating in a large white frame below the marigold rule, but keep\nenough breathing room to not look cramped.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: shrink layerLabel vertical padding so short lanes stop stretching\n\nThe extra ~28px of whitespace below the Use Cases tiles wasn''t from\n.layerBody padding — it was the vertical layerLabel (''USE CASES'')\ndemanding ~103px of row height (writing-mode: vertical-rl + heavy\nletter-spacing + padding: 0.85rem 0). Grid stretched the tile body\nto match, showing up as a big buffer below the tiles.\n\nTrim label padding to 0.15rem and letter-spacing 0.22em -> 0.18em so\nshort lanes size to their content instead of the label. Use Cases\ngap-above-tiles/gap-below-tiles is now 6px/8px (was 6px/34px).\nDiagram height at 1728px viewport: 724 -> 698.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: match deck 16:9 ratio, small banner bump\n\nBump wrapper cap 1200 -> 1240 and banner vertical padding\n1rem -> 1.1rem. At 1728px viewport the diagram is now 1240x701 =\n1.769:1, essentially matching the slide''s 1.778:1. Banner grew from\n88 -> 91px.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* IME: fix phone breakpoint losing to container-query !important\n\nThe @container (max-width: 900px) rule uses\n''.cellGrid:not([data-cols=\"1\"]) { ... !important }'' to force multi-\ncolumn layers into 2 columns. That out-specificity''d the phone rule\n''.cellGrid { grid-template-columns: 1fr }'', so multi-column grids\nstayed 2-column at phone widths.\n\nMatch specificity + add !important on the phone selector for both\n.cellGrid and .footerRow. Verified at viewport 500px: all four\ngrids (data-cols 3, 6, 2, custom) now render as a single column.\n\nAddresses CodeRabbit review comment #4098042300.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Move IMEDiagram to asset-only icons; swap star to inline SVG\n\n- Delete icons.tsx SVG registry and IconName type; content modules now\n  reference icons purely via iconSrc.\n- Add /img/ime/logos/star.svg (marigold, transparent) for the\n  Future Applications tile; drop the SVG-specific CSS branches for\n  .icon, .introIcon, and .footerIcon.\n- Prune icon fields from Cell, Intro, and FooterStrip in types.ts and\n  simplify CellIcon, IntroPanel, and FooterCell accordingly.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Refresh render-ime.mjs setup notes\n\nPlaywright is now a direct devDependency and the render:ime npm script\nruns ''playwright install chromium'' before the render, so a fresh\ncheckout no longer needs the old ''npm i -D playwright'' instructions.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Switch IMEDiagram star to outlined stroke\n\nFilled marigold read as an off-tone accent next to the other tile\nicons. Match the previous SVG style: stroked marigold outline, no fill.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Match star.svg color to sibling icons\n\nStar was too yellow (#FFBC1F) next to the sparkle icon\n(Human-Machine Teaming), which renders as warm gold #D5A130.\nMatch that tone.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Restore brand logo legibility in IMEDiagram dark mode\n\nDark surfaces were swallowing near-black brand marks (GitHub, OpenAI,\nSplunk, Mattermost, React Native, Plus). Two scoped fixes:\n\n- footer strips: white background with denim text in dark mode\n  (mirrors the deck, which paints these strips white regardless of\n  surrounding tone).\n- brand logos on non-strip surfaces (corner logos, logo grids,\n  intro strips): small white chip so dark marks retain contrast on\n  the near-black cell background.\n\nLight mode is unaffected.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Fix IMEDiagram dark-mode brand icon legibility and alignment\n\nDark surfaces were swallowing near-black brand marks (GitHub, OpenAI,\nSplunk, Mattermost, React Native, Plus, Ask Sage, Meta) across three\ncarrier types: footer strips, corner logos on tiles, and the 3×4\nlogo matrix on Layered Extensibility.\n\n- Wrap each brand mark in a soft-grey chip (#e6e8ec) in dark mode.\n  Uses border-box padding so strip and grid dimensions stay identical\n  to light mode.\n- Tighten the chip padding for the dense 3×4 grid and the tiny\n  corner logos so the brand mark isn''t crowded out.\n- Drop the logoStrip top margin inside footer strips — it was intended\n  for stacking-context use in intro columns and pushed the icons ~7px\n  below the text baseline in the horizontal strip layout.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtjwfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaSkQAIN9uXJ17l7j+sGe2JmYXimS\nSGuJXt/gb8DDiEyYwV4+XTH2TZcRMoqiYJlH/8c9N9lItm7Y7e/loRxenksXih6A\ncvwqSPDjYd64XsWV8db6uiZ98kP/2D8y+7NcNtvSLlPcqqrERmmHNvVeDF3iy1wy\nl