s{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/8559de7c5e41bfd60d5cf6afd1e7a9bab5d5c6af/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T18:44:57Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T18:44:57Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"chore: release v4.2.0\n\n* (@GermanBluefox) `npm run build:ts` no longer needs the optional `mysql2` and `sqlite3` drivers to be installed\n* (@GermanBluefox) Fixed buffered values being lost when the adapter stops, and unload no longer hangs when there is nothing else to write (#577)\n* (@GermanBluefox) `getCounter` no longer reads the NULL boundary marker that `writeNulls` stores on start and stop as a zero counter value (#577)\n* (@GermanBluefox) Fixed \"Test connection\" reporting a failure for a working configuration: the request was built as a text template that could produce invalid JSON, and it left out `dbname`, `doNotCreateDatabase` and the docker settings (#355)\n* (@GermanBluefox) \"Record changes only\" now compares the value instead of the controller''s last-change timestamp, so an alias with a read converter no longer stores a row per source change (#295)\n* (@GermanBluefox) Added a statistics tab listing every logged ID with its number of values and estimated size (#247)\n* (@GermanBluefox) Added a cleanup for datapoints that are no longer logged, with a confirmation dialog showing what would be deleted (#247)\n* (@GermanBluefox) The `Counter must have type \"number\"` error now names the datapoint and is logged once instead of for every value (#320)\n* (@DutchmanNL) PostgreSQL: \"do not create database\" now connects straight to the configured database instead of opening the maintenance database `postgres` first, so roles without `CONNECT` on it can be used\n* (@GermanBluefox) MySQL can now connect through a unix socket instead of host and port (#104)\n* (@DutchmanNL) Fixed `info.connection` staying `true` while the database was unreachable\n* (@GermanBluefox) Fixed crash (UNCAUGHT_EXCEPTION) when the database server closes the connection: the driver''s `error` event had no listener (#527)\n* (@GermanBluefox) A connection that the server dropped is now replaced instead of being handed out again","tree":{"sha":"5aafd13449138c169e39ae8a297aab077610365f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/trees/5aafd13449138c169e39ae8a297aab077610365f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/commits/8559de7c5e41bfd60d5cf6afd1e7a9bab5d5c6af","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/8559de7c5e41bfd60d5cf6afd1e7a9bab5d5c6af","node_id":"C_kwDOAsJ71NoAKDg1NTlkZTdjNWU0MWJmZDYwZDVjZjZhZmQxZTdhOWJhYjVkNWM2YWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/9b13324f0c4385ed4276d10c65d29c1cae6f927d","sha":"9b13324f0c4385ed4276d10c65d29c1cae6f927d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/9b13324f0c4385ed4276d10c65d29c1cae6f927d"}],"sha":"8559de7c5e41bfd60d5cf6afd1e7a9bab5d5c6af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/8559de7c5e41bfd60d5cf6afd1e7a9bab5d5c6af"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/9b13324f0c4385ed4276d10c65d29c1cae6f927d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T18:28:29Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T18:28:29Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"CLAUDE.md: correct the build, install and release-config facts\n\nFour statements had gone stale and one of them contradicted another part\nof the same file:\n\n- `npm run build` was described as plain `tsc`. It is\n  `build:ts && build:admin` and has been since 9455b55, so it builds the\n  admin component too.\n- \"the release script does not do it\" was wrong for the same reason:\n  `.releaseconfig.json` runs `npm run build` in `before_commit`, which\n  the \"Build before testing\" paragraph already said correctly.\n- `npm run npm:admin` does not exist; the script is called `npm` and\n  installs the root and the src-admin dependencies.\n- The layer overview predates `src/lib/optional-drivers.ts`.\n\nAdded three things this repository had to learn the hard way:\n\n- The build must not depend on the optional drivers either. A literal\n  `import(''sqlite3'')` makes tsc resolve the package, so a runner that\n  skipped the optional dependency fails with TS2307 - which is what took\n  out adapter-tests-sqlite on macOS.\n- `exec` commands in `.releaseconfig.json` run without a shell, so `&&`\n  does not chain and ends up as arguments to the first command. That is\n  how `before_check` produced\n  \"TS5042: Option ''project'' cannot be mixed with source files\".\n- A `node_modules` in a parent directory makes npm drop packages it can\n  resolve from there out of the local tree and the lockfile, and lets\n  lint report errors from a foreign version of a shared dependency.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bae9f98081b3c8817402f9b24b565b2df6fb36d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/trees/bae9f98081b3c8817402f9b24b565b2df6fb36d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/commits/9b13324f0c4385ed4276d10c65d29c1cae6f927d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/9b13324f0c4385ed4276d10c65d29c1cae6f927d","node_id":"C_kwDOAsJ71NoAKDliMTMzMjRmMGM0Mzg1ZWQ0Mjc2ZDEwYzY1ZDI5YzFjYWU2ZjkyN2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/03e717f9df75ebed221af734a60c0e69a4068346","sha":"03e717f9df75ebed221af734a60c0e69a4068346","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/03e717f9df75ebed221af734a60c0e69a4068346"}],"sha":"9b13324f0c4385ed4276d10c65d29c1cae6f927d","url":"https://api.githu