://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/4fcc211a183e6e09fea9d5c1ec29fb216cc2af30","node_id":"C_kwDOAsJ71NoAKDRmY2MyMTFhMTgzZTZlMDlmZWE5ZDVjMWVjMjlmYjIxNmNjMmFmMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/5672156fd61f6bfad3f89c5e5b6922e97591d1e0","sha":"5672156fd61f6bfad3f89c5e5b6922e97591d1e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/5672156fd61f6bfad3f89c5e5b6922e97591d1e0"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/b68990c1658141d98c46bed10c2456097c5c2bd9","sha":"b68990c1658141d98c46bed10c2456097c5c2bd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/b68990c1658141d98c46bed10c2456097c5c2bd9"}],"sha":"4fcc211a183e6e09fea9d5c1ec29fb216cc2af30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/4fcc211a183e6e09fea9d5c1ec29fb216cc2af30"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/b68990c1658141d98c46bed10c2456097c5c2bd9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T18:26:09Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T18:26:09Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"Name the datapoint in the counter type error (#320)\n\n`Counter must have type \"number\"!` said nothing about which datapoint it meant.\nOne reporter searched for the misconfigured one for over a year, and a second\nconfirmed the same. The message now carries the ID and the type the datapoint\nactually has, and says what to change:\n\n  Counter must have type \"number\", but \"modbus.5.inputRegisters.30536_Quelle\"\n  is stored as \"String\". Change the storage type of this datapoint to \"Number\",\n  or switch the counter option off.\n\nIt is also logged once per datapoint instead of once per value. The repetition\nwas half of the problem - the screenshot in the issue is a wall of the same\nline - and adding the ID without throttling would only have made that wall\nwider.\n\nTwo warnings in the same path had the same flaw and the ID right at hand:\n`No Connection to database` in prepareTaskCheckTypeAndDbId() and in\n#readIdIndexAndType() now say which datapoint could not be stored or looked up.\n\nThe text is built by counterTypeMismatch() in src/lib/errors.ts rather than\ninline, so it can be unit tested without importing main.ts - which pulls in\n@iobroker/adapter-core and exits when js-controller cannot be resolved. Covered\nin test/testErrors.js, which the CI unit list already runs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a33f909352b2d81d4ca8dbbaaddd8a06c67a7ba7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/trees/a33f909352b2d81d4ca8dbbaaddd8a06c67a7ba7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/commits/b68990c1658141d98c46bed10c2456097c5c2bd9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/b68990c1658141d98c46bed10c2456097c5c2bd9","node_id":"C_kwDOAsJ71NoAKGI2ODk5MGMxNjU4MTQxZDk4YzQ2YmVkMTBjMjQ1NjA5N2M1YzJiZDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/5672156fd61f6bfad3f89c5e5b6922e97591d1e0","sha":"5672156fd61f6bfad3f89c5e5b6922e97591d1e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/5672156fd61f6bfad3f89c5e5b6922e97591d1e0"}],"sha":"b68990c1658141d98c46bed10c2456097c5c2bd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/b68990c1658141d98c46bed10c2456097c5c2bd9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/26466cb2ab9f8551c7fef606f45594c9dac05d3f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T18:21:28Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T18:21:28Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"Add a statistics tab and a cleanup for datapoints that are no longer logged (#247)\n\nYears of enabling and deleting states leave a SQL database full of values\nnobody can reach any more - the reporter had over a million. Until now the only\nway to find and remove them was a forum script.\n\nAdapter side, two new messages:\n\n- `getDpStatistics` returns one row per ID in the `datapoints` table with its\n  storage type, exact number of values, oldest and newest timestamp, an\n  estimated size and a status, plus totals. It costs one `GROUP BY id` and one\n  size query per time series table rather than one query per datapoint, because\n  a long-running database holds thousands of IDs.\n- `cleanupOrphaned` removes the values of orphaned datapoints. Without\n  `confirm: true` it deletes nothing and only reports what a confirmed run\n  would remove, so the dialog can show the list and the counts first. Both\n  messages share one collection routine, so the preview and the deletion cannot\n  disagree about what is orphaned.\n\nThe status deliberately separates two cases that the request lumped together.\nA state that no longer exists in ioBroker cannot be charted by anyone, so\ndropping its history is safe and that is the default. A state that still exists\nbut has logging switched off is different: its history is reachable and may be\nwanted on purpose, so it is only included when the caller asks for it\nexplicitly, and the dialog warns about it.\n\nCleanup deletes from every `ts_*` table, not only the one the stored type\nsuggests: a datapoint whose storage type was changed over the years has rows in\nmore than one. It also removes the `datapoints` row, otherwise the ID would\nkeep appearing in the statistics with zero values.\n\nThree new SQL builders per dialect: `getIdCounts`, `getTableSize` and\n`deleteDatapoint`.\n\nAbout the size column: no SQL dialect can report the bytes of a single\ndatapoint, so it is the row count multiplied by the average row width the\ndatabase reports - MySQL `information_schema`, PostgreSQL\n`pg_total_relation_size`/`reltuples`, MS SQL `dm_db_partition_stats`, SQLite\n`dbstat`. It is labelled as an estimate throughout, and when a width cannot be\ndetermined - `dbstat` is not in every sqlite3 build, a restricted role may not\nreach the catalog - the answer carries null rather than a fabricated number,\nand a total that would be partial is null too.\n\nAdmin side: a `Statistics` panel holding a sortable, filterable table with the\nsummary, and a Clean up button that runs the dry run first and opens a\nconfirmation dialog listing every affected ID with its counts.\n\nTests: test/testStatistics.js, 17 cases, in the CI unit list. The pure helpers\nlive in src/lib/statistics.ts rather than main.ts so they are reachable without\nimporting @iobroker/adapter-core. The SQL is additionally exercised against a\nreal SQLite database, including a datapoint with rows in two tables, to show\nthat the cleanup empties both and leaves the surviving datapoint untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0d570c1bea9ebe3c78556e6a677c06d867a6c5c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/trees/0d570c1bea9ebe3c78556e6a677c06d867a6c5c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/commits/26466cb2ab9f8551c7fef606f45594c9dac05d3f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.