om/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/e3307df68888bc2331bb61cc678b41cd5a64ab2c"}],"sha":"96f14b7bbd3dc3c822218e92d9c1c72a0b2cd0f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/96f14b7bbd3dc3c822218e92d9c1c72a0b2cd0f9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/7cb39f1fd913784901826006a3a227941a6c2076/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T14:41:01Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T14:41:01Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"Make the processMessage guard testable in CI\n\ntest/testProcessMessage.js, added with #563, never ran in CI. It drove\nSqlAdapter.prototype.processMessage directly, which meant requiring\nbuild/main.js - and that pulls in @iobroker/adapter-core, whose module body\ncalls process.exit(10) when js-controller cannot be resolved. js-controller is\nnot a dependency of this repository; the integration suite installs it into\ntmp/ at runtime. So the file could only ever pass on a machine that had already\nrun the integration tests, and adding it to the CI unit list would have killed\nmocha instead. It was marked local-only in #565 as a stopgap.\n\nThe decision now lives in src/lib/messages.ts, which imports nothing:\nguardUninitialized(command, dialectKnown) returns either the response to answer\nwith or null, so both the command set and the answer shape are reachable from a\nplain unit test. processMessage() keeps only the three lines that log, send and\nreturn.\n\nThat split leaves one thing the pure function cannot see - the guard being\ndropped from processMessage() altogether. A second test asserts against the\ncompiled build/main.js that the call exists and precedes the command dispatch.\nIt matches a call pattern rather than the bare identifier, so an import alone\ndoes not satisfy it; removing the call from the compiled output makes it fail.\n\nAlso drops the `module.exports.SqlAdapter` export added in #563. Its only\nconsumer was the test that is gone, so the public surface goes back to the\ncompact-mode factory alone.\n\ntest/testMessageGuard.js replaces test/testProcessMessage.js and is in the CI\nunit list. The whole list was run in a worktree that has no tmp/, i.e. with\njs-controller unresolvable exactly as in CI: 142 passing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1456240f1653ee26f92ce86e0481a1332cfd2956","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/trees/1456240f1653ee26f92ce86e0481a1332cfd2956"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/commits/7cb39f1fd913784901826006a3a227941a6c2076","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/7cb39f1fd913784901826006a3a227941a6c2076","node_id":"C_kwDOAsJ71NoAKDdjYjM5ZjFmZDkxMzc4NDkwMTgyNjAwNmEzYTIyNzk0MWE2YzIwNzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/91d55b65292f54ca4fc9e731f781a70bf4137a3d","sha":"91d55b65292f54ca4fc9e731f781a70bf4137a3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/91d55b65292f54ca4fc9e731f781a70bf4137a3d"}],"sha":"7cb39f1fd913784901826006a3a227941a6c2076","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/7cb39f1fd913784901826006a3a227941a6c2076"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/e3307df68888bc2331bb61cc678b41cd5a64ab2c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T14:31:47Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T14:31:47Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"Add the missing English translation keys and fix a copied panel label\n\nThe adapter checker reports W5612 for jsonConfig keys that have no entry in\nadmin/i18n/en.json. Its output listed 10; walking both config files for every\ntranslatable attribute (label, help, text, title, tooltip, placeholder, desc,\nlabelTrue/False, ok, cancel, honouring noTranslation) found 15. The five it did\nnot name are \"Please confirm\", \"Root password\", \"Root URL\", \"Defines the root\nURL, ...\" and \"Grafana Docker\".\n\nTwo of them were not translation gaps:\n\n- The phpMyAdmin panel was labelled \"Grafana Docker\", copied from another\n  adapter - the panel holds dockerPhpMyAdmin.* fields and its counterpart is\n  called \"MySQL Docker\". Translating it as-is would have cemented the wrong\n  name, so the label itself is corrected to \"phpMyAdmin Docker\".\n- \"docker_explanation\" was an unresolved snake_case placeholder used as the\n  help of the Docker checkbox, so it got real prose instead of being mirrored.\n\nThe keys were missing from every language, not only English, so these panels\nwent in without any translation at all. Only en.json is touched here; Weblate\nowns the rest and fans out from English.\n\nThe data browser needs nothing: all 22 I18n.t() keys in src-admin resolve\nagainst src-admin/src/i18n/en.json.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"74cda098e73aa884b15b4c2f518682728f45e61f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/trees/74cda098e73aa884b15b4c2f518682728f45e61f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/commits/e3307df68888bc2331bb61cc678b41cd5a64ab2c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/e3307df68888bc2331bb61cc678b41cd5a64ab2c","node_id":"C_kwDOAsJ71NoAKGUzMzA3ZGY2ODg4OGJjMjMzMWJiNjFjYzY3OGI0MWNkNWE2NGFiMmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/91d55b65292f54ca4fc9e731f781a70bf4137a3d","sha":"91d55b65292f54ca4fc9e731f781a70bf4137a3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/91d55b65292f54ca4fc9e731f781a70bf4137a3d"}],"sha":"e3307df68888bc2331bb61cc678b41cd5a64ab2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/e3307df68888bc2331bb61cc678b41cd5a64ab2c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/4724644c60d87ee6916f8f10a9d5516bdb31ca53/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T11:50:21Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T11:50:21Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"CI: run every test/testPostgreSQL*.js, not only testPostgreSQL.js\n\nThe Postgres job named one exact file, so testPostgreSQLNoCreateDb.js added by\nthis PR would never have been executed - the same gap that kept\ntest/testSqlClient.js out of CI until #565. A glob picks up new files instead;\nalphabetical order puts testPostgreSQL.js first.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"95cbb0e44b931d0e5f99bfddcc664cc7b1d7b31d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/trees/95cbb0e44b931d0e5f99bfddcc664cc7b1d7b31d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/commits/4724644c60d87ee6916f8f10a9d5516bdb31ca53","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/4724644c60d87ee6916f8f10a9d5516bdb31ca53","node_id":"C_kwDOAsJ71NoAKDQ3MjQ2NDRjNjBkODdlZTY5MTZmOGYxMGE5ZDU1MTZiZGIzMWNhNTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/42ee1f83b2bcc270cd705bf175188654f83e16f8","sha":"42ee1f83b2bcc270cd705bf175188654f83e16f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/42ee1f83b2bcc270cd705bf175188654f83e16f8"}],"sha":"4724644c60d87ee6916f8f10a9d5516bdb31ca53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/4724644c60d87ee6916f8f10a9d5516bdb31ca53"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7318445?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DutchmanNL","id":7318445,"login":"DutchmanNL","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMTg0NDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/42ee1f83b2bcc270cd705bf175188654f83e16f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T23:35:29Z","email":"drozda.apple@icloud.com","name":"DutchmanNL"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T11:49:37Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"Connect directly to the configured PostgreSQL database when told not to create it\n\nThe two-phase PostgreSQL connect always opened the maintenance database\n\"postgres\" first. With \"do not create database\" set it connected there,\ndid nothing, disconnected and reconnected - so the option avoided the\nCREATE DATABASE, but not the connection that needs privileges nobody grants\non a managed PostgreSQL.\n\nA role without CONNECT on \"postgres\" therefore never reached its own\ndatabase at all: the first phase was refused with 42501 and the adapter\nlooped on the 30 s reconnect forever (#404). That is also what makes the\nSupabase request in #481 fail on the normal postgresql dbtype.\n\nWith the option set, connect() now skips the maintenance phase entirely.\nThe default path is unchanged. Table creation is unaffected either way:\ninit() only ever returns CREATE TABLE statements and runs against the\nconfigured database, tolerating tables that already exist.\n\nThe admin \"Test connection\" button had the same hardcoded database, which\nis the actual defect behind #285 - it reported a failure for a perfectly\ngood configuration. It now tests the configured database when the option\nis set.\n\nAdds test/testPostgreSQLNoCreateDb.js, which builds the situation it\nguards: a role with no CONNECT on \"postgres\" and a pre-existing database of\nits own. It asserts the adapter connects, creates its six tables in the\nconfigured database and round-trips a value. On the unfixed code it fails\nwith \"permission denied for database postgres\" and the adapter never\nconnects.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"77524dd17600fb848acab8122ce2ef1a3d7bef08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/trees/77524dd17600fb848acab8122ce2ef1a3d7bef08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/commits/42ee1f83b2bcc270cd705bf175188654f83e16f8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/42ee1f83b2bcc270cd705bf175188654f83e16f8","node_id":"C_kwDOAsJ71NoAKDQyZWUxZjgzYjJiY2MyNzBjZDcwNWJmMTc1MTg4NjU0ZjgzZTE2Zjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/91d55b65292f54ca4fc9e731f781a70bf4137a3d","sha":"91d55b65292f54ca4fc9e731f781a70bf4137a3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/91d55b65292f54ca4fc9e731f781a70bf4137a3d"}],"sha":"42ee1f83b2bcc270cd705bf175188654f83e16f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/42ee1f83b2bcc270cd705bf175188654f83e16f8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/91d55b65292f54ca4fc9e731f781a70bf4137a3d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T11:48:36Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"Bluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T11:48:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Merge pull request #565 from ioBroker/feat/mysql-unix-socket\n\nAdd support for MySQL unix sockets (#104)","tree":{"sha":"6f9e55b9c4e887b10bdfc95e12ca9c1371fcdca8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/trees/6f9e55b9c4e887b10bdfc95e12ca9c1371fcdca8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/commits/91d55b65292f54ca4fc9e731f781a70bf4137a3d","verification":{"payload":"tree 6f9e55b9c4e887b10bdfc95e12ca9c1371fcdca8\nparent fef4a91eda11ff3f5af29081b841f81a9f05ce53\nparent 2031caea7ba72119c4b0a04e9b03bdbc65853ff6\nauthor Bluefox <dogafox@gmail.com> 1790941716 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790941716 +0300\n\nMerge pull request #565 from ioBroker/feat/mysql-unix-socket\n\nAdd support for MySQL unix sockets (#104)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv5oUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmMoQAGEJ913rtghSooBTbq1o95Y9\nVgsbuhoUpzmpDPuVobpi/eKhV0k/Jitf0SlHed1pgZGp4eTlE7H7CJZ+Ehp4vKD6\nyhnlR3F6i1Odbd+jgo/qK+Wi/RubCDTrTpZzZw8qFbYJvQr8qz2dGW+ok505CtQG\nRqYHZ15Rp8kAkY+z1QxBxOtSC13NoTNPW5V6mB2SN18jGtMiPB75+eUEun9bvtsb\n5vu4PSy4iMDLYjDmbvr4IwtYptiKeDh+ngY0aQY+uCZ8fnOlsSFJhON3Sp57GeQo\ngMqpYWsnsva/kp/jwpAs0XnGWKGrBitPPgccKyv/kYWFrPlQ3CsSkdSBqNubbNTk\nmsZBU2s8ThXuhV/QT7qqGuqOEWAJlPNaw73vne0Bg4YwVyICm3LyRsT8fZWba2c8\nbAyyceLsm7gDnp4S27TcRdiH2FtpSz9S9Vd0n5UGGVPEmIsOd2AQ6DoSDOaPwJHt\nyNPZslg57eBbtOlQhULs2YuEY9Oc6PoLYr6pSbUz4EBxKTUc0dos5anw62rrVUi2\nifB2/xDKEJpkglrdpcLJckDPGxOoCAYb+8KeFOwb7bs8np+CSoElWXfB9vR2Nlzv\nEhJUTgJsY+x2oLeRrRqW1osidO/g3OOocrpBCY43VxTuJS0c7MNM5mNZxzqoJ5i5\n/ubOX7QwOe6bQL8uY3lP\n=2+YF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T11:48:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/91d55b65292f54ca4fc9e731f781a70bf4137a3d","node_id":"C_kwDOAsJ71NoAKDkxZDU1YjY1MjkyZjU0Y2E0ZmM5ZTczMWY3ODFhNzBiZjQxMzdhM2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/fef4a91eda11ff3f5af29081b841f81a9f05ce53","sha":"fef4a91eda11ff3f5af29081b841f81a9f05ce53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/fef4a91eda11ff3f5af29081b841f81a9f05ce53"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/2031caea7ba72119c4b0a04e9b03bdbc65853ff6","sha":"2031caea7ba72119c4b0a04e9b03bdbc65853ff6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/2031caea7ba72119c4b0a04e9b03bdbc65853ff6"}],"sha":"91d55b65292f54ca4fc9e731f781a70bf4137a3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/91d55b65292f54ca4fc9e731f781a70bf4137a3d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/2031caea7ba72119c4b0a04e9b03bdbc65853ff6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T09:33:49Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T11:31:15Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"Add support for MySQL unix sockets (#104)\n\nA unix socket is the only way to reach a database on the Docker host from a\ncontainer on a macvlan network, which is what the reporter ran into on a\nSynology, and on the same machine it is faster than TCP.\n\nmysql2 takes a `socketPath` and then ignores host and port. The two places\nthat built the MySQL options were byte-identical apart from where they read\nthe config from, so they are now one pure function, buildMySQLOptions(), in\nthe new src/lib/connection-options.ts. It returns either a socket or a\nhost/port shape - passing host and port along for a socket connection would\nonly make the logged options and the error messages misleading.\n\nThe startup gate needed widening as well: `if (dbtype === ''sqlite'' ||\nthis.config.host)` decides whether connect() is called at all, so a\nsocket-only configuration would have started the adapter, reported nothing and\nnever connected. Normalisation clears the field for any dialect other than\nMySQL, with a warning, rather than letting a leftover value silently change\nhow they connect, and applyDockerMysqlConfig() clears it too because the\ncontainer is reached over TCP on its published port.\n\nThe admin UI hides Host and Port while a socket is configured, so there are no\nfields left that look required but are ignored.\n\nThe helper lives in its own module rather than in main.ts because importing\nmain.ts pulls in @iobroker/adapter-core, which calls process.exit(10) at module\nload time when js-controller cannot be resolved - and js-controller is not a\ndependency of this repository, the integration suite installs it into tmp/ at\nruntime. A unit test importing main.ts therefore kills mocha in CI.\n\nWhile fixing that, two gaps in the CI test list: the unit-test step is an\nexplicit list, not a glob, so test/testSqlClient.js (added with #563) and\ntest/testPackageFiles.js were never executed by CI at all. Both are now in it,\ntogether with the new test, and the step carries a comment saying that a new\nfile has to be added there and must not import build/main.js.\ntest/testProcessMessage.js cannot satisfy that second condition as written and\nis marked as local-only.\n\nTests: test/testConnectionOptions.js, 6 cases. The whole unit list was verified\nwith tmp/ moved aside, i.e. with js-controller unresolvable exactly as in CI:\n110 passing. That the option really switches the transport was verified against\nthe driver: with no socket, connecting fails with ECONNREFUSED on\n127.0.0.1:3306; with a socket path that does not exist it fails with ENOENT.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"549d56264c3c877e09db45a6c23c90c58a684480","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/trees/549d56264c3c877e09db45a6c23c90c58a684480"},"url":"https://api.github.com/r