ttps://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/20a8ef013bf89d4eaf9c148a023155b8563f21bc","node_id":"C_kwDOAsJ71NoAKDIwYThlZjAxM2JmODlkNGVhZjljMTQ4YTAyMzE1NWI4NTYzZjIxYmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/dc12e4d01ad295fe3d3726bb5b148e6e9ab1404c","sha":"dc12e4d01ad295fe3d3726bb5b148e6e9ab1404c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/dc12e4d01ad295fe3d3726bb5b148e6e9ab1404c"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/eadd7380a1cfc48dffeab493b9d46bf45f94b3dd","sha":"eadd7380a1cfc48dffeab493b9d46bf45f94b3dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/eadd7380a1cfc48dffeab493b9d46bf45f94b3dd"}],"sha":"20a8ef013bf89d4eaf9c148a023155b8563f21bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/20a8ef013bf89d4eaf9c148a023155b8563f21bc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/eadd7380a1cfc48dffeab493b9d46bf45f94b3dd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T08:09:05Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T08:09:05Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"Stop UNCAUGHT_EXCEPTION on connection loss and before init (#527)\n\nTwo unguarded accesses took the adapter down several times a day for a\nreporter running against a shared-hosting MySQL over WAN - 14 crashes on one\nday, each costing ~40 s of unrecorded values. Both are regressions of the 4.x\nbranch; 3.0.1 is unaffected.\n\n1. The driver''s `error` event had no listener.\n\nAll four drivers hand out an EventEmitter (mysql2 `Connection`, pg `Client`,\nmssql `ConnectionPool`, sqlite3 `Database`) and emit `error` on it when the\nserver drops the socket - ECONNRESET, PROTOCOL_CONNECTION_LOST. EventEmitter\nthrows an `error` event that nobody listens to, so the adapter terminated\ninstead of reconnecting.\n\nThe listener in borrowClientFromPool() was meant to prevent exactly this\n(\"make sure we always have at least one error listener to prevent crashes\"),\nbut it sits on the SQLClient wrapper, which never emits: nothing in src/lib\ncalls emit(), and nothing attached a listener to the driver''s connection. It\nguarded the wrong object.\n\nSQLClient now attaches the listener itself, centrally for every dialect, in a\nnew #adoptConnection() shared by connect() and connectAsync(). It flags the\nclient and re-emits only when someone is listening, because emit(''error'')\nwithout a listener throws ERR_UNHANDLED_ERROR - the very crash being fixed.\nThe listener is deliberately never removed, so a driver emitting while or\nafter closing cannot throw either; an identity check ignores events from a\nconnection that has already been replaced.\n\nSQLClientPool.validate() only looked at max_age and so handed a dead\nconnection straight back out, which is where the reporter''s follow-up \"Can''t\nadd new command when connection is in closed state\" came from. A flagged\nclient is now invalid, so borrow() destroys it and opens a fresh connection.\nThat is the reconnect.\n\n2. getHistory before the dialect was known dereferenced null.\n\n`sqlFuncs` starts as null and is only set in main(), after an await on\n`system.config`. The message handler is installed in the constructor, so the\nmessage box delivers during that window - and charts that kept polling through\na restart have their requests delivered in one batch exactly then, which is why\na single restart produced an immediate crash in getId(). processMessage() now\nanswers the database-backed commands with an error while `sqlFuncs` is unset,\nwhich covers all ~30 `this.sqlFuncs!` uses at once. stateChange and\nobjectChange cannot reach this window: both subscribe only after it.\n\nTests: test/testSqlClient.js and test/testProcessMessage.js, 20 cases, all of\nwhich fail on the unfixed code. main.ts additionally exports the class so a\ntest can call one method on the prototype without starting an adapter.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5564fd376cedca28c6f02b6bc441e0cc5901268a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/trees/5564fd376cedca28c6f02b6bc441e0cc5901268a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/commits/eadd7380a1cfc48dffeab493b9d46bf45f94b3dd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/eadd7380a1cfc48dffeab493b9d46bf45f94b3dd","node_id":"C_kwDOAsJ71NoAKGVhZGQ3MzgwYTFjZmM0OGRmZmVhYjQ5M2I5ZDQ2YmY0NWY5NGIzZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/dc12e4d01ad295fe3d3726bb5b148e6e9ab1404c","sha":"dc12e4d01ad295fe3d3726bb5b148e6e9ab1404c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/dc12e4d01ad295fe3d3726bb5b148e6e9ab1404c"}],"sha":"eadd7380a1cfc48dffeab493b9d46bf45f94b3dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/eadd7380a1cfc48dffeab493b9d46bf45f94b3dd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7318445?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DutchmanNL","id":7318445,"login":"DutchmanNL","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMTg0NDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/68eea81497799b652b6a11e374d8a547a22ba153/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T23:27:00Z","email":"drozda.apple@icloud.com","name":"DutchmanNL"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T23:27:00Z","email":"drozda.apple@icloud.com","name":"DutchmanNL"},"message":"Report an honest info.connection\n\nborrowClientFromPool set info.connection to true as soon as a pool object\nexisted - before the borrow was even attempted - and a failing borrow never\ncleared it again. So the state stayed true while the database was\nunreachable, which is what #374 reports (connect ETIMEDOUT with\ninfo.connection = true).\n\nReport what actually happened instead: a successful borrow, i.e. a real\nworking connection handed to a caller, sets it true, and five consecutive\nborrow failures set it false. The threshold keeps a single transient failure\nfrom flapping the state.\n\nVerified against a real PostgreSQL at the pool level: with the server up a\nborrow yields a client and no error, and once the server is stopped every\nborrow comes back with an error and no client - so both transitions fire.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"788b4d2d0a6bf0b71c5d60f8ddf620e8ef2179f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/trees/788b4d2d0a6bf0b71c5d60f8ddf620e8ef2179f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/commits/68eea81497799b652b6a11e374d8a547a22ba153","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7318445?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/events{/privacy}","followers_ur