","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/dc12e4d01ad295fe3d3726bb5b148e6e9ab1404c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T21:46:24Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T21:46:24Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"chore: release v4.1.6\n\n* (@DutchmanNL) Fixed `getCounter` on PostgreSQL: the queries used MySQL-style backtick quoting\n* (@DutchmanNL) Fixed `getCounter` on SQLite: `ORDER BY`/`LIMIT` is not allowed on a compound-select member\n* (@DutchmanNL) Fixed `getCounter` on MS SQL: the counter subquery filtered on `ts_number` instead of `ts_counter`\n* (@GermanBluefox) `getCounter` now sorts in the outer query on all dialects, so the row order no longer depends on the query plan\n* (@DutchmanNL) Added `getCounter` test coverage for all four dialects","tree":{"sha":"ed208a58dfb2b63bbb6aae1f002e352ad2befa3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/trees/ed208a58dfb2b63bbb6aae1f002e352ad2befa3d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/commits/dc12e4d01ad295fe3d3726bb5b148e6e9ab1404c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/follo