lowing_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DutchmanNL","id":7318445,"login":"DutchmanNL","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMTg0NDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/12acfcf3cce8c543bde04f4c3dd627e6c03895e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T21:04:04Z","email":"drozda.apple@icloud.com","name":"DutchmanNL"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T21:04:04Z","email":"drozda.apple@icloud.com","name":"DutchmanNL"},"message":"Fix getCounter on SQLite and MS SQL and cover it on every dialect\n\ngetCounter worked only on MySQL. PostgreSQL was broken by MySQL-style\nbackticked identifiers (fixed separately); this fixes the remaining two\ndialects, both of which built SQL the engine rejects.\n\nSQLite: ORDER BY and LIMIT are not allowed directly on a parenthesized\nmember of a compound SELECT, so the UNION ALL of five TOP-1-style\nsubqueries was a syntax error. Each subquery is now wrapped as a\nFROM-subquery, where ORDER BY + LIMIT are legal, and the counter-changes\nmember drops its redundant ORDER BY. The outer ORDER BY is kept and is\nrequired: sendResponseCounter consumes the rows positionally.\n\nMS SQL: the ts_counter subquery filtered and ordered on ts_number columns\n- a table that is not in its FROM clause - and the UNION carried stray\nderived-table aliases (`UNION ALL (...) a`) that T-SQL does not accept in\nthat position. It now filters on ts_counter''s own columns and uses the\nsame DISTINCT-over-union shape as the other dialects.\n\nAdds a dialect-agnostic getCounter round trip to test/lib/testcases.js, so\nall four SQL dialects are covered (influxdb has no getCounter command and\nis skipped). It writes a counter sequence containing a reset\n(100 -> 200 -> 10 -> 110) and asserts the progression of 200, using a\nrun-unique window and explicit timestamps so reruns against an existing\ndatabase stay deterministic.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4d2a828b3f64e41f5bd0f18352ae7961fe7cf2ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/trees/4d2a828b3f64e41f5bd0f18352ae7961fe7cf2ed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/commits/12acfcf3cce8c543bde04f4c3dd627e6c03895e1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7318445?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DutchmanNL","id":7318445,"login":"DutchmanNL","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMTg0NDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/12acfcf3cce8c543bde04f4c3dd627e6c03895e1","node_id":"C_kwDOAsJ71NoAKDEyYWNmY2YzY2NlOGM1NDNiZGUwNGY0YzNkZDYyN2U2YzAzODk1ZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commit/258e51cfdee156022dfe9ccb93eff9d04a2cba94","sha":"258e51cfdee156022dfe9ccb93eff9d04a2cba94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/258e51cfdee156022dfe9ccb93eff9d04a2cba94"}],"sha":"12acfcf3cce8c543bde04f4c3dd627e6c03895e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/12acfcf3cce8c543bde04f4c3dd627e6c03895e1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7318445?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DutchmanNL","id":7318445,"login":"DutchmanNL","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMTg0NDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/commits/9fe5968f963760a301c672202f801ee6eb175036/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T20:49:09Z","email":"drozda.apple@icloud.com","name":"DutchmanNL"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T20:49:09Z","email":"drozda.apple@icloud.com","name":"DutchmanNL"},"message":"Fix getCounter on PostgreSQL: remove MySQL-style identifier quoting\n\ngetCounterDiff built its five subqueries with backtick-quoted qualified\ntable names (`db`.ts_number). Backticks are MySQL syntax and are a syntax\nerror in PostgreSQL, so getCounter has always failed on this dialect.\n\nEvery other builder in postgresql.ts already uses bare, unqualified table\nnames and ignores dbName (PostgreSQL connects to the target database\ndirectly), so align getCounterDiff with them. The resulting SQL matches\nthe SQLite builder textually. dbName becomes unused and is renamed to\n_dbName to keep noUnusedParameters happy.\n\nAdds a getCounter round-trip test to test/testPostgreSQL.js covering a\ncounter sequence with a reset (100 -> 200 -> 10 -> 110), which must return\nthe expected progression of 200.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e22b5a2d435b2380a312b8ffe9a9b3df2a9f8467","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/trees/e22b5a2d435b2380a312b8ffe9a9b3df2a9f8467"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sql/git/commits/9fe5968f963760a301c672202f801ee6eb175036","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7318445?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DutchmanNL","id":7318445,"login":"DutchmanNL","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMTg0NDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DutchmanNL/subscrip